// New recipes for Rose's EATS. [id,title,cat,emoji,minutes,difficulty,cozy,serves,desc,ingredients(;),steps(|),cuisine]
const NEWR=[[3001,"Macarona Bechamel","comfort","🍝",75,"Medium",9,8,"Egypt's beloved baked pasta layered with spiced beef sauce and a creamy golden bechamel.","1 lb|penne;1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|flour;4 cup|milk;2|eggs|beaten;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Boil the penne 2 minutes short of the package time, drain and toss with a spoon of butter.|Brown the ground beef with the onion in a skillet over medium-high heat for 8 minutes, then add garlic, cinnamon, salt and pepper.|Stir in the tomato sauce and simmer the meat sauce 10 minutes until thick.|For the bechamel, melt the butter, whisk in the flour and cook 2 minutes, then slowly whisk in the milk and cook until thick, about 8 minutes. Season with salt, pepper and nutmeg, cool slightly, then whisk in the eggs.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Spread half the penne in a 9x13 dish, cover with the meat sauce, then top with the remaining penne.|Pour the bechamel over everything, sprinkle with parmesan and bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden. Rest 10 minutes before cutting.","Egyptian"],
[3002,"Hawawshi","lunch","🥙",50,"Easy",8,4,"Crisp baked pita stuffed with spiced minced beef, onion and herbs, a classic Egyptian street sandwich.","1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely grated;1|bell pepper|finely diced;1/2 cup|parsley|chopped;1|tomatoes|finely diced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|pita|large rounds","Heat the oven to 425°F.|Mix the beef, onion, pepper, parsley, tomato, cumin, paprika, black pepper and salt with your hands until well combined.|Cut each pita open along one edge to make a pocket and stuff with a quarter of the meat, pressing it flat to the edges.|Brush both sides of each pita with oil and place on a baking sheet.|Bake 15 minutes, flip, and bake another 8 to 10 minutes until the bread is crisp and the meat is cooked through.|Rest 3 minutes, cut into wedges and serve with tahini or a tomato salad.","Egyptian"],
[3003,"Mahshi (Egyptian Stuffed Vegetables)","comfort","🥒",120,"Medium",9,6,"Zucchini and peppers filled with herbed tomato rice and simmered in a light tomato sauce.","1 1/2 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;6|zucchini|small, cored;3|bell pepper|halved and seeded;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1 bunch|dill|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|cilantro|finely chopped;1|onion|grated;3 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|tomato sauce;2 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the rice with the herbs, onion, 1 tbsp tomato paste, oil, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper to make the filling.|Fill each zucchini and pepper about three-quarters full, because the rice will expand as it cooks.|Stir the garlic, remaining tomato paste, tomato sauce and broth together in a wide pot with a pinch of salt.|Pack the stuffed vegetables snugly in the pot, open sides up, and lay a heatproof plate on top to keep them in place.|Bring to a simmer, cover and cook on low for 45 to 55 minutes until the rice and vegetables are tender.|Rest 10 minutes and serve with the sauce spooned over.","Egyptian"],
[3004,"Warak Enab","sides","🍃",120,"Medium",7.5,8,"Grape leaves rolled around herbed rice and simmered with lemon until soft and tangy.","1 jar|grape leaves|rinsed;1 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1|onion|finely chopped;2|tomatoes|finely chopped;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|dill|finely chopped;2 tbsp|tomato paste;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;2 cup|water;|black pepper|to taste","Combine the rice, onion, tomatoes, herbs, tomato paste, half the oil, cumin, salt and pepper for the filling.|Lay a grape leaf shiny side down, put a heaping teaspoon of filling near the stem end, fold in the sides and roll up tightly like a thin cigar.|Line the bottom of a heavy pot with a few torn leaves and pack the rolls in tight layers.|Pour over the remaining oil, the lemon juice and the water, and set a plate on top to weigh the rolls down.|Bring to a simmer, cover and cook on low for 50 to 60 minutes until the rice is tender and most of the liquid is absorbed.|Cool slightly and serve warm or at room temperature with lemon wedges.","Egyptian"],
[3005,"Om Ali","treats","🍮",50,"Easy",9,8,"Egypt's famous warm bread pudding made with flaky pastry, nuts, raisins and sweet creamy milk.","1 lb|puff pastry|baked and broken in pieces;3 cup|milk;1 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tsp|vanilla;1/2 cup|almonds|chopped;1/2 cup|pistachios|chopped;1/2 cup|raisins;1/2 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 400°F. Bake the puff pastry on a sheet for 20 minutes until deeply golden, then cool and break into bite-size pieces.|Warm the milk, 1/2 cup of the cream, sugar and vanilla in a pot until the sugar dissolves.|Scatter half the pastry in a baking dish, then half the nuts, raisins and coconut. Repeat with the remaining pastry and toppings.|Pour the hot milk mixture evenly over the top so the pastry soaks it up.|Whip the remaining cream to soft peaks and dollop on top, then dust with cinnamon.|Bake 15 to 20 minutes until bubbling and browned on top. Serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3006,"Basbousa","treats","🍰",55,"Easy",9,16,"Moist semolina cake soaked in lemony syrup and topped with an almond.","2 cup|semolina|fine;1 cup|sugar;1 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;1 cup|greek yogurt|plain;1/2 cup|butter|melted;2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|vanilla;16|almonds|blanched, whole;1 1/2 cup|sugar|for syrup;1 cup|water|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice|for syrup","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x13 pan.|Mix the semolina, 1 cup sugar, coconut, baking powder, yogurt, melted butter and vanilla into a thick batter and let it rest 10 minutes.|Spread the batter in the pan, score into diamonds and press an almond into the center of each.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden brown.|Meanwhile simmer the syrup sugar and water for 8 minutes, stir in the lemon juice and let cool.|Pour the cool syrup over the hot cake and let it soak at least 30 minutes before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3007,"Egyptian Kofta","comfort","🍢",40,"Easy",9,6,"Juicy grilled skewers of spiced ground beef with onion and parsley, served with tahini and bread.","2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|grated and squeezed dry;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|allspice;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;6|pita|for serving","Combine the beef, onion, parsley, garlic, cumin, coriander, cinnamon, allspice, salt and pepper and knead well for 2 minutes.|Chill the mixture 20 minutes so it holds together on skewers.|Shape into long, thin sausages around flat metal skewers or into 12 oval patties.|Heat a grill or grill pan to medium-high and brush lightly with oil.|Grill 8 to 10 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked to 160°F inside.|Serve in warm pita with tomatoes, onions and tahini.","Egyptian"],
[3008,"Roz Bel Laban","treats","🍚",50,"Easy",9,6,"Silky Egyptian rice pudding scented with vanilla and topped with cinnamon and nuts.","1/2 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1/2 cup|water;4 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tbsp|rose water|optional;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped;|cinnamon|for dusting","Simmer the rice with the water in a pot for 10 minutes until the water is absorbed.|Add the milk and bring to a gentle boil, then reduce the heat and cook 25 minutes, stirring often, until the rice is very soft.|Stir in the sugar and cornstarch mixture and cook 5 more minutes until thick and creamy.|Add the cream, vanilla and rose water and warm through 2 minutes.|Spoon into bowls and chill at least 1 hour, as it thickens when cold.|Top with pistachios and cinnamon before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3009,"Bamia (Egyptian Okra Stew)","comfort","🥘",90,"Easy",9,6,"Tender beef and okra simmered in a garlicky tomato sauce, served over rice.","1 1/2 lb|beef stew meat|cubed;1|onion|chopped;1 lb|okra|frozen whole, thawed;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|coriander;1 tsp|cumin;2 cup|beef broth;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Brown the beef in the oil in a heavy pot over medium-high heat for 6 minutes and add the onion, cooking 4 minutes more.|Add half the garlic, the tomato paste, cumin, salt and pepper and stir 1 minute.|Pour in the broth, cover and simmer on low for 50 minutes until the beef is nearly tender.|In a skillet, saute the okra in a little oil for 5 minutes to reduce sliminess.|Add the okra and tomato sauce to the pot and simmer 20 minutes.|Fry the remaining garlic with the coriander in a spoon of oil until fragrant and stir it in. Serve over rice.","Egyptian"],
[3010,"Shorbet Ads (Egyptian Lentil Soup)","soup","🍲",45,"Very easy",9.5,6,"Smooth, golden lentil soup with cumin and a squeeze of lemon, a staple on Egyptian tables.","1 1/2 cup|lentils|red, rinsed;1|onion|chopped;1|carrots|chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|turmeric;6 cup|chicken broth;|lemon|wedges, for serving;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Saute the onion and carrot in the oil in a large pot for 6 minutes until soft.|Stir in the garlic, cumin and turmeric for 1 minute.|Add the lentils and broth, bring to a boil, then simmer 25 minutes until the lentils fall apart.|Blend the soup until completely smooth with an immersion blender.|Season with salt and pepper and thin with hot water if too thick.|Serve with lemon wedges and toasted bread.","Egyptian"],
[3011,"Kebda Eskandarani","quick","🍽️",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Alexandrian-style liver seared with garlic, cumin and hot peppers and eaten in pita.","1 lb|beef liver|thinly sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|sliced;1|green chili|sliced, optional;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|paprika;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4|pita|for serving","Pat the liver dry and cut into thin strips, removing any membrane.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat until very hot.|Sear the liver in a single layer for 2 minutes without moving, then flip.|Add the garlic, bell pepper, chili, cumin, coriander, paprika, salt and pepper and cook 3 minutes.|Squeeze in the lemon juice and cook 1 minute more. Do not overcook or the liver turns tough.|Stuff into warm pita and serve right away.","Egyptian"],
[3012,"Sayadeya (Egyptian Fish and Rice)","light","🐟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Cumin-spiced white fish over deep golden caramelized onion rice, a coastal Egyptian classic.","2 lb|cod|fillets, cut in large pieces;4|onion|thinly sliced;2 cup|rice;3 cup|water;1/3 cup|vegetable oil;2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|flour|for dusting;2 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Season the fish with half the cumin, salt, pepper and lemon juice and let sit 15 minutes.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat for 20 to 25 minutes, stirring often, until deep brown. Remove half for topping.|To the onions in the pot add the garlic, coriander and remaining cumin and cook 1 minute.|Add the rice and water with salt, bring to a boil, cover and cook on low for 18 minutes.|Meanwhile dust the fish in flour and pan-fry in oil 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden.|Serve the fish on the rice topped with the reserved fried onions.","Egyptian"],
[3013,"Roz Bel Shareya","sides","🍚",35,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy Egyptian rice cooked with toasted vermicelli noodles in butter.","2 cup|rice|short or medium grain;1/2 cup|vermicelli|broken;3 tbsp|butter;3 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste","Rinse the rice until the water runs clear and drain well.|Melt the butter in a pot and toast the vermicelli over medium heat for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden brown.|Stir in the rice for 1 minute to coat in the butter.|Pour in the hot broth, add salt, and bring to a boil.|Reduce to the lowest heat, cover tightly and cook 18 minutes.|Rest, covered, 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork.","Egyptian"],
[3014,"Mesaka'a (Egyptian Moussaka)","comfort","🍆",70,"Easy",9,6,"Fried eggplant slow-cooked in a garlicky tomato and pepper sauce, nothing like Greek moussaka.","3 lb|eggplant|sliced 1/2 inch thick;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;5 clove|garlic|sliced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|vinegar;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Salt the eggplant slices, rest 20 minutes, then pat dry.|Heat the oven to 425°F, brush the slices with oil and roast on sheets 25 minutes, flipping once, until golden.|Saute the onion and peppers in a little oil for 6 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin and paprika for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, tomato paste and vinegar, season, and simmer 15 minutes.|Layer the eggplant in a deep pan and pour the sauce over the top.|Simmer gently, covered, for 20 minutes. Serve warm or at room temperature with rice or bread.","Egyptian"],
[3015,"Egyptian Goulash","comfort","🥧",80,"Medium",9,8,"A baked phyllo pie of spiced ground beef, tomato and creamy milk, an Egyptian home favorite.","1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|tomato sauce;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 cup|butter|melted;2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef with the onion for 8 minutes, add garlic, cumin, cinnamon, salt and pepper, then stir in the tomato sauce and simmer 10 minutes.|Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 9x13 dish.|Layer half the phyllo sheets in the dish, brushing each with butter.|Spread the meat filling over the phyllo and sprinkle with the mozzarella.|Cover with the remaining buttered phyllo sheets and cut through into squares.|Bake 30 minutes until golden, then pour the milk and cream mixed with a pinch of salt over the top and bake 15 more minutes until absorbed.","Egyptian"],
[3016,"Batates Bel Lahma (Egyptian Beef and Potato Stew)","comfort","🥔",100,"Easy",9,6,"Fall-apart beef and potatoes in a simple tomato gravy.","1 1/2 lb|beef stew meat|cubed;1|onion|chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;3 cup|beef broth;2 lb|potatoes|peeled, cut in chunks;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef in the oil in a heavy pot over medium-high heat for 7 minutes.|Add the onion and cook 4 minutes, then the garlic, tomato paste, cumin, cinnamon, salt and pepper for 1 minute.|Add the broth, cover and simmer on low for 50 minutes until the beef is almost tender.|Fry the potato chunks in a skillet until lightly golden, about 8 minutes, if you like a crisper edge.|Add the potatoes to the pot and simmer 25 minutes until tender and the sauce thickens.|Adjust the seasoning and serve with rice.","Egyptian"],
[3017,"Fasolia (Egyptian Green Bean Stew)","comfort","🫘",60,"Easy",9,4,"Green beans simmered with beef and tomatoes until tender, served over rice.","1 lb|green beans|trimmed;1 lb|beef stew meat|small cubes;1|onion|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cumin;2 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Brown the beef in the oil in a pot for 6 minutes, then add the onion and cook 4 minutes.|Add the garlic, coriander, cumin, salt and pepper and stir 1 minute.|Pour in the water, cover and simmer 35 minutes until the beef is tender.|Add the green beans and tomato sauce and simmer, partly covered, 20 minutes until the beans are very soft.|Reduce uncovered 5 minutes if the sauce is thin.|Serve over rice.","Egyptian"],
[3018,"Torly (Egyptian Baked Vegetable Casserole)","comfort","🥕",90,"Easy",9,6,"Layers of potatoes, zucchini, eggplant and peppers baked in tomato sauce until tender.","1 lb|potatoes|sliced;2|zucchini|sliced;1|eggplant|cubed;2|bell pepper|sliced;2|carrots|sliced;1|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|tomato sauce;1 lb|beef stew meat|small cubes, optional;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F.|If using beef, brown it in oil for 6 minutes and add the onion and garlic for 3 minutes.|Mix the tomato sauce with the water, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper.|Toss all the vegetables with oil and salt and spread in a deep baking dish with the meat.|Pour the sauce over, cover tightly with foil and bake 45 minutes.|Uncover and bake 20 to 25 minutes more until the vegetables are tender and the sauce thick. Serve with rice.","Egyptian"],
[3019,"Qatayef","treats","🥞",60,"Medium",9,12,"Ramadan pancakes folded around nuts or cream and dunked in sweet syrup.","1 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|semolina;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|sugar;2 cup|warm water;1 cup|walnuts|chopped;1/2 cup|raisins;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|sugar|for syrup;1/2 cup|water|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice|for syrup;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Blend the flour, semolina, baking powder, yeast, sugar and warm water into a thin batter and rest 30 minutes.|Boil the syrup sugar and water for 8 minutes, stir in the lemon juice and cool.|Mix the walnuts, raisins and cinnamon for the filling.|Pour small 3-inch rounds of batter onto a medium-hot nonstick pan and cook on one side only until the surface is covered in bubbles and set, about 1 to 2 minutes.|Put a spoon of filling in the center of each pancake, fold into a half moon and pinch the edges tightly closed.|Fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes until golden, drain, and dip in the cool syrup.","Egyptian"],
[3020,"Kahk","treats","🍪",75,"Medium",9,30,"Buttery Eid cookies stuffed with dates or nuts and dusted with powdered sugar.","3 cup|flour;1 cup|butter|melted;1/4 cup|sesame oil;1/2 cup|milk|warm;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|yeast;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sugar;1 cup|walnuts|chopped;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|powdered sugar|for dusting","Rub the flour, salt, butter and sesame oil together until the flour feels like wet sand, then rest 30 minutes.|Dissolve the yeast and sugar in the warm milk and knead into the flour to a soft, smooth dough.|Mix the walnuts with the cinnamon for the filling.|Roll the dough into walnut-size balls, flatten, fill, and close, then flatten slightly into rounds and mark the tops with a fork or tongs.|Place on a lined sheet and bake at 350°F for 20 to 25 minutes until just barely golden on the bottom.|Cool completely and dust heavily with powdered sugar.","Egyptian"],
[3021,"Egyptian Eggah","breakfast","🍳",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"A thick baked herb omelet, like a spiced Egyptian frittata cut in squares.","6|eggs;1 bunch|parsley|finely chopped;1/2 bunch|dill|finely chopped;1|onion|finely chopped;2 tbsp|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|coriander;3 tbsp|butter;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Saute the onion in 1 tbsp butter for 5 minutes until soft and let cool.|Whisk the eggs with the flour, baking powder, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper until smooth.|Stir in the herbs and cooled onion.|Melt the remaining butter in an 8-inch oven-safe pan, pour in the egg mixture and cook 2 minutes on the stove.|Bake 20 to 25 minutes until puffed and set, then cut into squares.","Egyptian"],
[3022,"Sahlab","treats","🥛",15,"Very easy",9,4,"A warm, creamy milk pudding drink topped with nuts, coconut and cinnamon.","4 cup|milk;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/3 cup|sugar;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tbsp|rose water;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped;1/4 cup|coconut|shredded, unsweetened;|cinnamon|for dusting","Whisk the cornstarch into 1 cup of the cold milk until smooth.|Heat the remaining milk with the sugar in a pot over medium heat until steaming.|Slowly whisk in the cornstarch mixture.|Cook, whisking constantly, for 5 to 6 minutes until thickened to a pudding-like drink.|Stir in the vanilla and rose water.|Pour into cups and top with pistachios, coconut and cinnamon.","Egyptian"],
[3023,"Bessara (Egyptian Fava Bean Soup)","soup","🌿",75,"Easy",9.5,6,"A thick, green, herb-packed puree of dried fava beans and greens.","2 cup|dried fava beans|peeled, split, soaked overnight;1|onion|chopped;1 bunch|parsley;1 bunch|dill;1 bunch|cilantro;1 head|lettuce|chopped;4 clove|garlic|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;3 tbsp|olive oil;6 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|lemon|wedges, for serving","Drain the soaked fava beans and place in a pot with the water and half the onion.|Bring to a boil, skim, then simmer 40 minutes until very soft.|Add the lettuce, parsley, dill and cilantro and simmer 10 more minutes.|Blend until completely smooth and season with salt, adding hot water if too thick.|Fry the remaining onion and garlic in the oil with the cumin until golden, about 6 minutes.|Serve the soup topped with the garlicky onions, olive oil and lemon.","Egyptian"],
[3024,"Egyptian Sambousek","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,8,"Crisp fried half-moon pastries filled with spiced beef or cheese.","2 cup|flour;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|warm water;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely chopped;1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 cup|pine nuts;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|black pepper|to taste","Knead the flour, oil, salt and water into a smooth dough and rest 20 minutes.|Brown the beef with the onion for 7 minutes, then stir in the cumin, cinnamon, pine nuts, salt and pepper and cool.|Roll the dough thin and cut 4-inch rounds.|Place a spoonful of filling in each, fold over and press the edges firmly with a fork to seal.|Fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes per side until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3025,"Betingan Makli (Fried Eggplant with Garlic Vinegar)","sides","🍆",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Golden fried eggplant slices tossed in a punchy garlic, vinegar and cumin dressing.","2 lb|eggplant|sliced 1/2 inch thick;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|white vinegar;1 tsp|cumin;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 tsp|salt;|black pepper|to taste","Salt the eggplant slices, rest 15 minutes and pat dry.|Heat 1/2 inch of oil in a skillet over medium-high heat.|Fry the slices 3 minutes per side until golden and tender, in batches, and drain on paper towels.|Stir the garlic, vinegar, cumin, salt and pepper together.|Arrange the eggplant on a platter and spoon the dressing over it.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve warm or at room temperature with bread.","Egyptian"],
[3026,"Roz Mu'ammar","comfort","🥣",60,"Easy",9,6,"Rich, creamy baked rice cooked in milk, butter and broth, the Egyptian comfort side.","1 cup|rice|short grain, rinsed;1 cup|milk;1 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Put the rice in an oven-safe pot or clay dish with the salt and pepper.|Heat the milk, broth and cream until steaming and pour over the rice.|Dot the top with the butter and cover tightly with foil or a lid.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until the rice is soft and creamy.|Stir and serve hot, optionally under the broiler 3 minutes for a golden top.","Egyptian"],
[3027,"Shish Tawook","lunch","🍢",50,"Easy",8,4,"Lemony yogurt-marinated chicken skewers grilled until juicy, served with garlic sauce.","2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 1/2 inch cubes;3/4 cup|greek yogurt;3 tbsp|lemon juice;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|tomato paste;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|cumin","Whisk the yogurt, lemon juice, oil, tomato paste, garlic, paprika, cumin, salt and pepper.|Add the chicken, toss well, cover and marinate in the fridge at least 2 hours or overnight.|Thread the chicken onto skewers.|Heat a grill or grill pan to medium-high.|Grill 10 to 12 minutes, turning every few minutes, until charred and 165°F inside.|Serve with pita, toum and pickles.","Lebanese"],
[3028,"Tabbouleh","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"A bright parsley salad with tomato, mint, bulgur and lemon.","4 bunch|parsley|flat leaf, finely chopped;1/2 bunch|mint|finely chopped;4|tomatoes|small dice;4|green onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|bulgur|fine, soaked in lemon juice;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;|black pepper|to taste;1 head|lettuce|romaine leaves, for serving","Soak the bulgur in the lemon juice for 15 minutes.|Wash the parsley and dry it thoroughly so the salad is not soggy, then chop very fine.|Combine the parsley, mint, tomatoes and green onion.|Add the soaked bulgur, olive oil, salt and pepper and toss gently.|Taste and add more lemon or salt as needed.|Serve in lettuce leaves.","Lebanese"],
[3029,"Fattoush","light","🥗",25,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crunchy Lebanese chopped salad with fried pita chips and tangy sumac dressing.","2|pita|torn;1 head|lettuce|romaine, chopped;2|cucumber|diced;4|tomatoes|diced;5|radish|sliced;4|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|mint|chopped;1/3 cup|olive oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sumac;1 tbsp|pomegranate molasses;1 clove|garlic|minced;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F and toss the torn pita with 2 tbsp olive oil and a pinch of salt.|Bake 8 to 10 minutes until crisp and golden and let cool.|Whisk the remaining oil, lemon juice, sumac, pomegranate molasses, garlic and salt.|Toss the lettuce, cucumbers, tomatoes, radishes, green onion and herbs in a large bowl.|Pour the dressing over and toss.|Add the pita chips just before serving so they stay crunchy.","Lebanese"],
[3030,"Mujadara","comfort","🧅",60,"Easy",9,6,"Lentils and rice crowned with deeply caramelized onions, the ultimate Levantine comfort dish.","1 cup|lentils|brown or green, rinsed;1 cup|rice;4|onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|olive oil;2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;4 cup|water;|black pepper|to taste;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving","Simmer the lentils in 3 cups of the water for 15 minutes until just starting to soften, then drain, saving the water.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat, stirring often, for 25 to 30 minutes until dark golden and crisp at the edges.|Remove half the onions for topping.|To the pot add the lentils, rice, cumin, salt, pepper and 2 cups of the reserved cooking water topped up with water.|Bring to a boil, cover and cook on low for 20 minutes.|Rest 10 minutes, fluff, top with the reserved onions and serve with yogurt.","Lebanese"],
[3031,"Manakish Za'atar","breakfast","🫓",90,"Medium",8.5,6,"Soft flatbreads brushed with olive oil and za'atar, the classic Lebanese breakfast.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast|2 1/4 tsp;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 cup|za'atar;1/2 cup|olive oil|for topping","Mix the yeast, sugar and warm water and wait 5 minutes until foamy.|Combine the flour and salt, add the yeast mixture and 2 tbsp oil and knead 8 minutes into a soft dough.|Cover and let rise 1 hour until doubled.|Heat the oven to 475°F with a baking sheet inside.|Divide the dough into 6 balls, flatten into 6-inch rounds and press dimples into them.|Mix the za'atar with the topping oil, spread over the dough and bake 8 to 10 minutes until golden.","Lebanese"],
[3032,"Baked Kibbeh (Kibbeh bil Sanieh)","comfort","🥘",90,"Medium",9,8,"Layers of spiced bulgur and lamb with a pine nut and onion filling, baked until golden.","1 1/2 cup|bulgur|fine;1 1/2 lb|ground lamb|divided;2|onion|divided, one grated and one chopped;1 tsp|allspice;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 cup|pine nuts;3 tbsp|olive oil;1/4 cup|butter|melted;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Soak the bulgur in cold water 15 minutes, drain and squeeze dry.|Process 1 lb of the lamb with the grated onion, bulgur, half the allspice, cinnamon, salt and pepper into a smooth paste.|For the filling, brown the remaining lamb with the chopped onion in the oil for 8 minutes, then add the pine nuts, remaining allspice, salt and pepper.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Press half the kibbeh paste into a greased 9x13 dish.|Spread the filling on top and cover with the remaining paste, smoothing the top.|Score into diamonds, pour over the butter and bake 40 to 45 minutes until browned.","Lebanese"],
[3033,"Iskender Kebab","comfort","🥩",50,"Medium",9,4,"Thin-sliced spiced beef on bread with hot tomato sauce, yogurt and sizzling butter.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|very thinly sliced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;4|pita|cut in squares;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tbsp|tomato paste;4 tbsp|butter;1 cup|greek yogurt;1 clove|garlic|minced;1|tomatoes|halved, grilled, optional","Toss the steak with the oil, cumin, paprika and salt.|Warm the pita squares in a 350°F oven for 5 minutes and spread on a platter.|Simmer the tomato sauce and tomato paste with a pinch of salt for 8 minutes.|Sear the meat in a very hot skillet in small batches for 2 minutes per batch until browned.|Pile the meat over the bread, ladle the hot tomato sauce on top and add a bed of yogurt mixed with garlic on the side.|Brown the butter in a small pan until nutty and pour sizzling over everything right before serving.","Turkish"],
[3034,"Menemen","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,3,"Soft-scrambled eggs cooked with tomatoes and peppers, a Turkish breakfast staple.","4|eggs;3|tomatoes|chopped;2|bell pepper|green, diced;1|onion|diced, optional;2 tbsp|butter;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;|bread|for serving","Melt the butter in a skillet and saute the peppers and onion 5 minutes until soft.|Add the tomatoes and cook 8 to 10 minutes until the juices reduce and thicken.|Season with salt, pepper and pepper flakes.|Crack the eggs over the top and stir gently or leave whole.|Cook 2 to 3 minutes until just set but still soft.|Serve in the pan with crusty bread.","Turkish"],
[3035,"Karniyarik","comfort","🍆",75,"Medium",9,4,"Split eggplants stuffed with spiced beef and baked in tomato sauce.","4|eggplant|small;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2|tomatoes|diced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Peel the eggplants in stripes, slit lengthwise leaving the ends intact and soak in salted water 15 minutes, then pat dry.|Fry the eggplants in oil until golden on all sides, about 8 minutes, and drain.|Brown the beef with the onion for 7 minutes, add the garlic, half the tomato, parsley, salt and pepper and cook 5 minutes.|Heat the oven to 375°F and arrange the eggplants in a baking dish.|Press the beef into the slits and top with the remaining tomato.|Mix the tomato paste with the water, pour around, and bake 30 minutes.","Turkish"],
[3036,"Kiymali Pide","lunch","🥖",100,"Medium",8,4,"Boat-shaped Turkish flatbread filled with spiced minced beef and baked until blistered.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;1 tbsp|olive oil;3/4 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely diced;1|bell pepper|finely diced;1|tomatoes|finely diced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|paprika;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing","Mix the yeast, sugar and water, wait 5 minutes, then knead with the flour, salt and oil for 8 minutes. Let rise 1 hour.|Combine the beef, onion, pepper, tomato, tomato paste, paprika and salt for the filling.|Heat the oven to 475°F with a baking sheet inside.|Divide the dough into 4, roll each into an oval and spread the filling down the center, leaving a border.|Fold the long edges over the filling and pinch the ends into a boat shape. Brush the crust with egg.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden and the meat is cooked.","Turkish"],
[3037,"Gozleme","lunch","🫓",50,"Easy",8,4,"Thin hand-rolled Turkish flatbreads filled with spinach and feta and griddled until crisp.","3 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 lb|spinach|fresh, wilted and squeezed dry;1 cup|feta|crumbled;1|onion|small, finely diced;3 tbsp|butter|melted;|black pepper|to taste","Knead the flour, salt, water and oil into a smooth dough, cover and rest 30 minutes.|Mix the spinach, feta, onion and pepper for the filling.|Divide the dough into 4 balls and roll each into a very thin round.|Spread the filling over half of each round, fold over and seal the edges.|Cook on a dry hot skillet 2 to 3 minutes per side until blistered and golden.|Brush with butter and serve with lemon.","Turkish"],
[3038,"Manti","comfort","🥟",120,"Medium",9,6,"Tiny Turkish beef dumplings under garlicky yogurt and paprika butter.","2 1/2 cup|flour;1|eggs;1/2 cup|water;1 tsp|salt;1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|grated;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 cup|greek yogurt;2 clove|garlic|minced;4 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;6 cup|beef broth","Knead the flour, egg, water and salt into a stiff dough and rest 30 minutes.|Mix the beef, onion, pepper and a pinch of salt.|Roll the dough very thin, cut into 1-inch squares, and place a pea-size bit of filling in each center. Pinch the corners together.|Mix the yogurt with the garlic and a pinch of salt.|Simmer the manti in the broth for 10 to 12 minutes until they float and are tender.|Melt the butter with the paprika and flakes. Spoon the manti with a little broth onto plates, top with yogurt and the sizzling butter.","Turkish"],
[3039,"Muhammara","sides","🌶️",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"A smoky roasted red pepper and walnut dip with a tangy-sweet pomegranate kick.","1 jar|roasted red peppers|12 oz, drained;1 cup|walnuts|toasted;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;2 tbsp|pomegranate molasses;1 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Toast the walnuts in a dry skillet for 4 minutes until fragrant and cool.|Add the peppers, walnuts, breadcrumbs, garlic, cumin and pepper flakes to a food processor.|Pulse until chunky.|Add the pomegranate molasses and lemon juice and blend while streaming in the olive oil.|Season with salt and chill 30 minutes.|Serve with a swirl of oil and warm pita.","Middle Eastern"],
[3040,"Toum (Lebanese Garlic Sauce)","sides","🧄",15,"Medium",7.5,12,"Fluffy, intensely garlicky white sauce for chicken and kebabs.","1 head|garlic|peeled;1 tsp|salt;1 1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1/4 cup|lemon juice;2 tbsp|ice water","Process the garlic and salt in a food processor to a fine paste, scraping the sides.|With the machine running, add the oil a few drops at a time at first, then in a thin stream.|Add the lemon juice in small portions, alternating with the oil.|Blend in the ice water to lighten the sauce.|Taste and adjust salt and lemon.|Refrigerate in a jar, where it will keep about 2 weeks.","Lebanese"],
[3041,"Batata Harra","sides","🥔",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crispy Lebanese potatoes tossed with garlic, cilantro, lemon and chili.","2 lb|baby potatoes|halved;1/4 cup|olive oil;6 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tsp|coriander;2 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Boil the potatoes in salted water 10 minutes until barely tender and drain well.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Fry the potatoes 15 minutes, turning, until crisp and golden.|Add the garlic, coriander and chili and cook 1 minute.|Remove from the heat and toss with the cilantro and lemon juice.|Season with salt and serve hot.","Lebanese"],
[3042,"Fatayer bi Sabanekh","sides","🥟",100,"Medium",7.5,12,"Soft triangle pies stuffed with lemony spinach and onion.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|warm water;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 lb|spinach|fresh, chopped;1|onion|finely diced;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sumac;3 tbsp|olive oil|for the filling;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the yeast, sugar and water, wait 5 minutes, then knead with the flour, salt and oil. Rise 1 hour.|Toss the spinach with 1 tsp salt, rest 10 minutes and squeeze out all the liquid.|Mix with the onion, lemon juice, sumac, oil and pepper.|Heat the oven to 400°F. Roll the dough thin and cut 4-inch rounds.|Place filling in the center and pinch the edges in three sides to form triangles, sealing completely.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until golden and brush with oil.","Lebanese"],
[3043,"Birria Tacos","comfort","🌮",240,"Medium",9,8,"Chile-braised beef in corn tortillas crisped in the red fat, served with a cup of rich consomme for dipping.","6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;3|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|tomatoes|quartered;1|onion|quartered;4 clove|garlic;3 lb|chuck roast|cut in large chunks;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;2|bay leaves;4 cup|beef broth;16|corn tortillas;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;1/2 cup|onion|finely diced, for serving;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;2|lime|cut in wedges;|salt|to taste","Toast the dried chiles in a dry skillet over medium heat for 30 seconds per side, then soak in hot water for 15 minutes until soft.|Blend the soaked chiles with the tomatoes, onion, garlic, vinegar, cumin, oregano and 1 cup of the broth until smooth, then strain.|Season the beef generously with salt and toss with the chile sauce in a Dutch oven. Add the bay leaves and the remaining broth.|Cover and braise in a 325°F oven for 3 hours until the beef shreds easily.|Skim the red fat from the top into a bowl, discard the bay leaves, and shred the meat, moistening it with some of the consomme.|Dip each tortilla in the reserved fat, fry on a hot skillet, add cheese and beef, fold, and crisp 1 to 2 minutes per side.|Serve with diced onion, cilantro, lime and a cup of warm consomme for dipping.","Mexican"],
[3044,"Carne Asada","comfort","🥩",50,"Easy",9,6,"Citrus-marinated skirt or flank steak grilled hot and sliced thin for tacos, tortas or plates.","2 lb|flank steak;1/2 cup|lime juice;1/2 cup|orange juice;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|jalapeno|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;12|corn tortillas|warmed, for serving","Whisk together the lime juice, orange juice, garlic, oil, cilantro, jalapeno, cumin, chili powder, oregano, salt and pepper.|Place the steak in a zip bag with the marinade and refrigerate for at least 2 hours and up to 8.|Heat a grill or cast iron pan to high heat, around 500°F.|Grill the steak 4 to 5 minutes per side for medium-rare, until it reaches 130°F inside.|Rest the meat 10 minutes, then slice thinly against the grain.|Serve in warm tortillas with salsa, onion and lime.","Mexican"],
[3045,"Tacos al Pastor","comfort","🌮",90,"Medium",9,6,"Thin pork marinated in chiles and pineapple, seared until charred and tucked into tortillas with fresh pineapple.","3|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 tbsp|chipotle in adobo|with sauce;1/2 cup|pineapple juice;1/4 cup|white vinegar;4 clove|garlic;2 tbsp|achiote paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;1 cup|pineapple|diced fresh;12|corn tortillas;1/2|onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|lime|cut in wedges","Soak the guajillos in hot water for 15 minutes until soft.|Blend the chiles with the chipotle, pineapple juice, vinegar, garlic, achiote, cumin, oregano and salt until smooth.|Coat the sliced pork in the marinade and refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight.|Heat a large cast iron skillet over high heat and sear the pork in batches, 3 to 4 minutes per side, until charred at the edges and cooked through.|Sear the pineapple in the same pan for 2 minutes until caramelized.|Chop the pork, warm the tortillas, and fill with pork, pineapple, onion and cilantro.|Serve with lime wedges.","Mexican"],
[3046,"Carnitas","prep","🐖",200,"Easy",9,8,"Pork simmered until tender in its own fat and orange, then crisped under the broiler for juicy, crackly edges.","4 lb|pork shoulder|cut in 3 inch chunks;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|oregano;1|onion|quartered;6 clove|garlic|smashed;2|bay leaves;2|oranges|juiced;1|lime|juiced;1/2 cup|water;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped","Season the pork with salt, pepper, cumin and oregano and let it sit 30 minutes.|Place the pork in a Dutch oven with the onion, garlic, bay leaves, orange juice, lime juice and water.|Bring to a simmer, cover, and cook in a 300°F oven for 2 1/2 to 3 hours until the meat is fork tender.|Shred the pork and discard the bay leaves, onion and skin.|Spread on a sheet pan, spoon over some pan juices, and broil 5 to 7 minutes until the edges are browned and crisp.|Serve in warm tortillas with cilantro, onion and salsa.","Mexican"],
[3047,"Chicken Tinga","comfort","🌶️",45,"Easy",9,6,"Shredded chicken in a smoky chipotle and tomato sauce, perfect for tostadas, tacos or tortas.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast;4 cup|chicken broth;1|onion|half quartered, half sliced;3 clove|garlic;4|tomatoes|roma, quartered;2 tbsp|chipotle in adobo|with sauce;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|cumin;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|salt|to taste;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|sour cream|for serving","Simmer the chicken in the broth with the quartered onion half and 1 clove garlic for 20 minutes until cooked through.|Shred the chicken and reserve 1/2 cup of the broth.|Blend the tomatoes, remaining garlic, chipotle, oregano, cumin and the reserved broth until smooth.|Saute the sliced onion in the oil for 5 minutes until soft, then pour in the sauce and simmer 8 minutes.|Stir in the shredded chicken and cook 5 more minutes, seasoning with salt.|Serve on warm tortillas or crisp tostadas topped with sour cream.","Mexican"],
[3048,"Pozole Rojo","soup","🍲",150,"Medium",9.5,8,"Hearty pork and hominy soup in a deep red guajillo broth, served with crunchy cabbage, radish and lime.","2 lb|pork shoulder|cut in chunks;8 cup|water;1|onion|halved;6 clove|garlic;2|bay leaves;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 can|hominy|25 oz each, drained;1 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|salt;2 cup|cabbage|shredded, for serving;6|radishes|sliced, for serving;2|lime|cut in wedges","Place the pork, water, half the onion, 3 cloves garlic, bay leaves and salt in a large pot and bring to a boil. Skim the foam.|Simmer covered for 1 hour 15 minutes until the pork is tender.|Soak the chiles in hot water for 15 minutes, then blend with the remaining onion and garlic, oregano, cumin and 1 cup of the broth until smooth. Strain.|Stir the chile sauce and hominy into the pot and simmer uncovered for 30 minutes.|Adjust the salt and shred some of the pork if you like.|Ladle into bowls and top with cabbage, radish, onion and a squeeze of lime.","Mexican"],
[3049,"Chicken Tortilla Soup","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"A smoky tomato and chile broth with shredded chicken, topped with crisp tortilla strips and avocado.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|jalapeno|diced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz, fire roasted;1 tbsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;6 cup|chicken broth;1 lb|chicken breast;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn;8|corn tortillas|cut in strips;1|avocado|diced;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;2|lime|juiced;|salt|to taste;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded","Toss the tortilla strips with a little oil and salt and bake at 400°F for 8 to 10 minutes until crisp.|Saute the onion and jalapeno in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, chili powder and cumin for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes and broth, then the chicken breasts, and simmer 18 to 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked.|Remove the chicken, shred it, and return to the pot with the beans and corn.|Simmer 5 more minutes, then stir in the lime juice and cilantro and season with salt.|Ladle into bowls and top with tortilla strips, avocado and cheese.","Mexican"],
[3050,"Chiles Rellenos","comfort","🫑",60,"Medium",9,4,"Roasted poblano peppers stuffed with cheese, dipped in fluffy egg batter, fried and served in tomato sauce.","4|poblano peppers;8 oz|mexican cheese blend|cut in strips;3|eggs|separated;1/4 cup|flour|plus more for dredging;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;1/4 cup|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|cumin;|salt|to taste","Char the poblanos over a flame or under the broiler until blackened all over, then steam in a covered bowl for 10 minutes and peel.|Make a slit in each pepper, remove the seeds, and stuff with cheese strips.|Simmer the tomato sauce with the onion, garlic, cumin and salt for 10 minutes.|Beat the egg whites to stiff peaks, fold in the yolks and 1/4 cup flour with a pinch of salt.|Dust the peppers in flour, dip into the batter, and fry in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve in the warm tomato sauce.","Mexican"],
[3051,"Pork Tamales","prep","🌽",240,"Medium",9,12,"Fluffy masa wrapped around red chile pork in corn husks and steamed, a holiday tradition.","30|dried corn husks;2 lb|pork shoulder|cut in chunks;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;3 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cumin;4 cup|masa harina;1 1/2 cup|lard|or vegetable shortening;1 tbsp|baking powder;4 cup|chicken broth|warm;2 tsp|salt","Soak the husks in hot water for 30 minutes until pliable.|Simmer the pork in water with a little salt for 1 1/2 hours until tender, then shred, saving 2 cups of the broth.|Soak the chiles in hot water 15 minutes, blend with garlic, cumin and 1 cup pork broth, strain, and toss with the shredded pork.|Whip the lard for 3 minutes until fluffy. Mix the masa harina, baking powder and salt, then beat into the lard alternately with the warm broth until it resembles thick frosting.|Spread 2 tbsp masa on each husk, add a spoonful of pork, fold and roll.|Stand the tamales upright in a steamer and steam covered for 1 hour 15 minutes, until the masa pulls cleanly from the husk.|Rest 15 minutes before serving.","Mexican"],
[3052,"Chilaquiles Rojos","breakfast","🍳",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crisp tortilla chips simmered briefly in red salsa and topped with eggs, cheese and cream.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|salsa|red, blended smooth;1/2 cup|chicken broth;8 oz|tortilla chips;4|eggs|fried;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|crumbled;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4|red onion|thinly sliced","Heat the oil and soften the onion and garlic for 3 minutes.|Add the salsa and broth and simmer 5 minutes until slightly thickened.|Fold in the tortilla chips and toss for 1 to 2 minutes until coated but still a little crisp.|Divide among plates right away.|Top with fried eggs, cheese, drizzles of sour cream, cilantro and red onion.","Mexican"],
[3053,"Elote (Mexican Street Corn)","sides","🌽",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Charred corn on the cob slathered with mayo, cotija cheese, chili powder and lime.","4|ears corn|husked;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1 tsp|chili powder;1|lime|cut in wedges;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste","Heat a grill to medium-high.|Grill the corn 10 to 12 minutes, turning, until charred in spots.|Mix the mayonnaise and sour cream and brush onto each hot ear.|Roll the corn in the cotija cheese.|Dust with chili powder and salt, sprinkle with cilantro and serve with lime.","Mexican"],
[3054,"Mexican Rice","sides","🍚",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy long grain rice toasted golden and simmered in a light tomato broth.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 1/2 cup|rice|long grain, rinsed;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|tomato sauce;2 1/2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|frozen peas|optional","Heat the oil in a saucepan over medium heat and toast the rice 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until golden.|Add the onion and garlic and cook 2 minutes.|Stir in the tomato sauce, broth, cumin and salt and bring to a boil.|Cover, reduce to low, and cook 18 minutes without lifting the lid.|Rest 5 minutes off the heat, fold in the peas if using, and fluff with a fork.","Mexican"],
[3055,"Refried Beans","sides","🫘",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Creamy, garlicky pinto beans mashed in a hot skillet, the classic side for tacos and enchiladas.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 can|pinto beans|15 oz, with their liquid;1/2 tsp|cumin;1/2 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded","Heat the oil in a skillet and cook the onion 4 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cumin and cook 30 seconds.|Add the beans with their liquid and the broth.|Mash with a potato masher while simmering 10 to 12 minutes until thick and creamy.|Season with salt and top with cheese.","Mexican"],
[3056,"Guacamole","sides","🥑",10,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Chunky ripe avocado mashed with onion, cilantro, jalapeno and lime.","3|avocado|ripe;1/4 cup|red onion|finely diced;1|jalapeno|seeded and minced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|lime juice;1/2 tsp|salt;1|tomatoes|seeded and diced","Halve and pit the avocados and scoop into a bowl.|Mash roughly with a fork, leaving some chunks.|Fold in the onion, jalapeno, cilantro, lime juice and salt.|Stir in the diced tomato.|Taste, adjust the salt and lime, and serve right away with tortilla chips.","Mexican"],
[3057,"Pico de Gallo","sides","🍅",10,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fresh chopped tomato, onion, jalapeno and cilantro with lime, the brightest salsa on the table.","4|tomatoes|roma, diced;1/2|onion|finely diced;1|jalapeno|seeded and minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|lime juice;1/2 tsp|salt","Dice the tomatoes and drain off excess juice in a sieve for 5 minutes.|Combine the tomatoes with the onion, jalapeno and cilantro.|Stir in the lime juice and salt.|Rest 10 minutes so the flavors blend, then serve.","Mexican"],
[3058,"Chile con Queso","sides","🧀",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Smooth, melty Tex-Mex cheese dip with green chiles and tomato, made for tortilla chips.","2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes with green chiles|10 oz, drained;1/2 cup|milk;8 oz|american cheese|cubed;4 oz|cream cheese|cubed;1 tsp|cumin;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;|tortilla chips|for serving","Melt the butter in a saucepan and cook the onion for 4 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cumin and cook 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes with green chiles and the milk and warm over low heat.|Stir in the american cheese and cream cheese a handful at a time until smooth.|Stir in the cilantro and serve warm with chips.","Tex-Mex"],
[3059,"Tres Leches Cake","treats","🍰",120,"Medium",9,12,"Airy sponge cake soaked in three milks and topped with whipped cream.","1 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;5|eggs|separated;1 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 can|evaporated milk|12 oz;1 can|sweetened condensed milk|14 oz;1/2 cup|heavy cream;2 cup|heavy cream|whipped, for topping;2 tbsp|powdered sugar;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x13 inch pan.|Beat the yolks with 3/4 cup sugar until pale, then mix in the milk and vanilla and fold in the flour and baking powder.|Whip the whites with the remaining sugar to stiff peaks and fold into the batter.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes until golden, then cool completely.|Whisk the evaporated milk, condensed milk and 1/2 cup cream and pierce the cake all over with a fork.|Pour the milk mixture slowly over the cake and chill at least 4 hours.|Whip the 2 cups cream with the powdered sugar, spread over the cake and dust with cinnamon.","Mexican"],
[3060,"Enchiladas Suizas","comfort","🌯",50,"Medium",9,6,"Chicken enchiladas smothered in creamy tomatillo sauce and melted cheese.","1 lb|tomatillos|husked;2|poblano peppers|roasted, seeded;1/2|onion;3 clove|garlic;1/2 cup|cilantro;1 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|chicken broth;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;12|corn tortillas;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;|salt|to taste","Simmer the tomatillos in water for 8 minutes until soft and drain.|Blend them with the poblanos, onion, garlic, cilantro, cream, broth and salt until smooth.|Warm the tortillas briefly in the oil so they stay pliable.|Fill each tortilla with chicken and a little cheese, roll, and place seam side down in a baking dish.|Pour the sauce over and top with the remaining cheese.|Bake at 375°F for 20 minutes until bubbling and golden.","Mexican"],
[3061,"Chicken Fajitas","quick","🌮",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Sizzling marinated chicken with peppers and onions, wrapped in warm flour tortillas.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|sliced in strips;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|salt;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;8|flour tortillas|warmed;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|sliced","Toss the chicken with 1 tbsp oil, lime juice, chili powder, cumin, paprika, garlic powder and salt and marinate 15 minutes.|Heat a large cast iron skillet over high heat with 1 tbsp oil.|Cook the chicken 5 to 6 minutes until browned and 165°F inside, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and cook the peppers and onion 5 minutes until charred at the edges.|Return the chicken to the pan and toss.|Serve in warm tortillas with sour cream and avocado.","Tex-Mex"],
[3062,"Beef Burrito Bowl","quick","🥗",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seasoned ground beef over rice with black beans, corn, salsa and all the toppings.","1 lb|ground beef;2 tbsp|taco seasoning;1/4 cup|water;2 cup|rice|cooked;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn|thawed;1 cup|salsa;1|avocado|diced;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/4 cup|sour cream;1|lime|cut in wedges","Brown the beef in a skillet over medium-high heat for 6 to 7 minutes and drain the fat.|Stir in the taco seasoning and water and simmer 3 minutes until thick.|Warm the black beans and corn separately in a small pan.|Divide the rice among bowls.|Top with beef, beans, corn, salsa, avocado, lettuce, cheese and sour cream.|Serve with lime wedges.","Tex-Mex"],
[3063,"Sopes","lunch","🫓",45,"Medium",8,6,"Thick masa cups with a pinched rim, crisped and topped with beans, meat, lettuce and crumbly cheese.","2 cup|masa harina;1 1/2 cup|warm water;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1 cup|refried beans;1 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|salsa;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1/4 cup|sour cream","Mix the masa harina, warm water and salt into a soft dough and rest 10 minutes.|Form 12 balls and press each into a 3 inch disc about 1/4 inch thick.|Cook on a dry hot skillet 2 minutes per side until lightly set.|Pinch a raised rim around each disc while still warm.|Fry the sopes in the oil 1 to 2 minutes per side until crisp and golden.|Spread with beans, then top with chicken, lettuce, salsa, cotija and sour cream.","Mexican"],
[3064,"Flautas","lunch","🌯",40,"Easy",8,4,"Tightly rolled corn tortillas stuffed with chicken and fried until shatteringly crisp.","2 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;1/2 cup|salsa;1 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;12|corn tortillas;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|diced","Mix the chicken with the salsa and cheese.|Warm the tortillas wrapped in a damp towel in the microwave for 30 seconds so they bend without cracking.|Spoon filling along one edge, roll tightly, and secure with a toothpick.|Heat the oil in a skillet to 350°F.|Fry the flautas seam side down 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels and serve over lettuce with sour cream and avocado.","Mexican"],
[3065,"Menudo","soup","🍲",240,"Medium",9.5,8,"Traditional red chile tripe and hominy soup, long simmered and eaten with oregano, onion and lime.","2 lb|beef tripe|cleaned and cut in pieces;1 lb|beef stew meat|cut in chunks;1|onion|halved;1 head|garlic|halved;10 cup|water;6|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;1 can|hominy|25 oz, drained;1 tbsp|oregano;2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|onion|diced, for serving;2|lime|cut in wedges","Simmer the tripe, beef, halved onion, garlic and salt in the water for 2 1/2 to 3 hours until the tripe is tender, skimming the foam.|Soak the chiles in hot water for 15 minutes, then blend with 1 cup of broth until smooth and strain.|Stir the chile sauce and hominy into the pot.|Simmer 30 minutes more and adjust the salt.|Serve hot topped with diced onion, oregano and lime.","Mexican"],
[3066,"Huevos Rancheros","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried eggs on crisp corn tortillas smothered in warm ranchero sauce with refried beans.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2|onion|diced;1|jalapeno|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz, fire roasted;1/2 tsp|cumin;8|corn tortillas;8|eggs;1 cup|refried beans|warmed;1/2 cup|cotija cheese|crumbled;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste","Saute the onion and jalapeno in the oil for 4 minutes, then add the garlic and cumin for 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes and simmer 8 minutes, then blend partly and season with salt.|Fry the tortillas in a little oil for 30 seconds per side until crisp but flexible.|Fry the eggs sunny side up.|Spread beans on two tortillas per plate, top with eggs, spoon over the sauce and finish with cotija and cilantro.","Mexican"],
[3067,"Beef Barbacoa","prep","🥩",240,"Easy",9,8,"Chipotle and adobo braised chuck, falling-apart tender, for tacos and burrito bowls.","3 lb|chuck roast|cut in large chunks;2|chipotle in adobo|chiles plus 2 tbsp sauce;1/4 cup|apple cider vinegar;1/4 cup|lime juice;5 clove|garlic;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|cloves|ground;2|bay leaves;1 cup|beef broth;2 tsp|salt;12|corn tortillas","Blend the chipotles, adobo, vinegar, lime juice, garlic, cumin, oregano, cloves and salt into a paste.|Place the beef in a slow cooker or Dutch oven with the sauce, bay leaves and broth.|Cook on low for 8 hours in the slow cooker, or covered at 300°F for 3 1/2 hours in the oven, until very tender.|Shred the beef and moisten with the cooking juices.|Serve in warm tortillas with onion, cilantro and lime.","Mexican"],
[3068,"Chicken Mole Poblano","comfort","🍗",120,"Medium",9,6,"Chicken simmered in Mexico's famed dark chile, nut and chocolate sauce, finished with sesame seeds.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;4|dried ancho chiles|stemmed and seeded;3|dried guajillo chiles|stemmed and seeded;2|dried pasilla chiles|stemmed and seeded;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|plus more for garnish;1/4 cup|almonds;1/4 cup|raisins;1|tomatoes|roasted;1/2|onion;3 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 slice|bread|toasted;2 oz|chocolate chips|dark;4 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;|salt|to taste","Simmer the chicken in the broth with a little salt for 25 minutes until cooked, then set aside, saving the broth.|Toast the chiles in a dry pan for 30 seconds, then soak in hot water 20 minutes.|Fry the sesame, almonds, raisins, onion, garlic and bread in a little oil until browned.|Blend the chiles, fried ingredients, tomato, cinnamon and pepper with 2 cups of the broth until very smooth.|Fry the sauce in the oil in a large pot for 10 minutes, stirring, until it darkens.|Add the chocolate and 2 more cups of broth and simmer 30 minutes, seasoning with salt.|Add the chicken and simmer 10 minutes, then garnish with sesame seeds and serve with rice.","Mexican"],
[3069,"Loaded Beef Nachos","sides","🧀",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sheet pan nachos layered with seasoned beef, beans and melted cheese, finished with fresh toppings.","1 lb|ground beef;2 tbsp|taco seasoning;10 oz|tortilla chips;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;1/2 cup|pickled jalapenos|sliced;1 cup|pico de gallo;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|avocado|diced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Brown the beef in a skillet 6 minutes, drain, and stir in the taco seasoning with 1/4 cup water.|Spread the chips over a sheet pan.|Scatter the beef, beans and cheese over the chips.|Bake at 400°F for 7 to 8 minutes until the cheese melts.|Top with jalapenos, pico, sour cream, avocado and cilantro and serve immediately.","Tex-Mex"],
[3070,"Carne Guisada","comfort","🍲",120,"Easy",9,6,"Tex-Mex stewed beef in a rich cumin-spiced gravy, spooned into flour tortillas.","2 lb|beef stew meat|cut in small cubes;2 tbsp|flour;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes with green chiles|10 oz;1 tbsp|chili powder;2 tsp|cumin;2 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|salt;8|flour tortillas|warmed","Toss the beef with the flour, salt and half the cumin.|Brown the beef in the oil in batches in a Dutch oven and set aside.|Cook the onion and bell pepper 5 minutes, then add the garlic, chili powder and remaining cumin for 1 minute.|Return the beef and add the tomatoes and broth.|Cover and simmer on low for 1 1/2 hours until tender and the gravy thickens.|Serve in flour tortillas or over rice.","Tex-Mex"],
[3071,"Cuban Picadillo","quick","🍛",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"Savory-sweet ground beef with tomato, olives and raisins, served over rice.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 cup|olives|green, sliced;1/3 cup|raisins;2 tbsp|white wine|dry;2|bay leaves;|salt|to taste;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Saute the onion and bell pepper in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the beef and cook 7 to 8 minutes until browned, breaking it up.|Stir in the cumin, oregano, tomato sauce, wine and bay leaves.|Simmer 15 minutes until thick.|Stir in the olives and raisins and cook 5 minutes more, seasoning with salt.|Serve over white rice.","Cuban"],
[3072,"Lechon Asado","comfort","🐖",300,"Easy",9,10,"Cuban roast pork marinated in garlicky sour orange mojo until fork tender.","5 lb|pork shoulder|bone-in;1 head|garlic|peeled;1 cup|orange juice;1/2 cup|lime juice;2 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|salt;1/4 cup|olive oil;1|onion|sliced","Blend the garlic with the orange juice, lime juice, cumin, oregano, pepper, salt and oil to make the mojo.|Poke the pork all over with a knife and pour the mojo over it in a pan or bag.|Marinate in the refrigerator for 12 to 24 hours.|Lay the onion slices in a roasting pan, set the pork on top, and pour in the marinade.|Cover with foil and roast at 325°F for 4 hours, then uncover and roast 30 minutes more until browned and 195°F inside.|Rest 20 minutes and shred, spooning pan juices over the top.","Cuban"],
[3073,"Moros y Cristianos","sides","🍚",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Cuban black beans and white rice cooked together with garlic, cumin and green pepper.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1 1/2 cup|rice|long grain;2 can|black beans|15 oz each, with liquid;1 cup|chicken broth;2|bay leaves;1 tbsp|white vinegar;1 tsp|salt","Saute the onion and bell pepper in the oil for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin and oregano for 1 minute.|Drain the beans, saving the liquid, and add enough broth to the liquid to make 3 cups.|Add the rice and bay leaves to the pot and stir for 1 minute.|Pour in the bean liquid mixture, salt and vinegar and bring to a boil.|Cover and cook on low 18 minutes, then stir in the beans.|Cover 5 minutes more, discard the bay leaves and fluff.","Cuban"],
[3074,"Tostones","sides","🍌",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Twice-fried green plantain discs, crisp outside and starchy inside, with a garlic dip.","3|green plantains;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|coarse salt|to taste;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 tbsp|lime juice","Peel the plantains and cut into 1 inch rounds.|Fry in 325°F oil for 3 minutes per side until pale golden.|Remove and smash each piece flat to 1/3 inch with the bottom of a glass.|Fry again at 375°F for 2 minutes per side until crisp and golden.|Drain, sprinkle with salt, and serve with a quick mojo made from the garlic, olive oil and lime juice.","Cuban"],
[3075,"Maduros (Fried Sweet Plantains)","sides","🍌",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Ripe plantains fried until caramelized, soft and sweet.","3|plantains|very ripe, black skins;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;|salt|pinch","Peel the plantains and slice on the diagonal 1/2 inch thick.|Heat the oil in a skillet over medium heat.|Fry the slices 2 to 3 minutes per side until deep golden and caramelized at the edges.|Drain on paper towels and sprinkle with a pinch of salt.","Cuban"],
[3076,"Arroz con Pollo","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,6,"One-pot chicken and yellow rice with peppers, peas and a splash of beer.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;2 cup|rice|long grain;3 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|frozen peas;1/2 cup|olives|green","Season the chicken with salt and brown in the oil in a wide Dutch oven for 4 minutes per side, then set aside.|Cook the onion and bell pepper in the drippings for 5 minutes, then add the garlic, cumin, paprika and turmeric for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato sauce and rice and toast 2 minutes.|Add the broth and bring to a boil, then nestle the chicken in the rice.|Cover and cook on low for 25 minutes until the rice is tender.|Scatter over the peas and olives, cover 5 minutes, and serve.","Cuban"],
[3077,"Vaca Frita","comfort","🥩",150,"Medium",9,6,"Cuban shredded flank steak seared crisp and tossed with lime, garlic and onions.","2 lb|flank steak;1|onion|half quartered, half sliced;6 clove|garlic;2|bay leaves;4 cup|water;1/3 cup|lime juice;2 tbsp|olive oil;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|oregano;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Simmer the steak with the quartered onion, 2 cloves garlic, bay leaves and 1 tsp salt in the water for 1 1/2 hours until tender.|Cool slightly and shred the beef finely.|Mince the remaining garlic and toss the beef with the lime juice, garlic, cumin, oregano, pepper and remaining salt and marinate 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat and sear the beef in batches 4 to 5 minutes, undisturbed, until crisp and browned.|Cook the sliced onion in the same pan until golden, then toss with the beef and serve with rice and beans.","Cuban"],
[3078,"Coxinha","treats","🍗",90,"Medium",9,24,"Teardrop-shaped Brazilian snacks of creamy shredded chicken in dough, breaded and fried.","2 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 cup|rotisserie chicken|finely shredded;1/2|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4 oz|cream cheese;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|salt|to taste","Cook the onion and garlic in 1 tbsp oil for 4 minutes, then mix in the chicken, cream cheese, parsley and salt for the filling and chill.|Bring the broth and butter to a boil, add all the flour at once, and stir over low heat 3 to 4 minutes until a smooth dough pulls from the pan.|Knead the dough on a counter until smooth and cool enough to handle.|Take a golf ball of dough, flatten in your palm, add a spoonful of filling, and shape into a teardrop sealing the edges.|Dip in the beaten eggs and roll in breadcrumbs.|Fry in 350°F oil for 3 to 4 minutes per batch until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm.","Brazilian"],
[3079,"Farofa","sides","🍚",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Toasted cassava flour with bacon and onion, sprinkled over rice, beans and grilled meats.","4 slice|bacon|diced;2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|cassava flour|farinha de mandioca, toasted;2|eggs|beaten;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste","Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium heat for 6 minutes until crisp and remove with a slotted spoon.|Add the butter, onion and garlic to the bacon fat and cook 4 minutes.|Push the onion aside, pour in the eggs and scramble until set.|Add the cassava flour a little at a time, stirring 3 to 4 minutes until golden and toasty.|Fold in the bacon and parsley and season with salt.","Brazilian"],
[3080,"Lomo Saltado","quick","🥩",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"Peruvian beef stir-fry with onion, tomato and fries in a soy and vinegar sauce, served with rice.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|cut in strips;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|red onion|cut in thick wedges;2|tomatoes|cut in wedges;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|minced;2 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1|jalapeno|sliced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 lb|potatoes|cut in fries and fried;2 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste","Toss the steak with 1 tbsp soy sauce, salt and pepper.|Heat a wok or large skillet until smoking and sear the beef in batches in the oil for 1 to 2 minutes until browned.|Add the onion, garlic, ginger and jalapeno and stir-fry 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, remaining soy sauce and the vinegar and toss 1 minute.|Return the beef, fold in the cilantro and the hot fried potatoes.|Serve immediately over white rice.","Peruvian"],
[3081,"Pollo a la Brasa","comfort","🍗",120,"Easy",9,4,"Peruvian rotisserie-style chicken marinated in garlic, cumin and soy, roasted until crisp and golden.","1|whole chicken|about 4 lb;6 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar","Mix the garlic, soy sauce, lime juice, oil, cumin, paprika, oregano, pepper, salt and vinegar into a paste.|Rub the paste all over and under the skin of the chicken.|Marinate in the refrigerator at least 4 hours or overnight.|Roast on a rack at 450°F for 20 minutes, then reduce to 375°F.|Roast another 50 to 60 minutes until the thigh reaches 165°F and the skin is crisp.|Rest 10 minutes, carve, and serve with fries and a green sauce.","Peruvian"],
[3082,"Peruvian Ceviche","light","🐟",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Raw white fish cured in sharp lime juice with red onion, chile and cilantro, served cold.","1 1/2 lb|cod|very fresh, cut in 1/2 inch cubes;3/4 cup|lime juice|fresh;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1|jalapeno|minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|salt;1|sweet potatoes|boiled and sliced;1 cup|corn|boiled, or cooked kernels","Rinse the sliced onion in cold water for 5 minutes and drain.|Combine the fish with the salt, garlic and jalapeno in a bowl.|Pour in the lime juice and stir.|Refrigerate for 10 to 15 minutes until the fish turns opaque on the outside.|Fold in the onion and cilantro and serve right away with sweet potato and corn.","Peruvian"],
[3083,"Aji de Gallina","comfort","🍛",60,"Medium",9,6,"Shredded chicken in a creamy yellow chile and walnut sauce over rice and potatoes.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast;4 cup|chicken broth;4 slice|bread|crusts removed;1 cup|milk;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|finely diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|aji amarillo paste;1/2 cup|walnuts;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;4|potatoes|boiled and sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked;4|eggs|hard boiled;1/2 cup|olives|black;|salt|to taste","Poach the chicken in the broth for 20 minutes until cooked, then shred and reserve the broth.|Soak the bread in the milk, then blend with the walnuts and 1 cup of the broth until smooth.|Cook the onion in the oil for 6 minutes, then add the garlic and aji amarillo paste for 3 minutes.|Stir in the blended mixture and another cup of broth and simmer 10 minutes.|Add the shredded chicken and parmesan and simmer until thick and creamy, seasoning with salt.|Serve over potato slices with rice, halved eggs and olives.","Peruvian"],
[3084,"Papa a la Huancaina","sides","🥔",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Boiled potatoes in a creamy, spicy yellow cheese sauce, a Peruvian starter.","2 lb|potatoes|boiled and sliced;1/2 cup|aji amarillo paste;8 oz|feta;1/2 cup|evaporated milk;4|crackers|saltines;1 clove|garlic;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|eggs|hard boiled;1/2 cup|olives|black;|lettuce|leaves, for serving","Blend the aji amarillo, feta, evaporated milk, crackers, garlic and oil until smooth and creamy.|Taste and adjust with a little salt or milk to reach a pourable thickness.|Line a platter with lettuce leaves.|Arrange the sliced potatoes on top.|Spoon the sauce generously over the potatoes and garnish with halved eggs and olives.","Peruvian"],
[3085,"Sesame Chicken","comfort","🍗",40,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy fried chicken pieces tossed in a glossy sweet-savory sauce and finished with toasted sesame seeds.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch pieces;1|eggs|beaten;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/4 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|honey;3 tbsp|brown sugar;2 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp water;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted;2|green onion|sliced","Toss the chicken with the egg and salt, then dredge in the cornstarch and flour mixed together, pressing to coat.|Heat the oil in a large skillet to 350°F.|Fry the chicken in batches for 4 to 5 minutes until golden and cooked through, then drain on a rack.|In a saucepan combine soy sauce, honey, brown sugar, vinegar, sesame oil, broth, garlic and ginger and simmer 3 minutes.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and simmer 1 to 2 minutes until the sauce is thick and glossy.|Toss the chicken in the sauce, sprinkle with sesame seeds and green onion, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3086,"Honey Walnut Shrimp","comfort","🍤",35,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy battered shrimp in a creamy honey-mayo sauce, topped with candied walnuts.","1 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined, large;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1|eggs|beaten;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|sweetened condensed milk|optional;1 cup|walnuts|halves;1/4 cup|sugar;2 cup|water|for boiling walnuts;|salt|to taste;1 cup|broccoli|steamed florets, for serving","Boil the walnuts in water for 5 minutes, drain well, and toss with the sugar until coated.|Fry the sugared walnuts in 350°F oil for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden, then spread on parchment to cool.|Whisk the mayonnaise, honey, lemon juice and condensed milk in a large bowl.|Toss the shrimp with a pinch of salt and the egg, then coat well in cornstarch.|Fry the shrimp in batches for 2 to 3 minutes until crisp and golden, and drain.|Toss the hot shrimp in the sauce, top with the walnuts, and serve with steamed broccoli and rice.","Chinese"],
[3087,"Mongolian Beef","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Tender sliced flank steak seared crisp and coated in a sweet, garlicky soy-brown sugar sauce with green onions.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 tbsp|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|water;3/4 cup|brown sugar;1 tbsp|hoisin sauce;6|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces","Toss the steak with the cornstarch until evenly coated.|Heat the oil in a large skillet or wok over medium-high heat and sear the beef in batches for 1 to 2 minutes until browned, then remove.|Pour off all but 1 tablespoon of oil and cook the garlic and ginger for 30 seconds.|Add the soy sauce, water, brown sugar and hoisin and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until slightly thickened.|Return the beef to the pan with the green onions and toss for 1 minute.|Serve over steamed rice.","Chinese"],
[3088,"Pepper Steak","quick","🫑",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Tender strips of steak stir-fried with bell peppers and onion in a savory soy-ginger sauce.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|cornstarch;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|bell pepper|sliced in strips;1|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|beef broth;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the steak with 2 tablespoons soy sauce and 1 tablespoon cornstarch and let sit 10 minutes.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat and sear the steak 2 minutes, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the peppers and onion for 3 minutes until crisp-tender.|Add the garlic and ginger and cook 30 seconds.|Stir in the broth, oyster sauce, sugar and black pepper, return the beef, and bring to a simmer.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook 1 minute until glossy, then serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3089,"Crab Rangoon","sides","🥟",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crispy fried wonton wrappers filled with a creamy, lightly sweet crab and cream cheese mixture.","8 oz|cream cheese|softened;6 oz|crab meat|canned or imitation, drained;2|green onion|minced;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|soy sauce;24|wonton wrappers;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Mix the cream cheese, crab, green onion, garlic, worcestershire and soy sauce until combined.|Place about 2 teaspoons of filling in the center of each wrapper.|Wet the edges with water, then fold corners up to the center and pinch to seal into a four-pointed star or fold into a triangle.|Heat 1 inch of oil in a skillet to 350°F.|Fry in batches for 1 to 2 minutes per side until golden, then drain on paper towels.|Serve warm with sweet chili sauce.","Chinese"],
[3090,"Pork Fried Rice","quick","🍚",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Day-old rice stir-fried with diced pork, scrambled egg, peas and carrots.","4 cup|rice|cooked and chilled, day-old;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|diced small;2 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|eggs|beaten;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1/2 cup|carrots|diced small;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;3|green onion|sliced;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the pork with 1 tablespoon soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and cook the pork 3 to 4 minutes until browned and cooked through, then remove.|Scramble the eggs in the same wok for 30 seconds, break into pieces, and remove.|Heat the remaining oil and stir-fry the onion, carrots and peas for 2 minutes, adding the garlic for the last 30 seconds.|Add the rice, breaking up clumps, and stir-fry 3 minutes until hot and slightly toasted.|Add the remaining soy sauce, oyster sauce, sesame oil and pepper, return the pork and egg, and toss with the green onions.","Chinese"],
[3091,"Chicken Chow Mein","quick","🍜",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried noodles with chicken, cabbage, carrots and celery in a savory soy-oyster sauce.","8 oz|lo mein noodles;1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 cup|cabbage|shredded;1|carrots|julienned;2 stalk|celery|sliced thin;1|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|sesame oil;1 cup|bean sprouts;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the noodles according to the package, drain, rinse and toss with a little oil.|Toss the chicken with the cornstarch and a splash of soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and cook the chicken 3 to 4 minutes until done, then remove.|Add 1 tablespoon oil and stir-fry the onion, celery, carrot and cabbage for 3 minutes.|Add the garlic, noodles, remaining soy sauce, oyster sauce, sugar and pepper and toss for 2 to 3 minutes.|Return the chicken, add the bean sprouts and sesame oil, and toss 1 minute before serving.","Chinese"],
[3092,"Dan Dan Noodles","quick","🍜",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Sichuan noodles topped with spicy minced pork in a sesame, chili oil and soy sauce.","12 oz|lo mein noodles|or fresh wheat noodles;1/2 lb|ground pork;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;2 tbsp|sesame paste|or tahini or peanut butter;3 tbsp|chili oil;1 tsp|sichuan peppercorns|toasted and ground;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 cup|spinach|or bok choy, blanched;3|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|peanuts|crushed","Brown the pork in the oil over medium-high heat for 5 minutes, breaking it up, then add 1 tablespoon soy sauce and cook 1 minute more.|Whisk the sesame paste, remaining soy sauce, vinegar, chili oil, ground peppercorns, garlic, sugar and broth to make the sauce.|Cook the noodles per package directions and blanch the greens in the same water for 30 seconds.|Divide the sauce among four bowls.|Top with the noodles, greens and pork, then sprinkle with green onion and peanuts.|Toss everything together before eating.","Chinese"],
[3093,"Char Siu","comfort","🍖",240,"Medium",9,6,"Cantonese barbecued pork with a sticky, sweet-savory red glaze, roasted until caramelized at the edges.","2 lb|pork shoulder|cut into 2 inch strips;1/4 cup|hoisin sauce;1/4 cup|honey;3 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|brown sugar;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|five spice powder;|red food coloring|optional;2 tbsp|honey|for basting","Whisk the hoisin, honey, soy sauce, brown sugar, oyster sauce, vinegar, garlic and five spice.|Reserve 1/4 cup of marinade, then coat the pork in the rest and refrigerate 4 hours or overnight.|Heat the oven to 425°F and set the pork on a rack over a foil-lined pan with a little water in the pan.|Roast 20 minutes, then brush with the reserved marinade and flip.|Roast another 20 to 25 minutes, brushing again, until the edges caramelize and the pork reaches 160°F.|Brush with honey, rest 10 minutes, and slice across the grain.","Chinese"],
[3094,"Cashew Chicken","quick","🥜",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried chicken and crisp vegetables in a savory brown sauce with roasted cashews.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch pieces;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1/2 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|hoisin sauce;1 tsp|rice vinegar;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;3/4 cup|cashews|roasted;2|green onion|sliced","Toss the chicken with 1 tablespoon cornstarch.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a wok over high heat and cook the chicken 4 to 5 minutes until browned and cooked through, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the pepper, celery and mushrooms for 3 minutes.|Add the garlic and ginger for 30 seconds.|Stir in the broth, soy sauce, oyster sauce, hoisin and vinegar, then the slurry, and simmer 1 minute.|Return the chicken, add the cashews and green onion, toss, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3095,"Lemon Chicken","comfort","🍋",40,"Medium",9,4,"Crispy battered chicken with a bright, tangy lemon sauce, a Chinese-American takeout favorite.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in strips;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/4 cup|flour;1|eggs;1 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3/4 cup|chicken broth;1/3 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|cornstarch|mixed with 2 tbsp water;1|lemon|sliced thin;2|green onion|sliced","Whisk the cornstarch, flour, baking powder, salt, egg and a few tablespoons of cold water into a thin batter and coat the chicken.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet.|Fry the chicken in batches for 4 to 5 minutes until golden and crisp, then drain.|Simmer the broth, sugar, lemon juice and soy sauce for 2 minutes.|Stir in the cornstarch slurry and cook until thickened and glossy.|Pour the sauce over the chicken, top with lemon slices and green onion, and serve with rice.","Chinese"],
[3096,"Pork Potstickers","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Pan-fried dumplings with a juicy pork and cabbage filling, crisp on the bottom and tender on top.","1 lb|ground pork;2 cup|cabbage|finely chopped, napa preferred;3|green onion|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch;40|dumpling wrappers|round;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/2 cup|water;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping","Toss the chopped cabbage with a pinch of salt, let sit 10 minutes, and squeeze out the liquid.|Mix the pork, cabbage, green onion, ginger, garlic, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar and cornstarch until sticky.|Put a heaping teaspoon of filling in each wrapper, wet the edge, and fold and pleat to seal.|Heat the oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-high heat and arrange the dumplings flat side down.|Fry 2 minutes until golden, then add the water, cover, and steam 6 to 7 minutes.|Uncover and cook until the water evaporates and the bottoms re-crisp, then serve with the soy and vinegar dip.","Chinese"],
[3097,"Scallion Pancakes","sides","🥞",60,"Medium",7.5,4,"Flaky, chewy, flatbread-style pancakes layered with sesame oil and green onions and pan-fried until crisp.","2 cup|flour;3/4 cup|water|boiling hot;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|sesame oil;1 cup|green onion|finely sliced;1/4 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping","Mix the flour and salt, stir in the hot water until shaggy, then knead 5 minutes until smooth and let rest covered for 30 minutes.|Divide the dough into 4 pieces and roll each into a thin 8 inch circle.|Brush with sesame oil, sprinkle with salt and green onions, and roll into a tight log.|Coil the log into a spiral, tuck the end under, and flatten with a rolling pin to about 1/4 inch.|Fry in a skillet with a few tablespoons of oil over medium heat 3 minutes per side until golden and crisp.|Cut into wedges and serve with soy-vinegar dip.","Chinese"],
[3098,"Hunan Beef","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Spicy, savory stir-fried beef and broccoli with dried chilies and garlic in a Hunan-style sauce.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak|sliced thin against the grain;1 tbsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|broccoli|small florets;1|bell pepper|sliced;5|dried red chilies|whole;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|hoisin sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water","Toss the steak with 1 tablespoon cornstarch and a splash of soy sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and sear the beef 2 minutes, then remove.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the broccoli and pepper for 3 minutes, adding a splash of water to steam.|Add the chilies, garlic and ginger and cook 30 seconds.|Stir in the soy sauce, hoisin, vinegar, sugar and broth and bring to a simmer.|Return the beef, stir in the slurry, cook 1 minute until glossy, and serve over rice.","Chinese"],
[3099,"Moo Shu Pork","comfort","🌯",35,"Medium",9,4,"Stir-fried pork, egg and shredded cabbage in hoisin sauce, wrapped in warm thin pancakes.","1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|cornstarch;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3|eggs|beaten;3 cup|cabbage|shredded;1|carrots|julienned;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;4|green onion|cut in 2 inch strips;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|grated;2 tbsp|hoisin sauce|plus more for spreading;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;8|flour tortillas|small, or mandarin pancakes","Marinate the pork in 1 tablespoon soy sauce and the cornstarch for 10 minutes.|Scramble the eggs in 1 tablespoon oil in a wok until just set, then remove.|Stir-fry the pork in 1 tablespoon oil over high heat for 3 minutes, then remove.|Add the last tablespoon of oil and stir-fry the cabbage, carrot, mushrooms, garlic and ginger for 3 to 4 minutes.|Return the pork and eggs, add the hoisin, soy sauce, sesame oil and green onions, and toss 1 minute.|Warm the tortillas, spread each with hoisin, fill with the mixture, and roll up.","Chinese"],
[3100,"Beef Chow Fun","quick","🍜",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Wide rice noodles wok-fried with tender beef, bean sprouts and green onions in a savory soy sauce.","1 lb|rice noodles|fresh wide, or dried and soaked;3/4 lb|flank steak|sliced thin;1 tbsp|cornstarch;4 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|dark soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|bean sprouts;4|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;1/2|onion|sliced;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the steak with the cornstarch and 1 tablespoon soy sauce and let sit 10 minutes.|Mix the remaining soy sauce, dark soy, oyster sauce and sugar.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a wok over very high heat and sear the beef 1 to 2 minutes, then remove.|Add 2 more tablespoons oil, stir-fry the onion and garlic 30 seconds, then add the noodles and gently toss for 2 minutes.|Pour in the sauce and toss until the noodles are evenly colored.|Return the beef and add the sprouts, green onion and pepper, toss 1 minute, and serve immediately.","Chinese"],
[3101,"Salt and Pepper Shrimp","light","🦐",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Lightly crisp shrimp wok-tossed with garlic, chilies and a peppery salt seasoning.","1 lb|shrimp|large, shell-on or peeled;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper|freshly ground;1/2 tsp|five spice powder;4 clove|garlic|minced;2|jalapeno|sliced thin;3|green onion|sliced","Pat the shrimp very dry and toss with the cornstarch to coat.|Heat the oil in a wok to 375°F and fry the shrimp in batches for 1 to 2 minutes until crisp and pink, then drain.|Pour off all but 1 tablespoon oil from the wok.|Stir-fry the garlic, jalapeno and green onions over high heat for 30 to 60 seconds until fragrant.|Return the shrimp and sprinkle with the salt, pepper and five spice.|Toss for 30 seconds and serve hot.","Chinese"],
[3102,"Twice-Cooked Pork","comfort","🥓",60,"Medium",9,4,"Sichuan classic of simmered pork belly sliced thin and stir-fried with leeks and spicy bean paste.","1 lb|pork belly|skin off;2 slice|ginger;3|green onion|whites cut in pieces;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|doubanjiang|spicy bean paste;1 tbsp|fermented black beans|optional;3|leeks|or green onion, sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced;3 clove|garlic|sliced;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|rice vinegar","Simmer the pork belly with the ginger and green onion whites in water to cover for 30 minutes until just cooked through.|Remove, cool for 15 minutes, then slice thinly.|Heat the oil in a wok over medium-high heat and fry the pork slices 3 to 4 minutes until the edges curl and crisp, then push aside.|Add the doubanjiang and black beans and fry 30 seconds until the oil turns red.|Add the garlic, leeks and pepper and stir-fry 2 to 3 minutes.|Add the soy sauce, sugar and vinegar, toss everything together, and serve with rice.","Chinese"],
[3103,"Beef Bulgogi","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thinly sliced beef marinated in a sweet soy, pear and garlic sauce, then seared until caramelized.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|sliced very thin;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|sesame oil;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1/2|apple|grated, or Asian pear;1/2|onion|sliced thin;3|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, garlic, ginger, grated apple and pepper in a bowl.|Add the beef, onion and half the green onions and marinate at least 20 minutes, or up to overnight.|Heat the oil in a large skillet or cast iron over high heat.|Cook the beef in two batches for 2 to 3 minutes each until browned and caramelized at the edges.|Top with the remaining green onion and sesame seeds.|Serve with rice and lettuce leaves for wrapping.","Korean"],
[3104,"Bibimbap","comfort","🍚",50,"Medium",9,4,"Korean rice bowl topped with seasoned vegetables, marinated beef, a fried egg and spicy gochujang sauce.","4 cup|rice|cooked;1/2 lb|ground beef|or sliced beef;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|spinach;1|carrots|julienned;1|zucchini|julienned;1 cup|bean sprouts;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;4|eggs;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|sesame oil|for sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Brown the beef with 1 tablespoon soy sauce, the sugar and half the garlic for 4 to 5 minutes and set aside.|Blanch the spinach 30 seconds, squeeze dry, and season with a little sesame oil, salt and garlic.|Blanch the bean sprouts 2 minutes, drain, and season with sesame oil and salt.|Saute the carrot, zucchini and mushrooms separately in a little oil for 2 to 3 minutes each, seasoning with salt.|Mix the gochujang, sesame oil, vinegar and 1 teaspoon sugar for the sauce.|Fry the eggs sunny side up, then arrange the rice, vegetables and beef in bowls, top with an egg, sesame seeds and sauce, and mix before eating.","Korean"],
[3105,"Kimchi Jjigae","soup","🍲",40,"Easy",9.5,4,"Hearty Korean stew of aged kimchi, pork and tofu simmered in a spicy, tangy broth.","2 cup|kimchi|aged, chopped, plus 1/2 cup juice;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin, or pork belly;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|gochugaru|Korean chili flakes;1 tbsp|gochujang;4 cup|water|or anchovy stock;14 oz|tofu|firm, sliced;3|green onion|sliced;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|soy sauce","Heat the sesame oil in a pot over medium-high heat and cook the pork for 3 to 4 minutes until lightly browned.|Add the kimchi, onion and garlic and stir-fry 4 to 5 minutes.|Stir in the gochugaru, gochujang, sugar and soy sauce.|Add the kimchi juice and water and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a simmer, cover, and cook 20 minutes.|Add the tofu and green onion and simmer 5 more minutes, then serve with rice.","Korean"],
[3106,"Japchae","comfort","🍜",45,"Medium",9,6,"Chewy glass noodles stir-fried with beef and colorful vegetables in a sweet sesame-soy sauce.","8 oz|sweet potato starch noodles|dangmyeon;1/2 lb|sirloin steak|sliced thin;4 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|sesame oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|carrots|julienned;1|onion|sliced;5 oz|spinach;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;|black pepper|to taste","Marinate the beef in 1 tablespoon soy sauce, 1 teaspoon sugar, 1 teaspoon sesame oil and half the garlic.|Boil the noodles 6 to 7 minutes until chewy, drain, rinse, cut into shorter lengths, and toss with 1 tablespoon sesame oil.|Blanch the spinach for 30 seconds, squeeze dry, and season with a little soy sauce and sesame oil.|Stir-fry the onion, carrot, pepper and mushrooms separately in a little oil for 2 to 3 minutes each.|Cook the beef 2 to 3 minutes.|Toss everything with the remaining soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, garlic, pepper and sesame seeds, and serve warm or at room temperature.","Korean"],
[3107,"Tteokbokki","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,3,"Chewy rice cakes simmered in a sweet, spicy gochujang sauce with fish cakes and green onion.","1 lb|rice cakes|cylinder-shaped, soaked if hard;3 cup|water|or anchovy stock;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|gochugaru;1 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;2 clove|garlic|minced;4 oz|fish cakes|sliced;3|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;2|eggs|hard-boiled;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Soak the rice cakes in warm water for 10 minutes if they are hard or refrigerated.|Bring the water to a boil in a wide pan and stir in the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar and garlic.|Add the rice cakes and simmer over medium heat for 8 to 10 minutes, stirring often.|Add the fish cakes and cook 3 to 4 minutes more until the sauce thickens and clings.|Add the green onion and eggs and cook 1 minute.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve hot.","Korean"],
[3108,"Korean Fried Chicken","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,4,"Extra-crunchy double-fried chicken wings glazed in a sticky, sweet and spicy gochujang sauce.","2 lb|chicken wings|split, or drumettes;1/2 cup|cornstarch;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;3 tbsp|gochujang;3 tbsp|honey;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Pat the wings very dry and toss with the cornstarch, flour, salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Heat 2 inches of oil to 325°F and fry the wings in batches 8 to 10 minutes until cooked, then drain.|Simmer the gochujang, honey, soy sauce, brown sugar, vinegar, garlic and sesame oil in a pan for 3 minutes until syrupy.|Raise the oil to 375°F and fry the wings again for 3 to 4 minutes until deeply crisp.|Toss the hot wings in the sauce until coated.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve right away.","Korean"],
[3109,"Galbi","comfort","🍖",50,"Medium",9,4,"Grilled Korean short ribs marinated in a sweet soy, pear and garlic sauce until tender and charred.","3 lb|beef short ribs|flanken cut, 1/2 inch thick;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|brown sugar;2 tbsp|sesame oil;1/2|apple|grated, or Asian pear;1/2|onion|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;2 tbsp|rice wine|mirin or similar;3|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the ribs in cold water for 30 minutes to draw out excess blood, then drain and pat dry.|Mix the soy sauce, brown sugar, sesame oil, apple, onion, garlic, ginger, rice wine and pepper.|Marinate the ribs in the mixture in the refrigerator at least 4 hours or overnight.|Heat a grill or cast-iron pan over high heat.|Grill the ribs 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and caramelized.|Sprinkle with green onion and sesame seeds, and serve with rice and lettuce.","Korean"],
[3110,"Sundubu Jjigae","soup","🍲",30,"Easy",9.5,2,"Bubbling Korean soft tofu stew with a spicy broth, clams or pork, and a cracked egg on top.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 lb|ground pork|or sliced pork;1 tbsp|gochugaru;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|water|or anchovy stock;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|fish sauce;1/2|onion|sliced;12 oz|soft tofu|sundubu;1/2 lb|clams|optional, scrubbed;2|green onion|sliced;1|eggs;1 tsp|sesame oil","Heat the oil in a small pot or stone bowl over medium heat and cook the pork 2 to 3 minutes.|Add the gochugaru and garlic and stir 30 seconds so the oil turns red.|Pour in the water, soy sauce and fish sauce, add the onion, and bring to a boil.|Add the clams if using and simmer until they open, about 4 minutes.|Spoon in the tofu in large chunks and simmer 4 to 5 minutes.|Crack the egg on top, add green onion and sesame oil, and serve boiling hot with rice.","Korean"],
[3111,"Kimchi Fried Rice","quick","🍳",20,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Day-old rice fried with tangy kimchi and gochujang, topped with a runny fried egg.","3 cup|rice|cooked and cold;1 cup|kimchi|chopped;2 tbsp|kimchi juice;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 lb|bacon|chopped, or spam;2|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|gochujang;1 tsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;2|eggs;1 tsp|sesame seeds;1 tsp|sugar","Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 3 to 4 minutes until crisp.|Add the kimchi and sugar and stir-fry 3 minutes.|Add the gochujang and cook 30 seconds.|Add the rice and kimchi juice, breaking up clumps, and fry 4 to 5 minutes until hot and slightly crisp.|Stir in the soy sauce, sesame oil and green onion.|Fry the eggs sunny side up, place on top, and sprinkle with sesame seeds.","Korean"],
[3112,"Dakgalbi","comfort","🌶️",45,"Easy",9,4,"Spicy stir-fried chicken with cabbage, sweet potato and rice cakes in a sweet gochujang sauce.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size pieces;3 tbsp|gochujang;2 tbsp|gochugaru;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|cabbage|chopped;1|sweet potatoes|sliced in half moons;1|onion|sliced;8 oz|rice cakes|optional;4|perilla leaves|optional;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar, honey, garlic, ginger, sesame oil and pepper.|Coat the chicken in the sauce and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large wide skillet over medium heat and add the sweet potato with a splash of water, covered, for 5 minutes.|Add the chicken, onion and cabbage and cook, stirring, 10 minutes.|Add the rice cakes and cook another 8 to 10 minutes until the chicken is cooked through and the sauce clings.|Top with perilla leaves and serve with rice.","Korean"],
[3113,"Pajeon","sides","🥞",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crispy Korean green onion pancakes with a chewy center, served with a tangy soy dipping sauce.","1 cup|flour;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1 1/4 cup|water|ice cold;1|eggs;1/2 tsp|salt;1 bunch|green onion|cut in 3 inch lengths;1/2 cup|shrimp|optional, chopped;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|soy sauce|for dipping;1 tbsp|rice vinegar|for dipping;1 tsp|gochugaru|for dipping;1 tsp|sesame seeds|for dipping","Whisk the flour, cornstarch, salt, egg and cold water into a thin batter.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat.|Spread half the green onions in the pan in a single layer, scatter the shrimp if using, and pour half the batter on top.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes until the bottom is golden and crisp, then flip and cook 3 minutes more, pressing down.|Repeat with remaining ingredients.|Mix the soy sauce, vinegar, gochugaru and sesame seeds and serve alongside.","Korean"],
[3114,"Jeyuk Bokkeum (Spicy Pork Stir-Fry)","quick","🥓",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin pork slices stir-fried in a fiery sweet gochujang sauce with onion and green onion.","1 1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;3 tbsp|gochujang;1 tbsp|gochugaru;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|sesame oil;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;1|onion|sliced;1|jalapeno|sliced;3|green onion|cut in 2 inch pieces;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Mix the gochujang, gochugaru, soy sauce, sugar, honey, sesame oil, garlic and ginger.|Coat the pork in the sauce and marinate for at least 20 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat.|Add the pork and onion and stir-fry 6 to 8 minutes until the pork is cooked and the edges caramelize.|Add the jalapeno and green onion and cook 1 more minute.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve with rice and lettuce.","Korean"],
[3115,"Kimbap","lunch","🍙",60,"Medium",8,4,"Korean seaweed rice rolls filled with seasoned vegetables, egg, pickled radish and beef or ham.","3 cup|rice|cooked short-grain, warm;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sesame seeds;4|nori sheets|roasted;4|eggs|beaten;1|carrots|julienned;1|cucumber|cut in long strips;4|pickled radish strips|danmuji;4 oz|spinach|blanched and squeezed;1/4 lb|ground beef|cooked with 1 tbsp soy sauce and 1 tsp sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil","Season the warm rice with sesame oil, salt and sesame seeds.|Beat the eggs with a pinch of salt, cook as a thin omelet in a little oil, and cut into long strips.|Saute the carrot for 1 to 2 minutes with a pinch of salt.|Lay a nori sheet shiny side down on a bamboo mat and spread a thin layer of rice, leaving the top inch bare.|Arrange the egg, carrot, cucumber, radish, spinach and beef in a line across the lower third.|Roll tightly, seal with a few grains of rice, brush with sesame oil, and slice into 1 inch rounds.","Korean"],
[3116,"Gyeran-jjim (Korean Steamed Egg)","sides","🥚",15,"Very easy",7.5,2,"Fluffy, savory steamed eggs puffed up in a hot stone pot, a classic Korean side.","4|eggs;3/4 cup|water|or anchovy stock;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|fish sauce|or soy sauce;2|green onion|finely sliced;1 tsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Beat the eggs with the salt, fish sauce and half the green onions until smooth.|Strain the eggs through a sieve for a silky texture and stir in the water.|Pour the mixture into a small heatproof or stone pot.|Cook over medium-low heat, stirring gently, until it begins to set at the bottom.|Cover and cook on the lowest heat 8 to 10 minutes until puffed and set.|Drizzle with sesame oil and top with remaining green onion and sesame seeds.","Korean"],
[3117,"Chicken Katsu","comfort","🍗",35,"Easy",9,4,"Crispy panko-breaded chicken cutlets served with shredded cabbage and tangy-sweet katsu sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|sliced in half to make 4 cutlets;1/2 cup|flour;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|panko;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;2 cup|cabbage|finely shredded;|rice|cooked, for serving","Pound the chicken to an even 1/2 inch thickness and season with salt and pepper.|Dredge in the flour, dip in the egg, then press into the panko.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat to about 350°F.|Fry the cutlets 3 to 4 minutes per side until deep golden and cooked through to 165°F.|Whisk together the ketchup, worcestershire, soy sauce and sugar for the katsu sauce.|Slice the cutlets and serve with cabbage, rice and sauce.","Japanese"],
[3118,"Chicken Teriyaki","quick","🍗",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seared chicken thighs glazed in a glossy homemade teriyaki sauce of soy, mirin and sugar.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, skin-on;1/4 cup|soy sauce;1/4 cup|mirin;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|sake|or water;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cornstarch|mixed with 1 tbsp water;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;2|green onion|sliced","Whisk the soy sauce, mirin, sugar, sake, ginger and garlic.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken skin side down for 6 to 7 minutes until deeply golden.|Flip and cook 5 minutes more, then pour off excess fat.|Pour in the sauce and simmer 3 to 4 minutes, spooning it over the chicken.|Stir in the slurry and cook 1 minute until thick and glossy and the chicken reaches 165°F.|Slice the chicken, spoon the sauce over, and top with sesame seeds and green onion.","Japanese"],
[3119,"Tonkotsu Ramen","soup","🍜",240,"Medium",9.5,4,"Rich, milky pork bone broth ramen with tender chashu pork, soft egg and green onion.","3 lb|pork bones|neck or trotters, blanched;1 lb|pork belly|rolled and tied;1|onion|halved;1 head|garlic|halved;3 slice|ginger;4|green onion|whites and greens separated;1/4 cup|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;2 tbsp|sugar;4|eggs|soft-boiled 6 1/2 minutes;14 oz|ramen noodles|fresh;1 tbsp|sesame oil;2 tbsp|soy sauce|for tare;1 tsp|salt|for tare;|nori|for topping","Boil the pork bones 10 minutes, drain, and scrub clean to remove scum.|Return the bones to a pot with 4 quarts water, onion, garlic, ginger and green onion whites and boil hard for 3 hours, topping up water, until the broth turns milky.|Meanwhile simmer the pork belly in 1/4 cup soy sauce, mirin, sugar and 1 1/2 cups water, covered, for 1 1/2 hours, turning occasionally.|Marinate the peeled soft-boiled eggs in some of the pork braising liquid.|Strain the broth, season with the 2 tablespoons soy sauce and salt, and keep hot.|Cook the noodles per package, divide into bowls, ladle in broth, and top with sliced pork, egg, green onion and a drizzle of sesame oil.","Japanese"],
[3120,"Gyudon","quick","🍚",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"Thinly sliced beef and onion simmered in a sweet dashi-soy broth and served over rice.","3/4 lb|ribeye steak|sliced paper thin;1|onion|sliced thin;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tsp|ginger|grated;2 cup|rice|cooked, hot;2|eggs|optional, soft yolks;|pickled ginger|beni shoga, optional;1|green onion|sliced","Combine the water, soy sauce, mirin, sugar and ginger in a skillet and bring to a simmer.|Add the onion and cook 5 minutes until soft.|Add the beef in one layer and cook 2 to 3 minutes, skimming any foam.|Simmer 3 more minutes until the beef is tender and the sauce is slightly reduced.|Divide the rice into bowls and spoon beef, onion and sauce over each.|Top with an egg yolk, pickled ginger and green onion.","Japanese"],
[3121,"Oyakodon","quick","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"Chicken and softly set egg simmered in sweet dashi-soy sauce over steamed rice.","3/4 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size pieces;1|onion|sliced thin;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;4|eggs|lightly beaten;2 cup|rice|cooked, hot;2|green onion|sliced;|nori|shredded, optional","Combine the water, soy sauce, mirin and sugar in a skillet and bring to a simmer.|Add the onion and chicken and cook 6 to 7 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Pour two-thirds of the beaten egg over the top in a circle and cover for 1 minute.|Pour the remaining egg over, cover, and turn off the heat for 30 to 60 seconds until just softly set.|Divide the rice into two bowls.|Slide the chicken and egg over the rice and top with green onion and nori.","Japanese"],
[3122,"Yakisoba","quick","🍝",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Japanese stir-fried noodles with pork, cabbage and carrots in a tangy sweet-savory sauce.","3 packet|yakisoba noodles|or ramen noodles, loosened;1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 cup|cabbage|chopped;1|carrots|julienned;1|onion|sliced;3 tbsp|worcestershire;2 tbsp|ketchup;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2|green onion|sliced;|pickled ginger|and bonito flakes, to top","Mix the worcestershire, ketchup, oyster sauce, soy sauce and sugar for the sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat and cook the pork 3 minutes until browned.|Add the onion, carrot and cabbage and stir-fry 3 to 4 minutes.|Push the vegetables aside, add the remaining oil, and loosen the noodles with a splash of water in the pan.|Pour in the sauce and toss everything together for 2 to 3 minutes.|Top with green onion, pickled ginger and bonito flakes.","Japanese"],
[3123,"Miso Soup","soup","🍲",15,"Very easy",9.5,4,"Light dashi broth with savory miso paste, soft tofu and wakame seaweed.","4 cup|water;2 tsp|dashi powder|or one 4-inch piece kombu;3 tbsp|miso paste;8 oz|tofu|silken, cubed;1 tbsp|wakame|dried seaweed;2|green onion|sliced","Soak the wakame in warm water for 5 minutes, then drain.|Bring the water and dashi powder to a gentle simmer in a pot.|Add the tofu and wakame and warm for 2 minutes.|Reduce the heat to low and place the miso in a ladle or small sieve.|Dissolve the miso into the broth by stirring, without letting it boil.|Serve immediately topped with green onion.","Japanese"],
[3124,"Okonomiyaki","lunch","🥞",35,"Medium",8,4,"Savory Japanese cabbage pancakes topped with okonomi sauce, mayo and bonito flakes.","1 cup|flour;3/4 cup|water|or dashi;3|eggs;4 cup|cabbage|finely shredded;3|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|tempura scraps|optional;4 slice|bacon|thin pork belly or bacon;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/4 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;|bonito flakes|and nori, to top","Whisk the flour, water and 1 egg until smooth, then fold in the cabbage, green onion and tempura scraps.|Stir the ketchup, worcestershire, oyster sauce and sugar to make the okonomi sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large skillet over medium heat and pour in half the batter, shaping a thick round pancake.|Lay 2 bacon slices on top and cook 5 minutes until the bottom is deep golden.|Flip carefully and cook 5 to 6 minutes more until cooked through.|Repeat, then top with the sauce, mayonnaise, bonito flakes and nori.","Japanese"],
[3125,"Yakitori","sides","🍢",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Skewered grilled chicken thighs glazed with a sweet, glossy soy tare.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, 1 inch pieces;6|green onion|cut in 1 inch pieces;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|mirin;1/4 cup|sake;3 tbsp|sugar;1 clove|garlic|smashed;1 slice|ginger;1 tsp|sesame seeds","Soak 12 bamboo skewers in water for 30 minutes.|Simmer the soy sauce, mirin, sake, sugar, garlic and ginger 10 to 12 minutes until syrupy, then strain.|Thread the chicken and green onion pieces alternately onto skewers.|Grill over medium-high heat or broil 4 minutes, turning once.|Brush with tare and keep grilling 5 to 6 minutes, turning and brushing until glossy and cooked through to 165°F.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve.","Japanese"],
[3126,"Tamagoyaki","sides","🍳",15,"Medium",7.5,2,"Japanese rolled omelet with layers of lightly sweet, savory egg, sliced into tender pinwheels.","4|eggs;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|water|or dashi;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|daikon|grated, to serve","Whisk the eggs with the sugar, mirin, soy sauce and water until combined but not frothy.|Oil a small nonstick or rectangular pan lightly over medium-low heat.|Pour in a thin layer of egg and cook until almost set but still wet on top.|Roll the egg from one side to the other and push to the edge of the pan.|Oil the empty part, pour in another thin layer under the roll, and repeat rolling until the egg is used.|Rest 2 minutes, slice into thick pieces, and serve with grated daikon.","Japanese"],
[3127,"Pan-Seared Ribeye with Garlic Butter","comfort","🥩",30,"Medium",9,2,"A thick, deeply browned ribeye basted in garlic and thyme butter, the steakhouse way.","2|ribeye steaks|1 1/4 inch thick, about 12 oz each;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|butter;4 clove|garlic|smashed;4 sprig|fresh thyme","Pat the steaks very dry and let them sit at room temperature for 30 minutes. Season both sides generously with salt and pepper.|Heat a cast-iron skillet over high heat for 3 minutes until smoking hot, then add the oil.|Sear the steaks 3 to 4 minutes without moving until a dark crust forms. Flip and sear 2 minutes more.|Reduce heat to medium, add the butter, garlic and thyme. Tilt the pan and spoon the foaming butter over the steaks for 2 minutes.|Cook to 125°F internal for rare, 130°F for medium-rare, or 140°F for medium.|Rest the steaks on a board for 8 minutes, spoon over the pan butter, and slice against the grain.","American"],
[3128,"New York Strip Steak","comfort","🥩",25,"Easy",9,2,"A classic skillet-seared strip steak with a salty crust and a juicy pink center.","2|ny strip steaks|1 inch thick, about 10 oz each;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Pat the steaks dry and season all over with salt and pepper. Let stand 20 minutes at room temperature.|Heat a heavy skillet over high heat until just smoking, then add the oil.|Sear the steaks 3 minutes per side for a dark crust. Render the fat cap by standing the steaks on their edge for 1 minute.|Lower the heat, add butter and thyme, and baste for 1 minute.|Cook to 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 5 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3129,"Filet Mignon","comfort","🥩",35,"Medium",9,2,"Tender beef filets seared in a skillet and finished in the oven with butter and herbs.","2|filet mignon steaks|1 1/2 inch thick, about 6 oz each;1 1/2 tsp|coarse salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 clove|garlic|smashed;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Take the filets out of the fridge 30 minutes ahead, pat dry, and season with salt and pepper. Heat the oven to 425°F.|Heat an oven-safe skillet over high heat and add the oil.|Sear the filets 2 minutes per side until deeply browned, also searing the edges for 30 seconds.|Add butter, garlic and thyme and baste for 1 minute.|Transfer the skillet to the oven for 4 to 6 minutes until 125°F for rare or 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 5 minutes, spoon the pan butter over, and serve.","American"],
[3130,"Steak au Poivre","comfort","🥩",35,"Medium",9,2,"Pepper-crusted steaks with a quick cognac cream pan sauce, a bistro favorite.","2|ny strip steaks|or filet mignon, 8 oz each;1 tbsp|black pepper|coarsely cracked;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;1|shallot|minced;1/4 cup|cognac|or brandy;1/2 cup|beef broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|dijon mustard","Pat the steaks dry, season with salt, and press the cracked pepper firmly into both sides.|Heat the oil in a heavy skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the steaks 4 minutes per side for medium-rare (130°F). Move to a plate and tent with foil.|Pour off most of the fat, add the butter and shallot, and cook 1 minute.|Off the heat, add the cognac, return to heat carefully and let it reduce by half, about 1 minute.|Add the broth and simmer 3 minutes, then stir in the cream and mustard and simmer 2 minutes until it coats a spoon.|Serve the steaks with the sauce spooned over.","French"],
[3131,"Chimichurri Flank Steak","light","🥩",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Grilled flank steak sliced thin and topped with a bright, garlicky parsley chimichurri.","1 1/2 lb|flank steak;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 cup|parsley|finely chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|red onion|minced;1/3 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|oregano;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes","Mix the parsley, garlic, red onion, 1/3 cup olive oil, vinegar, oregano, red pepper flakes and 1/2 tsp salt. Let it sit 20 minutes.|Pat the steak dry, rub with 1 tbsp olive oil, and season with salt and pepper.|Heat a grill or cast-iron pan over high heat.|Cook the steak 4 to 5 minutes per side to 130°F for medium-rare.|Rest 10 minutes, then slice thinly against the grain.|Serve topped with the chimichurri.","American"],
[3132,"Steak Frites","comfort","🍟",50,"Medium",9,2,"Pan-seared steak with crisp golden fries and a garlic-herb butter, a French bistro classic.","1 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|cut into 1/4 inch sticks;4 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;2|ny strip steaks|1 inch thick;1 1/2 tsp|coarse salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|butter|softened;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 clove|garlic|grated;1 tsp|lemon juice","Soak the potato sticks in cold water 30 minutes, then drain and dry thoroughly. Mix the butter, parsley, garlic and lemon juice and chill.|Heat the oil to 325°F in a heavy pot. Fry the potatoes in batches 5 minutes until pale and tender, then drain.|Season the steaks with salt and pepper. Sear in a very hot skillet 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F, then rest 5 minutes.|Raise the oil to 375°F and fry the potatoes again 3 to 4 minutes until golden and crisp. Drain and salt immediately.|Slice the steak, top with the herb butter, and serve with the fries.","French"],
[3133,"Reverse-Sear Porterhouse Steak","comfort","🥩",75,"Medium",9,2,"A thick steak slowly warmed in the oven, then seared hot for an edge-to-edge pink center.","2 lb|porterhouse steak|about 1 1/2 inches thick;2 tsp|coarse salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter;2 clove|garlic|smashed;2 sprig|fresh thyme","Salt the steak all over and refrigerate uncovered on a rack for at least 1 hour. Heat the oven to 250°F.|Pat dry, season with pepper, and set on a rack over a baking sheet.|Roast 35 to 45 minutes until 110°F in the thickest part for medium-rare.|Heat the oil in a cast-iron skillet over high heat until smoking. Sear the steak 1 to 2 minutes per side.|Add butter, garlic and thyme and baste for 30 seconds. Final temperature should be about 130°F.|Rest 5 minutes, then slice the strip and filet from the bone.","American"],
[3134,"Steak Fajitas","quick","🌮",40,"Easy",8.5,4,"Marinated skirt steak seared with sizzling peppers and onions, served in warm tortillas.","1 1/2 lb|skirt steak|or flank steak;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 tbsp|lime juice;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2|bell pepper|sliced;1|onion|sliced;8|flour tortillas|warmed;1/2 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|salsa","Whisk 2 tbsp oil with lime juice, garlic, cumin, chili powder, paprika, salt and pepper. Marinate the steak 30 minutes to 2 hours.|Heat a large cast-iron skillet over high heat. Cook the steak 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F. Rest on a board.|In the same pan, add the remaining oil and cook the peppers and onion 5 to 6 minutes until charred at the edges.|Slice the steak thinly against the grain.|Serve with the vegetables, warm tortillas, sour cream and salsa.","Tex-Mex"],
[3135,"Salisbury Steak","comfort","🍖",45,"Easy",9,4,"Seasoned beef patties simmered in a rich onion and mushroom gravy.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1/3 cup|breadcrumbs;1|eggs;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1|onion|sliced;2 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|flour;1 1/2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|ketchup","Mix the beef, breadcrumbs, egg, 1 tbsp worcestershire, salt and pepper gently and shape into 4 oval patties.|Brown the patties in the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat, 3 minutes per side. Remove to a plate.|Add the butter, onion and mushrooms to the pan and cook 6 to 8 minutes until golden.|Stir in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the broth, ketchup and remaining worcestershire.|Return the patties to the gravy, cover, and simmer 12 to 15 minutes until cooked through (160°F).|Serve over mashed potatoes or egg noodles.","American"],
[3136,"Chicken Fried Steak with Gravy","comfort","🍳",50,"Medium",9,4,"Tenderized steak breaded, fried until crisp, and smothered in creamy pepper gravy.","4|cube steaks|about 6 oz each;1 1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|salt;2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;2|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1 cup|vegetable oil;3 cup|milk|for gravy","Whisk the eggs with 1/2 cup milk. Mix the flour, salt, 1 tsp pepper, paprika and garlic powder in a shallow dish.|Dredge each steak in flour, dip in the egg mixture, then dredge in flour again, pressing firmly.|Heat the oil in a large skillet to 350°F. Fry the steaks 3 to 4 minutes per side until deep golden. Drain on a rack and keep warm.|Pour off all but 1/4 cup of the oil, leaving the browned bits.|Whisk in 1/4 cup of the seasoned flour and cook 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the 3 cups milk.|Simmer 5 minutes until thick, season with 1 tsp pepper and salt, and pour over the steaks.","Southern"],
[3137,"Garlic Butter Steak Tips","quick","🥩",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Juicy seared sirloin bites tossed in garlic butter, ready in about 25 minutes.","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|cut into 1 inch cubes;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4 tbsp|butter;5 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|worcestershire","Pat the steak dry and toss with salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over high heat until smoking.|Sear the steak in a single layer in two batches, 2 to 3 minutes total, turning once, until browned. Move to a plate.|Reduce the heat to medium, melt the butter, and cook the garlic 30 seconds.|Return the steak with the worcestershire and toss 1 minute.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve.","American"],
[3138,"Steak and Eggs","breakfast","🍳",25,"Easy",8.5,2,"A seared sirloin served with sunny-side-up eggs for a hearty diner-style breakfast.","12 oz|sirloin steak|about 1 inch thick;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|eggs;2 slice|bread|toasted;1 tbsp|chives|chopped","Pat the steak dry and season with salt and pepper.|Heat the oil in a skillet over high heat. Sear the steak 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F. Rest 5 minutes.|Wipe the skillet, melt the butter over medium heat, and fry the eggs 3 minutes until the whites are set and yolks runny.|Slice the steak against the grain.|Serve with the eggs, toast and chives.","American"],
[3139,"Philly Cheesesteak","lunch","🥪",35,"Easy",8,4,"Thinly sliced ribeye piled on a roll with sauteed onions and melted provolone.","1 1/2 lb|ribeye steak|partially frozen, sliced paper thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|onion|thinly sliced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;8 slice|provolone;4|french bread|rolls, split","Freeze the steak 30 minutes, then slice as thin as possible.|Heat 1 tbsp oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onions with a pinch of salt for 12 to 15 minutes until soft and golden. Move aside.|Raise the heat to high, add the remaining oil, and cook the beef 2 to 3 minutes, chopping it with spatulas, seasoned with salt and pepper.|Mix in the onions and form 4 portions in the pan. Top each with 2 slices of provolone, cover 1 minute until melted.|Toast the rolls briefly and scoop each portion into a roll.","American"],
[3140,"Steak Salad with Blue Cheese","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,2,"Sliced seared steak over crisp greens, tomatoes and red onion with a tangy vinaigrette.","12 oz|sirloin steak;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;6 cup|lettuce|chopped;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/4|red onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|blue cheese|crumbled;3 tbsp|olive oil|for dressing;1 tbsp|balsamic vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard","Season the steak with salt and pepper. Heat 1 tbsp oil in a skillet over high heat.|Sear 3 to 4 minutes per side to 130°F, then rest 8 minutes.|Whisk the dressing oil, vinegar and mustard with a pinch of salt.|Toss the lettuce, tomatoes and onion with half the dressing.|Slice the steak thinly against the grain and lay it on top.|Scatter the blue cheese and drizzle with the remaining dressing.","American"],
[3141,"Creamed Spinach","sides","🥬",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"The classic steakhouse side of spinach in a rich, nutmeg-scented cream sauce.","20 oz|frozen spinach|thawed and squeezed dry;2 tbsp|butter;1|shallot|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|flour;1 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a saucepan over medium heat and cook the shallot 2 minutes. Add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Stir in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the milk and cream and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until thickened.|Stir in the parmesan and nutmeg until melted.|Add the spinach and cook 4 to 5 minutes until hot and creamy. Season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3142,"Loaded Twice-Baked Potatoes","sides","🥔",100,"Easy",7.5,6,"Baked potato halves stuffed with a cheesy, bacony filling and baked again until golden.","3|russet potatoes|large;1 tbsp|olive oil;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|sour cream;1/4 cup|milk;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded, divided;6 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;3|green onion|sliced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 400°F. Rub the potatoes with oil and salt and bake 60 minutes until tender.|Cool 10 minutes, halve lengthwise, and scoop out the flesh, leaving a 1/4 inch shell.|Mash the flesh with the butter, sour cream, milk, 1 cup cheddar, half the bacon, half the green onion, salt and pepper.|Spoon the filling back into the shells and top with the remaining cheddar.|Bake 20 minutes until golden. Top with remaining bacon and green onion.","American"],
[3143,"Smash Burgers","quick","🍔",20,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin beef patties smashed on a hot skillet for crispy lacy edges, with melted cheese.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef|80/20, formed into 8 balls;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;8 slice|american cheese;4|burger buns|toasted;1/2|onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|pickles|sliced;3 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|ketchup;1 tsp|mustard","Mix the mayonnaise, ketchup and mustard for the sauce. Toast the buns.|Heat a cast-iron skillet or griddle over high heat until very hot.|Place the beef balls on the skillet and smash firmly flat with a sturdy spatula. Season with salt and pepper.|Cook 2 minutes until the edges are crisp, scrape and flip, top with cheese, and cook 30 to 45 seconds.|Stack 2 patties per bun with the sauce, onion and pickles.","American"],
[3144,"Classic Meatloaf","comfort","🍖",85,"Easy",9,6,"A tender beef meatloaf with a sweet tangy ketchup glaze.","2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3/4 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|milk;2|eggs;2 tbsp|worcestershire;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|ketchup;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|mustard","Heat the oven to 350°F. Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes.|Mix the beef, onion, garlic, soaked breadcrumbs, eggs, worcestershire, salt and pepper gently with your hands.|Shape into a loaf on a lined baking sheet or pack into a loaf pan.|Stir the ketchup, brown sugar and mustard and spread half over the loaf.|Bake 50 minutes, brush on the remaining glaze, and bake 15 more minutes until 160°F.|Rest 10 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3145,"Baby Back Ribs","comfort","🍖",195,"Medium",9,4,"Oven-roasted baby back ribs rubbed with spices and glazed in barbecue sauce, fall-off-the-bone tender.","2|pork ribs|racks baby back, about 2 lb each;3 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|paprika;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|onion powder;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 cup|bbq sauce","Heat the oven to 275°F. Remove the membrane from the back of the ribs with a paper towel.|Mix the brown sugar, paprika, salt, pepper, garlic powder, onion powder and cayenne and rub all over the ribs.|Wrap each rack tightly in foil, meat side up, and set on a baking sheet.|Bake 2 1/2 hours until very tender.|Unwrap, brush with barbecue sauce, and broil or grill 5 to 8 minutes until sticky and caramelized.|Rest 10 minutes and cut between the bones.","American"],
[3146,"Buffalo Wings","lunch","🍗",60,"Easy",8,4,"Crispy baked chicken wings tossed in tangy buttery buffalo sauce.","3 lb|chicken wings|split, tips removed;1 tbsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/2 cup|buffalo sauce;4 tbsp|butter|melted;1/2 cup|ranch dressing;4 stalk|celery|cut in sticks","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pat the wings completely dry.|Toss with baking powder, salt and garlic powder and arrange on a rack over a foil-lined sheet.|Bake 25 minutes, flip, and bake 25 to 30 minutes more until deep golden and crisp.|Whisk the buffalo sauce with the melted butter.|Toss the hot wings in the sauce and serve with ranch and celery.","American"],
[3147,"Chicken and Waffles","breakfast","🧇",75,"Medium",8.5,4,"Crispy buttermilk-fried chicken stacked on fluffy waffles with warm maple syrup.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in large pieces;1 cup|milk|with 1 tbsp lemon juice stirred in;1 1/2 cup|flour|for chicken;2 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;2 cup|flour|for waffles;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt|for waffles;2|eggs;1 3/4 cup|milk|for waffles;1/3 cup|butter|melted;1/2 cup|maple syrup|warmed","Marinate the chicken in the soured milk for at least 30 minutes.|Mix 1 1/2 cups flour with paprika, garlic powder, salt and pepper. Dredge the chicken, pressing to coat.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet. Fry the chicken 6 to 8 minutes, turning, until golden and 165°F inside. Drain on a rack.|Whisk the waffle flour, sugar, baking powder and salt. Whisk in the eggs, milk and melted butter until just combined.|Cook the batter in a hot waffle iron until golden and crisp.|Top each waffle with chicken and drizzle with warm syrup.","Southern"],
[3148,"Skillet Cornbread","sides","🌽",35,"Easy",7.5,8,"Golden cornbread with a crunchy edge, baked in a hot buttered cast-iron skillet.","1 1/2 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|baking soda;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|sugar;1 1/4 cup|milk|with 1 tbsp lemon juice stirred in;2|eggs;4 tbsp|butter|melted, divided","Heat the oven to 425°F and place a 10-inch cast-iron skillet inside to heat 10 minutes.|Whisk the cornmeal, flour, baking powder, baking soda, salt and sugar.|Whisk the soured milk, eggs and 3 tbsp melted butter, then stir into the dry ingredients until just combined.|Add the remaining butter to the hot skillet, swirl, and pour in the batter.|Bake 18 to 22 minutes until golden and a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 5 minutes before slicing.","Southern"],
[3149,"Creamy Coleslaw","sides","🥗",20,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crisp shredded cabbage and carrot in a tangy creamy dressing.","1|coleslaw mix|14 oz bag;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|celery seed|optional","Whisk the mayonnaise, sugar, vinegar, mustard, salt, pepper and celery seed until smooth.|Toss the coleslaw mix with the dressing.|Chill at least 30 minutes so the cabbage softens slightly.|Stir again and adjust seasoning before serving.","American"],
[3150,"Reuben Sandwich","lunch","🥪",20,"Easy",8,2,"Grilled rye with corned beef, sauerkraut, swiss and Russian dressing.","4 slice|rye bread;6 oz|corned beef|sliced deli;4 slice|swiss cheese;1/2 cup|sauerkraut|drained and squeezed dry;4 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|ketchup;1 tbsp|pickles|finely chopped;2 tbsp|butter|softened","Mix the mayonnaise, ketchup and chopped pickles for the Russian dressing.|Spread dressing on one side of each bread slice.|Layer 2 slices with swiss, corned beef, sauerkraut and another swiss slice, then top with remaining bread, dressing side down.|Butter the outside of the sandwiches.|Cook in a skillet over medium heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until the bread is golden and the cheese melted.|Slice in half and serve hot.","American"],
[3151,"BLT Sandwich","quick","🥪",15,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Crisp bacon, ripe tomato and lettuce with mayo on toasted bread.","8 slice|bacon;4 slice|bread|toasted;3 tbsp|mayonnaise;1|tomatoes|large, sliced;4|lettuce|leaves;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the bacon in a skillet over medium heat 8 to 10 minutes until crisp. Drain on paper towels.|Toast the bread and spread mayonnaise on each slice.|Season the tomato slices with salt and pepper.|Layer lettuce, tomato and bacon on 2 slices and top with remaining bread.|Cut in half and serve.","American"],
[3152,"Cobb Salad","light","🥗",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Chopped greens topped with rows of chicken, bacon, egg, avocado, tomato and blue cheese.","1 head|lettuce|chopped;2|chicken breast|cooked and diced;6 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;3|eggs|hard-boiled and chopped;2|avocado|diced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/2 cup|blue cheese|crumbled;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;1/4 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|dijon mustard;|salt|to taste","Hard-boil the eggs for 11 minutes, cool in ice water, peel and chop.|Whisk the olive oil, vinegar, mustard and salt for the dressing.|Spread the lettuce on a large platter.|Arrange the chicken, bacon, egg, avocado, tomatoes and blue cheese in rows on top.|Sprinkle with chives and drizzle with dressing just before serving.","American"],
[3153,"Classic Grilled Cheese","quick","🧀",12,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Buttery golden toast with gooey melted cheddar.","4 slice|bread;4 slice|american cheese;1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 tbsp|butter|softened","Butter one side of each bread slice.|Place 2 slices butter side down in a skillet over medium-low heat.|Layer the american cheese and cheddar on top and cover with the remaining bread, butter side up.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes until golden, flip, and cook 3 minutes more until the cheese is melted.|Slice and serve hot.","American"],
[3154,"Biscuits and Sausage Gravy","breakfast","🍳",35,"Easy",8.5,6,"Fluffy buttermilk-style biscuits smothered in peppery sausage cream gravy.","2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;6 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed;3/4 cup|milk;1 lb|breakfast sausage;1/4 cup|flour|for gravy;3 cup|milk|for gravy;1 tsp|black pepper;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 425°F. Whisk 2 cups flour, baking powder and salt, then cut in the cold butter until pea-sized crumbs form.|Stir in 3/4 cup milk just until a shaggy dough forms. Pat to 1 inch thick, cut 6 rounds, and place on a baking sheet.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden.|Brown the sausage in a large skillet over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up.|Sprinkle in 1/4 cup flour and cook 1 minute, then slowly stir in 3 cups milk.|Simmer 5 to 6 minutes until thick, season with pepper and salt, and ladle over split biscuits.","Southern"],
[3155,"Fudgy Brownies","treats","🍫",50,"Easy",9,16,"Dense, fudgy chocolate brownies with a shiny crackly top.","1/2 cup|butter;1 cup|sugar;2|eggs;1 tsp|vanilla;1/3 cup|cocoa powder;1/2 cup|flour;1/4 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|baking powder;1/2 cup|chocolate chips","Heat the oven to 350°F and line an 8-inch square pan with parchment.|Melt the butter and stir in the sugar, then beat in the eggs and vanilla.|Sift in the cocoa, flour, salt and baking powder and stir until just combined. Fold in the chocolate chips.|Spread in the pan and bake 22 to 26 minutes, until a toothpick has a few moist crumbs.|Cool completely before cutting into squares.","American"],
[3156,"Chicken and Sausage Gumbo","comfort","🍲",120,"Medium",9,8,"A dark roux gumbo with chicken, smoked sausage and the holy trinity, served over rice.","1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 cup|flour;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;3 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;8 cup|chicken broth;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, bite-size;1 lb|smoked sausage|sliced;2|bay leaves;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;3 cup|rice|cooked;4|green onion|sliced","Whisk the oil and flour in a heavy pot over medium-low heat, stirring constantly 25 to 35 minutes until the roux is the color of dark chocolate.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the warm broth, then add bay leaves, cajun seasoning and thyme.|Add the sausage and simmer 30 minutes.|Add the chicken and simmer 30 more minutes until tender. Skim off any fat.|Remove the bay leaves, adjust salt and cayenne, and serve over rice with green onion.","Cajun"],
[3157,"Jambalaya","comfort","🍤",60,"Easy",9,6,"A one-pot rice dish with smoked sausage, chicken and shrimp in Cajun spices.","1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 lb|smoked sausage|sliced;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, diced;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz;2 cup|rice|long-grain;3 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 lb|shrimp|peeled;3|green onion|sliced","Brown the sausage in the oil in a large Dutch oven over medium-high heat 4 minutes. Remove.|Brown the chicken 5 minutes, season with some cajun seasoning, and remove.|Cook the onion, pepper and celery in the drippings 5 minutes, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, rice, broth, remaining seasoning and thyme. Return the sausage and chicken.|Bring to a boil, cover, and cook on low 20 minutes without lifting the lid.|Lay the shrimp on top, cover, and cook 5 minutes until pink and the rice is tender. Fluff and add green onion.","Cajun"],
[3158,"Shrimp and Grits","comfort","🍤",45,"Easy",9,4,"Garlicky shrimp and bacon in a savory pan sauce over creamy cheddar grits.","1 cup|grits|stone-ground or old-fashioned;4 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;4 slice|bacon|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|paprika;1 tbsp|lemon juice;3|green onion|sliced;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring the broth to a boil, whisk in the grits, then reduce to low, cover, and cook 25 to 30 minutes, stirring often, until creamy.|Stir in the cheddar and butter and season with salt and pepper.|Cook the bacon in a skillet until crisp, then remove, leaving 1 tbsp fat.|Season the shrimp with paprika, salt and pepper and cook in the fat 2 minutes per side until pink.|Add the garlic for 30 seconds, then the lemon juice and bacon.|Spoon the shrimp over the grits and top with green onion.","Southern"],
[3159,"Red Beans and Rice","comfort","🍛",180,"Easy",9,8,"Creamy New Orleans-style kidney beans slow-simmered with andouille and served over rice.","1 lb|kidney beans|dried, soaked overnight;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 lb|smoked sausage|andouille, sliced;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;3 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;6 cup|chicken broth;2|bay leaves;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|dried thyme;3 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste;3|green onion|sliced","Drain the soaked beans. Brown the sausage in the oil in a large pot 5 minutes.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 6 minutes, then the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the beans, broth, bay leaves, cajun seasoning and thyme and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a low simmer, partly covered, and cook 2 to 2 1/2 hours until the beans are very tender, stirring occasionally.|Mash about a quarter of the beans against the pot to thicken, and season with salt.|Serve over rice topped with green onion.","Cajun"],
[3160,"Crawfish Etouffee","comfort","🦐",60,"Medium",9,6,"A blond-roux smothered stew of shrimp in Cajun trinity, served over rice.","6 tbsp|butter;1/3 cup|flour;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|chicken broth;1 can|diced tomatoes|14.5 oz;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|paprika;1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled, or crawfish tails;3|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;3 cup|rice|cooked","Melt the butter in a Dutch oven over medium heat, whisk in the flour, and cook 8 to 10 minutes to a peanut-butter colored roux.|Add the onion, bell pepper and celery and cook 6 minutes until soft. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, broth, cajun seasoning and paprika and simmer 20 minutes until thickened.|Add the shrimp and cook 4 to 5 minutes until pink.|Stir in the green onion and parsley and adjust seasoning.|Serve over rice.","Cajun"],
[3161,"Southern Collard Greens","sides","🥬",90,"Easy",7.5,6,"Tender collards simmered low and slow with smoky bacon and a splash of vinegar.","2 lb|collard greens|stemmed and chopped;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;4 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Wash the collards well and slice into 1 inch ribbons.|Cook the bacon in a large pot until crisp. Add the onion and cook 4 minutes, then the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the collards in batches, stirring until wilted.|Pour in the broth, vinegar, sugar and red pepper flakes and bring to a simmer.|Cover and cook on low 60 to 75 minutes until very tender.|Season with salt and pepper and serve with the pot liquor.","Southern"],
[3162,"Hush Puppies","sides","🧆",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crispy fried cornmeal fritters with sweet onion, perfect alongside fried fish.","1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|onion|finely minced;1|eggs;3/4 cup|milk;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Whisk the cornmeal, flour, baking powder, salt, sugar and pepper.|Stir in the onion, egg and milk to make a thick batter. Rest 5 minutes.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a heavy pot.|Drop the batter by tablespoons into the oil and fry 2 to 3 minutes, turning, until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm.","Southern"],
[3163,"Fried Catfish","comfort","🐟",35,"Easy",9,4,"Cornmeal-crusted catfish fillets fried until crispy and golden.","4|catfish fillets|about 6 oz each;1 cup|buttermilk|or milk with 1 tsp lemon juice;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|paprika;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1|lemon|cut in wedges","Soak the fillets in the buttermilk for 15 to 30 minutes.|Mix the cornmeal, flour, cajun seasoning, salt, pepper and paprika in a shallow dish.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a deep skillet.|Lift each fillet from the buttermilk, let it drip, and dredge in the cornmeal mix.|Fry 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden and the fish flakes at 145°F.|Drain on a rack and serve with lemon wedges.","Southern"],
[3164,"Shrimp Po' Boy","lunch","🥪",35,"Easy",8,4,"Crisp fried shrimp on a French roll with lettuce, tomato, pickles and spicy remoulade.","1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;2 tsp|cajun seasoning;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|milk;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;4|french bread|rolls or 4 pieces of baguette;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|cajun seasoning|for sauce;2 cup|lettuce|shredded;2|tomatoes|sliced;1/2 cup|pickles","Stir the mayonnaise, mustard, lemon juice and 1/2 tsp cajun seasoning for the remoulade.|Mix the cornmeal, flour, 2 tsp cajun seasoning and salt. Dip the shrimp in milk, then dredge in the cornmeal mixture.|Heat the oil to 350°F and fry the shrimp in batches 2 to 3 minutes until golden. Drain.|Split and lightly toast the rolls and spread with the remoulade.|Fill with lettuce, tomato, pickles and the shrimp.","Cajun"],
[3165,"Peach Cobbler","treats","🍑",70,"Easy",9,8,"Juicy cinnamon peaches under a golden buttery biscuit-style crust.","6 cup|peaches|sliced, fresh or frozen;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 cup|flour;1/2 cup|sugar|for topping;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/4 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|milk;6 tbsp|butter|melted","Heat the oven to 375°F. Toss the peaches with 1/2 cup sugar, cornstarch, lemon juice and cinnamon.|Pour into a 9x9-inch baking dish.|Whisk the flour, 1/2 cup sugar, baking powder and salt, then stir in the milk and melted butter until smooth.|Spoon the batter over the peaches in dollops.|Bake 40 to 45 minutes until golden and bubbling.|Cool 15 minutes and serve warm with vanilla ice cream.","Southern"],
[3166,"Banana Pudding","treats","🍌",50,"Easy",9,10,"Layers of vanilla custard, ripe bananas and vanilla wafers, chilled until soft.","3/4 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|flour;1/4 tsp|salt;3 cup|milk;4|eggs|yolks only;2 tbsp|butter;2 tsp|vanilla;4|banana|ripe, sliced;1|vanilla wafers|11 oz box;1 cup|heavy cream|whipped, for topping","Whisk the sugar, flour and salt in a saucepan, then whisk in the milk and egg yolks.|Cook over medium heat, stirring constantly, 8 to 10 minutes until thick.|Remove from the heat and stir in the butter and vanilla.|Layer wafers, banana slices and custard in a 2-quart dish, repeating twice.|Cover and chill at least 4 hours.|Top with whipped cream before serving.","Southern"],
[3167,"Nashville Hot Chicken","comfort","🌶️",90,"Medium",9,4,"Buttermilk-fried chicken brushed with a fiery cayenne oil and served on white bread with pickles.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1 1/2 cup|buttermilk;2 tbsp|hot sauce;1 tbsp|salt;2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|black pepper;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|hot, for sauce;2 tbsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;4 slice|bread;|pickles|to serve","Mix the buttermilk, hot sauce and 2 tsp salt. Marinate the chicken in it 4 hours or overnight.|Whisk the flour, 1 tbsp paprika, garlic powder, pepper and 1 tsp salt. Dredge the chicken, pressing, then dredge again.|Heat the frying oil to 325°F in a Dutch oven. Fry the chicken 14 to 18 minutes, turning, until 175°F. Drain on a rack.|Stir the cayenne, brown sugar, 1 tsp paprika and garlic powder into 1/2 cup hot frying oil.|Brush the hot sauce generously over the chicken.|Serve on bread with pickles.","Southern"],
[3168,"Pimento Cheese","sides","🧀",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"The South's classic cheddar spread with sweet pimentos, great on crackers or in sandwiches.","2 cup|cheddar|sharp, freshly shredded;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;1 jar|pimentos|4 oz, drained;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Beat the cream cheese and mayonnaise until smooth.|Stir in the pimentos, garlic powder, cayenne and pepper.|Fold in the shredded cheddar.|Chill 1 hour before serving with crackers, celery or on bread.","Southern"],
[3169,"Deviled Eggs","sides","🥚",30,"Very easy",7.5,12,"Creamy mustard-mayo egg yolk filling piped into tender egg whites with paprika.","6|eggs;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|apple cider vinegar;|salt|to taste;|paprika|to garnish;1 tbsp|chives|chopped","Place the eggs in a pot, cover with cold water, bring to a boil, then cover off the heat for 12 minutes.|Cool in ice water 5 minutes, then peel and halve lengthwise.|Mash the yolks with the mayonnaise, mustard, vinegar and salt until smooth.|Spoon or pipe the filling into the whites.|Dust with paprika and chives and chill until serving.","Southern"],
[3170,"Sweet Potato Pie","treats","🥧",110,"Medium",9,8,"A silky spiced sweet potato custard in a flaky crust, a Southern holiday favorite.","2 lb|sweet potatoes;1|pie crust|9 inch, unbaked;1/2 cup|butter|softened;3/4 cup|brown sugar;2|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|nutmeg;1/4 tsp|salt","Bake the sweet potatoes at 400°F for 50 to 60 minutes until very soft. Cool, peel, and mash until smooth (about 2 cups).|Lower the oven to 350°F and fit the crust into a 9-inch pie plate.|Beat the mashed sweet potato with the butter and brown sugar, then beat in the eggs, milk, vanilla, cinnamon, nutmeg and salt.|Pour into the crust.|Bake 50 to 55 minutes until the center is just set.|Cool completely before slicing.","Southern"],
[3171,"Palak Paneer","comfort","🥬",40,"Easy",9,4,"Cubes of soft paneer in a silky, spiced spinach sauce, finished with a swirl of cream.","1 lb|spinach|fresh or 10 oz frozen;14 oz|paneer|cubed;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|garam masala;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1/4 cup|heavy cream;|salt|to taste","Blanch the spinach in boiling water for 1 minute, then move it to ice water, drain well and blend to a smooth puree.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat and fry the paneer cubes 2 to 3 minutes per side until lightly golden. Remove and set aside.|In the same pan, cook the onion for 6 to 8 minutes until soft and golden, then stir in the garlic and ginger for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, cumin, coriander, turmeric, cayenne and salt and cook 5 minutes until the tomatoes break down into a paste.|Pour in the spinach puree and 1/2 cup water, and simmer 5 minutes.|Stir in the cream and garam masala, add the paneer and simmer gently 3 minutes. Serve with rice or naan.","Indian"],
[3172,"Chana Masala","comfort","🍛",35,"Easy",9,4,"Chickpeas simmered in a tangy, deeply spiced tomato and onion gravy.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|finely chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;2 can|chickpeas|15 oz each, drained;2 tsp|garam masala;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion 8 minutes until deep golden.|Add the garlic and ginger and cook 1 minute.|Stir in the cumin, coriander, turmeric, paprika and cayenne for 30 seconds until fragrant.|Add the tomatoes and salt and cook 8 minutes, mashing, until thick and the oil begins to separate.|Add the chickpeas and 1 cup water, and simmer 15 minutes, lightly crushing some chickpeas to thicken the sauce.|Stir in the garam masala and lemon juice, then top with cilantro. Serve with rice or naan.","Indian"],
[3173,"Chicken Biryani","comfort","🍚",90,"Medium",9,6,"Fragrant basmati layered with yogurt-marinated spiced chicken and fried onions, then steamed.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skinless;1 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|garam masala;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cayenne;2 cup|rice|basmati, rinsed;3|onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;4|cardamom pods;1|cinnamon|stick;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|mint|chopped;1/4 cup|milk|warmed, with a pinch of saffron;2 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste","Mix the chicken with the yogurt, ginger, garlic, garam masala, turmeric, cayenne and 2 teaspoons salt. Marinate at least 1 hour.|Fry the onions in the oil over medium heat 20 to 25 minutes, stirring often, until deep brown and crisp. Remove half and set aside for topping.|Add the marinated chicken to the remaining onions in the pot and cook 10 minutes, then spread it in an even layer.|Boil the rice in plenty of salted water with the cardamom and cinnamon for 5 minutes until 70 percent cooked, then drain.|Layer the rice over the chicken, then top with the reserved onions, cilantro, mint, saffron milk and butter.|Cover tightly with foil and a lid, and cook over the lowest heat for 30 minutes.|Rest 10 minutes, then gently fluff and serve with raita.","Indian"],
[3174,"Aloo Gobi","sides","🥔",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Dry-style potatoes and cauliflower tossed with turmeric, cumin and ginger.","3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|onion|chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 lb|potatoes|1-inch cubes;1 head|cauliflower|cut into florets;1 tsp|turmeric;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large lidded skillet over medium heat and toast the cumin 30 seconds.|Add the onion and cook 6 minutes until golden, then add the ginger and garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the turmeric, coriander, cayenne and tomato and cook 3 minutes.|Add the potatoes, cauliflower, salt and 1/4 cup water. Cover and cook 15 minutes, stirring now and then.|Uncover and cook 5 to 8 minutes more until the vegetables are tender and lightly browned.|Sprinkle with garam masala and cilantro before serving.","Indian"],
[3175,"Samosas","treats","🥟",75,"Medium",9,8,"Crisp, flaky pastry triangles filled with spiced potatoes and peas.","2 cup|flour;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1 lb|potatoes|boiled and mashed coarsely;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|coriander;1 tsp|garam masala;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|lemon juice;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Mix the flour, 1/4 cup oil and salt, then add about 1/2 cup cold water to form a stiff dough. Knead 5 minutes, cover and rest 30 minutes.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a pan, toast the cumin and ginger 30 seconds, then add the spices and peas and cook 2 minutes.|Fold in the potatoes and lemon juice, season with salt and cool completely.|Divide the dough into 8 balls and roll each into an oval, then cut in half to make 16 half-circles.|Shape each half into a cone, fill with about 2 tablespoons filling, wet the edge and pinch to seal.|Heat the frying oil to 325°F and fry the samosas in batches for 8 to 10 minutes until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm with chutney.","Indian"],
[3176,"Garlic Naan","sides","🫓",90,"Medium",7.5,6,"Soft, blistered skillet flatbread brushed with garlic butter.","1/2 cup|warm water;2 tsp|sugar;2 1/4 tsp|yeast|one packet;2 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|salt;4 tbsp|butter|melted;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped","Stir the warm water, sugar and yeast together and let sit 10 minutes until foamy.|Mix in the flour, yogurt, oil and salt, then knead 8 minutes until smooth and soft.|Cover and let rise in a warm place 1 hour until doubled.|Divide into 6 balls and roll each into a teardrop about 1/4 inch thick.|Heat a cast-iron skillet over high heat until very hot. Cook each naan 1 to 2 minutes per side until puffed and charred in spots.|Mix the melted butter with garlic and cilantro and brush over the hot naan.","Indian"],
[3177,"Chicken Korma","comfort","🍛",50,"Easy",9,4,"Tender chicken in a mild, creamy sauce of yogurt, onion and ground almonds.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;2 tbsp|butter;2|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;2 tsp|coriander;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|garam masala;1/3 cup|almonds|ground;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|chicken broth;|salt|to taste","Toss the chicken with yogurt and 1 teaspoon salt and marinate 30 minutes.|Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onions 10 minutes until soft and pale gold.|Add the garlic, ginger, coriander, cumin and turmeric and cook 1 minute.|Add the chicken with its marinade and brown lightly for 5 minutes.|Stir in the ground almonds and broth, cover and simmer 20 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Stir in the cream and garam masala and simmer 5 minutes. Serve with basmati rice.","Indian"],
[3178,"Chicken Vindaloo","comfort","🌶️",60,"Medium",9,4,"A fiery, tangy Goan-style curry of chicken in a vinegar and chile marinade.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1/4 cup|apple cider vinegar;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;6 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|cumin;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|cayenne;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|mustard|ground seed or mustard powder;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|onion|finely chopped;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2|potatoes|cubed, optional;|salt|to taste","Mix the vinegar, ginger, half the garlic, cumin, paprika, cayenne, turmeric and mustard into a paste. Coat the chicken and marinate at least 1 hour.|Heat the oil in a heavy pot over medium heat and cook the onions 10 minutes until browned.|Add the remaining garlic and tomato paste and cook 2 minutes.|Add the chicken with marinade, salt and 1 cup water, and add the potatoes if using.|Cover and simmer 30 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the chicken and potatoes are tender and the sauce is thick.|Taste, adjust salt and serve with rice.","Indian"],
[3179,"Paneer Tikka","sides","🍢",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Skewers of spiced yogurt-marinated paneer and peppers, charred until smoky.","14 oz|paneer|1 1/2-inch cubes;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|garam masala;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|bell pepper|cut in chunks;1|red onion|cut in chunks;|salt|to taste","Whisk the yogurt, ginger, garlic, spices, lemon juice, oil and salt.|Fold in the paneer, pepper and onion and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Thread onto skewers, alternating paneer and vegetables.|Heat the oven broiler to high, or a grill to 450°F.|Cook 4 to 5 minutes per side, turning, until charred at the edges.|Serve with lemon wedges and mint chutney.","Indian"],
[3180,"Cucumber Raita","sides","🥒",10,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Cooling yogurt with cucumber and toasted cumin, the perfect foil for spicy curries.","1 cup|greek yogurt;1|cucumber|grated and squeezed dry;1/2 tsp|cumin|toasted and ground;1 clove|garlic|grated;2 tbsp|mint|chopped;1/4 tsp|cayenne;|salt|to taste","Toast the cumin seeds in a dry skillet over medium heat 1 minute until fragrant, then grind.|Whisk the yogurt with 2 tablespoons water until smooth.|Stir in the cucumber, garlic, mint and cumin.|Season with salt, chill 15 minutes and dust with cayenne before serving.","Indian"],
[3181,"Gulab Jamun","treats","🍩",60,"Medium",9,8,"Soft milk-based dumplings fried golden and soaked in cardamom rose syrup.","1 cup|milk|powder, full fat;1/4 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|baking powder;2 tbsp|butter|melted;1/4 cup|milk|warm, plus more as needed;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 1/2 cup|sugar;1 1/2 cup|water;4|cardamom pods|crushed;1 tsp|lemon juice","Mix the milk powder, flour and baking powder, then work in the butter and enough warm milk to make a soft, smooth dough. Do not overknead.|Roll into 16 smooth, crack-free balls.|Simmer the sugar, water and cardamom for 8 minutes into a light syrup, add the lemon juice and keep warm.|Heat the oil to 275°F, a low temperature.|Fry the balls in batches 6 to 8 minutes, turning, until deep golden brown.|Drop the hot jamun into the warm syrup and soak at least 1 hour before serving.","Indian"],
[3182,"Chicken Jalfrezi","quick","🌶️",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"A bright stir-fried curry of chicken, peppers and onions in a spicy tomato sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in strips;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced;1|red pepper|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cayenne;1 can|crushed tomatoes|14 oz;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a large skillet over high heat and sear the chicken 4 minutes until browned. Remove.|Add the remaining oil, onion and peppers and stir-fry 4 minutes until just tender-crisp. Remove half.|Add the garlic, ginger and spices to the pan for 1 minute.|Pour in the tomatoes and salt and simmer 8 minutes.|Return the chicken and all vegetables and cook 5 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Finish with garam masala and cilantro.","Indian"],
[3183,"Kheer","treats","🍚",60,"Easy",9,6,"Slow-simmered rice pudding scented with cardamom and studded with nuts.","1/2 cup|rice|basmati, rinsed;6 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;4|cardamom pods|crushed;1/4 cup|almonds|sliced;1/4 cup|raisins;1 pinch|saffron","Bring the milk to a gentle simmer in a heavy pot over medium heat.|Add the rice and cardamom and simmer on low for 35 to 40 minutes, stirring often to prevent sticking.|Stir in the sugar, saffron, raisins and half the almonds and cook 10 minutes until thick and creamy.|Serve warm or chilled, topped with the remaining almonds.","Indian"],
[3184,"Vegetable Pakoras","sides","🧅",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crunchy chickpea-flour fritters of onion, potato and spinach.","1 cup|chickpea flour|besan;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 tsp|salt;2|onion|thinly sliced;1|potatoes|thinly sliced;1 cup|spinach|chopped;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Whisk the chickpea flour, baking powder, spices and salt with about 1/2 cup water into a thick batter.|Fold in the onion, potato and spinach so everything is coated.|Heat the oil to 350°F.|Drop spoonfuls of batter into the oil and fry in batches 4 to 5 minutes, turning, until deep golden and cooked through.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot with chutney.","Indian"],
[3185,"Rajma","comfort","🫘",50,"Easy",9,4,"Punjabi kidney beans in a thick, spiced tomato gravy, served over rice.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin;1|onion|finely chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|14 oz;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cayenne;2 can|kidney beans|15 oz each, drained;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and toast the cumin 30 seconds.|Add the onion and cook 8 minutes until golden, then the ginger and garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomatoes, coriander, turmeric, paprika, cayenne and salt and cook 8 minutes until thick.|Add the beans and 1 1/2 cups water and simmer 25 minutes, mashing some beans to thicken.|Stir in the garam masala and cilantro and serve with rice.","Indian"],
[3186,"Keema Matar","comfort","🍛",40,"Easy",9,4,"Spiced minced meat simmered with peas and tomatoes, great with naan or rice.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|chopped;1|ginger|1-inch piece, grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 lb|ground beef;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;2 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1 cup|frozen peas;1 tsp|garam masala;|salt|to taste;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 7 minutes until golden.|Add the ginger and garlic for 1 minute, then the beef and cook 8 minutes, breaking it up, until browned.|Stir in the cumin, coriander, turmeric, cayenne and salt and cook 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes and 1/2 cup water and simmer 10 minutes.|Add the peas and cook 5 minutes more.|Finish with garam masala and cilantro.","Indian"],
[3187,"Thai Red Curry","quick","🍛",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Chicken and vegetables in a creamy, spicy coconut red curry sauce.","1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 cup|chicken broth;1|bell pepper|sliced;1 cup|bamboo shoots|canned, drained;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1/2 cup|basil|Thai or regular;1|lime|juiced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Scoop the thick cream from the top of the coconut milk into a pot over medium heat and fry the curry paste 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and cook 3 minutes, stirring.|Pour in the remaining coconut milk and broth and bring to a simmer.|Add the bell pepper, bamboo shoots, fish sauce and sugar and cook 8 to 10 minutes until the chicken is cooked through.|Stir in the basil and lime juice and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3188,"Mango Sticky Rice","treats","🥭",60,"Easy",9,4,"Sweet coconut sticky rice served with ripe mango slices.","1 cup|rice|Thai glutinous sweet rice, soaked 4 hours;1 can|coconut milk|14 oz, divided;1/3 cup|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt;2|mango|ripe, peeled and sliced;1 tsp|cornstarch;1 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted","Drain the soaked rice and steam over boiling water in a lined steamer for 25 minutes until tender and translucent.|Warm 3/4 cup coconut milk with the sugar and 1/4 teaspoon salt until dissolved.|Fold the hot rice into the sweetened coconut milk, cover and let sit 20 minutes to absorb.|Whisk the remaining coconut milk, cornstarch and remaining salt in a pot and heat until slightly thickened, about 3 minutes.|Serve the rice with mango slices, a drizzle of the sauce and sesame seeds.","Thai"],
[3189,"Chicken Satay","sides","🍢",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Turmeric-coconut marinated chicken skewers with a rich peanut dipping sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, sliced in strips;1/2 cup|coconut milk;1 tbsp|curry powder;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 cup|peanut butter;1/2 cup|coconut milk;1 tbsp|red curry paste;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|lime juice;1 tbsp|brown sugar;|salt|to taste","Mix the 1/2 cup coconut milk, curry powder, soy sauce, sugar and fish sauce, add the chicken and marinate 30 minutes while soaking wooden skewers in water.|Thread the chicken onto the skewers.|Whisk the peanut butter, remaining coconut milk, curry paste, soy sauce, lime juice and sugar in a small pot and warm over low heat 5 minutes, thinning with water if needed.|Grill or broil the skewers at high heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.|Serve with the peanut sauce.","Thai"],
[3190,"Larb Gai","light","🥬",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Zesty Thai minced chicken salad with lime, fish sauce, herbs and toasted rice powder.","1 lb|ground chicken;2 tbsp|rice|uncooked, for rice powder;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;3|shallot|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;1/2 cup|mint|torn;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 head|butter lettuce|leaves separated","Toast the uncooked rice in a dry skillet over medium heat 5 minutes until golden, then grind into a coarse powder.|Cook the chicken in a skillet with 1/4 cup water over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up, until cooked through.|Take off the heat and stir in the lime juice, fish sauce, sugar and pepper flakes.|Fold in the shallots, green onion, mint, cilantro and rice powder.|Serve warm in lettuce leaves.","Thai"],
[3191,"Som Tam","light","🥗",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crunchy green papaya salad pounded with lime, chile, peanuts and tomatoes.","4 cup|green papaya|shredded, or carrot and cabbage;2 clove|garlic;2|chili|Thai, to taste;1 cup|green beans|cut in 1-inch pieces;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1/4 cup|peanuts|roasted","Pound the garlic and chiles in a large mortar, or mash them in a bowl, into a rough paste.|Add the green beans and bruise them lightly.|Add the lime juice, fish sauce and sugar and stir until the sugar dissolves.|Add the papaya and tomatoes and toss, lightly pounding to release their juices.|Top with the peanuts and serve right away.","Thai"],
[3192,"Khao Soi","soup","🍜",50,"Medium",9.5,4,"Northern Thai curry noodle soup with chicken, coconut milk and crispy noodles.","2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 tbsp|curry powder;1 tsp|turmeric;1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;8 oz|egg noodles;1/2 cup|red onion|thinly sliced;2|lime|cut in wedges;1/4 cup|cilantro;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for crispy noodles","Fry a handful of the dry egg noodles in 1/2 cup hot oil 20 to 30 seconds until puffed and golden, then drain on paper towels.|Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a pot over medium heat and fry the curry paste, curry powder and turmeric 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and stir 3 minutes.|Add the coconut milk, broth, fish sauce and sugar and simmer 20 minutes.|Boil the remaining noodles according to the package and divide among bowls.|Ladle the curry over the noodles and top with crispy noodles, red onion, cilantro and lime wedges.","Thai"],
[3193,"Thai Yellow Curry","comfort","🍛",40,"Easy",9,4,"A mild, golden coconut curry with chicken and potatoes.","1 can|coconut milk|14 oz;3 tbsp|curry powder;1 tbsp|red curry paste;1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, cut in chunks;2|potatoes|cubed;1|onion|cut in wedges;1 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|lime juice;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Scoop the thick cream from the coconut milk into a pot over medium heat and fry with the curry powder and paste 2 minutes.|Add the chicken and onion and stir 3 minutes.|Add the remaining coconut milk, broth, potatoes, fish sauce and sugar.|Simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes and chicken are tender.|Finish with lime juice and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3194,"Thai Cashew Chicken","quick","🥜",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Stir-fried chicken with cashews, peppers and a glossy savory-sweet sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|bite-size pieces;1 tbsp|cornstarch;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|diced;1/2|onion|cut in wedges;1/2 cup|cashews|roasted;3 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Toss the chicken with the cornstarch.|Heat the oil in a wok over high heat and stir-fry the chicken 4 to 5 minutes until browned and cooked. Remove.|Add the garlic, pepper and onion and stir-fry 2 minutes.|Mix the oyster sauce, soy sauce, fish sauce, sugar and 2 tablespoons water.|Return the chicken, add the sauce and cashews and toss 2 minutes until glossy.|Top with green onion and serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3195,"Thai Pineapple Fried Rice","quick","🍍",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried rice with sweet pineapple, cashews and curry powder, often served in a pineapple.","3 cup|rice|cooked and chilled;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2|onion|diced;2|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|pineapple|diced;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1 tsp|curry powder;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 cup|cashews|roasted;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced","Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over high heat and scramble the eggs 1 minute. Remove.|Add the remaining oil, garlic and onion and stir-fry 2 minutes.|Add the rice, breaking up clumps, and stir-fry 3 minutes.|Sprinkle in the curry powder, soy sauce and fish sauce and toss to coat.|Add the pineapple, peas, eggs and cashews and cook 3 minutes.|Top with green onion and serve.","Thai"],
[3196,"Pad Prik King","quick","🌶️",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"A dry stir-fry of pork and green beans in spicy red curry paste.","1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|red curry paste;1 lb|green beans|cut in 2-inch lengths;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tsp|sugar;2|lime|leaves, optional;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Heat the oil in a wok over medium-high heat and fry the curry paste 1 minute.|Add the pork and stir-fry 3 minutes until no longer pink.|Add the green beans and stir-fry 5 minutes until crisp-tender.|Add the fish sauce, soy sauce, sugar and 2 tablespoons water and toss 2 minutes.|Serve over rice.","Thai"],
[3197,"Thai Garlic Pepper Pork","quick","🥩",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Fried pork slices in a punchy garlic and black pepper coating.","1 1/2 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;8 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|black pepper|coarsely ground;2 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tsp|sugar;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving;1|cucumber|sliced, for serving","Mix the garlic, pepper, oyster sauce, soy sauce, fish sauce and sugar, add the pork and marinate 15 minutes.|Heat the oil in a wide skillet over high heat.|Cook the pork in a single layer in batches 2 to 3 minutes per side until browned and cooked through.|Serve with rice and cucumber slices.","Thai"],
[3198,"Gai Yang","comfort","🍗",75,"Easy",9,4,"Thai grilled chicken marinated in lemongrass, garlic and cilantro root, with a sweet chili dip.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;4 clove|garlic;1/4 cup|cilantro|stems and leaves;2 tbsp|lemongrass|chopped;2 tbsp|fish sauce;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Blend the garlic, cilantro, lemongrass, fish sauce, soy sauce, honey and pepper into a paste.|Coat the chicken and marinate at least 1 hour, or overnight.|Heat the oven to 425°F, or a grill to medium.|Roast on a rack-lined sheet pan 35 to 40 minutes until browned and 175°F inside, or grill about 30 minutes, turning.|Rest 5 minutes and serve with sweet chili sauce.","Thai"],
[3199,"Fresh Spring Rolls","light","🥬",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Rice paper rolls of shrimp, herbs and vermicelli with a peanut hoisin dip.","8|rice paper|8-inch rounds;12|shrimp|cooked, peeled and halved;2 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli, cooked;1 head|butter lettuce|leaves separated;1|carrots|julienned;1|cucumber|julienned;1/2 cup|mint;1/2 cup|cilantro;1/4 cup|hoisin sauce;2 tbsp|peanut butter;1 tsp|sriracha","Whisk the hoisin, peanut butter, sriracha and 2 tablespoons water into a dipping sauce.|Dip one rice paper into warm water for 10 seconds until just pliable and lay it on a damp board.|Arrange 3 shrimp halves in a row near the edge, then layer lettuce, noodles, carrot, cucumber and herbs.|Fold the bottom edge up over the filling, fold in the sides and roll tightly.|Repeat with the remaining wrappers and serve with the sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3200,"Vietnamese Lemongrass Chicken","comfort","🍗",45,"Easy",9,4,"Chicken seared in a fragrant lemongrass, garlic and fish sauce marinade.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, sliced;3 stalk|lemongrass|minced, white part;4 clove|garlic|minced;2|shallot|minced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Mix the lemongrass, garlic, shallots, fish sauce, sugar, soy sauce and pepper.|Add the chicken and marinate at least 30 minutes.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Cook the chicken in batches 5 to 6 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked through.|Sprinkle with pepper flakes and serve over rice.","Vietnamese"],
[3201,"Shaking Beef","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seared garlicky cubes of beef tossed in the wok, served on greens with lime-pepper dip (bo luc lac).","1 1/2 lb|sirloin steak|1-inch cubes;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|red onion|cut in wedges;2 tbsp|butter;4 cup|lettuce|for serving;2|tomatoes|sliced;2 tbsp|lime juice;|salt|to taste","Toss the beef with half the garlic, soy sauce, oyster sauce, sugar and 1 teaspoon pepper and marinate 20 minutes.|Mix the lime juice, 1 teaspoon pepper and 1/2 teaspoon salt for the dipping sauce.|Heat 1 tablespoon oil in a wok over very high heat and sear half the beef 2 minutes, shaking the pan, until browned. Repeat with the rest.|Add the onion and remaining garlic and cook 1 minute, then add the butter and return all the beef.|Serve on a bed of lettuce and tomatoes with the dipping sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3202,"Bun Cha","comfort","🍜",60,"Medium",9,4,"Hanoi grilled pork patties and slices in sweet-tangy broth with rice noodles and herbs.","1 lb|ground pork;1 lb|pork shoulder|sliced thin;3|shallot|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|fish sauce;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;1 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|fish sauce|for dipping broth;1/3 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|rice vinegar;1|carrots|julienned;8 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli;2 cup|lettuce|for serving;1/2 cup|mint;1/2 cup|cilantro","Mix the ground pork and sliced pork with the shallots, garlic, 3 tablespoons fish sauce, 2 tablespoons sugar, honey and pepper and marinate 30 minutes.|Stir the dipping fish sauce, 1/3 cup sugar, vinegar and 1 1/2 cups warm water until dissolved, and add the carrot.|Form the ground pork into small patties.|Grill or pan-sear the patties and pork slices over medium-high heat 4 minutes per side until charred and cooked through.|Cook the noodles per package and drain.|Serve the pork in the broth with noodles, lettuce and herbs on the side.","Vietnamese"],
[3203,"Cha Gio","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Crispy Vietnamese fried spring rolls filled with pork, shrimp and mushrooms.","1/2 lb|ground pork;1/4 lb|shrimp|minced;1 cup|mushrooms|finely chopped;1|carrots|grated;2 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli, soaked and chopped;3|shallot|minced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|fish sauce;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1|eggs;20|rice paper|8-inch rounds;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|fish sauce|for dipping;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|lime juice","Mix the pork, shrimp, mushrooms, carrot, noodles, shallots, garlic, 1 tablespoon fish sauce, pepper and egg thoroughly.|Soften a rice paper in warm water for a few seconds and lay it flat.|Spoon 2 tablespoons filling near the bottom, fold the bottom over, fold in the sides and roll tight.|Heat the oil to 340°F and fry the rolls in batches 8 to 10 minutes until golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels.|Stir the dipping fish sauce, sugar, lime juice and 1/4 cup water together and serve with the rolls.","Vietnamese"],
[3204,"Pho Ga","soup","🍜",90,"Medium",9.5,6,"Clear Vietnamese chicken noodle soup with charred ginger, onion and warm spices.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1|onion|halved;1|ginger|4-inch piece, halved;3|star anise;1|cinnamon|stick;4|cloves;1 tbsp|coriander;3 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;14 oz|rice noodles|flat;2 cup|bean sprouts;1/2 cup|basil|Thai;1/2 cup|cilantro;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2|lime|cut in wedges;|salt|to taste","Char the onion and ginger directly over a flame or under the broiler 5 to 8 minutes until blackened in spots.|Toast the star anise, cinnamon, cloves and coriander in a dry pot 1 minute.|Add the chicken, onion, ginger and 3 quarts water, bring to a boil, then skim and simmer 40 minutes.|Remove the chicken, shred the meat and discard the bones and skin.|Strain the broth, season with the fish sauce, sugar and salt, and keep hot.|Cook the noodles per package and divide among bowls.|Add the chicken and ladle in the hot broth. Serve with sprouts, herbs and lime.","Vietnamese"],
[3205,"Bun Bo Xao","quick","🥩",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Lemongrass beef stir-fry over vermicelli, fresh herbs and peanuts.","1 lb|flank steak|sliced thin;2 stalk|lemongrass|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;8 oz|rice noodles|vermicelli;1|cucumber|julienned;1|carrots|julienned;2 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2 cup|mint;1/4 cup|peanuts|crushed;1/4 cup|fish sauce|for dressing;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|sugar","Marinate the beef with the lemongrass, garlic, 2 tablespoons fish sauce and 1 tablespoon sugar for 15 minutes.|Stir the dressing fish sauce, lime juice, 2 tablespoons sugar and 3 tablespoons water.|Cook the noodles per package, rinse and drain.|Heat the oil in a wok over high heat and sear the beef 2 to 3 minutes until browned.|Divide the noodles, lettuce, cucumber, carrot and mint among bowls and top with beef and peanuts.|Drizzle with the dressing.","Vietnamese"],
[3206,"Com Ga","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,4,"Vietnamese poached chicken over ginger-scented rice with a scallion dipping sauce.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1|ginger|2-inch piece, sliced;1|onion|halved;2 cup|rice|jasmine, rinsed;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;2 tbsp|fish sauce;1 tbsp|lime juice;1 tsp|sugar;1|cucumber|sliced;|salt|to taste","Cover the chicken with water in a pot, add the ginger, onion and 1 tablespoon salt and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat, cover and simmer 25 minutes until the chicken reaches 175°F.|Remove the chicken and keep warm, reserving the broth.|Sauté the garlic in 1 tablespoon oil 1 minute, add the rice and stir 1 minute, then add 3 cups strained broth and cook covered 18 minutes.|Heat the remaining oil and pour over the green onion with the fish sauce, lime juice and sugar to make a dipping sauce.|Chop the chicken and serve over the rice with cucumber and sauce.","Vietnamese"],
[3207,"Chicken Adobo","comfort","🍗",55,"Easy",9,4,"The Filipino national dish: chicken braised in soy sauce, vinegar and garlic.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|apple cider vinegar;1 head|garlic|cloves smashed;3|bay leaves;1 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Combine the chicken, soy sauce, vinegar, garlic, bay leaves and pepper and marinate 30 minutes.|Lift the chicken from the marinade and pat dry.|Heat the oil in a large pot over medium-high heat and brown the chicken 4 minutes per side.|Add the marinade and 1/2 cup water, bring to a boil, cover and simmer 30 minutes.|Uncover, add the sugar and simmer 8 to 10 minutes until the sauce reduces and thickens.|Serve over rice.","Filipino"],
[3208,"Lumpia Shanghai","sides","🥟",60,"Medium",7.5,8,"Thin, crisp Filipino spring rolls stuffed with seasoned pork and vegetables.","1 lb|ground pork;1|carrots|finely grated;1/2|onion|minced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|green onion|sliced;1|eggs;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|salt;30|lumpia wrappers|spring roll wrappers;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/2 cup|sweet chili sauce|for dipping","Mix the pork, carrot, onion, garlic, green onion, egg, soy sauce, pepper and salt well.|Place about 1 tablespoon filling near the corner of a wrapper and roll up tightly, folding in the sides.|Seal the edge with a dab of water.|Heat the oil to 350°F.|Fry the rolls in batches 4 to 5 minutes, turning, until deep golden and cooked through.|Drain on paper towels and serve with sweet chili sauce.","Filipino"],
[3209,"Huli Huli Chicken","comfort","🍍",60,"Easy",9,6,"Hawaiian rotisserie-style chicken glazed with a sweet pineapple, ginger and soy sauce.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;3/4 cup|pineapple|juice;1/2 cup|soy sauce;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1/4 cup|ketchup;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Whisk the pineapple juice, soy sauce, sugar, ketchup, ginger, garlic, vinegar and pepper.|Reserve 1 cup of the sauce, and marinate the chicken in the rest for at least 4 hours.|Simmer the reserved sauce in a small pot 8 to 10 minutes until thickened to a glaze.|Heat a grill to medium or the oven to 400°F.|Cook the chicken 30 to 35 minutes, turning often, until 175°F inside.|Brush with the glaze during the last 10 minutes and serve.","Hawaiian"],
[3210,"Loco Moco","comfort","🍳",40,"Easy",9,4,"Hawaiian comfort plate: rice topped with a beef patty, fried egg and brown gravy.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1/4 cup|breadcrumbs;1|egg;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|sliced;3 tbsp|flour;2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|soy sauce;4|eggs|for frying;4 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Mix the beef, breadcrumbs, egg, salt and pepper and form 4 patties.|Cook the patties in a skillet over medium-high heat 4 to 5 minutes per side until cooked through. Remove.|In the same pan, melt the butter and cook the onion 4 minutes, then stir in the flour for 1 minute.|Whisk in the broth and soy sauce and simmer 5 minutes until the gravy thickens.|Fry the eggs sunny side up.|Layer rice, patty and egg on each plate and ladle on the gravy.","Hawaiian"],
[3211,"Chicken Parmesan","comfort","🍗",45,"Medium",9,4,"Crisp breaded chicken cutlets under marinara and melted mozzarella, served over spaghetti.","2|chicken breast|about 1 1/2 lb, sliced in half horizontally;1/2 cup|flour|;2|eggs|beaten;1 cup|panko|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, divided;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|olive oil|for frying;1 1/2 cup|marinara sauce|;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;8 oz|spaghetti|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pound the chicken cutlets to an even 1/2 inch thickness and season with salt and pepper.|Set up three shallow dishes: flour, beaten eggs, and panko mixed with 1/4 cup parmesan and the Italian seasoning.|Dredge each cutlet in flour, dip in egg, then press into the panko mixture to coat well.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Fry the cutlets 3 minutes per side until golden, then move to a baking sheet.|Spoon marinara over each cutlet, top with mozzarella and the remaining parmesan, and bake 10 to 12 minutes until bubbly and the chicken reaches 165°F.|Meanwhile boil the spaghetti in salted water until al dente and drain.|Serve the chicken over the spaghetti with extra sauce and parsley.","Italian"],
[3212,"Chicken Piccata","quick","🍋",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin pan-seared chicken in a bright lemon, caper and butter sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced in half horizontally into 4 cutlets;1/2 cup|flour|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 tbsp|olive oil|;4 tbsp|butter|divided;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|white wine|;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;3 tbsp|lemon juice|;3 tbsp|capers|drained;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Pound the cutlets to 1/2 inch thick, season with salt and pepper, and dredge in flour, shaking off the excess.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the chicken 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden and cooked through. Move to a plate.|Lower the heat to medium, add the garlic, and cook 30 seconds.|Pour in the wine and scrape up the browned bits. Simmer 2 minutes, then add the broth and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes until slightly reduced.|Whisk in the remaining 3 tablespoons butter and the capers.|Return the chicken to the pan and spoon the sauce over it for 1 minute. Sprinkle with parsley and serve.","Italian"],
[3213,"Chicken Marsala","comfort","🍄",35,"Easy",9,4,"Golden chicken cutlets and mushrooms simmered in a rich Marsala wine sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 thin cutlets;1/2 cup|flour|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 tbsp|butter|divided;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3/4 cup|marsala wine|;3/4 cup|chicken broth|;1/4 cup|heavy cream|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Pound the chicken to 1/2 inch thick, season, and dredge in flour.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Brown the chicken 3 to 4 minutes per side and remove to a plate.|Add 1 tablespoon butter and the mushrooms. Cook 5 to 6 minutes until browned, then add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Pour in the Marsala and simmer 3 minutes, scraping the pan.|Add the broth and simmer 5 minutes until reduced by about a third. Stir in the cream and remaining butter.|Return the chicken to the pan and simmer 3 minutes until cooked through. Top with parsley.","Italian"],
[3214,"Shrimp Scampi","quick","🍤",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Garlicky shrimp in a lemon-butter white wine sauce tossed with linguine.","12 oz|linguine|;1 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 tbsp|butter|;5 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/2 cup|white wine|;2 tbsp|lemon juice|;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Boil the linguine in salted water until al dente. Save 1/2 cup of the pasta water, then drain.|Pat the shrimp dry and season with salt and pepper.|Heat the olive oil and 1 tablespoon butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Cook the shrimp 1 to 2 minutes per side until just pink, then remove.|Lower the heat, add the remaining butter, garlic, and red pepper flakes, and cook 30 seconds.|Add the wine and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes.|Toss in the linguine, shrimp, and a splash of pasta water until glossy. Finish with parsley.","Italian"],
[3215,"Spaghetti and Meatballs","comfort","🍝",60,"Medium",9,6,"Tender baked meatballs simmered in a simple tomato sauce over spaghetti.","1 lb|ground beef|;1/2 lb|ground pork|;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs|;1/4 cup|milk|;2|eggs|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;2 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz each;1 tsp|dried basil|;1 lb|spaghetti|","Heat the oven to 400°F. Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes.|Mix the beef, pork, soaked crumbs, eggs, parmesan, half the garlic, parsley, salt, and pepper gently. Roll into about 24 meatballs.|Bake on a lined sheet pan 18 to 20 minutes until browned and cooked through.|Meanwhile heat the olive oil in a large pot and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the remaining garlic for 30 seconds.|Stir in the crushed tomatoes, basil, and a pinch of salt. Add the meatballs and simmer 20 minutes.|Cook the spaghetti in salted water until al dente, drain, and serve topped with meatballs and sauce.","Italian"],
[3216,"Cacio e Pepe","quick","🧀",20,"Medium",8.5,4,"Roman pasta with just pecorino, black pepper and starchy pasta water.","1 lb|spaghetti|;2 tsp|black pepper|freshly cracked;2 cup|pecorino romano|finely grated;2 tbsp|butter|optional for richness;|salt|to taste","Boil the spaghetti in well-salted water, using less water than usual so it stays starchy. Cook until 1 minute shy of al dente.|Toast the pepper in a large dry skillet over medium heat for 1 minute.|Ladle in 1 cup of pasta water and the butter and bring to a simmer.|Use tongs to move the pasta into the skillet and cook 1 minute, tossing.|Take the pan off the heat, add the pecorino in handfuls, and toss hard, adding splashes of pasta water until the sauce is smooth and creamy.|Serve right away with extra pepper.","Italian"],
[3217,"Penne alla Vodka","comfort","🍝",30,"Easy",9,4,"Penne in a creamy blush tomato sauce with a splash of vodka and parmesan.","1 lb|penne|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|tomato paste|;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/3 cup|vodka|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;3/4 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|basil|torn;|salt|to taste","Boil the penne in salted water until al dente. Save 1 cup of pasta water and drain.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato paste and cook 2 minutes until it darkens.|Add the vodka and simmer 2 minutes until mostly evaporated.|Add the crushed tomatoes and simmer 10 minutes, then stir in the cream and salt.|Toss in the penne and parmesan, loosening with pasta water. Top with basil.","Italian"],
[3218,"Lasagna Bolognese","comfort","🍝",180,"Medium",9,10,"Layers of pasta, slow-simmered meat sauce, creamy bechamel and parmesan.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;1|carrots|finely diced;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;1 lb|ground beef|;1/2 lb|ground pork|;1/2 cup|white wine|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste|;|salt|to taste;4 tbsp|butter|;1/3 cup|flour|;3 cup|milk|;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|ground;12|lasagna noodles|;1 1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded","Heat the oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 8 minutes. Add the beef and pork and brown 8 minutes, breaking it up.|Add the wine and cook 3 minutes, then stir in the tomatoes, paste, and salt. Simmer partly covered 1 hour, stirring occasionally.|For the bechamel, melt the butter, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, and slowly add the milk. Simmer 5 to 8 minutes until thick, then season with salt and nutmeg.|Boil the noodles 2 minutes short of the package time and drain. Heat the oven to 375°F.|In a 9x13 dish layer sauce, noodles, bechamel, and parmesan. Repeat to make 3 layers, finishing with bechamel, parmesan, and mozzarella.|Cover with foil and bake 30 minutes, then uncover and bake 20 minutes until golden. Rest 15 minutes before cutting.","Italian"],
[3219,"Tiramisu","treats","🍰",40,"Medium",9,9,"No-bake dessert of espresso-soaked ladyfingers layered with mascarpone cream and cocoa.","4|eggs|yolks only;2/3 cup|sugar|;16 oz|mascarpone|;1 cup|heavy cream|;1 1/2 cup|espresso|strong, cooled;3 tbsp|coffee liqueur|optional;24|ladyfingers|;2 tbsp|cocoa powder|unsweetened","Whisk the yolks and sugar in a heatproof bowl set over simmering water for 8 minutes until thick and pale and 160°F. Cool for 10 minutes.|Beat in the mascarpone until smooth.|Whip the cream to stiff peaks and fold it into the mascarpone mixture.|Mix the espresso and liqueur in a shallow dish. Dip each ladyfinger briefly, 1 to 2 seconds per side, and line the bottom of an 8x8 dish.|Spread half the cream over the ladyfingers, add a second dipped layer, then the remaining cream.|Chill at least 6 hours, then dust with cocoa before serving.","Italian"],
[3220,"Cannoli Dip","treats","🍨",15,"Very easy",9,10,"Sweet ricotta and mascarpone dip with mini chocolate chips, scooped up with cannoli shells or cookies.","15 oz|ricotta|well drained;8 oz|mascarpone|;1 cup|powdered sugar|;1 tsp|vanilla|;1/2 tsp|cinnamon|;3/4 cup|chocolate chips|mini;|waffle cookies|for dipping, to taste","Drain the ricotta in a fine strainer for 15 minutes, pressing out extra liquid.|Beat the ricotta, mascarpone, powdered sugar, vanilla, and cinnamon until smooth.|Fold in 1/2 cup of the chocolate chips.|Spoon into a bowl and top with the remaining chips.|Chill for 30 minutes, then serve with cannoli shells, waffle cookies, or graham crackers.","Italian"],
[3221,"Bruschetta","sides","🍅",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Toasted garlic bread topped with fresh tomato, basil and olive oil.","1|french bread|baguette, sliced 1/2 inch;4|tomatoes|ripe Roma, diced;1/4 cup|basil|thinly sliced;2 clove|garlic|1 minced, 1 halved;3 tbsp|olive oil|divided;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F. Brush the bread slices with 2 tablespoons olive oil and bake on a sheet pan 8 to 10 minutes until crisp and golden.|Mix the tomatoes, basil, minced garlic, remaining oil, salt, and pepper. Let sit 10 minutes.|Rub the toasted slices with the cut side of the halved garlic.|Spoon the tomato mixture on top, drizzle with balsamic glaze, and serve right away.","Italian"],
[3222,"Minestrone","soup","🥣",50,"Easy",9.5,8,"Hearty Italian vegetable soup with beans, small pasta and a parmesan finish.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;6 cup|vegetable broth|;1 can|kidney beans|15 oz, drained;1|zucchini|diced;1 cup|green beans|cut in 1 inch pieces;1 cup|pasta shells|small;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;2 cup|spinach|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated","Heat the olive oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 7 minutes.|Add the garlic and Italian seasoning for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, broth, beans, zucchini, and green beans. Bring to a boil and simmer 15 minutes.|Stir in the pasta and cook 8 to 10 minutes until tender.|Add the spinach until wilted, then season with salt and pepper.|Ladle into bowls and top with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3223,"Caprese Salad","sides","🍅",10,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Ripe tomato, fresh mozzarella and basil with olive oil and balsamic.","4|tomatoes|large ripe, sliced;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|sliced;1/4 cup|basil|whole leaves;3 tbsp|olive oil|;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Slice the tomatoes and mozzarella about 1/4 inch thick.|Arrange them on a platter in overlapping rows, tucking a basil leaf between slices.|Drizzle with olive oil and balsamic glaze.|Season with flaky salt and pepper and serve at room temperature.","Italian"],
[3224,"Panna Cotta","treats","🍮",20,"Easy",9,6,"Silky chilled vanilla cream dessert with berry sauce.","1 packet|gelatin|unflavored, 2 1/4 tsp;3 tbsp|milk|cold;2 cup|heavy cream|;1/3 cup|sugar|;1 tsp|vanilla|;1 cup|strawberries|sliced;1 tbsp|sugar|for the berries","Sprinkle the gelatin over the cold milk and let it bloom for 5 minutes.|Heat the cream and sugar in a saucepan until steaming and the sugar dissolves. Do not boil.|Remove from the heat, whisk in the gelatin until fully dissolved, then add the vanilla.|Pour into 6 ramekins or glasses and chill at least 4 hours until set.|Toss the strawberries with 1 tablespoon sugar and let them release their juices.|Spoon the berries over the panna cotta, or unmold onto plates.","Italian"],
[3225,"Spaghetti Aglio e Olio","quick","🍝",20,"Very easy",8.5,4,"Spaghetti tossed in garlic-infused olive oil with chili flakes and parsley.","1 lb|spaghetti|;1/3 cup|olive oil|;6 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes|;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, optional;|salt|to taste","Boil the spaghetti in well-salted water until al dente. Save 1 cup of pasta water and drain.|Meanwhile warm the olive oil and garlic in a large skillet over medium-low heat 3 to 4 minutes until the garlic is pale gold. Do not let it brown.|Add the red pepper flakes for 30 seconds.|Add the spaghetti and 1/2 cup pasta water and toss over medium heat 1 minute until the sauce clings.|Off the heat stir in parsley, add more pasta water if needed, and serve with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3226,"Chicken Saltimbocca","quick","🍗",30,"Medium",8.5,4,"Chicken cutlets topped with prosciutto and sage, pan-seared in a white wine butter sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;8|sage|fresh leaves;4 slice|prosciutto|;1/4 cup|flour|;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 tbsp|butter|;1/2 cup|white wine|;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;1 tbsp|lemon juice|","Pound the cutlets to 1/2 inch, season with pepper, and lay 2 sage leaves on each, then wrap with a slice of prosciutto, pressing to stick.|Lightly dust the cutlets with flour on the chicken side only.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Place the cutlets prosciutto-side down and cook 3 minutes, then flip and cook 3 to 4 minutes until 165°F. Remove to a plate.|Add the wine to the pan and simmer 2 minutes, then add the broth and lemon juice and simmer 3 minutes.|Whisk in the butter, return the chicken, and spoon the sauce over.","Italian"],
[3227,"Chicken Souvlaki","light","🍢",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Lemon-oregano marinated chicken skewers grilled and served with pita and tzatziki.","2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless skinless, cut in 1 inch cubes;1/4 cup|olive oil|;1/4 cup|lemon juice|;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|oregano|dried;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1 tsp|paprika|;4|pita|;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving;1|cucumber|sliced;1|tomatoes|sliced","Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, salt, pepper, and paprika. Toss with the chicken and marinate 30 minutes to 4 hours in the fridge.|Soak 8 wooden skewers in water if using them, then thread the chicken on.|Grill over medium-high heat or cook in a grill pan 10 to 12 minutes, turning, until browned and 165°F.|Warm the pita briefly on the grill.|Serve the skewers in pita with yogurt or tzatziki, cucumber, and tomato.","Greek"],
[3228,"Chicken Gyro Bowl","light","🥙",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Spiced chicken over rice with cucumber, tomato, feta and tzatziki.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|boneless skinless, sliced;3 tbsp|olive oil|;2 tbsp|lemon juice|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|oregano|;1 tsp|cumin|;1 tsp|paprika|;|salt|to taste;2 cup|rice|cooked;1|cucumber|diced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|feta|crumbled;1 cup|greek yogurt|;|olives|kalamata, to taste","Toss the chicken with 2 tablespoons olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, cumin, paprika, and salt. Marinate 15 minutes or up to overnight.|Heat the remaining oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken 8 to 10 minutes until browned and cooked through.|Mix the yogurt with a pinch of salt and a squeeze of lemon for a quick sauce, or use tzatziki.|Divide the rice among bowls and top with chicken, cucumber, tomatoes, onion, feta, and olives.|Drizzle with the yogurt sauce.","Greek"],
[3229,"Spanakopita","sides","🥬",75,"Medium",7.5,8,"Flaky phyllo pie filled with spinach, feta, dill and herbs.","2 lb|frozen spinach|thawed and squeezed very dry;2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|finely diced;4|green onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;8 oz|feta|crumbled;1 cup|ricotta|;3|eggs|beaten;1/4 cup|dill|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;|black pepper|to taste;1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;3/4 cup|butter|melted","Heat the oven to 375°F. Cook the onion in the olive oil 5 minutes, then add the green onion and garlic for 2 minutes. Cool slightly.|Combine the spinach, onion mixture, feta, ricotta, eggs, dill, parsley, nutmeg, and pepper.|Brush a 9x13 dish with butter. Layer 10 sheets of phyllo, brushing each with butter, keeping the rest covered with a damp towel.|Spread the filling over the phyllo, then layer 10 more buttered sheets on top. Tuck in the edges.|Score the top into squares with a sharp knife, cutting through the top layers.|Bake 45 to 50 minutes until deep golden. Rest 10 minutes before cutting.","Greek"],
[3230,"Pastitsio","comfort","🍝",120,"Medium",9,10,"Greek baked pasta with cinnamon-spiced meat sauce and thick bechamel.","1 lb|penne|or ziti;1 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;1 lb|ground beef|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|tomato paste|;1 can|crushed tomatoes|15 oz;1/2 cup|red wine|optional, or use broth;1/2 tsp|cinnamon|;1 tsp|oregano|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4 tbsp|butter|;1/2 cup|flour|;4 cup|milk|warm;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;3|eggs|beaten;1 cup|parmesan|grated, divided","Boil the pasta 2 minutes short of al dente, drain, and toss with 1/2 cup parmesan.|Brown the onion and beef in the olive oil 8 minutes. Add the garlic, tomato paste, tomatoes, wine, cinnamon, oregano, salt, and pepper and simmer 25 minutes until thick.|For the bechamel melt the butter, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the milk. Cook, stirring, 8 to 10 minutes until thick. Season with salt and nutmeg.|Cool the sauce 5 minutes, then whisk in the eggs and 1/4 cup parmesan.|Heat the oven to 350°F. Layer half the pasta in a 9x13 dish, then all of the meat sauce, then the remaining pasta.|Spread the bechamel on top, sprinkle with the remaining parmesan, and bake 40 to 45 minutes until golden. Rest 15 minutes before cutting.","Greek"],
[3231,"Avgolemono Soup","soup","🍋",40,"Medium",9.5,6,"Silky Greek chicken soup with rice, thickened with egg and lemon.","8 cup|chicken broth|;1/2 cup|rice|long grain;2 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;3|eggs|;1/3 cup|lemon juice|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|dill|chopped","Bring the broth to a boil in a large pot, add the rice, and simmer 15 to 18 minutes until tender.|Add the shredded chicken and warm through. Turn the heat to low.|Whisk the eggs in a bowl until frothy, then whisk in the lemon juice.|Slowly ladle in 2 cups of hot broth, a little at a time, whisking constantly to temper the eggs.|Stir the egg mixture back into the pot and heat gently 3 to 5 minutes without boiling until slightly thickened.|Season with salt and pepper and serve with dill.","Greek"],
[3232,"Greek Salad","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Chunky tomato, cucumber, red onion, olives and feta with oregano and olive oil.","4|tomatoes|cut in wedges;1|cucumber|sliced in half moons;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1|bell pepper|green, sliced;1/2 cup|olives|kalamata;6 oz|feta|a slab or crumbled;1/4 cup|olive oil|;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar|;1 tsp|oregano|dried;|salt|to taste","Combine the tomatoes, cucumber, onion, bell pepper, and olives in a large bowl.|Whisk the olive oil, vinegar, oregano, and salt and pour over the vegetables. Toss gently.|Top with the feta and a sprinkle of oregano.|Serve right away.","Greek"],
[3233,"Tzatziki","sides","🥒",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Cool Greek yogurt dip with grated cucumber, garlic, lemon and dill.","1|cucumber|grated and squeezed dry;2 cup|greek yogurt|;2 clove|garlic|finely minced;1 tbsp|olive oil|;1 tbsp|lemon juice|;1 tbsp|dill|chopped;|salt|to taste","Grate the cucumber, salt it lightly, and let it sit 10 minutes, then squeeze out all the liquid in a towel.|Stir the cucumber into the yogurt with the garlic, olive oil, lemon juice, and dill.|Season with salt and chill at least 30 minutes so the flavors blend.|Serve with pita, vegetables, or grilled meat.","Greek"],
[3234,"Baklava","treats","🍯",90,"Medium",9,24,"Crisp phyllo layered with spiced walnuts and soaked in honey syrup.","1 lb|walnuts|finely chopped;1/2 cup|sugar|for the filling;1 tsp|cinnamon|;1/4 tsp|cloves|ground;1 lb|phyllo dough|thawed;1 cup|butter|melted;1 cup|water|;1 cup|sugar|for the syrup;1/2 cup|honey|;1|lemon|a few strips of peel and 1 tbsp juice;1 tsp|vanilla|","Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix the walnuts, 1/2 cup sugar, cinnamon, and cloves.|Brush a 9x13 pan with butter. Layer 8 phyllo sheets, brushing each with butter, trimming to fit.|Spread with one third of the nut mix, then top with 4 buttered sheets. Repeat twice more, ending with 8 buttered sheets on top.|Cut into diamonds or squares all the way through before baking.|Bake 45 to 50 minutes until deep golden.|Meanwhile simmer 1 cup water, 1 cup sugar, honey, lemon peel, and juice for 10 minutes, then stir in the vanilla. Cool.|Pour the cooled syrup over the hot baklava and let it set for at least 4 hours before serving.","Greek"],
[3235,"Greek Lemon Potatoes","sides","🥔",75,"Easy",7.5,6,"Oven-roasted potatoes soaked in lemon, garlic, oregano and olive oil until golden and tender.","3 lb|potatoes|yukon gold, cut in wedges;1/3 cup|olive oil|;1/3 cup|lemon juice|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|oregano|dried;1 cup|chicken broth|;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Put the potatoes in a large roasting pan and add the olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, oregano, salt, and pepper. Toss well.|Pour the broth around the potatoes and spread them in a single layer.|Roast 60 to 70 minutes, turning once or twice, until the potatoes are golden and the liquid has been absorbed.|Sprinkle with parsley and a squeeze of lemon.","Greek"],
[3236,"Keftedes (Greek Meatballs)","comfort","🧆",45,"Easy",9,6,"Herby beef and mint meatballs, pan-fried and served with tzatziki and pita.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs|;1|eggs|;2 tbsp|mint|fresh, chopped;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|oregano|;1 tsp|salt|;1/2 tsp|black pepper|;1/4 cup|flour|for dusting;1/3 cup|olive oil|for frying;4|pita|;1 cup|greek yogurt|for serving","Mix the beef, onion, garlic, breadcrumbs, egg, mint, parsley, oregano, salt, and pepper until just combined.|Chill 15 minutes, then roll into about 24 balls and dust lightly with flour.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat.|Fry the meatballs in batches 8 to 10 minutes, turning, until browned and cooked through at 160°F.|Serve with warm pita and yogurt or tzatziki.","Greek"],
[3237,"Marry Me Chicken","comfort","💍",35,"Easy",9,4,"Seared chicken in a creamy sun-dried tomato and parmesan sauce.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 tsp|paprika|;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|sun-dried tomatoes|chopped;3/4 cup|chicken broth|;3/4 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes|;2 tbsp|basil|chopped","Season the chicken with salt, pepper, and paprika.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Sear the chicken 4 minutes per side until golden. Remove to a plate.|Lower the heat to medium and cook the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes 1 minute.|Add the broth, cream, parmesan, Italian seasoning, and red pepper flakes. Simmer 4 to 5 minutes until slightly thickened.|Return the chicken to the sauce and simmer 5 minutes until cooked to 165°F.|Top with basil and serve with pasta, rice, or bread.","American"],
[3238,"Tuscan Chicken","comfort","🍗",35,"Easy",9,4,"Pan-seared chicken in a creamy garlic sauce with spinach and sun-dried tomatoes.","2|chicken breast|sliced into 4 cutlets;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|olive oil|;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|sun-dried tomatoes|chopped;1/2 cup|chicken broth|;1 cup|heavy cream|;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;3 cup|spinach|","Season the chicken with salt and pepper.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the chicken 5 minutes per side until golden and 165°F. Remove to a plate.|Add the garlic and sun-dried tomatoes to the pan for 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and cream, add the parmesan and Italian seasoning, and simmer 4 to 5 minutes until thickened.|Stir in the spinach until wilted, about 2 minutes.|Return the chicken and spoon the sauce over it. Serve with pasta or mashed potatoes.","Italian"],
[3239,"Chicken Cordon Bleu","comfort","🧀",55,"Medium",9,4,"Chicken breast rolled around ham and Swiss, breaded and baked until crisp.","4|chicken breast|small, or 2 large halved;4 slice|deli ham|thin;4 slice|swiss cheese|;1/2 cup|flour|;2|eggs|beaten;1 cup|panko|;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tsp|garlic powder|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;3 tbsp|butter|melted;1 tbsp|dijon mustard|","Heat the oven to 400°F. Butterfly each chicken breast and pound to 1/4 inch thick. Season with salt and pepper.|Spread a little Dijon on each, lay ham and Swiss on top, roll up tightly, and secure with toothpicks.|Dredge in flour, dip in egg, and coat in panko mixed with parmesan and garlic powder.|Place seam-side down on a lined baking sheet and drizzle with the melted butter.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden and 165°F inside. Rest 5 minutes and remove the toothpicks.","French"],
[3240,"Lemon Herb Roast Chicken","comfort","🍋",105,"Easy",9,6,"Whole roast chicken with crisp golden skin, lemon, garlic and herbs.","4 lb|whole chicken|patted very dry;4 tbsp|butter|softened;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|fresh thyme|chopped;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1|lemon|zested, then halved;1 1/2 tsp|salt|;1 tsp|black pepper|;1|onion|quartered;1 lb|baby potatoes|halved;3|carrots|cut in chunks","Heat the oven to 425°F. Mix the butter, garlic, thyme, parsley, lemon zest, salt, and pepper.|Loosen the skin over the breast and rub half the herb butter underneath. Rub the rest all over the outside.|Stuff the cavity with the lemon halves and onion. Tie the legs together.|Scatter the potatoes and carrots in a roasting pan and set the chicken on top, breast side up.|Roast 1 hour 10 minutes to 1 hour 25 minutes until the thickest part of the thigh reaches 165°F.|Rest 15 minutes before carving.","American"],
[3241,"Honey Mustard Chicken","quick","🍯",35,"Very easy",8.5,4,"Baked chicken thighs glazed with a tangy honey Dijon sauce.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in skin-on;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/4 cup|honey|;1/4 cup|dijon mustard|;2 tbsp|mustard|whole grain;2 tbsp|olive oil|;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F. Pat the chicken dry and season with salt and pepper.|Whisk the honey, Dijon, whole grain mustard, olive oil, garlic, and paprika.|Toss the chicken in half of the sauce and place skin-side up in a baking dish.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes until 175°F, brushing with the remaining sauce for the last 5 minutes.|Garnish with parsley.","American"],
[3242,"Chicken Alfredo Bake","comfort","🧀",50,"Easy",9,6,"Penne and chicken in creamy Alfredo sauce, topped with melted mozzarella.","1 lb|penne|;2 tbsp|butter|;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|flour|;2 cup|heavy cream|;1 cup|milk|;1 1/2 cup|parmesan|grated, divided;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/4 tsp|nutmeg|;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the penne 2 minutes short of al dente and drain.|Melt the butter in a large pot and cook the garlic 30 seconds. Whisk in the flour for 1 minute.|Slowly add the cream and milk, whisking, and simmer 4 minutes until thickened.|Stir in 1 cup parmesan, salt, pepper, and nutmeg until smooth.|Fold in the penne and chicken and transfer to a 9x13 dish.|Top with the mozzarella and remaining parmesan. Bake 20 to 25 minutes until bubbly and golden. Top with parsley.","Italian"],
[3243,"Bang Bang Chicken","quick","🌶️",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crispy chicken bites tossed in a creamy, sweet and spicy bang bang sauce.","1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch cubes;1/2 cup|cornstarch|;1 tsp|garlic powder|;1 tsp|paprika|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/3 cup|vegetable oil|;1/3 cup|mayonnaise|;1/3 cup|sweet chili sauce|;1 tbsp|sriracha|;1 tbsp|honey|;2|green onion|sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Toss the chicken with the cornstarch, garlic powder, paprika, salt, and pepper until well coated.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat. Fry the chicken in batches 5 to 6 minutes until golden and crisp, then drain on paper towels.|Whisk the mayonnaise, sweet chili sauce, sriracha, and honey in a large bowl.|Toss the hot chicken in the sauce to coat.|Serve over rice topped with green onion.","American"],
[3244,"Chicken Tortellini Bake","comfort","🍝",40,"Very easy",9,6,"Cheese tortellini and chicken baked in marinara with plenty of melted mozzarella.","20 oz|tortellini|refrigerated cheese;2 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;2 cup|marinara sauce|;1/2 cup|heavy cream|;2 cup|spinach|;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the tortellini 2 minutes less than the package says and drain.|In a large bowl mix the marinara, cream, garlic, Italian seasoning, and salt.|Stir in the tortellini, chicken, and spinach and pour into a 9x13 dish.|Top with the mozzarella and parmesan.|Cover with foil and bake 15 minutes, then uncover and bake 10 minutes until bubbly and golden.","Italian"],
[3245,"Zuppa Toscana","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy Italian sausage soup with potatoes, kale and bacon.","1 lb|italian sausage|mild or hot, casings removed;4 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes|;6 cup|chicken broth|;1 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|sliced 1/4 inch thick;1 bunch|kale|stemmed and chopped;1 cup|heavy cream|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the sausage in a large pot over medium-high heat, breaking it up, about 7 minutes. Move to a bowl.|Cook the bacon in the same pot until crisp. Remove, leaving about 2 tablespoons of fat.|Cook the onion 5 minutes, then add the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Add the broth and potatoes and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Return the sausage and add the kale and cream. Simmer 5 minutes.|Season with salt and pepper and top with the bacon.","Italian"],
[3246,"Cabbage Roll Soup","soup","🥬",55,"Easy",9.5,8,"All the flavor of stuffed cabbage in a hearty tomato soup with beef and rice.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1|cabbage|small head, chopped about 6 cups;1 can|diced tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;4 cup|beef broth|;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tbsp|brown sugar|;1 cup|rice|cooked;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef and onion in a large pot over medium-high heat 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the cabbage, tomatoes, tomato sauce, broth, Worcestershire, paprika, and brown sugar.|Bring to a boil, then simmer 30 minutes until the cabbage is very tender.|Stir in the cooked rice and heat through. Season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3247,"Beef Chili","soup","🌶️",75,"Easy",9.5,8,"Classic thick beef and bean chili with tomatoes and warm spices.","2 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;1|bell pepper|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|chili powder|;2 tsp|cumin|;1 tsp|paprika|;1 tsp|oregano|;1 can|diced tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;2 tbsp|tomato paste|;1 can|kidney beans|15 oz, drained;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|beef broth|;|salt|to taste;|sour cream|for serving, to taste;|cheddar|shredded, for serving, to taste","Brown the beef with the onion and bell pepper in a large pot over medium-high heat 8 to 10 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the garlic, chili powder, cumin, paprika, and oregano and stir 1 minute.|Stir in the tomato paste, diced tomatoes, tomato sauce, and broth.|Bring to a boil, then simmer partly covered 45 minutes, stirring now and then.|Add the beans and simmer 15 minutes more. Season with salt.|Serve topped with cheddar and sour cream.","American"],
[3248,"Pasta e Fagioli","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Rustic Italian soup of small pasta and white beans in a tomato broth.","2 tbsp|olive oil|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;4 cup|chicken broth|;2 can|cannellini beans|15 oz each, drained;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 cup|pasta shells|small, or ditalini;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated","Heat the oil in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 7 minutes.|Add the garlic and Italian seasoning for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, broth, and 1 can of beans. Mash the other can of beans and add it to thicken the soup.|Bring to a simmer, stir in the pasta, and cook 8 to 10 minutes until tender.|Season with salt and pepper and serve topped with parmesan.","Italian"],
[3249,"Stracciatella Soup","soup","🥣",25,"Easy",9.5,4,"Italian egg drop soup with parmesan and spinach in clear chicken broth.","6 cup|chicken broth|;3|eggs|;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/8 tsp|nutmeg|;3 cup|spinach|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring the broth to a gentle simmer in a medium pot.|Whisk the eggs with the parmesan, parsley, and nutmeg.|Add the spinach to the broth and cook 1 minute.|Slowly pour the egg mixture into the simmering broth while stirring in one direction so it forms thin ribbons.|Cook 1 to 2 minutes, season with salt and pepper, and serve with extra parmesan.","Italian"],
[3250,"Hamburger Soup","soup","🍲",45,"Very easy",9.5,6,"Easy ground beef and vegetable soup in a savory tomato broth.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|sliced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2|potatoes|diced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;4 cup|beef broth|;1 tbsp|tomato paste|;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tsp|italian seasoning|;1 cup|frozen peas|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef with the onion in a large pot over medium-high heat 6 to 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the carrots, celery, and garlic and cook 3 minutes.|Stir in the potatoes, tomatoes, broth, tomato paste, Worcestershire, and Italian seasoning.|Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes are tender.|Add the peas, cook 3 minutes, and season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3251,"Chicken Pot Pie Soup","soup","🥧",40,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy chicken and vegetable soup with all the flavor of pot pie, topped with biscuit crumbs.","4 tbsp|butter|;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/3 cup|flour|;4 cup|chicken broth|;1 cup|milk|;1 lb|potatoes|diced small;3 cup|rotisserie chicken|shredded;1 cup|frozen peas|;1 tsp|dried thyme|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;4|refrigerated biscuits|baked and crumbled","Melt the butter in a large pot and cook the onion, carrot, and celery 6 minutes. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the broth and milk. Add the potatoes and thyme and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Add the chicken and peas and cook 5 minutes.|Season with salt and pepper and serve topped with crumbled biscuits.","American"],
[3252,"Cheeseburger Soup","soup","🍔",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Creamy potato soup with ground beef and melted cheddar.","1 lb|ground beef|;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|butter|;3 tbsp|flour|;3 cup|beef broth|;1 lb|potatoes|diced small;2 cup|milk|;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 tbsp|worcestershire|;1 tbsp|ketchup|;1 tbsp|mustard|;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;|pickles|chopped, for topping, to taste","Brown the beef and onion in a large pot 7 minutes. Drain excess fat and add the garlic for 1 minute.|Move the beef to a bowl. Melt the butter in the pot and whisk in the flour for 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the broth, add the potatoes, and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Add the milk, return the beef, and stir in the Worcestershire, ketchup, and mustard. Heat gently without boiling.|Stir in the cheddar a handful at a time until melted. Season and top with pickles.","American"],
[3253,"Sourdough Bread","baking","🍞",960,"Medium",8.5,12,"A crusty, tangy loaf with an open crumb, made with an active sourdough starter.","1 cup|sourdough starter|active, bubbly;4 cup|flour|bread flour;2 tsp|salt","Mix the starter, warm water, flour and salt into a shaggy dough and rest 30 minutes.|Do 4 sets of stretch and folds, 30 minutes apart, then let the dough rise covered at room temperature 4 to 6 hours until about 50 percent bigger.|Shape into a tight round and place seam-up in a floured bowl or banneton.|Cover and refrigerate 8 to 12 hours.|Preheat a Dutch oven in a 475°F oven for 45 minutes.|Turn the dough onto parchment, score the top with a sharp knife, and bake covered 20 minutes.|Remove the lid and bake 20 to 25 minutes more until deep golden brown.|Cool on a rack at least 1 hour before slicing.","American"],
[3254,"Classic White Sandwich Bread","baking","🍞",180,"Easy",8.5,12,"A soft, tender pan loaf that slices cleanly for sandwiches and toast.","1 1/4 cup|milk|warm;2 tsp|yeast;2 tbsp|sugar;3 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|butter|softened","Stir the warm milk, yeast and sugar together and let sit 5 minutes until foamy.|Add the flour, salt and butter and knead 8 minutes until smooth and elastic.|Let the dough rise in a covered oiled bowl 1 hour until doubled.|Shape into a loaf and place in a greased 9x5 inch pan.|Cover and let rise 45 minutes until the dough crowns above the rim.|Bake at 375°F for 30 minutes until golden and hollow-sounding when tapped.|Turn out onto a rack and brush the top with butter; cool before slicing.","American"],
[3255,"Whole Wheat Bread","baking","🍞",200,"Easy",8.5,12,"A hearty, lightly sweet whole wheat sandwich loaf with a soft crumb.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;3 tbsp|honey;3 cup|flour|whole wheat;1 cup|flour|bread flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil","Combine the warm water, yeast and honey and let stand 5 minutes until foamy.|Add both flours, salt and olive oil and knead 10 minutes until smooth.|Let rise in an oiled covered bowl 1 hour until doubled.|Shape into a loaf and set in a greased 9x5 inch pan.|Cover and rise 40 minutes until the dough peeks over the rim.|Bake at 350°F for 35 minutes until deep brown and hollow-sounding.|Cool on a rack for 30 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3256,"Cinnamon Raisin Bread","baking","🍞",210,"Easy",8.5,12,"Soft yeast bread swirled with cinnamon sugar and plump raisins.","1 cup|milk|warm;2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1/3 cup|sugar;3 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|butter|softened;1|eggs;1 cup|raisins;1/4 cup|sugar|for the filling;2 tsp|cinnamon","Mix the warm milk, yeast and sugar and rest 5 minutes until foamy.|Add the flour, salt, butter and egg and knead 8 minutes, kneading in the raisins at the end.|Let rise covered 1 hour until doubled.|Roll the dough into a 9x18 inch rectangle, brush with a little water and sprinkle with the cinnamon sugar.|Roll up tightly from the short end, pinch the seam and place in a greased 9x5 inch pan.|Rise 45 minutes, then bake at 350°F for 40 minutes, tenting with foil if browning too fast.|Cool in the pan 10 minutes, then on a rack before slicing.","American"],
[3257,"Plain Bagels","baking","🥯",150,"Medium",8.5,8,"Chewy, shiny homemade bagels boiled in honey water and baked until golden.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|honey;4 cup|flour|bread flour;2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|honey|for the boiling water;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing","Mix the warm water, yeast and honey and let stand 5 minutes.|Stir in the flour and salt and knead 10 minutes into a very stiff dough.|Cover and rise 1 hour until puffy.|Divide into 8 pieces, roll each into a ball, poke a hole through the center and stretch to a 2 inch ring.|Rest 15 minutes while you bring a large pot of water and the honey to a gentle boil and heat the oven to 425°F.|Boil bagels 1 minute per side, then place on a parchment-lined sheet.|Brush with beaten egg and bake 20 minutes until deep golden.|Cool on a rack before slicing.","American"],
[3258,"Everything Bagels","baking","🥯",150,"Medium",8.5,8,"Chewy boiled bagels coated in sesame, poppy seeds, garlic and onion.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|honey;4 cup|flour|bread flour;2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|honey|for the boiling water;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing;3 tbsp|everything bagel seasoning","Mix the warm water, yeast and honey and rest 5 minutes until foamy.|Add flour and salt and knead 10 minutes into a stiff, smooth dough.|Cover and rise 1 hour until puffy.|Divide into 8 pieces, shape into balls, poke a hole in each and stretch into rings.|Rest 15 minutes while you boil a large pot of water with the honey and preheat the oven to 425°F.|Boil each bagel 1 minute per side and set on a parchment-lined sheet.|Brush with egg, press on the everything seasoning and bake 20 minutes until golden.|Cool on a rack before slicing.","American"],
[3259,"English Muffins","baking","🥯",120,"Medium",8.5,8,"Griddle-cooked yeast muffins with the classic nooks and crannies for butter.","1 cup|milk|warm;2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|sugar;3 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|butter|melted;1/2 cup|polenta|fine cornmeal, for dusting","Stir the warm milk, yeast and sugar and let stand 5 minutes.|Mix in the flour, salt and melted butter and knead 5 minutes until smooth.|Cover and rise 1 hour until doubled.|Roll the dough 1/2 inch thick on a cornmeal-dusted surface and cut 8 rounds with a 3 inch cutter.|Rest the rounds 30 minutes on cornmeal.|Cook in a lightly greased skillet over medium-low heat 6 to 7 minutes per side until deep golden.|If any feel doughy inside, finish in a 350°F oven for 5 minutes.|Cool, then split with a fork and toast.","British"],
[3260,"Blueberry Muffins","baking","🧁",35,"Easy",8.5,12,"Tender bakery-style muffins bursting with blueberries and a crackly sugar top.","2 cup|flour;3/4 cup|sugar;2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;2|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 1/2 cup|blueberries;2 tbsp|sugar|for topping","Heat the oven to 400°F and line a 12-cup muffin tin with liners.|Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder and salt.|In another bowl whisk the oil, eggs, milk and vanilla.|Fold the wet into the dry until just combined, then gently fold in the blueberries.|Fill the cups to the top and sprinkle with the extra sugar.|Bake 5 minutes at 400°F, then lower to 350°F and bake 15 to 18 minutes more until a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 5 minutes in the pan before moving to a rack.","American"],
[3261,"Banana Muffins","baking","🧁",35,"Very easy",8.5,12,"Moist, lightly sweet muffins made with ripe bananas.","3|banana|very ripe, mashed;1/2 cup|butter|melted;3/4 cup|sugar;1|eggs;1 tsp|vanilla;1 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 350°F and line a 12-cup muffin tin.|Mash the bananas in a large bowl and stir in the melted butter, sugar, egg and vanilla.|Sprinkle in the baking soda, salt and cinnamon, then fold in the flour until just combined.|Divide the batter among the cups.|Bake 20 to 22 minutes until golden and a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 5 minutes in the pan, then transfer to a rack.","American"],
[3262,"Bran Muffins","baking","🧁",40,"Easy",8.5,12,"Hearty, honey-sweet muffins with wheat bran and raisins.","1 1/2 cup|wheat bran;1 cup|milk;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;1/3 cup|brown sugar;1/4 cup|honey;1|eggs;1 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|raisins","Heat the oven to 375°F and grease or line a 12-cup muffin tin.|Stir the bran and milk together and let soak 10 minutes.|Whisk in the oil, brown sugar, honey and egg.|Combine the flour, baking powder, baking soda and salt and fold into the bran mixture with the raisins until just mixed.|Fill the cups about 3/4 full.|Bake 18 to 20 minutes until springy and a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool in the pan 5 minutes before removing.","American"],
[3263,"Cheese Muffins","baking","🧁",35,"Easy",8.5,12,"Savory cheddar muffins with a tender crumb, good with soup or breakfast.","2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 cup|milk;1/3 cup|vegetable oil;1|eggs;2 tbsp|chives|chopped","Heat the oven to 400°F and grease a 12-cup muffin tin.|Whisk the flour, baking powder, salt and garlic powder, then stir in 1 1/4 cups of the cheddar and the chives.|Whisk the milk, oil and egg and pour into the dry ingredients; stir until just combined.|Divide among the cups and top with the remaining cheese.|Bake 18 to 20 minutes until golden and a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 5 minutes in the pan and serve warm.","American"],
[3264,"Lemon Poppy Seed Muffins","baking","🧁",40,"Easy",8.5,12,"Bright, moist lemon muffins flecked with poppy seeds and finished with a glaze.","2 cup|flour;3/4 cup|sugar;2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|poppy seeds;3/4 cup|milk;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;2|eggs;1/4 cup|lemon juice;2 tbsp|lemon|zest;1 cup|powdered sugar|for glaze;2 tbsp|lemon juice|for glaze","Heat the oven to 375°F and line a 12-cup muffin tin.|Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder, salt and poppy seeds.|In another bowl whisk the milk, oil, eggs, lemon juice and zest.|Fold the wet into the dry until just combined.|Fill the cups 3/4 full and bake 18 to 20 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 10 minutes, then whisk the powdered sugar and lemon juice and drizzle over the muffins.","American"],
[3265,"Cinnamon Rolls","baking","🥐",180,"Medium",8.5,12,"Soft, gooey rolls swirled with brown sugar and cinnamon and topped with cream cheese icing.","1 cup|milk|warm;2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1/3 cup|sugar;3 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1/3 cup|butter|melted;2|eggs;3/4 cup|brown sugar|for filling;2 tbsp|cinnamon;1/3 cup|butter|softened, for filling;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1/4 cup|butter|softened, for icing;1 1/2 cup|powdered sugar;1 tsp|vanilla","Stir the warm milk, yeast and sugar and let stand 5 minutes.|Add the flour, salt, melted butter and eggs and knead 8 minutes into a soft dough.|Rise covered 1 hour until doubled.|Roll into a 12x18 inch rectangle, spread with softened butter and sprinkle with brown sugar and cinnamon.|Roll up from the long side and cut into 12 rolls.|Place in a greased 9x13 inch pan, cover and rise 30 minutes.|Bake at 350°F for 22 to 25 minutes until golden.|Beat the cream cheese, butter, powdered sugar and vanilla and spread over the warm rolls.","American"],
[3266,"Dinner Rolls","baking","🥖",140,"Easy",8.5,12,"Soft, buttery pull-apart rolls for any meal.","1 cup|milk|warm;2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1/4 cup|sugar;3 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|butter|melted;1|eggs;2 tbsp|butter|melted, for brushing","Mix the warm milk, yeast and sugar and rest 5 minutes until foamy.|Add the flour, salt, melted butter and egg and knead 8 minutes until smooth.|Cover and rise 1 hour until doubled.|Divide into 12 pieces, roll into balls and arrange in a greased 9x13 inch pan.|Cover and rise 30 minutes.|Bake at 375°F for 15 to 18 minutes until golden.|Brush with melted butter while hot.","American"],
[3267,"Brioche","baking","🍞",300,"Medium",8.5,10,"A rich, buttery French loaf with a tender, feathery crumb.","1/4 cup|milk|warm;2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1/4 cup|sugar;3 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;3|eggs;3/4 cup|butter|softened, cubed;1|eggs|beaten, for egg wash","Mix the warm milk, yeast and a pinch of the sugar and let stand 5 minutes.|Add the flour, rest of the sugar, salt and 3 eggs and knead 10 minutes until sticky and elastic.|Add the butter a few cubes at a time, kneading 10 more minutes until smooth and glossy.|Cover and rise 1 1/2 hours, then refrigerate 8 hours or overnight.|Divide into 8 balls and place in a greased 9x5 inch loaf pan.|Rise 1 1/2 hours until puffy, brush with egg wash.|Bake at 375°F for 30 to 35 minutes until deep golden.|Cool in the pan 10 minutes, then on a rack.","French"],
[3268,"Focaccia","baking","🍞",180,"Easy",8.5,12,"Dimpled, olive-oil-rich Italian flatbread with a crisp bottom and airy crumb.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;4 cup|flour;2 tsp|salt;1/3 cup|olive oil;1 tsp|coarse salt;2 sprig|fresh rosemary;1 tbsp|olive oil|for topping","Stir the warm water, yeast and sugar and let stand 5 minutes.|Mix in the flour and salt to a wet, sticky dough, cover and rest 1 hour.|Pour the 1/3 cup olive oil into a 9x13 inch pan, turn the dough into it and flip to coat.|Stretch the dough into the corners, cover and rise 45 minutes.|Heat the oven to 450°F.|Dimple deeply with oiled fingers, drizzle with the extra oil and top with coarse salt and rosemary.|Bake 22 to 25 minutes until deep golden.|Cool in the pan for 10 minutes before cutting.","Italian"],
[3269,"Pizza Dough","baking","🍕",90,"Easy",8.5,8,"A reliable yeast dough that bakes up crisp outside and chewy inside.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;2 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil","Stir the warm water, yeast and sugar and let stand 5 minutes until foamy.|Add the flour, salt and olive oil and knead 8 minutes until smooth.|Cover and rise in an oiled bowl 1 hour until doubled.|Heat the oven with a pizza stone or sheet pan to 475°F.|Divide in two, stretch each into a 12 inch round, add your sauce and toppings.|Bake 10 to 12 minutes until the crust is golden and the cheese bubbles.","Italian"],
[3270,"Pita Bread","baking","🫓",120,"Easy",8.5,8,"Puffy homemade pockets baked in a very hot oven.","2 1/4 tsp|yeast;1 tsp|sugar;3 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil","Stir the warm water, yeast and sugar and let stand 5 minutes.|Add the flour, salt and olive oil and knead 8 minutes until smooth.|Cover and rise 1 hour until doubled.|Heat the oven to 475°F with a baking sheet or stone inside.|Divide into 8 balls and roll each into a 6 inch round about 1/4 inch thick; rest 10 minutes.|Bake the pitas on the hot sheet 3 to 4 minutes until puffed and lightly golden.|Wrap in a clean towel to keep soft.","Middle Eastern"],
[3271,"Scones","baking","🧁",35,"Easy",8.5,8,"Flaky, buttery British scones, lovely with jam and cream.","2 1/2 cup|flour;1/3 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|butter|cold, cubed;2/3 cup|heavy cream;1|eggs;1 tsp|vanilla;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing","Heat the oven to 400°F and line a baking sheet.|Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder and salt, then rub in the cold butter until crumbly.|Whisk the cream, egg and vanilla and stir into the dry mix until a shaggy dough forms.|Pat out to 1 inch thick and cut rounds with a 2 1/2 inch cutter, pressing straight down.|Place on the sheet, brush with beaten egg.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until risen and golden.|Serve warm with jam and cream.","British"],
[3272,"Country Loaf","baking","🍞",840,"Easy",8.5,12,"A rustic, crusty loaf with a mild tang, made with a long cold rise and no starter.","2 cup|flour|bread flour;1 cup|flour|whole wheat;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|yeast","Mix the flours, salt, yeast and cool water into a shaggy dough and cover.|Let rest 12 to 18 hours at room temperature until bubbly and doubled.|Turn out onto a floured surface, fold the dough over itself a few times and shape into a round.|Rest on parchment 1 hour, covered.|Preheat a Dutch oven in a 450°F oven for 30 minutes.|Score the loaf and bake covered 30 minutes.|Remove the lid and bake 15 minutes more until deep brown.|Cool on a rack 1 hour.","French"],
[3273,"Buttermilk Biscuits","baking","🧁",30,"Easy",8.5,8,"Tall, flaky Southern biscuits with a golden top.","2 1/2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|butter|cold, cubed;1 cup|buttermilk|cold;2 tbsp|butter|melted, for brushing","Heat the oven to 450°F.|Whisk the flour, baking powder, sugar and salt, then cut in the cold butter until pea-sized crumbs remain.|Stir in the buttermilk just until the dough comes together.|Pat to 1 inch thick, fold in thirds twice, then cut with a 2 1/2 inch cutter without twisting.|Place touching on a baking sheet and brush with melted butter.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden.","Southern"],
[3274,"Irish Soda Bread","baking","🍞",55,"Easy",8.5,8,"A quick, no-yeast loaf with a craggy crust and tender, slightly tangy crumb.","4 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking soda;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|sugar;1 3/4 cup|buttermilk;2 tbsp|butter|melted","Heat the oven to 425°F and dust a baking sheet with flour.|Whisk the flour, baking soda, salt and sugar.|Make a well and pour in the buttermilk; stir with a fork until a shaggy dough forms.|Knead briefly on a floured surface into a round, flatten slightly and cut a deep cross in the top.|Bake 15 minutes, lower to 400°F and bake 25 to 30 minutes more until it sounds hollow when tapped.|Brush with melted butter and cool 20 minutes before slicing.","British"],
[3275,"Zucchini Bread","baking","🍞",85,"Very easy",8.5,20,"A moist, cinnamon-spiced quick bread packed with shredded zucchini.","3|eggs;1 cup|vegetable oil;1 1/2 cup|sugar;2 tsp|vanilla;2 cup|zucchini|shredded and squeezed dry;3 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;2 tsp|cinnamon","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease two 9x5 inch loaf pans.|Whisk the eggs, oil, sugar and vanilla, then stir in the zucchini.|Combine the flour, baking soda, baking powder, salt and cinnamon and fold into the wet mixture until just combined.|Divide between the pans.|Bake 55 to 60 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 10 minutes in the pans, then turn out onto a rack.","American"],
[3276,"Pumpkin Bread","baking","🍞",85,"Very easy",8.5,12,"A moist, warmly spiced loaf made with canned pumpkin.","1 can|pumpkin puree|15 oz;1 cup|vegetable oil;2|eggs;1 1/2 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|nutmeg","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 9x5 inch loaf pan.|Whisk the pumpkin, oil, eggs and both sugars until smooth.|Mix the flour, baking soda, baking powder, salt, cinnamon and nutmeg and fold into the wet mixture until just combined.|Pour into the pan.|Bake 60 to 70 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean, tenting with foil if browning too fast.|Cool 15 minutes in the pan, then on a rack.","American"],
[3277,"Thai Peanut Chicken Wraps","wraps","🌯",25,"Easy",8,4,"Chicken, crunchy vegetables and a creamy peanut sauce rolled in a tortilla.","1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1/3 cup|peanut butter;2 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|honey;1 tsp|ginger|grated;1 tbsp|lime juice;4|flour tortillas|large;2 cup|coleslaw mix;1|carrots|shredded;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Season the chicken with salt and pepper and cook in the oil over medium-high heat 6 to 7 minutes until cooked through.|Whisk the peanut butter, soy sauce, rice vinegar, honey, ginger and lime juice with 2 to 3 tablespoons warm water until pourable.|Toss the chicken with a third of the sauce.|Warm the tortillas 20 seconds per side.|Layer each with coleslaw mix, carrot, chicken and cilantro and drizzle with more sauce.|Fold in the sides, roll tightly and slice in half.","Thai"],
[3278,"Beef Burritos","wraps","🌯",40,"Easy",8,6,"Seasoned ground beef, rice, beans and cheese rolled in a warm flour tortilla.","1 lb|ground beef;1 packet|taco seasoning;1 cup|rice|cooked;1 can|refried beans|16 oz;2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;6|flour tortillas|burrito size;1/2 cup|salsa;1/2 cup|sour cream","Brown the beef in a skillet over medium-high heat 6 to 8 minutes and drain the fat.|Stir in the taco seasoning and 1/3 cup water and simmer 3 minutes.|Warm the refried beans in a small pot.|Warm the tortillas to make them pliable.|Layer beans, rice, beef, cheese, salsa and sour cream down the center of each tortilla.|Fold in the sides and roll up tightly.|Sear seam-side down in a dry skillet 1 to 2 minutes per side until lightly crisp.","Mexican"],
[3279,"Turkey and Cheese Roll-Ups","wraps","🌯",10,"Very easy",8,4,"Easy deli roll-ups with turkey, cheese and a cream cheese spread in a tortilla.","4|flour tortillas|8 inch;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1 tbsp|dijon mustard;8 slice|deli turkey;4 slice|provolone;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1|tomatoes|thinly sliced","Mix the cream cheese and mustard.|Spread the mixture over each tortilla leaving a small border.|Layer 2 slices of turkey, 1 slice of provolone, lettuce and tomato on each.|Roll up tightly.|Chill 15 minutes if time allows, then slice each into pinwheels or halves.","American"],
[3280,"BBQ Chicken Wraps","wraps","🌯",25,"Easy",8,4,"Saucy barbecue chicken with crisp lettuce, red onion and cheddar in a tortilla.","1 lb|chicken breast|boneless;1/2 cup|bbq sauce;4|flour tortillas|large;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|ranch dressing","Season the chicken with salt and pepper and simmer in water or broth 15 minutes or bake at 400°F 20 minutes until 165°F.|Shred the chicken and toss with the barbecue sauce.|Warm the tortillas.|Fill each with chicken, cheddar, lettuce and red onion and drizzle with ranch.|Fold in the sides and roll tightly.","American"],
[3281,"Egg Salad Lettuce Wraps","wraps","🥬",20,"Very easy",8,4,"Creamy egg salad tucked into crisp butter lettuce cups for a low-carb lunch.","6|eggs;3 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;1 tsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;8|butter lettuce|leaves","Cover the eggs with cold water, bring to a boil, cover and remove from heat for 11 minutes.|Cool the eggs in ice water, peel and chop.|Mix with the mayonnaise, mustard, celery, chives and lemon juice and season with salt and pepper.|Spoon into the lettuce leaves and serve right away.","American"],
[3282,"Tuna Salad Wraps","wraps","🌯",15,"Very easy",8,4,"Creamy tuna salad with celery and crunch wrapped in a tortilla with greens.","2 can|tuna|5 oz, drained;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 stalk|celery|diced;2 tbsp|red onion|minced;1 tbsp|lemon juice;4|flour tortillas|large;1 cup|spinach","Flake the tuna into a bowl.|Stir in the mayonnaise, mustard, celery, onion and lemon juice and season with salt and pepper.|Lay the tortillas flat and top each with spinach and tuna salad.|Fold in the sides, roll tightly and slice in half.","American"],
[3283,"Southwest Chicken Wraps","wraps","🌯",25,"Easy",8,4,"Chicken, black beans, corn and cheese in a tortilla with a zesty chipotle sauce.","1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 tbsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn|thawed;1 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;4|flour tortillas|large;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1/4 cup|sour cream;1 tbsp|chipotle in adobo|minced","Toss the chicken with chili powder, cumin, salt and pepper.|Cook in the olive oil over medium-high heat 6 to 7 minutes until cooked through.|Mix the sour cream and chipotle.|Warm the tortillas and fill with chicken, beans, corn, cheese and lettuce.|Drizzle with chipotle cream, fold in the sides and roll tightly.","Tex-Mex"],
[3284,"Chicken Bacon Ranch Wraps","wraps","🌯",25,"Easy",8,4,"Crispy bacon, juicy chicken and ranch in a tortilla.","1 lb|chicken breast|sliced thin;1 tbsp|olive oil;6 slice|bacon;4|flour tortillas|large;1/3 cup|ranch dressing;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 cup|lettuce|shredded;1|tomatoes|diced","Cook the bacon in a skillet until crisp, drain and crumble.|Season the chicken with salt and pepper and cook in the olive oil 6 to 7 minutes until cooked through.|Warm the tortillas and spread each with ranch.|Top with chicken, bacon, cheddar, lettuce and tomato.|Fold in the sides and roll tightly; slice in half.","American"],
[3285,"Turkey Avocado BLT Wraps","wraps","🌯",20,"Very easy",8,4,"Turkey, bacon, avocado and tomato rolled with a little mayo.","6 slice|bacon;4|flour tortillas|large;2 tbsp|mayonnaise;8 slice|deli turkey;1|avocado|sliced;1|tomatoes|sliced;1 cup|lettuce|shredded","Cook the bacon until crisp and drain on paper towels.|Warm the tortillas and spread with mayonnaise.|Layer turkey, bacon, avocado, tomato and lettuce on each.|Season lightly with salt and pepper, fold in the sides and roll tightly.|Slice in half.","American"],
[3286,"Chicken Gyro Wraps","wraps","🌯",35,"Easy",8,4,"Marinated chicken with tzatziki, tomato and red onion in a warm pita.","1 lb|chicken thighs|boneless, sliced;2 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|lemon juice;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|oregano;1 cup|greek yogurt;1|cucumber|grated and squeezed dry;4|pita|large, warmed;1|tomatoes|sliced;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced","Toss the chicken with the olive oil, lemon juice, 1 clove of the garlic, oregano, salt and pepper and marinate 15 minutes.|Stir the yogurt, cucumber, remaining garlic, a pinch of salt and a squeeze of lemon into a quick tzatziki.|Cook the chicken in a hot skillet 7 to 8 minutes until browned and cooked through.|Warm the pitas.|Fill with chicken, tzatziki, tomato and red onion and fold or roll.","Greek"],
[3287,"Spinach Feta Breakfast Wraps","wraps","🌯",15,"Very easy",8,4,"Soft scrambled eggs with spinach and feta in a warm tortilla.","6|eggs;1/4 cup|milk;1 tbsp|butter;2 cup|spinach;1/2 cup|feta|crumbled;4|flour tortillas|8 inch;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Whisk the eggs with the milk, salt and pepper.|Melt the butter in a nonstick skillet over medium heat and wilt the spinach 1 minute.|Add the eggs and stir gently 2 to 3 minutes until just set.|Fold in the feta.|Warm the tortillas, divide the eggs among them, fold in the sides and roll.","American"],
[3288,"Chicken Pesto Wraps","wraps","🌯",20,"Easy",8,4,"Chicken, mozzarella, tomato and basil pesto rolled up in a tortilla.","2|chicken breast|cooked and sliced;1/3 cup|pesto;4|flour tortillas|large;1 cup|fresh mozzarella|sliced;1|tomatoes|sliced;1 cup|arugula","Season the chicken with salt and pepper and cook in a skillet 6 minutes per side until 165°F, then slice.|Spread pesto over each tortilla.|Top with chicken, mozzarella, tomato and arugula.|Fold in the sides and roll tightly.|Slice in half, or toast in a skillet 1 minute per side.","Italian"],
[3289,"Egyptian Chicken Soup with Vermicelli","soup","🍲",65,"Easy",9.5,6,"A golden chicken broth scented with cardamom and bay, finished with toasted vermicelli and a squeeze of lemon.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skin removed;1|onion|halved;2|carrots|peeled and halved;2 stalk|celery|halved;2|bay leaves;6|cardamom pods|lightly crushed;1 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|vermicelli|broken into short pieces;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|lemon juice|to finish","Place the chicken, onion, carrots, celery, bay leaves and cardamom in a large pot and cover with 8 cups of cold water.|Bring to a boil, skim off the foam, then reduce to a gentle simmer and cook partly covered for 40 minutes until the chicken is very tender.|Remove the chicken and vegetables, strain the broth, and return the broth to the pot. Shred the chicken, discarding the bones.|Melt the butter in a small pan over medium heat and toast the vermicelli, stirring, for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden.|Add the vermicelli to the simmering broth and cook 5 to 6 minutes until tender. Season with salt and pepper.|Return the shredded chicken and a few carrot slices to the pot, stir in the lemon juice and serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3290,"Shorbet Lisan Asfour (Egyptian Orzo Soup)","soup","🥣",100,"Easy",9.5,6,"Comforting beef broth soup with buttery toasted orzo, called bird's tongue soup in Egypt, served at nearly every family table.","1 1/2 lb|beef stew meat|bone-in shank or chuck pieces;1|onion|quartered;2|bay leaves;6|cardamom pods|crushed;1|cinnamon|stick;1 tbsp|butter;3/4 cup|orzo;1 tbsp|tomato paste;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;|parsley|chopped, to garnish","Place the beef, onion, bay leaves, cardamom and cinnamon in a pot with 8 cups of water and bring to a boil.|Skim the foam, lower the heat, cover and simmer 1 1/2 hours until the meat is tender.|Strain the broth and shred or cube the beef, discarding bones, onion and spices.|In the clean pot, melt the butter over medium heat and toast the orzo 2 to 3 minutes until golden. Stir in the tomato paste for 30 seconds.|Pour in the strained broth, bring to a simmer and cook 8 to 10 minutes until the orzo is tender.|Return the beef to the soup, season with salt and pepper, and serve with parsley.","Egyptian"],
[3291,"Shorbet Khodar (Egyptian Vegetable Soup)","soup","🥕",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"A light tomato-tinged soup of carrots, potatoes, zucchini and peas simmered in broth with a touch of cumin.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2|carrots|diced;2|potatoes|peeled and diced;1|zucchini|diced;1 cup|frozen peas;2|tomatoes|grated;1 tbsp|tomato paste;6 cup|vegetable broth;1 tsp|cumin;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped","Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes until soft. Add the garlic and cook 30 seconds.|Stir in the carrots and potatoes and cook 3 minutes.|Add the grated tomatoes, tomato paste and cumin and cook 3 minutes until the tomatoes darken.|Pour in the broth, bring to a boil, then simmer 15 minutes until the potatoes are nearly tender.|Add the zucchini and peas and simmer 8 minutes more.|Season with salt and pepper, stir in the parsley and serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3292,"Shorbet Freekeh (Egyptian Freekeh and Chicken Soup)","soup","🍲",90,"Easy",9.5,6,"A hearty soup of smoky cracked freekeh and tender chicken in a warmly spiced broth.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;1|onion|diced;2 tbsp|butter;3/4 cup|freekeh|cracked, rinsed;1|cinnamon|stick;4|cardamom pods|crushed;2|bay leaves;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1/2 tsp|allspice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the chicken and brown lightly for 4 minutes.|Stir in the tomato paste, allspice, cinnamon stick, cardamom and bay leaves and cook 1 minute.|Add 8 cups of water, bring to a boil, skim the foam and simmer covered 35 minutes until the chicken is tender.|Lift out the chicken, shred it and discard the bones, skin and whole spices.|Add the freekeh to the broth and simmer 25 minutes until tender, adding a little water if it gets too thick.|Return the chicken to the pot, season with salt, pepper and lemon juice, and serve.","Egyptian"],
[3293,"Eggs with Pastrami (Beid bel Basterma)","breakfast","🍳",15,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Spiced cured beef sizzled in butter with eggs cracked right over the top, a classic Egyptian breakfast skillet.","2 tbsp|butter;4 oz|pastrami|thinly sliced, torn;1|tomato|diced, optional;4|eggs;|black pepper|to taste;|bread|warm, for serving","Melt the butter in a small skillet over medium heat.|Add the pastrami and fry 2 minutes until the edges begin to crisp and the fat renders.|Add the tomato, if using, and cook 1 minute.|Crack the eggs over the pastrami and cover the pan.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes for set whites and runny yolks, or longer to your liking.|Season with black pepper and serve straight from the pan with warm bread.","Egyptian"],
[3294,"Eggs with Sausage (Beid bel Sogo)","breakfast","🍳",20,"Very easy",8.5,2,"Spicy Egyptian-style beef sausage fried with onion and tomato and finished with soft eggs.","1 tbsp|olive oil;8 oz|smoked sausage|spicy beef sausage, sliced;1/2|onion|thinly sliced;1|tomato|diced;1/2 tsp|cumin;4|eggs;|salt|to taste;|bread|warm, for serving","Heat the oil in a skillet over medium heat and cook the sausage slices 4 minutes until browned on both sides.|Add the onion and cook 3 minutes until soft.|Stir in the tomato and cumin and cook 3 minutes until the juices reduce.|Make four wells in the mixture and crack an egg into each.|Cover and cook 3 to 4 minutes until the whites are set.|Season lightly with salt and serve with warm bread.","Egyptian"],
[3295,"Tahini and Black Molasses (Tahina bel Asal Eswed)","breakfast","🍯",5,"Very easy",8.5,3,"A classic Egyptian breakfast dip of swirled tahini and dark molasses, scooped up with warm bread.","1/2 cup|tahini;1/4 cup|blackstrap molasses;1/2 tsp|cinnamon|optional;4|pita|torn or baladi bread","Spoon the tahini into one side of a shallow plate and stir to loosen the oil if it has separated.|Pour the molasses into the other side of the plate.|Swirl the two together lightly with a spoon, leaving streaks.|Dust with cinnamon if you like.|Serve right away with warm torn bread for dipping.","Egyptian"],
[3296,"Eishta with Honey and Baladi Bread","breakfast","🍯",50,"Medium",8.5,6,"Thick homemade Egyptian clotted cream drizzled with honey and eaten with warm bread, a beloved weekend breakfast.","2 cup|milk;1 cup|heavy cream;2 tbsp|cornstarch;1 slice|bread|white, crusts removed;1/2 cup|honey;6|pita|warm, or baladi bread;2 tbsp|pistachios|chopped, optional","Whisk the cornstarch with 1/2 cup of the cold milk until smooth.|Pour the remaining milk and the cream into a saucepan, crumble in the bread, and heat over medium heat until steaming.|Whisk in the cornstarch mixture and cook, whisking constantly, 5 to 6 minutes until thick like pudding.|Pour into a shallow dish, cool 15 minutes uncovered, then chill at least 2 hours until firm.|Cut into squares or spoon into bowls, drizzle generously with honey and top with pistachios.|Serve with warm bread.","Egyptian"],
[3297,"Shatta (Egyptian Hot Sauce)","sides","🌶️",15,"Very easy",7.5,12,"Fiery red chili and garlic sauce spooned over koshari, falafel and grilled meats across Egypt.","8 oz|red chili peppers|stemmed, such as fresno;4 clove|garlic;1/4 cup|white vinegar;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|cumin;2 tbsp|vegetable oil","Wear gloves and roughly chop the chili peppers, keeping the seeds for heat.|Blend the chilies, garlic, vinegar, salt and cumin in a food processor until a coarse paste forms.|Heat the oil in a small pan over medium heat and fry the paste 4 to 5 minutes, stirring, until it darkens slightly and loses its raw smell.|Cool completely and spoon into a clean jar.|Refrigerate up to 3 weeks and use in small spoonfuls.","Egyptian"],
[3298,"Dakka (Egyptian Garlic Vinegar Sauce)","sides","🧄",10,"Very easy",7.5,8,"A sharp garlic, vinegar and cumin dressing spooned over koshari for its signature tangy bite.","6 clove|garlic|minced very fine;1/2 cup|white vinegar;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes","Mash the garlic with the salt in a bowl until nearly a paste.|Stir in the vinegar, lemon juice, cumin and red pepper flakes.|Add the warm water and stir well.|Let stand at least 30 minutes so the flavors mellow.|Spoon over koshari, lentils or grilled meat. Refrigerate up to 1 week.","Egyptian"],
[3299,"Egyptian Duqqa","sides","🌰",15,"Easy",7.5,16,"A crunchy dry blend of toasted hazelnuts, sesame, coriander and cumin for dipping with bread and olive oil.","1/2 cup|hazelnuts;1/4 cup|sesame seeds;2 tbsp|coriander|whole seeds;1 tbsp|cumin|whole seeds;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|coarse salt","Toast the hazelnuts in a dry skillet over medium heat 4 to 5 minutes until golden, then rub off loose skins and cool.|Toast the sesame seeds 2 minutes until light golden, then transfer to a plate.|Toast the coriander and cumin seeds 1 minute until fragrant.|Pulse the hazelnuts in a food processor into coarse crumbs, taking care not to make a paste.|Pulse in the sesame, coriander, cumin, pepper and salt just until coarsely ground.|Store in a jar for up to 1 month. Dip bread in olive oil, then in duqqa.","Egyptian"],
[3300,"Egyptian Rice with Nuts and Raisins (Roz bel Mekassarat)","sides","🍚",40,"Easy",7.5,6,"Buttery rice cooked in broth and scattered with toasted pine nuts, almonds and plump raisins.","2 cup|rice|long grain, rinsed;3 tbsp|butter;3 1/2 cup|chicken broth;1/4 cup|pine nuts;1/4 cup|almonds|slivered;1/4 cup|raisins;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;|salt|to taste","Melt 1 tablespoon of the butter in a small pan over medium heat and toast the pine nuts and almonds 3 minutes until golden. Set aside.|Melt the remaining butter in a pot over medium heat, add the rice and stir 2 minutes to coat.|Add the broth, cinnamon and salt, and bring to a boil.|Reduce to the lowest heat, cover and cook 15 minutes.|Scatter the raisins over the rice, cover again, and rest off the heat 10 minutes.|Fluff with a fork and top with the toasted nuts.","Egyptian"],
[3301,"Salata Baladi (Egyptian Tomato and Cucumber Salad)","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"A chopped salad of ripe tomato, cucumber and parsley dressed with lemon, olive oil and a pinch of cumin.","3|tomatoes|diced;2|cucumber|diced;1/2|red onion|finely diced;1|bell pepper|green, diced;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;3 tbsp|lemon juice;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|cumin;|salt|to taste","Combine the tomatoes, cucumbers, red onion, bell pepper and parsley in a bowl.|Whisk the lemon juice, olive oil, cumin and salt in a small bowl.|Pour the dressing over the vegetables and toss.|Let stand 10 minutes so the juices mingle.|Serve with grilled meats, fish or fried falafel.","Egyptian"],
[3302,"Egyptian Yogurt and Cucumber Salad (Zabadi bil Khiar)","sides","🥒",10,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Cool yogurt with crisp cucumber, garlic and dried mint, a refreshing side for rich meats.","2 cup|greek yogurt;2|cucumber|diced;2 clove|garlic|crushed;1 tbsp|dried mint;1 tbsp|olive oil;|salt|to taste","Stir the yogurt, garlic, mint and salt together in a bowl.|Fold in the diced cucumber.|Chill 20 minutes.|Drizzle with olive oil before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3303,"Torshi Lift (Egyptian Pickled Turnips)","sides","🫙",30,"Very easy",7.5,12,"Crunchy pink pickled turnip sticks tinted with beet, ready after three days and served beside falafel and fuul.","2 lb|turnips|peeled, cut into sticks;1|carrots|optional, sliced;1|beets|raw, peeled and sliced;3 clove|garlic|halved;3 tbsp|coarse salt;1/2 cup|white vinegar","Pack the turnips, optional carrot, beet slices and garlic into a large clean jar.|Stir the salt and vinegar into 3 cups of water until the salt dissolves.|Pour the brine into the jar until the vegetables are fully covered, pressing them down.|Seal and leave at room temperature 3 days until the turnips are bright pink and tangy.|Refrigerate and use within 1 month.","Egyptian"],
[3304,"Egyptian Fried Cauliflower with Tahini (Qarnabeet Makly)","sides","🥦",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Cauliflower florets fried in a light flour coating and served with lemony tahini sauce, a staple of the mezze table.","1 head|cauliflower|cut into florets;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|salt;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 cup|tahini;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 clove|garlic|minced","Boil the florets in salted water 3 minutes until just tender, drain and pat very dry.|Mix the flour, cumin and salt, and toss the florets in the mixture to coat lightly.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350 degrees F.|Fry the florets in batches 3 to 4 minutes until deep golden and drain on paper towels.|Whisk the tahini, lemon juice, garlic, water and a pinch of salt into a smooth sauce.|Serve the hot cauliflower with the tahini sauce for dipping.","Egyptian"],
[3305,"Egyptian Grilled Chicken (Firakh Mashwi)","comfort","🍗",100,"Easy",9,4,"Chicken marinated overnight in yogurt, lemon, garlic and warm spices, then roasted or grilled until charred and juicy.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skin-on;1 cup|greek yogurt;1/4 cup|lemon juice;6 clove|garlic|minced;2 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|coriander;2 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Whisk the yogurt, lemon juice, garlic, cumin, coriander, paprika, turmeric, olive oil, salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Add the chicken and turn to coat, then marinate at least 2 hours or overnight in the refrigerator.|Heat the oven to 425 degrees F or heat a grill to medium-high.|Roast on a rimmed sheet pan 40 to 45 minutes, or grill 10 minutes per side with the lid down, until the juices run clear and the thickest part reaches 175 degrees F.|Broil the chicken 2 to 3 minutes at the end for charred edges.|Rest 5 minutes and serve with rice and salad.","Egyptian"],
[3306,"Samak Meshwi (Egyptian Grilled Fish)","light","🐟",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Whole fish rubbed with garlic, cumin and lemon, then grilled or broiled until the skin crackles.","2|whole fish|branzino or sea bream, about 1 lb each, cleaned;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|lemon juice;3 tbsp|olive oil;1|tomatoes|sliced;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|red pepper flakes","Score each fish with three diagonal cuts on both sides.|Mix the garlic, cumin, salt, lemon juice, olive oil and red pepper flakes into a paste and rub it inside the cavity and over the fish.|Stuff the cavities with tomato slices and parsley and rest 15 minutes.|Heat a grill or the broiler to high.|Cook the fish 8 to 10 minutes per side until the skin is blistered and the flesh flakes at the bone.|Serve with lemon wedges, rice and salata baladi.","Egyptian"],
[3307,"Samak Makly (Egyptian Fried Fish)","light","🐟",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Cumin and garlic marinated fish fillets dusted with spiced flour and fried until crisp, a coastal Egyptian favorite.","1 1/2 lb|cod|cut into large pieces;3 clove|garlic|crushed;1 tbsp|cumin;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|flour;1 tsp|coriander;1 tsp|paprika;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Toss the fish with the garlic, half the cumin, lemon juice and salt and marinate 15 minutes.|Mix the flour, remaining cumin, coriander and paprika on a plate.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350 degrees F.|Press each piece into the flour mixture, shake off excess, and fry in batches 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot with lemon wedges and tahini sauce.","Egyptian"],
[3308,"Hamam Mahshi (Egyptian Stuffed Cornish Hens)","comfort","🍗",110,"Medium",9,4,"Cornish hens filled with smoky freekeh, onion and almonds, the traditional Egyptian stuffed pigeon made home-friendly.","4|cornish hens|about 1 1/4 lb each;1 cup|freekeh|cracked, rinsed;2 1/2 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|butter;1|onion|finely diced;1/4 cup|almonds|slivered;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|allspice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 tbsp|olive oil","Simmer the freekeh in the broth, covered, 18 to 20 minutes until almost tender and the liquid is absorbed.|Melt 2 tablespoons of butter in a skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 6 minutes. Add the almonds, cinnamon and allspice and cook 2 minutes.|Stir the onion mixture into the freekeh and season with salt and pepper. Cool slightly.|Heat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the hens inside and out with salt and pepper and fill each loosely with stuffing, sealing the cavity with toothpicks.|Rub the hens with olive oil and the remaining melted butter and place in a roasting pan.|Roast 60 to 70 minutes until golden and the thickest part of the thigh reaches 165 degrees F.|Rest 10 minutes and serve with any leftover stuffing.","Egyptian"],
[3309,"Kawareh (Egyptian Braised Lamb Shanks)","comfort","🍖",190,"Medium",9,4,"Lamb shanks simmered with cardamom and bay until tender, then roasted in butter until browned.","4|lamb shanks|about 1 lb each;1|onion|quartered;2|bay leaves;8|cardamom pods|crushed;1|cinnamon|stick;1 tbsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper;3 tbsp|butter;6 clove|garlic|whole;1 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Place the lamb shanks in a large pot with the onion, bay leaves, cardamom, cinnamon, salt and pepper and cover with water.|Bring to a boil, skim the foam, then cover and simmer 2 hours until the meat is tender but not falling apart.|Heat the oven to 425 degrees F.|Transfer the shanks to a roasting pan, dot with the butter, tuck in the garlic and ladle over 1 cup of the cooking broth.|Roast 25 to 30 minutes, basting once, until browned and glossy.|Serve over rice with a spoonful of the pan juices.","Egyptian"],
[3310,"Tagen Batates (Egyptian Potato Tagine)","comfort","🥔",65,"Easy",9,4,"Sliced potatoes baked in a garlicky tomato sauce with peppers until soft, bubbling and lightly caramelized.","2 lb|potatoes|peeled, sliced 1/4 inch thick;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|green, sliced;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 cup|chicken broth","Heat the oven to 400 degrees F.|Cook the onion in the oil in a skillet 5 minutes, add the garlic and pepper and cook 2 minutes.|Stir in the tomato sauce, tomato paste, cumin, paprika, salt, pepper and broth, and simmer 5 minutes.|Layer the potato slices in a baking dish and pour the sauce over, tucking the potatoes under the liquid.|Cover with foil and bake 35 minutes.|Uncover and bake 15 minutes more until the potatoes are tender and the top is lightly browned.|Serve hot with rice or bread.","Egyptian"],
[3311,"Gambari Tagine (Egyptian Shrimp Casserole)","light","🍤",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Shrimp baked in a spicy tomato and garlic sauce with peppers until bubbling in a clay pot or baking dish.","1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1|bell pepper|diced;4|tomatoes|chopped;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 425 degrees F.|Melt the butter in a skillet over medium heat and cook the onion and pepper 5 minutes. Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, tomato paste, cumin, paprika, cayenne and salt and simmer 10 minutes until saucy.|Stir the shrimp into the sauce and pour into a baking dish or clay pot.|Bake 10 to 12 minutes until the shrimp are pink and the sauce bubbles.|Scatter with parsley and serve with rice or bread.","Egyptian"],
[3312,"Besella (Egyptian Peas and Carrots Stew)","comfort","🫛",80,"Easy",9,6,"Tender peas and carrots stewed with beef in a mildly spiced tomato sauce and served over rice.","12 oz|beef stew meat|cut in small cubes;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3|carrots|diced;1 lb|frozen peas;2 tbsp|tomato paste;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1/2 tsp|allspice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef in the oil in a pot over medium-high heat 5 minutes. Add the onion and garlic and cook 3 minutes.|Cover with 2 cups of water, bring to a simmer and cook covered 45 minutes until the beef is tender.|Stir in the tomato paste, tomato sauce, carrots, allspice, salt and pepper.|Simmer 10 minutes, then add the peas.|Cook 10 to 12 minutes more until the carrots are tender and the sauce is thick.|Serve over white rice.","Egyptian"],
[3313,"Kebab Halla (Egyptian Lamb and Onion Stew)","comfort","🍖",120,"Easy",9,6,"Chunks of lamb slowly cooked with plenty of onion, tomato and cardamom until the sauce turns rich and silky.","2 lb|lamb shoulder|cut into 1 1/2 inch cubes;2 tbsp|butter;3|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2|tomatoes|grated;1 tbsp|tomato paste;4|cardamom pods|crushed;1|cinnamon|stick;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 cup|beef broth","Brown the lamb in the butter in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat 6 to 8 minutes. Remove and set aside.|Cook the onions in the same pot 10 minutes until golden, then add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Stir in the grated tomatoes and tomato paste and cook 4 minutes.|Return the lamb to the pot with the cardamom, cinnamon, salt, pepper and broth.|Cover and simmer over low heat 1 1/2 hours until the lamb is very tender and the sauce is thick.|Serve over rice or with bread.","Egyptian"],
[3314,"Egyptian Fried Chicken (Firakh Makly)","comfort","🍗",60,"Medium",9,4,"Chicken pieces simmered in garlic and cumin then fried until bronze for a juicy bird with a crisp skin.","3 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skin-on;6 clove|garlic|crushed;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|paprika;1 tsp|coriander;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|salt;1 cup|flour;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Place the chicken in a pot with the garlic, half the cumin, lemon juice and salt, cover with water and simmer 15 minutes. Drain well and pat dry.|Mix the flour with the remaining cumin, paprika and coriander.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350 degrees F.|Dredge each piece in the flour mixture and shake off excess.|Fry in batches 6 to 8 minutes, turning once, until deep golden and cooked through to 175 degrees F.|Drain on a rack and serve with lemon wedges.","Egyptian"],
[3315,"Sabanekh bil Lahma (Egyptian Spinach and Beef Stew)","comfort","🥬",50,"Easy",9,4,"Deep green spinach stewed with ground beef, garlic and tomato, served over white rice.","1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 lb|frozen spinach|thawed and squeezed;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|coriander;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Brown the beef in a large pot over medium-high heat 6 minutes, breaking it up.|Add the onion and cook 5 minutes until soft, then add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Stir in the spinach, tomato sauce, cumin, coriander, salt and pepper.|Add 1 cup of water, cover and simmer 25 minutes, stirring occasionally.|Stir in the lemon juice and cook uncovered 5 minutes more.|Serve over rice.","Egyptian"],
[3316,"Egyptian Sausage Sandwich (Sogo Sandwich)","wraps","🥙",25,"Easy",8,4,"Spiced beef sausage sauteed with onions, peppers and tomato and tucked into warm pita bread.","1 lb|smoked sausage|spicy beef sausage, sliced;1 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|sliced;1|bell pepper|sliced;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;4|pita|warmed;2 tbsp|tahini|optional;|salt|to taste","Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the sausage 4 minutes until browned.|Add the onion and pepper and cook 5 minutes until soft.|Stir in the tomatoes and cumin and cook 4 minutes until the juices thicken.|Season lightly with salt.|Split each pita, fill with the sausage mixture and drizzle with tahini if using.","Egyptian"],
[3317,"Egyptian Pastrami and Cheese Sandwich (Basterma Sandwich)","wraps","🥪",15,"Very easy",8,2,"Spiced cured beef crisped in a skillet and tucked into bread with melted white cheese and tomato.","4 oz|pastrami|thinly sliced;4 slice|mozzarella|or Egyptian rumi cheese;1|tomatoes|sliced;1 tbsp|butter;2|pita|or small rolls, split;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a skillet over medium heat and fry the pastrami 2 minutes until the edges crisp.|Lay the cheese on the pastrami, cover and cook 1 minute until the cheese melts.|Warm the bread in a dry pan or toaster.|Fill each with the pastrami and cheese and top with sliced tomato.|Season with pepper and serve hot.","Egyptian"],
[3318,"Aish Baladi (Egyptian Whole Wheat Flatbread)","baking","🍞",120,"Medium",8.5,8,"Puffy whole wheat pita-style bread with a chewy crust, the everyday loaf of Egyptian tables.","3 cup|flour|whole wheat;1 cup|flour|bread flour;1 packet|yeast|2 1/4 tsp;1 tsp|sugar;2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/4 cup|oats|or wheat bran, for dusting","Stir the yeast and sugar into the warm water and let stand 5 minutes until foamy.|Mix both flours and the salt in a bowl, add the yeast liquid and the oil, and knead 8 to 10 minutes until smooth and slightly tacky.|Cover and let rise 1 hour until doubled.|Heat the oven to 475 degrees F with a baking stone or inverted baking sheet inside.|Divide the dough into 8 balls, rest 10 minutes, then roll each into a 7-inch round and dust with bran.|Bake the rounds on the hot surface 6 to 8 minutes until puffed and browned.|Cool wrapped in a towel to keep them soft.","Egyptian"],
[3319,"Aish Fino (Egyptian Bread Rolls)","baking","🥖",130,"Medium",8.5,8,"Soft, elongated Egyptian bread rolls with a thin golden crust, perfect for sandwiches of liver, sausage or falafel.","4 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast|2 1/4 tsp;2 tbsp|sugar;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|milk|warm;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing;1 tbsp|sesame seeds|optional","Combine the yeast, sugar, milk and warm water and let stand 5 minutes until foamy.|Mix the flour and salt in a large bowl, add the yeast mixture and oil, and knead 8 minutes until smooth.|Cover and let rise 1 hour until doubled.|Divide into 8 pieces, shape each into a 6-inch oval roll and place on a lined baking sheet. Cover and rise 30 minutes.|Heat the oven to 400 degrees F. Slash each roll lengthwise, brush with egg and top with sesame seeds.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until golden and cool on a rack.","Egyptian"],
[3320,"Fatayer Gebna (Egyptian Cheese Pastries)","baking","🥟",100,"Medium",8.5,12,"Soft yeasted pastry boats filled with salty white cheese and parsley, baked until golden.","3 cup|flour;1 packet|yeast|2 1/4 tsp;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|milk;1/4 cup|olive oil;8 oz|feta|crumbled;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing","Dissolve the yeast and sugar in the warm water and let stand 5 minutes.|Mix the flour and salt, add the yeast mixture, milk and oil, and knead 8 minutes until smooth.|Cover and rise 1 hour until doubled.|Combine the feta, mozzarella and parsley.|Heat the oven to 400 degrees F. Divide the dough into 12 balls, roll each into a 5-inch oval and fill the center with the cheese.|Fold the sides up over the filling and pinch the ends into boat shapes. Brush with egg.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until golden and serve warm.","Egyptian"],
[3321,"Mahalabiya (Egyptian Milk Pudding)","treats","🍮",40,"Easy",9,6,"A silky chilled milk pudding perfumed with rose water and topped with pistachios.","4 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|cornstarch;1 tsp|rose water;1 tsp|vanilla;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped","Whisk the cornstarch with 1 cup of the cold milk until smooth.|Heat the remaining milk and sugar in a saucepan over medium heat until steaming.|Whisk in the cornstarch mixture and cook, stirring constantly, 6 to 8 minutes until thick enough to coat a spoon.|Remove from the heat and stir in the rose water and vanilla.|Pour into six bowls and cool 15 minutes, then chill at least 3 hours.|Top with chopped pistachios before serving.","Egyptian"],
[3322,"Basbousa with Cream Filling (Basbousa bil Eishta)","treats","🍰",75,"Medium",9,12,"Tender semolina cake split and filled with sweet cream, then soaked in lemon syrup.","2 cup|semolina|fine;1/2 cup|flour;3/4 cup|sugar;1 cup|greek yogurt;1/2 cup|butter|melted;2 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|vanilla;1/4 cup|almonds|blanched, for topping;1 cup|heavy cream;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;2 tbsp|powdered sugar;1 1/2 cup|sugar|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Heat the oven to 350 degrees F and grease a 9 by 13 inch pan.|Mix the semolina, flour, 3/4 cup sugar and baking powder, then stir in the yogurt, melted butter and vanilla until combined and let stand 10 minutes.|Spread half the batter in the pan, cover with the remaining batter and press almonds on top in rows.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until golden.|Meanwhile simmer the syrup sugar with 3/4 cup water 8 minutes, add the lemon juice and cool.|Pour cooled syrup over the hot cake and let stand 15 minutes.|Whip the cream, cream cheese and powdered sugar until thick. Cut the cake in squares, split horizontally, fill with cream and replace the tops.","Egyptian"],
[3323,"Ghorayeba (Egyptian Shortbread Cookies)","treats","🍪",45,"Easy",9,24,"Melt-in-your-mouth butter cookies, topped with a pistachio and baked pale so they stay tender.","1 cup|butter|melted and cooled;3/4 cup|powdered sugar;2 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|vanilla;24|pistachios|whole, for topping","Heat the oven to 300 degrees F and line two baking sheets with parchment.|Whisk the melted butter and powdered sugar until smooth, then stir in the vanilla.|Add the flour and mix until a soft dough forms, chilling 15 minutes if sticky.|Roll tablespoon portions into balls, place 1 inch apart and press a pistachio into the center of each.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until set but still pale.|Cool completely on the pan before moving, as they are fragile when warm.","Egyptian"],
[3324,"Date Maamoul Cookies","treats","🍪",75,"Medium",9,24,"Buttery semolina cookies stuffed with spiced date paste, a staple of Egyptian holiday trays.","2 1/2 cup|semolina;1 cup|flour;1 cup|butter|melted;1/4 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|milk;1 tbsp|rose water;1 lb|dates|pitted;2 tbsp|butter|softened, for filling;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 cup|powdered sugar|for dusting","Mix the semolina, flour, sugar and melted butter, rub together with your fingers and rest covered 30 minutes.|Knead in the milk and rose water until the dough holds together.|Blend the dates, softened butter and cinnamon into a smooth paste and roll into 24 small balls.|Heat the oven to 350 degrees F.|Flatten a ball of dough in your palm, enclose a date ball, seal and gently press into a round cookie, patterning with a fork.|Bake 20 to 25 minutes until just golden on the bottom.|Cool and dust with powdered sugar.","Egyptian"],
[3325,"Zalabia (Egyptian Fried Dough in Syrup)","treats","🍩",80,"Medium",9,8,"Crisp fried dough nuggets drenched in light sugar syrup, a festive Egyptian street sweet.","2 cup|flour;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1 tsp|yeast;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1/4 tsp|salt;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 1/2 cup|sugar|for syrup;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|rose water","Whisk the flour, cornstarch, yeast, sugar and salt, then stir in the yogurt and warm water to make a thick, sticky batter.|Cover and rest 45 minutes until bubbly.|Boil the syrup sugar with 3/4 cup water 8 minutes, stir in lemon juice and rose water, and cool.|Heat the oil in a deep pot to 350 degrees F.|Drop spoonfuls of batter into the oil and fry in batches 3 to 4 minutes until deep golden.|Drain briefly, then dip into the syrup and serve warm.","Egyptian"],
[3326,"Eish el Saraya (Egyptian Bread Pudding with Cream)","treats","🍮",60,"Medium",9,10,"Syrup-soaked toast layered with thick cream and pistachios, the palace bread dessert.","10 slice|bread|white, toasted until dry;1 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|lemon juice;2 cup|milk;1 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/4 cup|sugar|for cream;1/4 cup|pistachios|crushed","Boil 1 cup sugar with 3/4 cup water 8 minutes, stir in the lemon juice and cool.|Whisk the cornstarch with 1/2 cup cold milk, then heat the remaining milk, cream and 1/4 cup sugar until steaming.|Whisk in the cornstarch mixture and cook 5 minutes until thick, then cool to room temperature.|Arrange half the toast in a dish and drizzle with half the syrup.|Spread half the cream over the toast, repeat with remaining toast and syrup, then top with remaining cream.|Chill at least 3 hours and serve with crushed pistachios.","Egyptian"],
[3327,"Semsemiya (Egyptian Sesame Bars)","treats","🍬",30,"Easy",9,16,"Crunchy sesame brittle bars with honey and caramelized sugar, a classic Egyptian sweet.","2 cup|sesame seeds;3/4 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|honey;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|butter","Toast the sesame seeds in a dry skillet over medium heat 4 to 5 minutes until golden, then set aside.|Grease a baking sheet and a rolling pin with butter.|Melt the sugar and honey in a heavy saucepan over medium heat 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until deep amber.|Stir in the lemon juice and the sesame seeds quickly.|Pour onto the sheet, roll to 1/4 inch thick and cut into bars while still warm.|Cool completely and store airtight.","Egyptian"],
[3328,"Belila (Egyptian Sweet Wheat Berry Pudding)","treats","🥣",150,"Easy",9,6,"Tender wheat berries simmered in sweet milk with raisins, coconut and nuts for a cozy winter dessert.","1 cup|wheat berries|rinsed;4 cup|milk;1/2 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|raisins;1/2 cup|coconut flakes|unsweetened;1/4 cup|almonds|chopped;1/4 cup|pistachios|chopped;1/2 tsp|cinnamon","Cover the wheat berries with 4 cups of water and simmer partly covered 1 1/2 hours until tender, adding water if needed.|Drain, then add the milk and sugar and simmer 15 minutes, stirring now and then.|Stir in the raisins and half the coconut and cook 10 minutes more until creamy.|Spoon into bowls and top with the remaining coconut, almonds, pistachios and cinnamon.|Serve warm or chilled.","Egyptian"],
[3329,"Garlic Bread","sides","🥖",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crusty bread slathered in garlic-parsley butter and baked until golden and crisp at the edges.","1|french bread|1 loaf, about 16 inches;1/2 cup|butter|softened;4 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|parmesan|finely grated;1/4 tsp|salt","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Mash the softened butter with the garlic, parsley, parmesan and salt until evenly blended.|Slice the loaf in half lengthwise and spread the garlic butter generously over both cut sides.|Place the halves cut side up on a baking sheet and bake 10 to 12 minutes until the butter is bubbling.|Broil 1 to 2 minutes for deeper color, watching closely so the edges do not burn.|Slice crosswise into pieces and serve warm.","Italian"],
[3330,"Arancini","sides","🍙",75,"Medium",7.5,6,"Crispy fried risotto balls with a melty mozzarella center, a Sicilian street food favorite.","3 cup|rice|cooked and chilled risotto or arborio rice;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2|eggs|1 in the rice, 1 for coating;6 oz|fresh mozzarella|cut in small cubes;1 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|flour;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|marinara sauce|warmed, for dipping;|salt|to taste","Stir the cold cooked rice with the parmesan, 1 beaten egg and a pinch of salt until it holds together.|Scoop about 3 tablespoons of rice into your wet palm, press a mozzarella cube in the center and shape into a ball, sealing the rice around it.|Beat the second egg in a bowl and set out the flour and breadcrumbs in two more bowls.|Roll each ball in flour, dip in egg, then coat in breadcrumbs. Chill 15 minutes.|Heat the oil to 350°F in a heavy pot.|Fry the balls in batches 3 to 4 minutes until deep golden, turning once.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot with warm marinara.","Italian"],
[3331,"Caponata","sides","🍆",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Sicilian sweet and sour eggplant stew with celery, tomato, olives and capers, lovely warm or at room temperature.","2 lb|eggplant|cut in 3/4 inch cubes;1/3 cup|olive oil;1|onion|diced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;1 cup|diced tomatoes|canned or fresh;1/4 cup|olives|green, pitted and sliced;2 tbsp|capers|drained;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|basil|torn;|salt|to taste","Toss the eggplant cubes with 1 teaspoon salt and let them sit 15 minutes, then pat dry.|Heat half the oil in a large skillet over medium-high and brown the eggplant in batches, about 6 minutes per batch. Set aside.|Add the remaining oil, the onion and celery and cook over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes until softened.|Stir in the tomatoes, olives and capers and simmer 8 minutes.|Add the vinegar and sugar, return the eggplant and simmer 10 minutes more until glossy and tender.|Cool to warm or room temperature, stir in the basil and adjust the salt and vinegar.","Italian"],
[3332,"Roasted Broccolini with Garlic","sides","🥦",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Tender-crisp broccolini roasted with sliced garlic, lemon and a shower of parmesan.","2 bunch|broccoli|broccolini, ends trimmed;3 tbsp|olive oil;4 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/2|lemon|juiced;1/4 cup|parmesan|shaved;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 425°F with a baking sheet inside.|Toss the broccolini with the olive oil, garlic, red pepper flakes and 1/2 teaspoon salt.|Spread on the hot sheet in a single layer.|Roast 10 to 12 minutes until the stalks are tender and the tips are charred.|Squeeze the lemon over the top, scatter with parmesan and serve at once.","Italian"],
[3333,"Tuscan White Bean Salad","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Creamy cannellini beans tossed with red onion, tomato, sage and a lemony olive oil dressing.","2 can|cannellini beans|15 oz each, drained and rinsed;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|dried basil;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the sliced red onion in cold water for 5 minutes to mellow its bite, then drain.|Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, dried basil, salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Add the beans, onion, tomatoes and parsley.|Toss gently, then let stand 10 minutes so the beans absorb the dressing.|Taste for salt and lemon and serve at room temperature or chilled.","Italian"],
[3334,"Stuffed Mushrooms","sides","🍄",40,"Easy",7.5,6,"Baby bella caps filled with Italian sausage, garlic, breadcrumbs and parmesan, baked until golden.","24|mushrooms|baby bella, stems removed and finely chopped;6 oz|italian sausage|casings removed;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|olive oil","Heat the oven to 375°F and lightly oil a baking sheet.|Brown the sausage with the chopped mushroom stems in a skillet over medium-high for 6 minutes, breaking it up.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute, then take off the heat.|Stir in the cream cheese, breadcrumbs, half the parmesan and the parsley until combined.|Mound the filling into the mushroom caps and arrange on the sheet.|Top with the remaining parmesan and bake 20 to 22 minutes until browned and tender.","Italian"],
[3335,"Polenta Fries","sides","🍟",90,"Medium",7.5,6,"Firm polenta cut into sticks and baked until crisp outside and creamy within, great with marinara.","1 cup|polenta|coarse cornmeal;4 cup|water;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1 cup|marinara sauce|warmed, for dipping","Bring the water and salt to a boil in a heavy saucepan, then whisk in the polenta in a slow stream.|Reduce to low and cook 25 to 30 minutes, stirring often, until very thick.|Stir in the butter and parmesan, then spread into a greased 8 by 8 inch pan.|Chill at least 1 hour until completely firm.|Heat the oven to 425°F. Turn the polenta out and cut into sticks about 1/2 inch thick.|Toss with the olive oil and garlic powder and bake on a lined sheet 35 to 40 minutes, flipping once, until crisp and golden.|Serve hot with the warm marinara.","Italian"],
[3336,"Panzanella","sides","🍅",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Tuscan bread salad of toasted bread, ripe tomatoes, cucumber and basil soaked in a red wine vinaigrette.","6 cup|french bread|cut in 1 inch cubes, a day old;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 1/2 lb|tomatoes|ripe, chopped;1|cucumber|peeled and sliced;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|basil|torn;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 clove|garlic|minced;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F. Toss the bread cubes with 2 tablespoons olive oil and a pinch of salt.|Bake 10 to 12 minutes until golden and crisp at the edges. Cool.|Combine the tomatoes, cucumber and red onion in a large bowl and sprinkle with salt.|Whisk the remaining oil, vinegar, garlic and pepper into a dressing.|Add the bread, basil and dressing to the vegetables and toss.|Let stand 15 minutes so the bread soaks up the juices, then serve.","Italian"],
[3337,"Roast Potatoes","sides","🥔",70,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy inside and shatteringly crisp outside, parboiled and roasted in hot fat the Sunday-lunch way.","3 lb|potatoes|russet or Maris Piper style, peeled and cut in large chunks;1/3 cup|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|salt|for the boiling water;4 clove|garlic|smashed, in their skins;3 sprig|fresh thyme;|coarse salt|to finish","Heat the oven to 425°F and put the oil in a roasting pan on the middle rack to get very hot.|Boil the potatoes in well-salted water 8 to 10 minutes until the edges are soft but the centers are firm.|Drain and let steam dry 3 minutes, then shake the colander so the edges roughen.|Carefully add the potatoes to the hot oil, turning to coat, and roast 25 minutes.|Turn them, add the garlic and thyme, and roast 25 to 30 minutes more until deep golden and crisp.|Sprinkle with coarse salt and serve straight away.","British"],
[3338,"Mushy Peas","sides","🟢",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Soft, buttery, lightly mashed peas with mint, the classic partner to fish and chips.","4 cup|frozen peas;3 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|fresh mint|chopped;1/2 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the peas in a saucepan of boiling water for 5 minutes until very tender.|Drain well, reserving a few tablespoons of the cooking water.|Return the peas to the pot with the butter, sugar and a pinch of salt.|Mash roughly with a potato masher, leaving some texture, adding splashes of cooking water if too stiff.|Stir in the mint, lemon juice and pepper, then adjust the salt and serve hot.","British"],
[3339,"Bubble and Squeak","sides","🥬",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Leftover mashed potato and cabbage fried into a crusty golden cake, a British kitchen classic.","2 cup|mashed potatoes|cold, leftover;2 cup|cabbage|cooked, chopped;1|onion|finely diced;2 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt half the butter in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes until soft.|In a bowl mix the cold mashed potato, cabbage and cooked onion with plenty of salt and pepper.|Add the oil and remaining butter to the skillet and heat over medium-high.|Press the mixture into the pan in an even cake about 3/4 inch thick.|Cook 8 minutes without moving until the bottom is deeply browned, then flip in sections or slide onto a plate and invert back into the pan.|Fry 6 to 8 minutes more until crusty on both sides and hot throughout, then cut into wedges.","British"],
[3340,"Scotch Eggs","sides","🥚",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Soft-boiled eggs wrapped in seasoned sausage, breaded and fried until crunchy.","6|eggs|large, for boiling;1 lb|breakfast sausage|bulk, uncased;1/2 tsp|dried thyme;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|flour;1|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|panko;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 tbsp|dijon mustard|for serving","Lower 6 eggs into boiling water and cook exactly 6 minutes for a soft yolk. Move to ice water for 10 minutes, then peel.|Mix the sausage with the thyme and pepper and divide into 6 equal portions.|Flatten each portion into a thin round on wet hands and wrap it around an egg, sealing all seams.|Roll each wrapped egg in flour, then the beaten egg, then the panko.|Heat the oil to 340°F in a deep pot.|Fry 3 eggs at a time 6 to 7 minutes, turning, until deep golden and the sausage is cooked through (160°F).|Drain on a rack, cool a few minutes and serve warm or cold with mustard.","British"],
[3341,"Sausage Rolls","sides","🥐",50,"Easy",7.5,12,"Seasoned pork filling wrapped in flaky puff pastry and baked until golden, perfect party food.","1 lb|ground pork;1/2|onion|grated;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;1 tsp|dried thyme;1/2 tsp|dried sage;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2|puff pastry|sheets, thawed;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing;1 tbsp|sesame seeds","Thaw the puff pastry sheets according to the package and heat the oven to 400°F.|Mix the pork, onion, breadcrumbs, thyme, sage, salt and pepper until just combined.|Unfold the pastry and cut each sheet in half lengthwise.|Spoon a log of filling along the center of each strip, brush one edge with egg and fold over to seal.|Cut each roll into 6 pieces, place seam side down on a lined sheet and brush with egg.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and bake 25 to 30 minutes until puffed, golden and cooked through (160°F).","British"],
[3342,"Cauliflower Cheese","sides","🧀",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Tender cauliflower in a mustardy cheddar sauce, baked until bubbling, a Sunday roast staple.","1 head|cauliflower|cut in florets;3 tbsp|butter;3 tbsp|flour;2 cup|milk;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|sharp, grated;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1/4 tsp|paprika;1/4 cup|breadcrumbs;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F. Boil the florets in salted water 5 to 6 minutes until just tender, then drain well.|Melt the butter in a saucepan, whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Gradually whisk in the milk and simmer 5 minutes until thick enough to coat a spoon.|Off the heat stir in 1 cup of the cheddar, the mustard, paprika and salt.|Arrange the cauliflower in a baking dish and pour the sauce over.|Top with the remaining cheese and the breadcrumbs and bake 20 to 25 minutes until golden and bubbling.","British"],
[3343,"Mashed Potatoes","sides","🥔",35,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy, buttery mashed potatoes made with warm cream, the comfort-food side for every holiday table.","3 lb|russet potatoes|peeled and cut in chunks;1/2 cup|butter;3/4 cup|heavy cream|warmed;2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|chives|chopped, optional","Put the potatoes in a large pot, cover with cold water by 1 inch and add 1 tablespoon salt.|Bring to a boil and simmer 15 to 20 minutes until a knife slides in with no resistance.|Drain well and return to the hot pot for 1 minute to steam off moisture.|Mash with a masher or ricer, then fold in the butter until melted.|Add the warm cream gradually, stirring until smooth and fluffy.|Season with salt and pepper and top with chives.","American"],
[3344,"Macaroni Salad","sides","🥗",35,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Cold elbow macaroni in a tangy creamy dressing with celery, pepper and onion, a picnic favorite.","1 lb|elbow macaroni;1 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tbsp|mustard|yellow;1 tbsp|sugar;2 stalk|celery|finely diced;1/2|bell pepper|finely diced;1/4|red onion|finely diced;1 tsp|paprika;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the macaroni in salted water 1 minute past the package time so it stays tender once chilled.|Drain, rinse under cold water and drain again thoroughly.|Whisk the mayonnaise, vinegar, mustard, sugar, salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Fold in the macaroni, celery, bell pepper and onion.|Cover and chill at least 2 hours, then stir in a splash of milk if it looks dry.|Dust with paprika and serve cold.","American"],
[3345,"Creamed Corn","sides","🌽",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sweet corn simmered in cream and butter until thick and spoonable, no can needed.","5 cup|frozen corn|thawed;3 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|milk;1 tbsp|flour;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat.|Add 4 cups of the corn and cook 4 minutes, stirring.|Whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Add the cream, milk, sugar, salt and pepper and simmer 8 to 10 minutes until thickened.|Blend or mash the remaining 1 cup of corn with a splash of the sauce and stir it back in for a creamy body.|Cook 2 minutes more, taste for salt and serve hot.","American"],
[3346,"Green Bean Casserole","sides","🫛",50,"Easy",7.5,8,"Green beans and mushrooms in a creamy sauce under crispy fried onions, a Thanksgiving classic made from scratch.","1 1/2 lb|green beans|trimmed and cut in 2 inch pieces;3 tbsp|butter;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|flour;1 cup|chicken broth;3/4 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|soy sauce;1 1/2 cup|fried onions|crispy store-bought;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the green beans in salted water 4 minutes, then drain and rinse with cold water.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium-high and cook the mushrooms 8 minutes until browned.|Add the garlic and flour and stir 1 minute.|Pour in the broth, cream and soy sauce and simmer 5 minutes until thick.|Stir in the green beans and half the fried onions, season with salt and pepper and pour into a 2 quart baking dish.|Bake 20 minutes, top with the remaining fried onions and bake 5 minutes more.","American"],
[3347,"Onion Rings","sides","🧅",35,"Medium",7.5,4,"Thick onion slices in a crunchy buttermilk-style beer-free batter, fried until golden.","2|onion|large sweet, sliced 1/2 inch thick;1 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|milk;1|eggs;1 cup|panko;3 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Separate the onion slices into rings.|Whisk the flour, baking powder, paprika, garlic powder and salt, then whisk in the milk and egg to a smooth batter.|Spread the panko on a plate.|Heat the oil to 375°F in a heavy pot.|Dip each ring in the batter, let the excess drip off, then press into the panko.|Fry in small batches 2 to 3 minutes per side until deep golden.|Drain on a rack, sprinkle with salt and serve hot.","American"],
[3348,"American Potato Salad","sides","🥔",50,"Easy",7.5,8,"Cookout-style potato salad with eggs, celery and a creamy mustard dressing.","3 lb|potatoes|red or yukon gold, scrubbed;4|eggs|hard-boiled and chopped;3/4 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|mustard|yellow;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;2 stalk|celery|diced;1/4|red onion|finely diced;2 tbsp|pickles|sweet relish;1 tsp|paprika;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cover the potatoes with cold salted water and boil 15 to 20 minutes until just fork tender.|Drain, cool 10 minutes, then peel if you like and cut into 3/4 inch cubes.|Toss the warm potatoes with the vinegar and 1 teaspoon salt and let cool.|Stir the mayonnaise, mustard, relish and pepper together.|Fold the dressing, eggs, celery and onion into the potatoes.|Chill at least 2 hours, dust with paprika and serve cold.","American"],
[3349,"Roasted Brussels Sprouts","sides","🥬",35,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Halved sprouts roasted until caramelized and crisp, finished with a balsamic drizzle.","1 1/2 lb|brussels sprouts|trimmed and halved;3 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze;2 tbsp|parmesan|shaved, optional","Heat the oven to 425°F with a rimmed baking sheet inside.|Toss the sprouts with the olive oil, salt and pepper.|Spread cut side down on the hot sheet.|Roast 20 to 25 minutes, shaking the pan once, until the cut sides are deeply browned and the outer leaves are crisp.|Drizzle with the balsamic glaze, top with parmesan and serve hot.","American"],
[3350,"Glazed Carrots","sides","🥕",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Tender carrots cooked in butter and honey until shiny and lightly sweet.","1 1/2 lb|carrots|peeled and sliced on the bias;3 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|honey;1/2 cup|water;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|lemon juice","Put the carrots, butter, water and salt in a wide skillet.|Bring to a simmer, cover and cook 8 minutes until nearly tender.|Uncover, add the honey and cook over medium-high 5 to 6 minutes, stirring, until the liquid reduces to a glossy glaze.|Stir in the lemon juice and parsley and serve hot.","American"],
[3351,"Spinach Salad with Warm Bacon Dressing","sides","🥗",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Fresh spinach, egg and mushrooms wilted slightly under a sweet-sour warm bacon vinaigrette.","8 oz|spinach|baby, washed;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;4 oz|mushrooms|sliced;2|eggs|hard-boiled and sliced;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tsp|dijon mustard;|black pepper|to taste","Place the spinach in a large bowl with the sliced mushrooms and eggs.|Cook the bacon in a skillet over medium heat 8 to 10 minutes until crisp, then remove with a slotted spoon.|Leave about 3 tablespoons of fat in the pan and cook the onion 3 minutes until soft.|Whisk in the vinegar, brown sugar and mustard and simmer 1 minute.|Pour the hot dressing over the spinach, add the bacon and toss.|Season with pepper and serve immediately.","American"],
[3352,"Sweet Potato Casserole","sides","🍠",70,"Easy",7.5,8,"Mashed sweet potatoes with warm spice, topped with a crunchy brown sugar pecan streusel.","3 lb|sweet potatoes|peeled and cubed;4 tbsp|butter|melted, for the potatoes;1/2 cup|milk;1/4 cup|brown sugar;1 tsp|vanilla;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|flour|for topping;1/2 cup|brown sugar|for topping;4 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed for topping;1 cup|pecans|chopped","Heat the oven to 350°F and butter a 9 by 13 inch dish.|Boil the sweet potatoes 15 minutes until very tender, then drain well.|Mash with the melted butter, milk, 1/4 cup brown sugar, vanilla, cinnamon and salt until smooth.|Spread in the baking dish.|Rub the flour, remaining 1/2 cup brown sugar and cold butter together to coarse crumbs, then stir in the pecans.|Scatter over the potatoes and bake 30 minutes until the topping is crisp and golden.","American"],
[3353,"Saganaki","sides","🧀",15,"Easy",7.5,4,"Pan-fried Greek cheese with a golden crust, served sizzling with a squeeze of lemon.","8 oz|halloumi|cut in 1/2 inch slabs;1/4 cup|flour;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|lemon|cut in wedges;1/2 tsp|oregano;1 tbsp|honey|optional","Pat the cheese dry and dredge the slabs lightly in the flour, shaking off the excess.|Heat the oil in a nonstick skillet over medium-high until shimmering.|Fry the cheese 1 to 2 minutes per side until deep golden.|Transfer to a warm plate, squeeze lemon over, sprinkle with oregano and drizzle with honey if you like.|Serve immediately while soft and sizzling.","Greek"],
[3354,"Fava Santorinis","sides","🟡",60,"Easy",7.5,6,"Silky yellow split pea puree topped with capers, red onion and olive oil, the signature dip of Santorini.","1 1/2 cup|lentils|yellow split peas;1|onion|halved;5 cup|water;1/3 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|lemon juice;2 tbsp|capers|drained;1/2|red onion|finely diced;|salt|to taste","Rinse the split peas and put them in a pot with the water and halved onion.|Bring to a boil, skim the foam, then simmer partly covered 40 to 45 minutes, stirring often, until completely soft and the water is absorbed.|Discard the onion and blend the peas with half the olive oil and 1 teaspoon salt until smooth.|Stir in the lemon juice and adjust the salt.|Spread on a platter and let it set about 15 minutes.|Top with the capers, red onion and the remaining olive oil.","Greek"],
[3355,"Briam","sides","🍆",90,"Easy",7.5,6,"Greek roasted summer vegetables, potato, zucchini and eggplant baked in olive oil and tomato.","1 lb|potatoes|sliced 1/4 inch thick;2|zucchini|sliced;1|eggplant|cubed;2|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|sliced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;1/3 cup|olive oil;1 tsp|oregano;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Toss the potatoes, zucchini, eggplant, onion and garlic in a large roasting pan with the olive oil, oregano, 1 1/2 teaspoons salt and pepper.|Pour the diced tomatoes and 1/2 cup water over the top.|Bake 30 minutes, then stir.|Bake 40 to 50 minutes more, stirring once, until the vegetables are tender and lightly browned and the sauce has thickened.|Stir in the parsley and serve warm or at room temperature.","Greek"],
[3356,"Esquites","sides","🌽",20,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Mexican street corn served in a cup, with mayo, lime, cotija-style cheese and chile.","5 cup|frozen corn|thawed;2 tbsp|butter;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|feta|crumbled, or cotija;2 tbsp|lime juice;1/2 tsp|chili powder;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;1|jalapeno|minced, optional;|salt|to taste","Melt the butter in a large skillet over high heat.|Add the corn in a single layer and cook, stirring only occasionally, 6 to 8 minutes until charred in spots.|Transfer to a bowl and cool 5 minutes.|Stir in the mayonnaise, sour cream, lime juice, half the cheese, jalapeno and salt.|Spoon into cups and top with the remaining cheese, chili powder and cilantro.","Mexican"],
[3357,"Charro Beans","sides","🫘",150,"Easy",7.5,8,"Slow-simmered pinto beans with bacon, tomato and jalapeno, the cowboy-style Mexican bean pot.","1 lb|pinto beans|dried, rinsed;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2|tomatoes|diced;1|jalapeno|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|oregano;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;6 cup|water;|salt|to taste","Cook the bacon in a large pot over medium heat 6 to 8 minutes until crisp.|Add the onion and jalapeno and cook 5 minutes, then the garlic for 1 minute.|Stir in the beans, water, cumin and oregano and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a gentle simmer, partly covered, and cook 1 1/2 to 2 hours until the beans are tender.|Add the tomatoes and 1 1/2 teaspoons salt and simmer 20 minutes more until the broth thickens.|Stir in the cilantro and serve in bowls.","Mexican"],
[3358,"Calabacitas con Elote","sides","🥒",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Sauteed zucchini, corn and tomato with poblano and a touch of cream, a homey Mexican vegetable side.","1 lb|zucchini|diced;1 1/2 cup|frozen corn;1|poblano peppers|diced;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|tomatoes|diced;1 tbsp|olive oil;1/4 cup|sour cream;1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend;|salt|to taste","Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Cook the onion and poblano 4 minutes until starting to soften, then add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Add the zucchini and corn and cook 6 to 8 minutes, stirring, until the zucchini is tender-crisp.|Stir in the tomatoes and 3/4 teaspoon salt and cook 3 minutes.|Reduce the heat, stir in the sour cream and cheese until melted and creamy.|Taste for salt and serve warm.","Mexican"],
[3359,"Pickled Red Onions","sides","🧅",40,"Very easy",7.5,10,"Bright pink Yucatan-style pickled onions that brighten tacos, rice bowls and sandwiches.","2|red onion|thinly sliced;1 cup|apple cider vinegar;1/2 cup|water;1 tbsp|sugar;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|oregano;3 clove|garlic|smashed;1|lime|juiced","Put the onion slices in a heatproof jar or bowl.|Bring the vinegar, water, sugar, salt, oregano and garlic to a simmer, stirring to dissolve.|Pour the hot brine and the lime juice over the onions.|Press the onions under the liquid and let cool 30 minutes at room temperature.|Serve right away or refrigerate up to 2 weeks.","Mexican"],
[3360,"Garlic Edamame","sides","🫛",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Steamed edamame pods tossed with garlic, chili flakes and flaky salt, the easy izakaya snack.","1 lb|edamame|in the pod, frozen;1 tbsp|sesame oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tsp|soy sauce;|coarse salt|to taste","Boil the edamame in salted water 4 to 5 minutes until tender and bright green, then drain.|Heat the sesame oil in a skillet over medium heat and cook the garlic and red pepper flakes 30 to 45 seconds until fragrant.|Add the edamame and soy sauce and toss 1 minute to coat.|Transfer to a bowl, sprinkle with coarse salt and serve warm, squeezing the beans from their pods.","Japanese"],
[3361,"Garlic Bok Choy","sides","🥬",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Baby bok choy quickly stir-fried with garlic and ginger in a light savory sauce.","1 1/2 lb|baby bok choy|halved lengthwise;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;4 clove|garlic|sliced;1 tbsp|ginger|minced;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|oyster sauce;1 tsp|sesame oil;1/4 cup|water","Rinse the bok choy well, keeping the halves intact, and drain.|Stir together the soy sauce, oyster sauce, sesame oil and water.|Heat the oil in a wok or large skillet over high heat and stir-fry the garlic and ginger 20 seconds.|Add the bok choy cut side down and cook 2 minutes until lightly browned.|Pour in the sauce, cover and cook 2 to 3 minutes until the stems are just tender.|Serve hot with the sauce spooned over.","Chinese"],
[3362,"Napa Cabbage Kimchi","sides","🥬",120,"Medium",7.5,16,"Spicy fermented napa cabbage with gochugaru, garlic and ginger, ready to eat fresh or let sour in the fridge.","2 lb|cabbage|napa, cut in 2 inch pieces;1/4 cup|coarse salt;1 cup|water;1 tbsp|sugar;1/2 cup|red pepper flakes|gochugaru;2 tbsp|fish sauce;6 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|minced;4|green onion|cut in 1 inch pieces;1/2 cup|carrots|matchstick","Toss the cabbage with the coarse salt and let stand 1 1/2 to 2 hours, turning every 30 minutes, until limp.|Rinse the cabbage 3 times in cold water and drain very well, squeezing out the excess.|Mix the pepper flakes, fish sauce, garlic, ginger and sugar into a paste, adding a splash of water if stiff.|Wearing gloves, toss the cabbage with the paste, green onion and carrots until evenly coated.|Pack tightly into a clean jar, pressing down, leaving 1 inch of headspace.|Leave at room temperature 1 to 2 days until slightly tangy and bubbly, then refrigerate. It keeps about 3 weeks.","Korean"],
[3363,"Miso Eggplant","sides","🍆",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Broiled eggplant halves glazed with sweet miso, nasu dengaku style, soft and deeply savory.","2|eggplant|japanese or small, halved lengthwise;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|miso paste;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|rice vinegar|or mirin;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;1|green onion|sliced","Heat the oven to 425°F. Score the cut sides of the eggplant in a diamond pattern.|Brush with oil and roast cut side down on a lined sheet 15 to 20 minutes until soft.|Whisk the miso, sugar and vinegar with 2 tablespoons water in a small saucepan and simmer 2 minutes until glossy.|Turn the eggplant cut side up and spread the glaze over the tops.|Broil 3 to 4 minutes until bubbling and browned in spots.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and green onion.","Japanese"],
[3364,"Sesame Green Beans","sides","🫛",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Blistered green beans tossed in garlic, soy and toasted sesame, ready in 20 minutes.","1 lb|green beans|trimmed;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|rice vinegar;1 tsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes","Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet or wok over high heat.|Add the green beans in one layer and cook 5 to 6 minutes, stirring now and then, until blistered in spots.|Add the garlic and red pepper flakes and cook 30 seconds.|Pour in the soy sauce, vinegar and 2 tablespoons water, cover and steam 2 minutes until just tender.|Remove from the heat, toss with the sesame oil and sesame seeds and serve.","Chinese"],
[3365,"Sigeumchi Namul","sides","🥬",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Korean seasoned spinach, blanched and dressed with sesame oil, garlic and soy, a staple banchan.","1 lb|spinach|fresh, not baby;2 tsp|sesame oil;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1|green onion|finely sliced;|salt|to taste","Boil a large pot of water with a pinch of salt and blanch the spinach 30 to 45 seconds until just wilted.|Drain and plunge into ice water, then squeeze out as much water as possible.|Loosen the spinach with your fingers and cut into 3 inch lengths.|Toss with the sesame oil, garlic, soy sauce, green onion and half the sesame seeds.|Garnish with the remaining seeds and serve at room temperature or chilled.","Korean"],
[3366,"Labneh with Za'atar","sides","🥣",720,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Thick strained yogurt spread with olive oil and za'atar, a creamy dip for warm pita.","3 cup|greek yogurt|plain, full fat;3/4 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tsp|za'atar;1 tbsp|mint|dried or fresh, optional;1|cucumber|sliced, for serving;2|pita|warmed, for serving","Stir the salt into the yogurt.|Line a sieve with a double layer of cheesecloth or a clean thin towel and set it over a bowl.|Spoon in the yogurt, fold the cloth over and refrigerate 8 to 24 hours until thick and spreadable like cream cheese.|Spread the labneh in a shallow bowl, swirling the top with the back of a spoon.|Drizzle with the olive oil and sprinkle with za'atar and mint.|Serve with warm pita and cucumber.","Middle Eastern"],
[3367,"Tahini Roasted Cauliflower","sides","🥦",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Golden roasted cauliflower with a lemony tahini sauce and a scatter of parsley and pomegranate.","1 head|cauliflower|cut in florets;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|paprika;1/4 cup|tahini;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 clove|garlic|grated;3 tbsp|warm water;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 450°F.|Toss the cauliflower with the olive oil, cumin, paprika and 3/4 teaspoon salt.|Roast on a rimmed sheet 25 to 30 minutes, turning once, until deeply golden and tender.|Whisk the tahini, lemon juice, garlic, warm water and a pinch of salt to a smooth pourable sauce, thinning with more water if needed.|Spread the sauce on a platter, pile the cauliflower on top and sprinkle with parsley.","Middle Eastern"],
[3368,"Shirazi Salad","sides","🥒",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Persian chopped cucumber, tomato and onion in lime and mint, light and refreshing.","4|cucumber|persian or small, diced;3|tomatoes|diced;1/2|red onion|finely diced;2 tbsp|fresh mint|chopped;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;3 tbsp|lime juice;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|dried mint;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Combine the cucumber, tomatoes and red onion in a bowl.|Whisk the lime juice, olive oil, dried mint, salt and pepper.|Pour over the vegetables, add the fresh mint and parsley and toss.|Let rest 10 minutes and serve cold within an hour for the crispest texture.","Middle Eastern"],
[3369,"Carottes Rapees","sides","🥕",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"French grated carrot salad with a mustardy lemon vinaigrette, a bistro and picnic staple.","1 lb|carrots|peeled and grated;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|honey;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, mustard, honey, 1/2 teaspoon salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Add the grated carrots and parsley.|Toss well until coated.|Chill 15 minutes so the carrots soften slightly and absorb the dressing, then adjust the seasoning and serve.","French"],
[3370,"Haricots Verts Amandine","sides","🫛",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Slim green beans tossed in browned butter with toasted almonds and lemon.","1 lb|green beans|haricots verts, trimmed;3 tbsp|butter;1/3 cup|almonds|sliced;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Boil the beans in well-salted water 3 to 4 minutes until crisp-tender, then drain and rinse in cold water.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat and add the almonds.|Cook 3 to 4 minutes, stirring, until the butter smells nutty and the almonds are golden.|Add the garlic for 30 seconds, then the beans and cook 2 minutes to heat through.|Stir in the lemon juice, season with salt and pepper and serve.","French"],
[3371,"Gougeres","sides","🧀",55,"Medium",7.5,8,"Light, airy French cheese puffs made from choux pastry and gruyere, perfect with a glass of wine.","1/2 cup|water;1/2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|butter|cubed;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|flour;4|eggs;1 cup|gruyere|grated;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 pinch|nutmeg","Heat the oven to 425°F and line two baking sheets with parchment.|Bring the water, milk, butter and salt to a boil in a saucepan, then dump in the flour all at once.|Stir hard over medium heat 2 minutes until the dough pulls away from the pan and a film forms on the bottom.|Beat in 4 eggs one at a time with a wooden spoon or mixer until smooth and glossy.|Mix in three quarters of the gruyere, the pepper and nutmeg.|Spoon or pipe tablespoon mounds 2 inches apart and sprinkle with the remaining cheese.|Bake 10 minutes, reduce to 375°F and bake 15 to 18 minutes more until deep golden and puffed. Serve warm.","French"],
[3372,"Roasted Fennel with Parmesan","sides","🌿",50,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Wedges of fennel roasted until sweet and caramelized, finished with melted parmesan and lemon.","2|fennel bulbs|trimmed and cut into wedges;3 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1/2 cup|parmesan|freshly grated;1/2|lemon|juiced;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F and line a rimmed baking sheet with parchment.|Toss the fennel wedges with the olive oil, salt, and pepper and arrange them cut side down in a single layer.|Roast for 25 minutes, then flip the wedges and roast 10 minutes more until tender and browned at the edges.|Sprinkle the parmesan over the fennel and return to the oven for 5 minutes until melted and golden.|Squeeze the lemon over the top, scatter with parsley, and serve warm.","Italian"],
[3373,"Sauteed Broccoli Rabe with Garlic and Chili","sides","🥬",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"Pleasantly bitter broccoli rabe blanched, then sauteed with plenty of garlic and a kick of chili.","1 1/2 lb|broccoli rabe|tough ends trimmed;1 tbsp|salt|for the water;1/4 cup|olive oil;5 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/2|lemon|juiced;|salt|to taste","Bring a large pot of water to a boil and add 1 tablespoon of salt.|Blanch the broccoli rabe for 2 minutes, then drain well and let it steam dry for a minute.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute until fragrant but not browned.|Add the broccoli rabe and toss for 4 to 5 minutes until tender and coated in the oil.|Season with salt, squeeze over the lemon juice, and serve hot.","Italian"],
[3374,"Eggplant Involtini","sides","🍆",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Grilled eggplant slices rolled around creamy ricotta and baked in tomato sauce under melted mozzarella.","2|eggplant|sliced lengthwise 1/4 inch thick;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 1/2 cup|ricotta;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1|eggs;1/4 cup|basil|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;2 cup|marinara sauce;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded","Heat the oven to 400°F. Brush the eggplant slices on both sides with olive oil and sprinkle with a little salt.|Broil or grill the slices 3 to 4 minutes per side until soft and lightly browned, then let them cool.|Stir together the ricotta, half of the parmesan, the egg, basil, and salt.|Spread a thin layer of marinara in a baking dish. Put a spoonful of ricotta filling on the end of each slice and roll it up.|Place the rolls seam side down in the dish, spoon the remaining sauce over them, and top with mozzarella and the remaining parmesan.|Bake for 25 minutes until bubbling and golden, then rest 5 minutes before serving.","Italian"],
[3375,"Fried Zucchini Blossoms","sides","🌼",30,"Medium",7.5,4,"Delicate squash blossoms stuffed with mozzarella and fried in a light, crisp batter.","12|zucchini blossoms|stamens removed;4 oz|fresh mozzarella|cut into small strips;1 cup|flour;1 cup|water|ice cold;1 pinch|salt;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|coarse salt|to finish;1|lemon|cut into wedges","Gently open each blossom and tuck a strip of mozzarella inside, then twist the petals closed.|Whisk the flour, ice-cold water, and a pinch of salt just until the batter is loose and slightly lumpy.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350°F.|Dip each blossom in the batter, let the excess drip off, and fry in batches for 1 to 2 minutes per side until pale golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels, sprinkle with coarse salt, and serve immediately with lemon wedges.","Italian"],
[3376,"Giardiniera","sides","🥒",30,"Easy",7.5,12,"Crunchy Italian pickled vegetables in a garlicky vinegar brine, good with sandwiches and antipasto boards.","2|carrots|sliced;1/2 head|cauliflower|cut into small florets;2 stalk|celery|sliced;1|bell pepper|cut into strips;1|red onion|sliced;2 cup|white vinegar;2 cup|water;1/4 cup|sugar;3 tbsp|coarse salt;4 clove|garlic|smashed;1 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tsp|oregano","Combine the carrots, cauliflower, celery, bell pepper, and onion in a large heatproof bowl.|In a saucepan, bring the vinegar, water, sugar, and salt to a boil, stirring until dissolved.|Add the garlic, red pepper flakes, and oregano to the vegetables and pour the hot brine over them.|Let cool to room temperature, then pack into clean jars with the brine.|Refrigerate for at least 24 hours before eating. It keeps for up to 3 weeks in the refrigerator.","Italian"],
[3377,"Cacio e Pepe Potatoes","sides","🥔",50,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crisp roasted potatoes tossed with pecorino and a generous hit of cracked black pepper.","2 lb|baby potatoes|halved;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|butter;2 tsp|black pepper|coarsely cracked;3/4 cup|parmesan|finely grated, or pecorino","Heat the oven to 425°F with a baking sheet inside.|Toss the potatoes with the olive oil and salt and spread them cut side down on the hot sheet.|Roast for 30 to 35 minutes until deeply golden and tender.|Melt the butter in a small skillet, add the cracked pepper, and toast it for 1 minute until fragrant.|Toss the hot potatoes with the pepper butter, then scatter the cheese over them and toss again so it clings and melts.|Serve right away.","Italian"],
[3378,"Caprese Skewers","sides","🍅",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Cherry tomatoes, mozzarella pearls, and basil on picks with a drizzle of balsamic glaze.","1 pint|cherry tomatoes;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|small pearls, or cubes;24|basil|small leaves;2 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|balsamic glaze;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Thread a cherry tomato, a basil leaf folded in half, and a mozzarella ball onto each short skewer or toothpick.|Arrange the skewers on a platter.|Drizzle with the olive oil and balsamic glaze.|Season lightly with salt and pepper and serve within an hour.","Italian"],
[3379,"Fagioli all'Uccelletto","sides","🫘",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"A Tuscan side of cannellini beans simmered with sage, garlic, and tomato until thick and savory.","2 can|cannellini beans|15 oz, drained and rinsed;1/4 cup|olive oil;4 clove|garlic|lightly crushed;6|sage|fresh leaves;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 cup|crushed tomatoes;1/2 cup|water;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Warm the olive oil in a wide saucepan over medium-low heat and add the garlic, sage, and red pepper flakes.|Cook for 2 minutes until the garlic is just golden and the oil smells of sage.|Stir in the crushed tomatoes and water and simmer for 8 minutes.|Add the beans, season with salt and pepper, and simmer gently for 15 minutes, mashing a few beans against the pan to thicken the sauce.|Taste, adjust the seasoning, and serve warm with a drizzle of olive oil.","Italian"],
[3380,"Carciofi alla Romana","sides","🌿",70,"Medium",7.5,4,"Whole artichokes braised upside down in olive oil, garlic, and mint until meltingly tender.","4|artichokes|large, trimmed and chokes scooped out;1|lemon|halved, plus juice for water;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;2 tbsp|mint|chopped;1/2 cup|olive oil;1 cup|water;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Trim the artichokes down to the tender heart and inner leaves, cut off the top third, and scoop out the fuzzy choke. Rub with lemon and keep in lemon water.|Mix the garlic, parsley, mint, salt, and pepper and press some of the mixture into the center of each artichoke.|Stand the artichokes upside down, stems up, snugly in a pot just big enough to hold them.|Pour in the olive oil and water, cover, and simmer over medium-low heat for 35 to 45 minutes until a knife slides easily into the base.|Lift out the artichokes, spoon the pan juices over them, and serve warm or at room temperature.","Italian"],
[3381,"Pesto Potatoes with Green Beans","sides","🥔",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"The Ligurian trio of potatoes, green beans, and basil pesto, served warm or at room temperature.","1 1/2 lb|baby potatoes|cut into bite-size pieces;8 oz|green beans|trimmed and halved;1/2 cup|pesto;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|salt|for the water;2 tbsp|parmesan|grated;|black pepper|to taste","Put the potatoes in a pot of cold water with the salt, bring to a boil, and cook for 10 minutes.|Add the green beans to the pot and cook 5 minutes more until both are tender.|Reserve 1/4 cup of the cooking water, then drain the vegetables and return them to the pot.|Stir the pesto and olive oil with a few spoonfuls of the reserved water until loose, then fold it through the warm vegetables.|Finish with parmesan and black pepper and serve warm.","Italian"],
[3382,"Burrata with Roasted Tomatoes","sides","🍅",35,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Jammy slow-roasted cherry tomatoes spooned over creamy burrata with toast for scooping.","1 pint|cherry tomatoes;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 clove|garlic|sliced;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|oregano;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|one ball of burrata;2 tbsp|basil|torn;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze;4 slice|bread|toasted","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Toss the tomatoes with the olive oil, garlic, salt, and oregano on a small baking sheet.|Roast for 20 to 25 minutes until blistered and juicy.|Set the burrata on a plate and tear it open slightly.|Spoon the warm tomatoes and their juices over the burrata and top with basil and a drizzle of balsamic glaze.|Serve at once with the toasted bread.","Italian"],
[3383,"Marinated Olives","sides","🫒",15,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Mixed olives steeped in olive oil with garlic, lemon zest, rosemary, and chili for an instant antipasto.","2 cup|olives|mixed, drained;1/2 cup|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1|lemon|zest in strips;2 sprig|rosemary;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tsp|fennel seeds|lightly crushed","Warm the olive oil, garlic, lemon zest, rosemary, red pepper flakes, and fennel seeds in a small saucepan over low heat for 5 minutes. Do not let it fry.|Place the olives in a jar or bowl and pour the warm oil over them.|Let cool, then cover and marinate in the refrigerator for at least 4 hours, ideally overnight.|Bring to room temperature before serving. They keep for 2 weeks refrigerated.","Italian"],
[3384,"Supplì","sides","🍙",90,"Medium",7.5,6,"Roman fried rice croquettes in tomato risotto with a molten mozzarella center that stretches like a phone cord.","1 cup|arborio rice;2 1/2 cup|chicken broth|hot;1 cup|tomato sauce;2 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2|eggs|1 for the rice, 1 beaten;4 oz|fresh mozzarella|cut into small cubes;1 cup|breadcrumbs;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;|salt|to taste","Simmer the rice in the broth and tomato sauce with a pinch of salt for 18 minutes, stirring often, until tender and thick.|Stir in the butter, parmesan, and one egg, spread the rice on a tray, and cool completely, at least 30 minutes.|Take about 3 tablespoons of rice, flatten it in your palm, and press in a cube of mozzarella. Close the rice around it into an oval croquette.|Dip each croquette in the beaten egg, then roll in breadcrumbs.|Heat the oil to 350°F and fry the supplì in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve hot, so the cheese pulls into strings.","Italian"],
[3385,"Frittata di Zucchine","sides","🍳",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"A thick Italian zucchini frittata with parmesan and herbs, delicious hot, warm, or cold in wedges.","3|zucchini|thinly sliced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|thinly sliced;6|eggs;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|basil|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F.|In a 10-inch ovenproof skillet, heat the olive oil over medium heat and cook the onion for 4 minutes, then add the zucchini and cook 6 minutes until soft and lightly golden.|Whisk the eggs with the parmesan, basil, salt, and pepper.|Pour the eggs over the vegetables, stir once, and cook for 2 minutes until the edges set.|Transfer the skillet to the oven and bake 10 to 12 minutes until set and puffed in the center.|Rest for 5 minutes, then cut into wedges.","Italian"],
[3386,"Sauteed Spinach with Garlic","sides","🥬",12,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Spinaci all'aglio, a quick Italian side of wilted spinach in garlicky olive oil with a squeeze of lemon.","1 1/2 lb|spinach|baby, washed;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1 pinch|red pepper flakes;1/4 tsp|salt;1/2|lemon|cut into wedges","Warm the olive oil in a very large skillet or Dutch oven over medium heat.|Add the garlic and red pepper flakes and cook for 1 minute until the garlic is pale gold.|Add the spinach by the handful, tossing as each batch wilts, and sprinkle with salt.|Cook for 3 to 4 minutes until all the spinach has wilted and most of the liquid has cooked off.|Serve hot with lemon wedges.","Italian"],
[3387,"Radicchio Salad with Gorgonzola and Walnuts","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Bitter radicchio balanced by sweet pear, creamy gorgonzola, toasted walnuts, and a honey vinaigrette.","1 head|radicchio|torn into bite-size pieces;1|pear|thinly sliced;1/2 cup|walnuts|toasted and chopped;3 oz|gorgonzola|crumbled;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze;1 tbsp|honey;1/4 tsp|salt","Whisk the olive oil, balsamic glaze, honey, and salt in a large bowl.|Add the radicchio and toss to coat. Let it sit for 5 minutes to soften slightly.|Fold in the pear slices and half the walnuts.|Transfer to a platter and top with the gorgonzola and remaining walnuts.|Serve right away.","Italian"],
[3388,"Italian Pasta Salad","sides","🥗",30,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Rotini tossed with salami, mozzarella, olives, and crisp vegetables in a zesty Italian vinaigrette.","1 lb|rotini;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1|cucumber|diced;1/2 cup|olives|sliced;4 oz|pepperoni|diced, or salami;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|small pearls;1/4 cup|red onion|finely diced;1/3 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|italian seasoning;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|parmesan|grated","Boil the rotini in well-salted water for 1 minute less than the package time, then drain and rinse under cold water.|Whisk the olive oil, red wine vinegar, Italian seasoning, and salt in a large bowl.|Add the pasta, tomatoes, cucumber, olives, pepperoni, mozzarella, and red onion.|Toss well and sprinkle with parmesan.|Chill at least 30 minutes before serving and toss again, adding a splash of oil if the pasta has absorbed the dressing.","Italian"],
[3389,"Sauteed Escarole with Olives and Capers","sides","🥬",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"Neapolitan scarola in padella, tender greens in garlicky oil with briny olives, capers, and raisins.","2 head|escarole|chopped and washed;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|sliced;1/3 cup|olives|pitted, black or green;2 tbsp|capers|rinsed;2 tbsp|raisins;1 pinch|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste","Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the garlic and red pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Add the escarole with the water still clinging to the leaves, cover, and cook for 5 minutes until wilted.|Uncover and stir in the olives, capers, and raisins.|Cook uncovered for 5 to 6 minutes until the liquid evaporates and the greens are very tender.|Season with salt as needed and serve warm.","Italian"],
[3390,"Peperonata","sides","🫑",45,"Easy",7.5,6,"Slow-cooked sweet bell peppers, onion, and tomato in olive oil, served warm or cold.","3|bell pepper|mixed red and yellow, sliced;1|onion|sliced;1/4 cup|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|sliced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;1 tbsp|capers|optional;1 tbsp|balsamic glaze;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|basil|torn","Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion for 5 minutes.|Add the peppers and garlic and cook for 10 minutes, stirring now and then, until the peppers start to soften.|Stir in the tomatoes, salt, and capers and bring to a simmer.|Cover and cook over low heat for 20 minutes until the peppers are silky and the sauce is thick.|Stir in the balsamic glaze and basil and serve warm or at room temperature.","Italian"],
[3391,"Sicilian Orange and Fennel Salad","sides","🍊",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Insalata di arance e finocchio, a bright salad of juicy oranges, shaved fennel, olives, and red onion.","3|oranges|peeled and sliced into rounds;1|fennel bulbs|shaved paper thin;1/4|red onion|thinly sliced;1/3 cup|olives|black, pitted;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1/4 tsp|salt;1 pinch|red pepper flakes","Soak the sliced red onion in ice water for 5 minutes, then drain.|Arrange the orange slices and shaved fennel on a platter.|Scatter over the red onion and olives.|Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, salt, and red pepper flakes and drizzle it over the salad.|Serve at once, topped with fennel fronds if you have them.","Italian"],
[3392,"Zucchini alla Scapece","sides","🥒",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fried zucchini coins marinated in vinegar, garlic, and mint, a classic Neapolitan summer side served at room temperature.","2 lb|zucchini|cut into 1/4 inch rounds;1/2 cup|olive oil|for frying;3 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|red wine vinegar;2 tbsp|mint|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Pat the zucchini slices dry with paper towels.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and fry the zucchini in batches for 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden. Drain on paper towels.|Layer the warm zucchini in a shallow dish, sprinkling each layer with garlic, mint, salt, and pepper.|Drizzle with the vinegar and toss gently.|Let marinate at room temperature for at least 1 hour before serving.","Italian"],
[3393,"Prosciutto e Melone","sides","🍈",10,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sweet, ripe cantaloupe wrapped in salty prosciutto, the simplest Italian starter for summer.","1|cantaloupe|ripe, seeded and cut into 12 wedges;6 oz|prosciutto|thinly sliced;1 tbsp|olive oil;|black pepper|freshly cracked;1 tbsp|basil|torn","Peel the cantaloupe wedges and chill them for 30 minutes so they are cold.|Wrap each wedge with a slice of thinly sliced prosciutto, folding it loosely.|Arrange on a platter and drizzle with a little olive oil.|Finish with cracked black pepper and torn basil and serve immediately.","Italian"],
[3394,"Mozzarella in Carrozza","sides","🧀",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Fried mozzarella sandwiches dipped in egg and breadcrumbs, crisp outside with a molten cheese center.","8 slice|bread|white sandwich bread, crusts removed;8 oz|fresh mozzarella|sliced and patted dry;2|eggs;2 tbsp|milk;1/2 cup|flour;1 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|marinara sauce|warmed, for dipping","Make 4 sandwiches with the bread and mozzarella, leaving a small border, and press the edges together firmly.|Whisk the eggs, milk, and salt in a shallow dish. Put the flour and breadcrumbs in two other dishes.|Coat each sandwich in flour, then egg, then breadcrumbs, pressing so the coating sticks.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat to about 350°F.|Fry the sandwiches for 2 to 3 minutes per side until deeply golden and the cheese is melted.|Cut into triangles and serve hot with warm marinara.","Italian"],
[3395,"Olive all'Ascolana","sides","🫒",75,"Medium",7.5,8,"Large green olives stuffed with seasoned meat, breaded, and fried, a street-food specialty from Ascoli Piceno.","24|olives|large green, pitted;6 oz|ground pork;4 oz|ground beef;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;1|eggs|plus 2 more for coating;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1/2 cup|flour;1 cup|breadcrumbs;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1/4 tsp|salt","Brown the pork and beef in the olive oil for 8 minutes, stir in the tomato paste, and cook 2 more minutes, then cool.|Pulse the meat in a food processor with the parmesan, 1 egg, nutmeg, and salt into a smooth paste.|Press a small amount of the filling into each olive, reshaping the olive around it.|Beat the 2 remaining eggs. Roll the stuffed olives in flour, then egg, then breadcrumbs.|Heat the oil to 350°F and fry in batches for 2 to 3 minutes until deep golden.|Drain on paper towels and serve warm.","Italian"],
[3396,"Panelle","sides","🟡",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Crisp Sicilian chickpea flour fritters, a Palermo street snack seasoned with lemon and parsley.","1 1/2 cup|chickpea flour;3 cup|water;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|parsley|finely chopped;1/4 tsp|black pepper;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1|lemon|cut into wedges","Whisk the chickpea flour into the cold water in a saucepan until smooth, then add the salt and pepper.|Cook over medium heat, whisking constantly, for 8 to 10 minutes until it is very thick and pulls away from the pan. Stir in the parsley.|Spread the paste about 1/4 inch thick on an oiled baking sheet and let it cool and set for 30 minutes.|Cut into rectangles or triangles.|Fry in 350°F oil in batches for 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden and crisp.|Drain, sprinkle with salt, and serve hot with lemon.","Italian"],
[3397,"Espinacas con Garbanzos","sides","🥬",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"A Seville tapas classic of spinach and chickpeas simmered with cumin, paprika, garlic, and a splash of vinegar.","1 can|chickpeas|15 oz, drained and rinsed;1 lb|spinach|fresh, washed;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 slice|bread|cut into cubes;4 clove|garlic|sliced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1/2 cup|water;|salt|to taste","Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and fry the bread cubes and half the garlic until golden, about 3 minutes. Remove them to a mortar or blender.|Add the remaining garlic to the pan with the cumin and paprika and cook for 30 seconds.|Add the spinach in batches until wilted, then stir in the chickpeas and water and simmer for 8 minutes.|Mash the fried bread and garlic with the vinegar and a splash of water into a paste and stir it into the pan.|Cook 5 more minutes until thick, season with salt, and serve warm.","Spanish"],
[3398,"Berenjenas con Miel","sides","🍆",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crisp fried eggplant sticks drizzled with honey, a sweet and salty tapas favorite from Andalusia.","2|eggplant|cut into sticks or thick rounds;1 cup|milk;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;2 cup|olive oil|for frying;1/4 cup|honey|warmed;1 tsp|fresh thyme|optional","Soak the eggplant in the milk with half the salt for 15 minutes to remove bitterness, then drain and pat dry.|Toss the pieces in the flour mixed with the remaining salt, shaking off the excess.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 360°F.|Fry the eggplant in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until golden and crisp, then drain on paper towels.|Pile onto a plate, drizzle with the warm honey, and scatter with thyme. Serve immediately.","Spanish"],
[3399,"Escalivada","sides","🫑",75,"Easy",7.5,6,"Catalan roasted eggplant, peppers, and onion torn into strips and dressed with olive oil and garlic.","2|eggplant;2|bell pepper|red;2|onion|medium, unpeeled;4|tomatoes|optional;1/3 cup|olive oil;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sherry vinegar;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F. Place the whole eggplants, peppers, and onions on a baking sheet and prick the eggplant skins with a fork.|Roast for 45 to 60 minutes, turning once, until the skins are blackened and the vegetables are collapsed and tender.|Cover them with foil for 15 minutes to steam, then peel off the skins and remove the pepper seeds.|Tear the vegetables into long strips and arrange on a platter.|Dress with olive oil, garlic, vinegar, salt, and parsley and serve warm or at room temperature.","Spanish"],
[3400,"Dátiles con Bacon","sides","🥓",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Bacon-wrapped dates stuffed with almonds, baked until sticky, salty, and sweet.","24|dates|medjool, pitted;24|almonds|whole, toasted;12 slice|bacon|cut in half;1 tbsp|honey;1/4 tsp|paprika","Heat the oven to 400°F and line a baking sheet with foil.|Stuff each date with an almond.|Wrap each date in half a slice of bacon and secure with a toothpick.|Arrange seam side down on the baking sheet and bake for 15 minutes.|Flip them, brush with honey, dust with paprika, and bake 8 to 10 minutes more until the bacon is crisp.|Cool for a few minutes and serve warm.","Spanish"],
[3401,"Champiñones al Ajillo","sides","🍄",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Mushrooms sizzled in olive oil with plenty of garlic, white wine, and parsley, a staple of Spanish tapas bars.","1 1/2 lb|mushrooms|cleaned and halved;1/4 cup|olive oil;6 clove|garlic|thinly sliced;1 pinch|red pepper flakes;1/4 cup|white wine|or dry sherry;1/2 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/2|lemon|juiced","Heat the olive oil in a wide skillet over high heat.|Add the mushrooms in one layer and cook without stirring for 4 minutes, then stir and cook 4 minutes more until browned.|Reduce the heat to medium, add the garlic and red pepper flakes, and cook for 1 minute until fragrant.|Pour in the wine and simmer for 2 minutes until nearly evaporated.|Season with salt, stir in the parsley and lemon juice, and serve hot with crusty bread.","Spanish"],
[3402,"Patatas a lo Pobre","sides","🥔",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Spanish poor man's potatoes, slowly cooked in olive oil with onion and green pepper until soft and golden.","2 lb|potatoes|peeled and thinly sliced;1|onion|sliced;1|bell pepper|green, sliced;1 cup|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar","Heat the olive oil in a large deep skillet over medium-low heat.|Add the potatoes and sprinkle with the salt. Cook gently, turning now and then, for 15 minutes.|Add the onion and pepper and cook for 15 minutes more until the potatoes are tender and just lightly golden.|Add the garlic for the last 2 minutes of cooking.|Lift the vegetables out with a slotted spoon, drizzle with the vinegar, and top with parsley.|Serve warm.","Spanish"],
[3403,"Batatas a Murro","sides","🥔",55,"Easy",7.5,4,"Portuguese punched potatoes, small roasted spuds smashed open and baked again with olive oil, garlic, and coarse salt.","2 lb|baby potatoes|small, unpeeled;1 tbsp|coarse salt;1/3 cup|olive oil;5 clove|garlic|lightly crushed;2 sprig|rosemary;|black pepper|to taste;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F.|Boil the potatoes in salted water for 15 minutes until almost tender, then drain.|Arrange on a baking sheet and punch each one with the bottom of a glass to split the skin and flatten it slightly.|Drizzle with the olive oil, scatter with garlic, rosemary, coarse salt, and pepper.|Roast for 25 to 30 minutes until the edges are crisp and golden.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve hot.","Portuguese"],
[3404,"Peixinhos da Horta","sides","🫛",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Portuguese green bean tempura, the crisp original that inspired Japanese tempura.","12 oz|green beans|trimmed;1 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|water|sparkling or ice cold;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1|lemon|cut into wedges","Boil the green beans in salted water for 3 minutes, then drain and dry thoroughly.|Whisk the flour, baking powder, and salt with the cold water until just combined into a thin, slightly lumpy batter.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350°F.|Bundle 2 or 3 beans together, dip in the batter, and fry for 2 to 3 minutes until golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels, sprinkle with extra salt, and serve hot with lemon wedges.","Portuguese"],
[3405,"Amêijoas à Bulhão Pato","sides","🐚",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Clams steamed open in white wine, garlic, olive oil, and cilantro, the Lisbon tavern starter.","2 lb|clams|littleneck, scrubbed;1/4 cup|olive oil;6 clove|garlic|sliced;1/2 cup|white wine;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|lemon|juiced;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the clams in cold salted water for 20 minutes, then drain and rinse.|Warm the olive oil in a wide pot over medium heat and cook the garlic for 1 minute until fragrant.|Add the clams and wine, cover, and steam for 5 to 7 minutes, shaking the pot, until the clams open. Discard any that stay closed.|Stir in the cilantro, lemon juice, and pepper.|Serve in a bowl with the cooking juices and plenty of bread.","Portuguese"],
[3406,"Arroz de Tomate","sides","🍚",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy Portuguese tomato rice cooked with onion and garlic, the traditional partner to grilled fish and meat.","1 1/2 cup|rice;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|finely chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;2 cup|chicken broth;1|bay leaves;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat the olive oil in a saucepan over medium heat and cook the onion for 5 minutes until soft.|Stir in the garlic and tomato paste and cook for 1 minute.|Add the diced tomatoes, broth, bay leaf, and salt and bring to a boil.|Stir in the rice, cover, and cook over low heat for 18 minutes until the liquid is absorbed.|Rest covered for 5 minutes, discard the bay leaf, fluff with a fork, and top with parsley.","Portuguese"],
[3407,"Rotkohl","sides","🥬",75,"Easy",7.5,6,"German braised red cabbage with apples, onion, and cloves, sweet-sour and perfect with roasts and sausages.","1 head|cabbage|red, about 2 lb, shredded;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|sliced;2|apple|tart, peeled and chopped;1/3 cup|apple cider vinegar;1/4 cup|brown sugar;1/2 cup|water;2|bay leaves;1/4 tsp|ground cloves;1 tsp|salt","Melt the butter in a large Dutch oven over medium heat and cook the onion for 5 minutes.|Add the apples and cook 3 minutes, then stir in the cabbage in handfuls until it begins to wilt.|Add the vinegar, brown sugar, water, bay leaves, cloves, and salt.|Cover and simmer over low heat for 50 to 60 minutes, stirring now and then, until very tender.|Uncover and cook a few more minutes if there is excess liquid, then remove the bay leaves and cloves.|Taste and add a little more sugar or vinegar to balance.","German"],
[3408,"Spätzle","sides","🍝",30,"Medium",7.5,6,"Tender, irregular German egg noodles boiled from a loose batter and tossed in butter and nutmeg.","2 cup|flour;4|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|water;1 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;3 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Whisk the flour, eggs, milk, water, salt, and nutmeg into a thick, smooth batter that falls slowly from a spoon. Let it rest for 10 minutes.|Bring a large pot of well-salted water to a gentle boil.|Press the batter through a spätzle press, a large-holed colander, or scrape small bits off a board with a knife directly into the water.|Cook for 2 to 3 minutes until the spätzle float, then lift out with a slotted spoon.|Melt the butter in a large skillet and toss the noodles for 2 minutes until lightly golden.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve.","German"],
[3409,"Bratkartoffeln","sides","🥔",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"German pan-fried potatoes with crisp bacon and onion, best made with leftover boiled potatoes.","2 lb|potatoes|waxy, boiled and cooled;4 slice|bacon|diced;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tsp|paprika;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Peel the cooled potatoes and cut them into 1/4 inch slices.|Cook the bacon in a large cast-iron skillet over medium heat for 6 minutes until crisp, then remove it, leaving the fat in the pan.|Add the butter and potatoes in an even layer and cook for 8 minutes without stirring until golden underneath.|Turn the potatoes and cook another 8 minutes, then add the onion and cook 5 minutes more.|Return the bacon to the pan, season with salt, pepper, and paprika, and toss.|Sprinkle with parsley and serve hot.","German"],
[3410,"Semmelknödel","sides","🍞",60,"Medium",7.5,6,"Bavarian bread dumplings flecked with parsley and onion, made to soak up gravy.","10 oz|bread|stale rolls or white bread, cubed;1 cup|milk|warm;2 tbsp|butter;1/2|onion|finely diced;3|eggs;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|nutmeg","Place the bread cubes in a large bowl and pour the warm milk over them.|Melt the butter in a skillet and cook the onion for 4 minutes until soft, then add to the bread.|Add the eggs, parsley, flour, salt, and nutmeg and mix with your hands, then rest for 15 minutes.|Wet your hands and shape the mixture into 8 round dumplings.|Lower the dumplings into a large pot of barely simmering salted water, and cook uncovered for 20 minutes without boiling hard.|Lift out with a slotted spoon and serve with gravy or mushroom sauce.","German"],
[3411,"Spargel with Hollandaise","sides","🥦",40,"Medium",7.5,4,"White asparagus, a German spring tradition, gently simmered and served with silky hollandaise and new potatoes.","2 lb|asparagus|white, peeled and woody ends trimmed;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|butter;3|eggs|yolks only;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 cup|butter|melted and warm;1 pinch|cayenne;|salt|to taste","Fill a wide pot with water and add the sugar, salt, and 1 tablespoon of butter and bring to a simmer.|Add the asparagus and cook for 8 to 12 minutes until a knife slides in easily at the thick end.|Meanwhile, whisk the yolks and lemon juice in a heatproof bowl set over a pan of barely simmering water until thick and pale, about 3 minutes.|Remove from the heat and slowly whisk in the melted butter in a thin stream until the sauce is smooth and creamy.|Season with salt and cayenne.|Drain the asparagus well and serve with the warm hollandaise.","German"],
[3412,"Obatzda","sides","🧀",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"A Bavarian beer garden cheese spread of ripe camembert, butter, and paprika served with pretzels and radishes.","8 oz|brie|very ripe, or camembert;4 tbsp|butter|softened;1/4 cup|cream cheese;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cumin|ground caraway also works;1/4 cup|onion|finely diced;2 tbsp|beer|wheat beer;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;|salt|to taste","Let the cheese and butter come to room temperature.|Mash the cheese with a fork in a bowl until mostly smooth.|Mix in the butter, cream cheese, paprika, cumin, and beer until creamy but still a little textured.|Fold in half of the onion and season with salt.|Pile into a bowl, top with the remaining onion and the chives, and serve with pretzels, bread, and radishes.","German"],
[3413,"Mizeria","sides","🥒",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"A cool Polish cucumber salad in sour cream with dill, the classic partner to fried cutlets and potatoes.","3|cucumber|thinly sliced;1/2 tsp|salt;3/4 cup|sour cream;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|dill|chopped;1 tsp|sugar;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the cucumber slices with the salt and let them sit in a colander for 10 minutes.|Squeeze out the excess liquid gently with your hands.|Stir the sour cream, lemon juice, dill, sugar, and pepper in a bowl.|Fold in the cucumbers and taste for seasoning.|Chill for 15 minutes and serve cold.","Polish"],
[3414,"Kopytka","sides","🥟",50,"Medium",7.5,4,"Polish potato dumplings cut into little hoof shapes and tossed in butter and breadcrumbs.","2 lb|russet potatoes|peeled and cut up;1 1/4 cup|flour;1|eggs;1 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|butter;1/4 cup|breadcrumbs;2 tbsp|dill|chopped","Boil the potatoes in salted water for 20 minutes until tender, then drain and let them steam dry for 5 minutes.|Mash or rice the potatoes until completely smooth and let cool slightly.|Mix in the egg, salt, and flour to form a soft dough, adding flour only as needed.|Roll the dough into ropes about 3/4 inch thick and cut diagonally into 1-inch pieces.|Boil in salted water in batches until they float, about 3 minutes, and lift out.|Brown the breadcrumbs in the butter for 2 minutes, toss with the dumplings, and sprinkle with dill.","Polish"],
[3415,"Buraczki","sides","🥕",45,"Easy",7.5,4,"Warm Polish grated beets cooked down with a touch of vinegar and sugar, the classic side for roast meat.","1 1/2 lb|beets|cooked, peeled, and coarsely grated;2 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|flour;1/2 cup|water;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|dill|optional","Melt the butter in a saucepan over medium heat and whisk in the flour for 1 minute.|Add the water and whisk until slightly thickened.|Stir in the grated beets, lemon juice, sugar, and salt.|Simmer on low heat for 10 to 12 minutes, stirring now and then.|Taste, balancing sweet and sour with more lemon or sugar, and stir in dill if using.","Polish"],
[3416,"Kasza Gryczana with Mushrooms","sides","🍄",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Toasted buckwheat groats with caramelized onion and mushrooms, a hearty Polish side for stews and roasts.","1 cup|buckwheat groats|roasted kasha;2 cup|chicken broth;3 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Bring the broth to a boil in a saucepan, add the buckwheat and half the salt, then cover and cook over low heat for 15 minutes until the liquid is absorbed.|Turn off the heat and rest covered for 5 minutes.|Meanwhile, melt the butter in a skillet and cook the onion for 8 minutes until golden.|Add the mushrooms, the remaining salt, and pepper, and cook for 8 minutes until browned.|Fold the mushroom mixture into the buckwheat with the parsley and serve warm.","Polish"],
[3417,"Loaded Baked Potato Bites","sides","🥔",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Crispy roasted baby potatoes topped with melted cheddar, bacon, sour cream and chives.","1 1/2 lb|baby potatoes|halved;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;4 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;1/2 cup|sour cream;2|green onion|thinly sliced","Heat the oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with parchment.|Toss the halved potatoes with the olive oil, salt and pepper and arrange cut side down on the sheet.|Roast for 25 to 30 minutes until the cut sides are deep golden and a knife slides in easily.|Press the top of each potato gently with the back of a spoon to make a small well.|Sprinkle the cheddar over the potatoes and bake 3 to 4 minutes until melted.|Top each bite with a dollop of sour cream, crumbled bacon and green onion and serve warm.","American"],
[3418,"Twice-Baked Sweet Potatoes","sides","🍠",90,"Easy",7.5,6,"Sweet potato halves baked, mashed with butter and cinnamon, then topped with a brown sugar pecan crunch.","3|sweet potatoes|medium, scrubbed;4 tbsp|butter|softened, divided;1/4 cup|milk;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|pecans|chopped;1 tbsp|maple syrup","Heat the oven to 400°F. Prick the sweet potatoes with a fork and bake on a lined sheet for 50 to 60 minutes until very soft.|Let them cool 10 minutes, then halve lengthwise and scoop out the flesh into a bowl, leaving a thin shell.|Mash the flesh with 3 tablespoons butter, the milk, 1 tablespoon brown sugar, cinnamon and salt until smooth.|Spoon the filling back into the shells and set them on the baking sheet.|Mix the pecans with the remaining butter, brown sugar and the maple syrup and sprinkle over the tops.|Lower the oven to 375°F and bake 15 to 20 minutes until hot and the topping is bubbling.","American"],
[3419,"Cornbread Stuffing","sides","🌽",75,"Easy",7.5,8,"Savory stuffing of crumbly cornbread, sage, celery and onion, baked until golden on top and tender inside.","8 cup|cornbread|cubed and dried out;4 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;3 stalk|celery|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sage|chopped;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 1/2 cup|chicken broth;2|eggs|beaten;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 350°F and butter a 9x13 inch baking dish. Spread the cornbread cubes on a sheet and let them dry in the oven for 15 minutes.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion and celery 6 to 8 minutes until soft.|Stir in the garlic, sage, thyme, salt and pepper and cook 1 minute.|Tip the cornbread into a large bowl and add the vegetables.|Whisk the broth and eggs together, pour over the cornbread and fold gently until evenly moist.|Spread in the dish, cover with foil and bake 25 minutes, then uncover and bake 15 to 20 minutes until golden.","American"],
[3420,"Scalloped Potatoes","sides","🥔",105,"Medium",7.5,8,"Thinly sliced potatoes baked in a creamy garlic and onion sauce until tender with a golden top.","2 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|peeled and sliced 1/8 inch thick;3 tbsp|butter;1|onion|finely diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|flour;2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 1/4 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 9x13 inch baking dish.|Melt the butter in a saucepan over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes until soft, then add the garlic for 1 minute.|Whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the milk and cream.|Add the thyme, salt and pepper and simmer, stirring, 3 to 4 minutes until the sauce coats a spoon.|Layer the potato slices in the dish, pouring some sauce over each layer, finishing with sauce on top.|Cover with foil and bake 45 minutes, then uncover and bake 25 to 30 minutes until golden and the potatoes are tender.|Rest 10 minutes before serving so the sauce thickens.","American"],
[3421,"Potatoes au Gratin","sides","🧀",95,"Medium",7.5,8,"Sliced potatoes layered with garlic cream and plenty of Gruyere and Parmesan, baked bubbling and browned.","2 lb|potatoes|Yukon Gold, sliced 1/8 inch thick;1 1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|milk;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|butter|for the dish and top;1 1/2 cup|gruyere|shredded;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 9x13 inch baking dish.|Warm the cream, milk, garlic, nutmeg, salt and pepper in a saucepan over medium-low heat for 5 minutes without boiling.|Layer one third of the potatoes in the dish and sprinkle with one third of the Gruyere and Parmesan, then repeat twice.|Pour the warm cream mixture over the top and press the potatoes down so they are mostly covered.|Dot with the butter, cover with foil and bake 40 minutes.|Uncover and bake 20 to 25 minutes until the top is deeply golden and a knife slides through the potatoes.|Rest 10 minutes before cutting.","American"],
[3422,"Roasted Cauliflower with Garlic and Parmesan","sides","🥦",40,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Cauliflower florets roasted until caramelized at the edges and tossed with garlic and Parmesan.","1 head|cauliflower|cut into florets;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1|lemon|cut in wedges","Heat the oven to 425°F with a large baking sheet inside.|Toss the florets with the olive oil, salt and pepper.|Spread on the hot sheet in a single layer and roast 20 minutes, turning once, until browned at the edges.|Scatter the garlic and half the Parmesan over the cauliflower and roast 5 more minutes.|Finish with the remaining Parmesan and the parsley and serve with lemon wedges.","American"],
[3423,"Broccoli Salad","sides","🥗",30,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Crunchy raw broccoli with bacon, red onion, dried cranberries and sunflower seeds in a tangy creamy dressing.","2 head|broccoli|cut into small florets;8 slice|bacon;1/2 cup|red onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|dried cranberries;1/2 cup|sunflower seeds;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;3/4 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1/4 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Cook the bacon in a skillet over medium heat 8 to 10 minutes until crisp, drain on paper towels and crumble.|Whisk the mayonnaise, sugar, vinegar, salt and pepper in a large bowl until smooth.|Add the broccoli, red onion, cranberries and cheddar and toss to coat.|Chill at least 1 hour so the flavors blend and the broccoli softens slightly.|Stir in the bacon and sunflower seeds just before serving to keep them crunchy.","American"],
[3424,"Bacon Ranch Pasta Salad","sides","🥗",35,"Very easy",7.5,10,"Rotini tossed with crispy bacon, cheddar, tomatoes and cucumber in a creamy ranch dressing.","1 lb|rotini;8 slice|bacon;1 cup|ranch dressing;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|milk;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1|cucumber|diced;1 cup|cheddar|cubed or shredded;3|green onion|sliced;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the rotini in salted boiling water until al dente, drain and rinse under cold water until cool.|Cook the bacon in a skillet until crisp, drain on paper towels and crumble.|Whisk the ranch, mayonnaise, milk and garlic powder in a large bowl.|Add the pasta, tomatoes, cucumber, cheddar and green onion and toss to coat.|Fold in most of the bacon and season with salt and pepper.|Chill 1 hour, loosen with a splash of milk if needed and top with the remaining bacon before serving.","American"],
[3425,"Jalapeno Popper Deviled Eggs","sides","🥚",35,"Easy",7.5,12,"Deviled eggs with a cream cheese, jalapeno and bacon filling that tastes like a jalapeno popper.","12|eggs;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|mustard;2|jalapeno peppers|seeded and finely diced;4 slice|bacon|cooked and crumbled;1/2 cup|cheddar|finely shredded;1/4 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|paprika","Place the eggs in a pot, cover with cold water by 1 inch and bring to a boil. Turn off the heat, cover and let stand 12 minutes.|Move the eggs to an ice bath for 10 minutes, then peel and halve lengthwise.|Pop the yolks into a bowl and mash with the cream cheese, mayonnaise, mustard and salt until smooth.|Stir in the jalapenos, half the bacon and the cheddar.|Spoon or pipe the filling into the whites.|Top with the remaining bacon and a dusting of paprika and chill 15 minutes before serving.","American"],
[3426,"Texas Toast","sides","🍞",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Thick-cut bread slathered in garlic butter and baked until crisp outside and soft within.","8 slice|bread|thick-cut Texas toast or 1 inch slices;6 tbsp|butter|softened;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/4 tsp|salt","Heat the oven to 400°F and set a rack in the upper third.|Mash the butter with the garlic, garlic powder, salt, half the Parmesan and the parsley.|Spread the garlic butter generously over one side of each slice and set them butter side up on a baking sheet.|Sprinkle with the remaining Parmesan.|Bake 8 to 10 minutes until the edges are crisp and golden, then broil 1 minute for extra color.|Serve hot.","American"],
[3427,"Cheesy Garlic Mashed Cauliflower","sides","🥦",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Silky mashed cauliflower with roasted-style garlic, cheddar and Parmesan, a creamy low-carb stand-in for potatoes.","1 head|cauliflower|large, cut into florets;4 tbsp|butter;4 clove|garlic|peeled;1/4 cup|sour cream;3/4 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Steam the cauliflower and garlic cloves over boiling water for 12 to 15 minutes until very tender.|Drain well and let the steam escape for 2 minutes, then blot with a clean towel to remove moisture.|Transfer to a food processor with the butter, sour cream, salt and pepper and blend until smooth.|Add the cheddar and Parmesan and pulse until melted and creamy.|Taste for salt, spoon into a bowl and top with the chives.","American"],
[3428,"Tater Tot Casserole","sides","🍲",65,"Easy",7.5,8,"Seasoned ground beef and green beans in a creamy cheese sauce under a crown of crispy tater tots.","1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|cream of mushroom soup|10.5 oz;1/2 cup|milk;1 tbsp|worcestershire;1 can|green beans|14.5 oz, drained;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 bag|frozen tater tots|32 oz;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F and grease a 9x13 inch baking dish.|Brown the beef with the onion in a large skillet over medium-high heat 8 minutes, breaking it up, then add the garlic for 1 minute and drain any fat.|Stir in the soup, milk, Worcestershire, salt and pepper and simmer 3 minutes.|Fold in the green beans and 1 cup of the cheddar and spread the mixture in the dish.|Arrange the tater tots in tight rows over the top.|Bake 35 minutes, sprinkle with the remaining cheddar and bake 5 to 10 minutes more until the tots are crisp and the cheese melts.","American"],
[3429,"Grilled Corn with Garlic Herb Butter","sides","🌽",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sweet corn on the cob grilled until lightly charred and brushed with garlic parsley butter.","6|corn|ears, husked;1 tbsp|olive oil;4 tbsp|butter|softened;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat a grill to medium-high, about 450°F.|Mash the butter with the garlic, parsley, chives, half the salt and the pepper.|Rub the corn with the olive oil and sprinkle with the remaining salt.|Grill 10 to 12 minutes, turning every 3 minutes, until tender with charred spots.|Brush each ear with the herb butter while still hot and serve right away.","American"],
[3430,"Mac and Cheese Bites","sides","🧀",55,"Medium",7.5,8,"Mini muffin-tin bites of cheddar mac and cheese with a crisp panko crust, easy to eat by hand.","8 oz|elbow macaroni;2 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|flour;1 cup|milk;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;1|eggs|beaten;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 cup|panko;1 tbsp|olive oil","Heat the oven to 375°F and grease a 24-cup mini muffin tin well.|Cook the macaroni 1 minute short of the package time and drain.|Melt the butter in the pot, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the milk and simmer 3 minutes until thick.|Off the heat, stir in the cheddar, half the Parmesan, garlic powder, salt and pepper until smooth.|Fold in the macaroni, let cool 5 minutes, then stir in the egg.|Toss the panko with the olive oil and remaining Parmesan. Press the mac mixture into the cups and top with the panko.|Bake 18 to 20 minutes until golden, cool 5 minutes in the tin and loosen with a knife.","American"],
[3431,"Homemade Cranberry Sauce","sides","🍒",20,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Tart fresh cranberries simmered with orange and sugar into a glossy sauce that sets as it cools.","12 oz|cranberries|fresh or frozen;1 cup|sugar;3/4 cup|orange juice;1|orange|zested;1/4 tsp|cinnamon;1 pinch|salt","Combine the cranberries, sugar, orange juice, zest, cinnamon and salt in a medium saucepan.|Bring to a boil over medium-high heat, stirring to dissolve the sugar.|Reduce to a simmer and cook 10 to 12 minutes until most berries have popped and the sauce thickens.|Mash a few berries against the pan for a looser texture if you like.|Cool to room temperature, then chill, as it will thicken further in the fridge.","American"],
[3432,"Corn and Black Bean Salad","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"A colorful Southwest-style salad of sweet corn, black beans, peppers and avocado in a lime cumin dressing.","1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained and rinsed;2 cup|frozen corn|thawed;1|bell pepper|diced;1/2|red onion|finely diced;1|avocado|diced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;3 tbsp|lime juice;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|cumin;1/2 tsp|chili powder;1/2 tsp|salt","Whisk the lime juice, olive oil, cumin, chili powder and salt in a large bowl.|Add the beans, corn, bell pepper and red onion and toss well.|Let sit 10 minutes so the onion mellows and the flavors absorb.|Fold in the cilantro and avocado gently just before serving.|Taste and adjust salt and lime.","American"],
[3433,"Seven-Layer Dip","sides","🥑",25,"Very easy",7.5,12,"A party dip of seasoned refried beans, guacamole, sour cream, salsa, cheese and toppings, served with tortilla chips.","1 can|refried beans|16 oz;1 tbsp|taco seasoning;2|avocado|ripe;1 tbsp|lime juice;1/4 tsp|salt;1 cup|sour cream;1 cup|salsa|drained;1 1/2 cup|mexican cheese blend|shredded;1/2 cup|cherry tomatoes|diced;1/4 cup|olives|sliced black;3|green onion|sliced;1 bag|tortilla chips|for serving","Stir the taco seasoning into the refried beans and spread in an even layer in a 9 inch pie plate or square dish.|Mash the avocados with the lime juice and salt and spread gently over the beans.|Spread the sour cream over the guacamole.|Spoon the drained salsa over the sour cream.|Sprinkle with the cheese, then scatter the tomatoes, olives and green onion over the top.|Chill 30 minutes if time allows and serve with tortilla chips.","American"],
[3434,"Creamy Cucumber Salad","sides","🥒",45,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Thin cucumber and onion slices chilled in a tangy sour cream and dill dressing.","3|cucumber|thinly sliced;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|sour cream;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|white vinegar;1 tsp|sugar;2 tbsp|dill|chopped;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Toss the cucumbers with the salt in a colander and let drain 15 minutes, then pat dry.|Whisk the sour cream, mayonnaise, vinegar, sugar, dill and pepper in a large bowl.|Add the cucumbers and red onion and stir to coat.|Chill at least 30 minutes, taste and adjust seasoning.|Serve cold, stirring before serving.","American"],
[3435,"Garlic Parmesan Roasted Green Beans","sides","🥬",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Fresh green beans roasted at high heat until blistered, then tossed with garlic and Parmesan.","1 1/2 lb|green beans|trimmed;2 tbsp|olive oil;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/3 cup|parmesan|grated;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Heat the oven to 425°F with a baking sheet inside.|Toss the green beans with the olive oil, salt and pepper.|Spread on the hot sheet and roast 12 minutes.|Sprinkle with the garlic and Parmesan and roast 4 to 5 minutes more until blistered and the cheese is golden.|Squeeze the lemon juice over the beans and serve.","American"],
[3436,"Southern Fried Okra","sides","🥘",30,"Easy",7.5,6,"Sliced okra coated in seasoned cornmeal and fried until crunchy and golden.","1 lb|okra|sliced into 1/2 inch rounds;1/2 cup|buttermilk;1|eggs;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1 1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Whisk the buttermilk and egg in a bowl and toss the okra in it to coat.|Mix the cornmeal, flour, salt, pepper, garlic powder and cayenne in a shallow dish.|Heat the oil in a deep skillet to 350°F.|Lift the okra from the buttermilk with a slotted spoon, toss in the cornmeal mixture and shake off the excess.|Fry in batches 3 to 4 minutes, turning once, until deep golden and crisp.|Drain on a wire rack or paper towels and sprinkle with a little more salt.","Southern"],
[3437,"Fried Green Tomatoes","sides","🍅",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Firm green tomato slices in a crisp cornmeal crust, pan-fried until golden and tangy inside.","4|tomatoes|firm green, sliced 1/2 inch thick;1 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|flour;2|eggs;1/2 cup|buttermilk;1 cup|cornmeal;1/2 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1 cup|vegetable oil|for frying","Lay the tomato slices on paper towels, sprinkle with the salt and let sit 10 minutes, then pat dry.|Put the flour in one dish, whisk the eggs and buttermilk in a second and mix the cornmeal, paprika, pepper and cayenne in a third.|Dredge each slice in flour, then the egg mixture, then press into the cornmeal.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat to about 350°F.|Fry the slices in batches 3 minutes per side until deep golden.|Drain on a rack and serve hot with a pinch of salt.","Southern"],
[3438,"Southern Mustard Greens","sides","🥬",65,"Easy",7.5,6,"Peppery mustard greens simmered low and slow with bacon, onion and a splash of vinegar.","2 bunch|mustard greens|stemmed and chopped;4 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 cup|chicken broth;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Wash the greens in several changes of water to remove grit and chop into 2 inch pieces.|Cook the bacon in a large pot over medium heat 6 minutes until crisp, then add the onion and cook 5 minutes.|Add the garlic and pepper flakes for 1 minute.|Add the greens in handfuls, stirring as they wilt, then pour in the broth, sugar, salt and pepper.|Cover and simmer over medium-low heat 40 to 45 minutes until very tender.|Stir in the vinegar, taste for salt and serve with some of the pot liquor.","Southern"],
[3439,"Southern Black-Eyed Peas","sides","🫘",130,"Easy",7.5,8,"Dried black-eyed peas simmered with a smoked ham hock, onion and celery until creamy and savory.","1 lb|black-eyed peas|dried, rinsed;1|ham hock|smoked;1|onion|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2|bay leaves;1 tsp|dried thyme;4 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;|hot sauce|for serving","Put the peas in a large pot, cover with water by 2 inches and bring to a boil for 2 minutes. Remove from the heat, cover and let stand 1 hour, then drain.|Return the peas to the pot with the ham hock, onion, celery, garlic, bay leaves and thyme.|Add the broth and enough water to cover by 1 inch and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat, cover partially and simmer 50 to 60 minutes until the peas are tender and creamy.|Remove the ham hock, shred the meat, discard the bones and skin and stir the meat back in.|Season with the salt and pepper, discard the bay leaves and serve with hot sauce.","Southern"],
[3440,"Southern Squash Casserole","sides","🧀",65,"Easy",7.5,8,"Tender yellow squash and onion in a cheesy mayo-sour cream sauce with a buttery cracker topping.","2 lb|yellow squash|sliced;1|onion|diced;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;1/2 cup|sour cream;1|eggs|beaten;1 cup|crackers|crushed butter crackers;3 tbsp|butter|melted;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 350°F and grease a 2 quart baking dish.|Simmer the squash and onion in a pot of salted water 8 to 10 minutes until tender, then drain very well, pressing out excess water.|Stir the mayonnaise, sour cream, egg, three quarters of the cheddar, salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Fold in the squash and onion and spread in the dish.|Mix the cracker crumbs with the melted butter and scatter over the top with the remaining cheddar.|Bake 30 minutes until bubbling and golden.","Southern"],
[3441,"Southern Cheese Grits","sides","🥣",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Slow-cooked stone-ground grits finished with butter and sharp cheddar for a creamy, savory side.","1 cup|grits|stone-ground;2 cup|chicken broth;2 cup|milk;4 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|sharp, shredded;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1/4 tsp|cayenne","Bring the broth and milk to a gentle simmer in a heavy saucepan.|Slowly whisk in the grits, stirring constantly so no lumps form.|Reduce the heat to low, cover and cook 35 to 40 minutes, stirring every 5 minutes, until thick and tender. Add a splash of milk if they get stiff.|Stir in the butter, salt, pepper and cayenne.|Take off the heat and stir in the cheddar until melted.|Serve right away, as grits firm up as they cool.","Southern"],
[3442,"Southern Fried Cabbage","sides","🥬",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Cabbage cooked down in bacon drippings with onion until sweet and silky with browned edges.","1 head|cabbage|small, cored and chopped;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|butter;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/4 tsp|red pepper flakes;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar","Cook the bacon in a large deep skillet over medium heat 8 minutes until crisp, then lift out with a slotted spoon and leave the drippings.|Add the butter and onion and cook 5 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cabbage in batches, stirring as it wilts.|Season with the salt, black pepper and pepper flakes.|Cook uncovered, stirring now and then, 12 to 15 minutes until tender with golden edges.|Stir in the vinegar and bacon and serve hot.","Southern"],
[3443,"Candied Yams","sides","🍠",55,"Easy",7.5,8,"Sweet potato chunks simmered in a buttery brown sugar and cinnamon syrup until glossy and tender.","3 lb|sweet potatoes|peeled, cut in 1 inch chunks;6 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1/4 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|orange juice;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 tsp|vanilla;1/4 tsp|salt","Melt the butter in a large deep skillet or Dutch oven over medium heat.|Stir in the brown sugar, sugar, orange juice, cinnamon, nutmeg and salt until dissolved.|Add the sweet potatoes and toss to coat, then bring to a simmer.|Cover and cook over medium-low heat 20 to 25 minutes, stirring gently every 5 minutes, until almost tender.|Uncover and simmer 8 to 10 minutes more until the syrup thickens and glazes the potatoes.|Stir in the vanilla and serve warm.","Southern"],
[3444,"Southern Butter Beans","sides","🫘",55,"Easy",7.5,6,"Creamy baby lima beans simmered with bacon and onion until they make their own silky gravy.","1 bag|frozen butter beans|16 oz baby lima beans;4 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|diced;2 tbsp|butter;2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 tsp|dried thyme;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Cook the bacon in a medium pot over medium heat 6 minutes until crisp.|Add the onion and cook in the drippings 4 minutes until soft.|Add the frozen butter beans, broth, thyme, salt and pepper and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a low simmer, cover and cook 30 to 35 minutes until the beans are tender and the liquid is creamy.|Stir in the butter, mashing a few beans against the pot to thicken, and season to taste.","Southern"],
[3445,"Southern Tomato Pie","sides","🍅",100,"Medium",7.5,8,"Ripe tomato slices layered in a flaky crust with basil and a baked cheddar mayonnaise topping.","1|pie crust|9 inch, refrigerated;4|tomatoes|large, ripe, sliced 1/4 inch;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/2 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|basil|chopped;2|green onion|sliced;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|garlic powder","Heat the oven to 400°F. Fit the crust in a 9 inch pie dish, prick the bottom and blind bake with pie weights 12 minutes, then remove the weights and bake 5 more minutes.|Lay the tomato slices on paper towels, sprinkle with the salt and let drain 30 minutes, then blot dry.|Lower the oven to 375°F.|Layer the tomatoes in the crust, sprinkling basil, green onion and pepper between layers.|Mix the cheddar, mozzarella, mayonnaise and garlic powder and spread over the top.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden and bubbling, then rest 15 minutes before slicing.","Southern"],
[3446,"Honey Roast Parsnips","sides","🥕",55,"Easy",7.5,6,"Parsnips parboiled then roasted with honey and thyme until sticky, sweet and crisp at the edges.","2 lb|parsnips|peeled, cut into batons;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|honey;2 sprig|fresh thyme;1 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 425°F and put a roasting tray with the olive oil inside to heat.|Boil the parsnips in salted water for 5 minutes and drain well, shaking them in the colander to roughen the edges.|Carefully tip the parsnips into the hot tray and toss in the oil, adding the thyme.|Roast 25 minutes, turning once, until golden.|Drizzle with the honey, toss and roast 8 to 10 minutes more until sticky and caramelized.|Season with salt and pepper and serve hot.","British"],
[3447,"Braised Red Cabbage with Apple","sides","🥬",105,"Easy",7.5,8,"Shredded red cabbage slowly braised with apple, vinegar and warm spices until sweet-sour and tender.","1 head|red cabbage|small, cored and shredded;2|apple|cooking, peeled and chopped;1|onion|sliced;3 tbsp|butter;1/4 cup|red wine vinegar;1/4 cup|brown sugar;1/2 cup|apple juice;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 tsp|ground cloves;1|bay leaves;1 tsp|salt","Heat the oven to 325°F.|Melt the butter in a large ovenproof pot over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes until soft.|Add the cabbage, apples, vinegar, brown sugar, apple juice, cinnamon, cloves, bay leaf and salt and stir well.|Cover tightly and braise in the oven 1 hour 15 minutes, stirring halfway, until very soft.|Uncover, discard the bay leaf and simmer on the stovetop a few minutes if too wet.|Taste and add a splash more vinegar or sugar to balance.","British"],
[3448,"Minted New Potatoes","sides","🥔",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Small new potatoes boiled with a sprig of mint and tossed in butter and fresh chopped mint.","2 lb|baby potatoes|new potatoes, scrubbed;3 sprig|mint;1 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|butter;1/4 cup|mint|fresh, finely chopped;|black pepper|to taste;|salt|to taste","Put the potatoes in a pot with 2 sprigs of mint and the salt and cover with cold water.|Bring to a boil, then simmer 15 to 20 minutes until a knife slides in easily.|Drain well, discard the mint sprigs and return the potatoes to the hot pot for 1 minute to steam dry.|Add the butter and chopped mint and toss until the potatoes are glossy.|Season with pepper and salt and serve warm.","British"],
[3449,"Pigs in Blankets","sides","🥓",40,"Easy",7.5,6,"Little pork sausages wrapped in streaky bacon and roasted until the bacon is crisp, with a honey mustard glaze.","12|pork sausages|small chipolatas or cocktail sausages;12 slice|bacon|thin streaky;1 tbsp|honey;1 tsp|mustard;1 tsp|dried thyme","Heat the oven to 400°F and line a baking tray with parchment.|Stretch each bacon slice with the back of a knife so it is longer and thinner.|Wrap one slice tightly around each sausage, spiraling from end to end, and place seam side down on the tray.|Mix the honey, mustard and thyme and brush it lightly over the bacon.|Roast 25 to 30 minutes, turning halfway, until the bacon is crisp and the sausages are cooked through.|Serve hot.","British"],
[3450,"Welsh Rarebit","sides","🍞",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"Thick toast covered with a sharp cheddar, ale and mustard sauce, then grilled until bubbling and brown.","1 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|flour;1/2 cup|beer|ale or stout;1 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|mustard|English;6 oz|cheddar|sharp, grated;1|eggs|yolk only;1/4 tsp|cayenne;4 slice|bread|thick, toasted","Heat the broiler to high.|Melt the butter in a small saucepan, whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Whisk in the beer, Worcestershire and mustard and simmer 2 minutes until thickened.|Take off the heat, stir in the cheddar until melted, then beat in the egg yolk and cayenne.|Spread the mixture thickly over the toast, edge to edge.|Broil 3 to 4 minutes until bubbling and flecked with brown and serve right away.","British"],
[3451,"Ploughman's Board","sides","🧀",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"A classic pub lunch spread of cheddar, ham, pickled onions, chutney, apple and crusty bread.","8 oz|cheddar|mature, cut in wedges;4 oz|stilton|or other blue cheese;8 oz|ham|thick sliced;1 lb|crusty bread|sliced or torn;4 tbsp|butter;1/2 cup|chutney|fruit or pickle;4|pickled onions;4|eggs|hard-boiled, halved;2|apple|sliced;2 stalk|celery|cut in sticks;1/4 cup|pickles|cornichons","Boil the eggs 10 minutes, cool in cold water, peel and halve.|Arrange the cheeses, folded ham and bread on a large board or platter.|Put the butter, chutney, pickled onions and pickles in small bowls or piles around the board.|Add the eggs, apple slices and celery sticks.|Squeeze a little lemon over the apple if desired to prevent browning and serve at room temperature.","British"],
[3452,"Coronation Chicken Salad","sides","🥗",25,"Easy",7.5,6,"Cold shredded chicken in a mild curry, mango chutney and apricot-sweet cream dressing with raisins and almonds.","1 lb|rotisserie chicken|shredded or cubed;1 tsp|vegetable oil;1 tbsp|curry powder;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|greek yogurt;2 tbsp|mango chutney;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|tomato paste;1/4 cup|raisins;1/4 cup|almonds|sliced and toasted;2|green onion|sliced;|salt|to taste","Heat the oil in a small pan over low heat, stir in the curry powder and cook 1 minute until fragrant, then cool.|Whisk the cooled curry with the mayonnaise, yogurt, chutney, lemon juice and tomato paste.|Chop any large mango pieces in the chutney so the dressing is smooth.|Fold in the chicken, raisins and green onion until coated.|Season with salt, chill 30 minutes and top with the toasted almonds before serving.","British"],
[3453,"Cucumber Sandwiches","sides","🥒",25,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Delicate afternoon-tea finger sandwiches of thin cucumber on buttered bread with lemony cream cheese.","1|cucumber|English, very thinly sliced;1/2 tsp|salt;8 slice|bread|soft white sandwich;4 tbsp|butter|softened;4 oz|cream cheese|softened;1 tbsp|dill|chopped;1 tsp|lemon juice;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Lay the cucumber slices on paper towels, sprinkle with the salt and let drain 15 minutes, then pat dry.|Mix the cream cheese with the dill, lemon juice and pepper.|Spread the bread with the butter right to the edges, then spread 4 slices with the cream cheese.|Layer the cucumber over the cream cheese in overlapping rows and top with the buttered slices.|Trim off the crusts with a serrated knife and cut each sandwich into 4 triangles or fingers.|Serve within an hour or cover with a damp cloth and chill.","British"],
[3454,"Soda Farls","sides","🍞",25,"Easy",7.5,8,"Quick griddle-cooked buttermilk soda bread triangles from Northern Ireland, soft inside and lightly crusty.","2 cup|flour|plus extra for dusting;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|buttermilk|plus a splash if needed","Sift the flour, baking soda and salt into a bowl and make a well in the middle.|Pour in most of the buttermilk and mix quickly with your hand to a soft, slightly sticky dough, adding more buttermilk if dry.|Turn onto a floured surface, knead lightly 3 to 4 times and divide in two.|Pat each half into a round about 1/2 inch thick and cut each into quarters.|Heat a dry heavy skillet or griddle over medium heat and cook the farls 5 to 6 minutes per side until golden and cooked through.|Serve warm with butter or as part of a fry-up.","Irish"],
[3455,"Potato Farls","sides","🥔",50,"Easy",7.5,4,"Soft Irish potato bread triangles, cooked in a pan until golden and best eaten hot with butter or a fry-up.","1 1/2 lb|russet potatoes|peeled and cut up;2 tbsp|butter;1 tsp|salt;1 cup|flour|plus extra for dusting;1 tbsp|vegetable oil|for the pan","Boil the potatoes in salted water 15 to 20 minutes until tender, drain well and let steam dry 2 minutes.|Mash with the butter and salt until completely smooth with no lumps.|Work in the flour while the potatoes are still warm until a soft, pliable dough forms.|Divide in half and roll each piece on a floured surface into a 1/2 inch thick round, then cut into quarters.|Heat a skillet over medium heat with a little oil and cook the farls 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden brown.|Serve hot with butter.","Irish"],
[3456,"Leek and Potato Gratin","sides","🧅",85,"Medium",7.5,6,"Sliced potatoes and soft leeks baked in cream with thyme and a crust of melted cheddar.","1 1/2 lb|potatoes|waxy, sliced 1/8 inch thick;3|leeks|large, white and light green parts sliced;2 tbsp|butter;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/4 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|milk;1 tsp|fresh thyme|leaves;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 2 quart baking dish.|Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the leeks 8 minutes until soft, adding the garlic for the last minute.|Warm the cream and milk with the thyme, nutmeg, salt and pepper.|Layer half the potatoes in the dish, then half the leeks and a third of the cheese, then repeat.|Pour the warm cream over the top and sprinkle with the remaining cheese.|Cover with foil and bake 40 minutes, then uncover and bake 20 minutes until golden and tender.","British"],
[3457,"Creamed Leeks","sides","🧅",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Leeks gently stewed in butter and finished in a light cream sauce with a touch of mustard.","4|leeks|trimmed, sliced 1/2 inch thick and washed;3 tbsp|butter;1 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|flour;1/2 cup|chicken broth;3/4 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Melt the butter in a large skillet over medium-low heat.|Add the leeks and a pinch of salt, cover and cook 8 to 10 minutes, stirring now and then, until very soft but not browned.|Stir in the garlic and flour and cook 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and cream, add the mustard and simmer uncovered 5 to 6 minutes until thickened and coating the leeks.|Season with the salt and pepper, scatter with the chives and serve.","British"],
[3458,"Sage and Onion Stuffing","sides","🧅",60,"Easy",7.5,8,"Traditional roast dinner stuffing of buttery onions, fresh sage and bread, baked until crisp on top.","4 tbsp|butter;2|onion|finely diced;10 slice|bread|stale, torn into cubes;1/4 cup|sage|fresh, chopped;1 tsp|dried thyme;3/4 cup|chicken broth;1|eggs|beaten;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a baking dish.|Melt the butter in a skillet over medium-low heat and cook the onions 10 to 12 minutes until soft and translucent.|Stir in the sage and thyme and cook 1 minute, then cool slightly.|Combine the bread cubes with the onion mixture, salt and pepper in a large bowl.|Mix in the broth and egg until the bread is moist but not soggy.|Spread in the dish and bake 30 to 35 minutes until golden and crisp on top.","British"],
[3459,"Bread Sauce","sides","🥣",40,"Easy",7.5,6,"A creamy spiced milk and breadcrumb sauce, infused with onion and cloves, served with roast poultry.","1|onion|small, peeled and halved;6|whole cloves;1|bay leaves;2 cup|milk;1 cup|breadcrumbs|fresh white;2 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|heavy cream;1/8 tsp|nutmeg;1/2 tsp|salt;|black pepper|to taste","Stud the onion halves with the cloves and put them in a saucepan with the bay leaf and milk.|Heat gently until just steaming, then remove from the heat, cover and infuse 20 minutes.|Remove the onion and bay leaf and return the pan to low heat.|Whisk in the breadcrumbs and simmer 8 to 10 minutes, stirring, until thick and creamy.|Stir in the butter, cream, nutmeg, salt and pepper and thin with a splash of milk if needed.|Serve warm.","British"],
[3460,"Wakame Seaweed Salad","sides","🥗",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Silky green wakame tossed in a tangy sesame-ginger dressing, the classic sushi bar starter.","1 oz|dried wakame;2 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|ginger|finely grated;1/2|cucumber|thinly sliced;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1|green onion|thinly sliced","Soak the dried wakame in a large bowl of cold water for 10 minutes until fully softened and expanded.|Drain the wakame, squeeze out the excess water, and trim off any thick stems.|Whisk the rice vinegar, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar, and grated ginger until the sugar dissolves.|Toss the wakame and cucumber slices with the dressing.|Top with toasted sesame seeds and green onion and serve chilled.","Japanese"],
[3461,"Quick Pickled Daikon","sides","🥒",45,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crisp, lightly sweet and tangy daikon rounds that cut through rich grilled meats and fried foods.","1 lb|daikon|peeled and sliced into thin half moons;1/2 cup|rice vinegar;3 tbsp|sugar;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|black pepper|whole peppercorns","Toss the daikon slices with the salt in a bowl and let them sit for 10 minutes, then squeeze out the liquid they release.|Warm the rice vinegar, sugar, and 1/2 cup water in a small saucepan over low heat just until the sugar dissolves, about 2 minutes.|Stir in the lemon juice and let the brine cool for 10 minutes.|Pack the daikon and peppercorns into a clean jar and pour the brine over until covered.|Refrigerate at least 30 minutes before serving, or up to 2 weeks.","Japanese"],
[3462,"Spinach Namul","sides","🥬",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Blanched spinach seasoned with garlic, sesame oil, and toasted sesame seeds, a staple Korean banchan.","1 lb|spinach;2 clove|garlic|minced;1|green onion|finely chopped;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sesame seeds|toasted;|salt|to taste","Bring a large pot of salted water to a boil and prepare a bowl of ice water.|Blanch the spinach for 30 to 40 seconds until bright green and wilted.|Transfer the spinach to the ice water, then drain and squeeze out as much water as possible.|Loosen the spinach into a bowl and add the garlic, green onion, soy sauce, and sesame oil.|Toss gently with your hands, taste for salt, and sprinkle with sesame seeds before serving.","Korean"],
[3463,"Kongnamul Muchim","sides","🌱",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Crunchy steamed bean sprouts dressed with sesame oil, garlic, and a hint of chili flakes.","1 lb|bean sprouts;2|green onion|chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1/2 tsp|gochugaru|optional","Rinse the bean sprouts and remove any brown tails.|Bring 1/2 cup water and 1/2 teaspoon of the salt to a boil in a pot with a lid, add the sprouts, cover, and cook for 5 minutes without lifting the lid.|Drain the sprouts and rinse under cold water to stop the cooking, then drain well.|Toss with the green onion, garlic, sesame oil, remaining salt, and gochugaru.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and serve cold or at room temperature.","Korean"],
[3464,"Japanese Cabbage Salad with Sesame Dressing","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Paper-thin cabbage and carrot in a nutty sesame-soy dressing, the crunchy salad served with tonkatsu.","1/2 head|cabbage|very thinly shredded;1|carrot|shredded;2 tbsp|sesame seeds|toasted and ground;2 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|mayonnaise","Soak the shredded cabbage in ice water for 5 minutes to crisp it up, then drain and dry thoroughly.|Grind the toasted sesame seeds with a mortar and pestle or in a spice grinder until mostly crushed.|Whisk the ground sesame, rice vinegar, soy sauce, sugar, sesame oil, and mayonnaise until smooth.|Toss the cabbage and carrot with the dressing just before serving so it stays crisp.","Japanese"],
[3465,"Agedashi Tofu","sides","🍢",30,"Medium",7.5,4,"Lightly crisp fried tofu cubes floating in warm, savory dashi broth with grated daikon.","14 oz|firm tofu|drained and pressed;1/3 cup|potato starch;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1 cup|dashi;3 tbsp|soy sauce;3 tbsp|mirin;3 tbsp|daikon|finely grated;1|green onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|bonito flakes|optional","Wrap the tofu in paper towels, set a plate on top, and press for 15 minutes, then cut into 8 cubes.|Simmer the dashi, soy sauce, and mirin in a small saucepan for 2 minutes, then keep warm.|Heat the oil in a deep pan to 350°F.|Pat the tofu dry, dust all sides lightly with potato starch, and fry in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until pale golden and crisp.|Drain the tofu on a rack, then place in shallow bowls and ladle the warm broth around it.|Top with grated daikon, green onion, and bonito flakes and serve immediately.","Japanese"],
[3466,"Japanese Potato Salad","sides","🥔",50,"Easy",7.5,6,"Creamy, lightly mashed potato salad with cucumber, carrot, and egg, seasoned with rice vinegar.","1 1/2 lb|potatoes|peeled and cut into chunks;1|carrot|thinly sliced into half moons;1/2|cucumber|thinly sliced;2|eggs;1/4 cup|onion|very thinly sliced;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1/2 tsp|sugar;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Hard boil the eggs for 10 minutes, cool in ice water, peel, and chop.|Toss the cucumber and onion with 1/2 teaspoon salt, let sit 10 minutes, then squeeze out the water.|Boil the potatoes and carrot in salted water for 15 minutes until a knife slides in easily, then drain and let steam dry for 2 minutes.|Mash the potatoes roughly in a bowl, leaving some chunks, and stir in the rice vinegar and sugar while warm.|Let cool for 10 minutes, then fold in the mayonnaise, eggs, cucumber, and onion.|Season with salt and pepper and chill before serving.","Japanese"],
[3467,"Gamja Jorim (Korean Braised Potatoes)","sides","🥔",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Bite-size potatoes simmered until glossy in a sweet and salty soy glaze, a favorite Korean banchan.","1 1/2 lb|potatoes|cut into 1-inch chunks;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|honey;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1|green onion|sliced","Rinse the potato chunks in cold water to remove surface starch and drain.|Heat the vegetable oil in a wide skillet over medium-high heat and sear the potatoes for 4 minutes until lightly browned in spots.|Add 1 cup water, the soy sauce, sugar, and garlic, bring to a boil, then cover and simmer over medium heat for 12 minutes.|Uncover, stir in the honey, and cook 5 more minutes, stirring often, until the sauce is thick and glossy and the potatoes are tender.|Stir in the sesame oil, top with sesame seeds and green onion, and serve warm or at room temperature.","Korean"],
[3468,"Kinpira Gobo","sides","🥕",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Matchsticks of burdock root and carrot sauteed in a sweet soy glaze, a traditional Japanese home side.","8 oz|burdock root|scrubbed and cut into matchsticks;1|carrot|cut into matchsticks;1 tbsp|sesame oil;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tsp|sesame seeds|toasted;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes|optional","Soak the burdock matchsticks in cold water for 5 minutes to remove bitterness and prevent browning, then drain well.|Heat the sesame oil in a skillet over medium-high heat and stir-fry the burdock for 3 minutes.|Add the carrot and cook 2 more minutes.|Stir in the soy sauce, mirin, sugar, and 2 tablespoons water and cook for 5 minutes, stirring, until the liquid reduces to a glaze.|Finish with the sesame seeds and pepper flakes and serve warm or cold.","Japanese"],
[3469,"Hobak Namul (Korean Sauteed Zucchini)","sides","🥒",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Tender zucchini half moons stir-fried with garlic and sesame oil, lightly salted and sprinkled with sesame.","2|zucchini|cut into half moons;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 clove|garlic|minced;1|green onion|chopped;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sesame seeds|toasted","Toss the zucchini with the salt and let it sit for 5 minutes, then pat dry with paper towels.|Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat.|Add the zucchini in a single layer and cook for 2 to 3 minutes until lightly golden, then stir.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute until fragrant, being careful not to overcook the zucchini.|Remove from heat, stir in the green onion and sesame oil, and sprinkle with sesame seeds.","Korean"],
[3470,"Kabocha Nimono (Japanese Simmered Kabocha)","sides","🎃",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Sweet, tender kabocha squash simmered in dashi, soy, and mirin until it soaks up every drop.","1 1/2 lb|kabocha squash|seeded and cut into 2-inch chunks;1 cup|dashi;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|mirin;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tsp|ginger|thinly sliced","Leave some skin on the kabocha for color and shave away the rest in a few spots with a peeler.|Arrange the chunks skin-side down in a wide pot in a single layer.|Add the dashi, soy sauce, mirin, sugar, and ginger and bring to a boil over medium-high heat.|Reduce the heat to medium-low, cover with a lid that sits just on the surface or foil, and simmer for 15 to 18 minutes until a skewer slides in easily.|Turn off the heat and let it rest for 10 minutes so the squash absorbs the broth, then serve warm.","Japanese"],
[3471,"Hot and Sour Shredded Cabbage","sides","🥬",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Wok-charred cabbage tossed with dried chilies, Sichuan pepper, and black vinegar in just a few minutes.","1/2 head|cabbage|shredded;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;4|dried red chilies|snipped in half;1 tsp|sichuan peppercorns;3 clove|garlic|sliced;3 tbsp|black vinegar;1 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt","Mix the black vinegar, soy sauce, sugar, and salt in a small bowl.|Heat the oil in a wok over medium heat, add the Sichuan peppercorns and dried chilies, and stir for 30 seconds until fragrant.|Add the garlic and stir for 15 seconds.|Turn the heat to high, add the cabbage, and stir-fry for 2 to 3 minutes until it begins to wilt but stays crisp at the edges.|Pour in the sauce and toss for 30 seconds, then serve immediately.","Chinese"],
[3472,"Thai Cucumber Relish (Ajad)","sides","🥒",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Sweet-and-sour cucumber, shallot, and chili salad with crushed peanuts, served with satay and fish cakes.","2|cucumbers|halved and thinly sliced;1/2 cup|rice vinegar;1/3 cup|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt;2|shallots|thinly sliced;1|red chili|thinly sliced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|peanuts|roughly crushed","Combine the rice vinegar, sugar, salt, and 1/4 cup water in a small saucepan and heat for 3 minutes, stirring, until the sugar dissolves.|Let the syrup cool completely, about 15 minutes.|Place the cucumber, shallots, and chili in a bowl.|Pour the cooled syrup over the vegetables and stir.|Top with cilantro and crushed peanuts just before serving.","Thai"],
[3473,"Do Chua (Vietnamese Pickled Carrot and Daikon)","sides","🥕",45,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Sweet and tangy julienned carrot and daikon, the essential pickle for banh mi and rice plates.","1/2 lb|carrot|julienned;1/2 lb|daikon|julienned;1 tbsp|salt;1/2 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|white vinegar;1 cup|warm water|from tap","Toss the carrot and daikon with the salt and 1 tablespoon of the sugar and massage for 3 minutes until slightly softened.|Rinse under cold water and squeeze out the excess liquid.|Stir the remaining sugar into the warm water until dissolved, then stir in the vinegar.|Pack the vegetables into a clean jar and pour the brine over to cover.|Let sit at room temperature for 30 minutes, then refrigerate. It keeps for 3 weeks.","Vietnamese"],
[3474,"Jeera Rice","sides","🍚",30,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Fluffy basmati rice tempered with toasted cumin seeds and ghee, the everyday partner for dal and curry.","1 1/2 cup|basmati rice;2 tbsp|ghee;2 tsp|cumin seeds;1|bay leaf;1|cinnamon stick;1 tsp|salt","Rinse the rice in several changes of cold water until it runs mostly clear, then soak for 20 minutes and drain.|Heat the ghee in a heavy saucepan over medium heat and add the cumin seeds, bay leaf, and cinnamon stick, cooking for 30 seconds until the cumin sizzles and darkens.|Add the drained rice and stir for 1 minute to coat in the ghee.|Add 2 1/4 cups water and the salt and bring to a boil.|Cover, reduce the heat to low, and cook for 12 minutes, then turn off the heat and rest covered for 5 minutes.|Fluff with a fork and remove the whole spices if you like.","Indian"],
[3475,"Bhindi Masala","sides","🥬",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crisp-tender okra stir-fried with onion, tomato, and warm spices, with no slime when you cook it right.","1 lb|okra|trimmed and cut into 1-inch pieces;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|cumin seeds;1|onion|thinly sliced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|ginger|minced;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1/2 tsp|garam masala;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Wash and thoroughly dry the okra before cutting, since moisture causes sliminess.|Heat 1 tablespoon of the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and cook the okra for 6 to 8 minutes until browned in spots, then remove to a plate.|Add the remaining oil and the cumin seeds and cook 20 seconds, then add the onion and cook 5 minutes until golden.|Stir in the garlic, ginger, turmeric, coriander, and cayenne for 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes and 1/2 teaspoon salt and cook 5 minutes until they break down into a thick masala.|Return the okra to the pan, toss to coat, and cook 3 minutes.|Finish with garam masala and lemon juice and adjust the salt.","Indian"],
[3476,"Aloo Jeera","sides","🥔",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Golden potato cubes pan-fried with toasted cumin seeds, turmeric, and fresh cilantro.","1 1/2 lb|potatoes|cut into 3/4-inch cubes;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tsp|cumin seeds;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|coriander;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1|green chili|slit lengthwise;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Boil the potato cubes in salted water for 5 minutes until just barely tender, then drain and let steam dry.|Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium heat and add the cumin seeds, cooking 20 seconds until they sizzle.|Add the green chili, turmeric, coriander, and cayenne and stir for 10 seconds.|Add the potatoes and salt, spreading them out in a single layer.|Cook 10 to 12 minutes, turning occasionally, until crisp and golden on the edges.|Finish with the cilantro and lemon juice.","Indian"],
[3477,"Kachumber Salad","sides","🥗",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"A cooling chopped cucumber, tomato, and onion salad with lemon, cumin, and cilantro.","2|cucumbers|diced;3|tomatoes|seeded and diced;1|red onion|finely diced;1|green chili|minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|cumin|ground;1/2 tsp|chaat masala;1/2 tsp|salt","Combine the cucumbers, tomatoes, onion, green chili, and cilantro in a large bowl.|Sprinkle with the cumin, chaat masala, and salt.|Add the lemon juice and toss gently.|Let sit for 5 minutes so the flavors blend, and serve right away so it stays crisp.","Indian"],
[3478,"Mint Chutney","sides","🌿",10,"Very easy",7.5,8,"A bright green blend of mint, cilantro, green chili, and lemon, the essential dip for samosas and pakoras.","1 bunch|mint|leaves picked;1 bunch|cilantro|tender stems and leaves;2|green chili|roughly chopped;1 tbsp|ginger|chopped;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|cumin|ground;1/2 tsp|sugar;1/2 tsp|salt","Add the mint, cilantro, green chilies, ginger, lemon juice, cumin, sugar, and salt to a blender.|Add 2 tablespoons cold water and blend, scraping down the sides, until smooth.|Add more water a tablespoon at a time if needed to reach a thick, spoonable consistency.|Taste for salt and lemon and serve at once, or refrigerate up to 4 days.","Indian"],
[3479,"Mango Chutney","sides","🥭",55,"Easy",7.5,10,"Sweet, tangy, lightly spiced mango preserve to spoon over curries, cheese, and grilled meats.","2|mangoes|firm-ripe, peeled and diced;1|onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1 cup|apple cider vinegar;1/2 cup|raisins;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|mustard seeds;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1 tsp|salt","Combine the vinegar, brown sugar, onion, ginger, garlic, mustard seeds, pepper flakes, cinnamon, and salt in a heavy saucepan.|Bring to a boil and simmer for 10 minutes until the onion softens.|Add the mango and raisins and return to a gentle simmer.|Cook uncovered for 30 to 35 minutes, stirring often, until the mixture is thick and jammy.|Cool completely and spoon into a jar. The flavor improves after a day in the refrigerator and keeps 3 weeks.","Indian"],
[3480,"Coconut Chutney","sides","🥥",15,"Very easy",7.5,6,"South Indian coconut and green chili chutney with a sizzling mustard seed and curry leaf tempering.","1 cup|shredded coconut|unsweetened, fresh or frozen;2 tbsp|roasted chana dal;2|green chili;1 tbsp|ginger|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|coconut oil;1 tsp|mustard seeds;1 sprig|curry leaves;2|dried red chilies;1 pinch|asafoetida","Blend the coconut, chana dal, green chilies, ginger, and salt with 1/3 cup water until smooth, adding a splash more if needed.|Pour the chutney into a serving bowl.|Heat the coconut oil in a small pan over medium heat until shimmering.|Add the mustard seeds and cook until they pop, about 30 seconds.|Add the dried chilies, curry leaves, and asafoetida and cook 10 seconds.|Pour the sizzling mixture over the chutney and stir. Serve with dosa, idli, or vada.","Indian"],
[3481,"Cabbage Poriyal","sides","🥬",20,"Easy",7.5,4,"South Indian stir-fried cabbage with mustard seeds, curry leaves, and fresh coconut.","1 lb|cabbage|finely shredded;2 tbsp|coconut oil;1 tsp|mustard seeds;1 tbsp|chana dal;2|dried red chilies;1 sprig|curry leaves;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|salt;1/3 cup|shredded coconut;1|green chili|chopped","Heat the coconut oil in a wide pan over medium heat and add the mustard seeds until they pop.|Add the chana dal, dried chilies, and curry leaves and cook 1 minute until the dal turns golden.|Add the green chili and turmeric and stir for 10 seconds.|Add the cabbage and salt, toss well, cover, and cook 5 minutes over medium-low heat, stirring once.|Uncover and cook 3 more minutes until tender but still slightly crunchy.|Stir in the coconut and serve warm.","Indian"],
[3482,"Melitzanosalata","sides","🍆",60,"Easy",7.5,6,"Smoky roasted eggplant dip with garlic, olive oil, and red wine vinegar, a classic Greek meze.","2|eggplant|about 2 lb total;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|red wine vinegar;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 425°F and prick the eggplants all over with a fork.|Roast on a lined baking sheet for 45 minutes, turning once, until collapsed and very soft. For extra smokiness, char them first over a gas flame or grill.|Cut open the eggplants and scoop the flesh into a colander, discarding the skin, and drain for 10 minutes.|Chop the flesh finely with a knife and place in a bowl.|Stir in the garlic, then slowly beat in the olive oil, vinegar, and lemon juice.|Fold in the parsley, season with salt and pepper, and chill before serving with bread.","Greek"],
[3483,"Skordalia","sides","🧄",40,"Easy",7.5,8,"A thick, garlicky Greek potato dip with olive oil and lemon, served with fried fish or roasted beets.","1 lb|potatoes|peeled and cut into chunks;6 clove|garlic|crushed;1/2 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|salt","Boil the potatoes in salted water for 20 minutes until very tender, then drain, reserving 1/2 cup of the cooking water.|Pass the hot potatoes through a ricer or mash until completely smooth.|Mash the garlic with the salt into a paste and stir it into the potatoes.|Beat in the olive oil in a slow stream, then the vinegar and lemon juice, adding reserved cooking water a tablespoon at a time until creamy.|Adjust the salt and serve at room temperature.","Greek"],
[3484,"Lebanese Cabbage Salad (Salatet Malfouf)","sides","🥬",25,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Finely shredded cabbage dressed with lemon, garlic, olive oil, and dried mint, a mezze table staple.","1/2 head|cabbage|very finely shredded;1/4 cup|lemon juice;1/4 cup|olive oil;2 clove|garlic|crushed;1 tbsp|dried mint;1 tsp|salt","Place the shredded cabbage in a large bowl and sprinkle with the salt.|Massage the cabbage for 1 to 2 minutes until it begins to soften, then let sit for 10 minutes.|Whisk the lemon juice, olive oil, and crushed garlic together.|Pour the dressing over the cabbage, add the dried mint, and toss well.|Rest 10 minutes before serving, and adjust the lemon and salt.","Lebanese"],
[3485,"Labneh with Olive Oil","sides","🧀",480,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Thick, tangy strained yogurt cheese drizzled with olive oil and za'atar for scooping with warm pita.","32 oz|plain yogurt|whole milk;1/2 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|za'atar;1/4 cup|olives|optional;1 tbsp|mint|chopped","Stir the salt into the yogurt.|Line a sieve with a double layer of cheesecloth, set it over a bowl, and spoon in the yogurt.|Gather the cloth corners, tie them closed, and refrigerate for at least 8 hours or up to 24 hours. Longer straining gives a firmer labneh.|Discard the whey and spread the labneh in a shallow bowl, making swirls with a spoon.|Drizzle with olive oil, sprinkle with za'atar and mint, and top with olives. Serve with warm pita.","Lebanese"],
[3486,"Bulgur Pilaf","sides","🍚",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Nutty coarse bulgur cooked with onion, green pepper, and tomato paste in the Turkish style.","1 1/2 cup|bulgur|coarse;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|butter;1|onion|finely diced;1|green bell pepper|diced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;3 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the olive oil and butter in a saucepan over medium heat.|Cook the onion and green pepper for 6 minutes until soft.|Stir in the tomato paste and cook 2 minutes until it darkens slightly.|Add the bulgur and stir 1 minute to coat in the oil.|Pour in the hot chicken broth, add the salt and pepper, and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat to low, cover, and cook for 15 minutes, then turn off the heat and let it rest covered for 10 minutes.|Fluff with a fork before serving.","Turkish"],
[3487,"Za'atar Roasted Potatoes","sides","🥔",50,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crisp-edged baby potatoes roasted in olive oil and za'atar with a squeeze of lemon.","2 lb|baby potatoes|halved;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tbsp|za'atar;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|lemon juice","Heat the oven to 425°F.|Toss the potatoes with the olive oil, za'atar, salt, and pepper on a rimmed baking sheet.|Arrange cut side down in a single layer.|Roast for 35 to 40 minutes, flipping once at 20 minutes, until deep golden and crisp.|Toss with the garlic in the last 5 minutes of cooking.|Squeeze the lemon juice over the hot potatoes and serve.","Lebanese"],
[3488,"Spanakorizo (Greek Spinach Rice)","sides","🍚",40,"Easy",7.5,6,"Lemony Greek rice simmered with spinach, dill, and green onions in olive oil.","1 lb|spinach|chopped;1 cup|long-grain rice;1|onion|chopped;3|green onion|sliced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1/4 cup|dill|chopped;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion and green onions for 5 minutes until soft.|Add the spinach in batches and cook until wilted, about 4 minutes.|Stir in the rice and tomato paste and cook for 1 minute.|Add 2 cups hot water, the salt, and pepper and bring to a simmer.|Cover and cook over low heat for 18 minutes until the rice is tender and the liquid is absorbed.|Stir in the dill and lemon juice and rest 5 minutes before serving.","Greek"],
[3489,"Piyaz (Turkish White Bean Salad)","sides","🫘",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Creamy white beans with red onion, parsley, and sumac in a sharp olive oil and vinegar dressing.","2 can|cannellini beans|15 oz, drained and rinsed;1|red onion|thinly sliced;2|tomatoes|diced;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|sumac;2|eggs|hard boiled and sliced;1/2 tsp|salt","Toss the sliced onion with the sumac and a pinch of salt and rub for 1 minute, then let sit 5 minutes to soften.|Whisk the olive oil, red wine vinegar, and remaining salt together.|In a bowl, gently combine the beans, tomatoes, parsley, and onion.|Pour the dressing over and toss.|Top with the sliced eggs and serve at room temperature.","Turkish"],
[3490,"Fava (Santorini Yellow Split Pea Puree)","sides","🫘",60,"Easy",7.5,6,"A silky Greek puree of yellow split peas topped with capers, red onion, and good olive oil.","1 cup|yellow split peas;1|onion|chopped;2 clove|garlic|whole;1|bay leaf;1/4 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|capers;1/2|red onion|finely chopped;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Rinse the split peas and place in a pot with the onion, garlic, bay leaf, and 4 cups water.|Bring to a boil, skim off the foam, then simmer partially covered for 40 to 45 minutes, stirring often, until the peas completely fall apart.|Remove the bay leaf and stir in the salt.|Blend with an immersion blender, adding the 1/4 cup olive oil and the lemon juice, until silky smooth.|Spread in a shallow dish, let it set for 15 minutes, then top with capers, red onion, parsley, and a drizzle of oil.","Greek"],
[3491,"Zeytinyagli Pirasa (Turkish Braised Leeks)","sides","🧅",50,"Easy",7.5,4,"Leeks braised with carrot and a little rice in olive oil, lemon, and dill, served cool as a meze.","4|leeks|cleaned and cut into 1-inch rounds;1/4 cup|olive oil;1|carrot|sliced;1/4 cup|short-grain rice;1 tsp|sugar;2 tbsp|lemon juice;1 sprig|dill|chopped;1 tsp|salt","Heat the olive oil in a wide pot over medium heat.|Add the leeks and carrot and cook for 5 minutes, stirring.|Stir in the rice, sugar, and salt.|Add 1 cup hot water, cover, and simmer over low heat for 25 to 30 minutes until the leeks and rice are tender.|Stir in the lemon juice and let cool to room temperature.|Sprinkle with dill and serve at room temperature or chilled.","Turkish"],
[3492,"Calabacitas","sides","🥒",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Tender zucchini simmered with corn, tomato, and poblano, finished with melting cheese.","1 1/2 lb|zucchini|diced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1/2|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|corn|kernels;1|poblano pepper|diced;2|tomatoes|diced;1/2 tsp|cumin|ground;1/2 cup|queso fresco|crumbled;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste","Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion and poblano for 5 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cumin and stir for 30 seconds.|Add the zucchini and corn and cook for 5 minutes, stirring occasionally.|Stir in the tomatoes and 1/2 teaspoon salt, cover, and cook over medium-low heat for 8 minutes until the zucchini is tender.|Top with the queso fresco, cover for 1 minute to soften it, and finish with cilantro.","Mexican"],
[3493,"Jicama Salad with Lime and Chili","sides","🥗",20,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Crisp jicama and cucumber sticks tossed with lime, orange, cilantro, and chili powder.","1|jicama|about 1 1/2 lb, peeled and cut into matchsticks;1|cucumber|cut into matchsticks;1/4 cup|red onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|lime juice;2 tbsp|orange juice;1 tbsp|honey;1 tsp|chili powder;1/2 tsp|salt","Place the jicama, cucumber, and red onion in a large bowl.|Whisk the lime juice, orange juice, honey, and salt until the honey dissolves.|Pour the dressing over the vegetables and toss.|Add the cilantro and sprinkle with the chili powder.|Chill for 10 minutes before serving.","Mexican"],
[3494,"Jalapenos en Escabeche","sides","🌶️",40,"Easy",7.5,12,"Tangy pickled jalapenos, carrots, and onion, the taqueria condiment served with tacos and tortas.","6|jalapeno|sliced into rounds;3|carrot|sliced;1|onion|sliced;4 clove|garlic|peeled;1 1/2 cup|white vinegar;2 tbsp|olive oil;2|bay leaf;1 tsp|oregano;1 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper|whole peppercorns","Heat the olive oil in a large saucepan over medium heat and cook the onion and garlic for 3 minutes.|Add the carrots and cook 3 minutes.|Add the vinegar, 1 cup water, bay leaves, oregano, sugar, salt, and peppercorns and bring to a boil.|Add the jalapenos and simmer for 4 to 5 minutes until the carrots are crisp-tender and the chilies turn olive green.|Cool to room temperature, then transfer with the brine to a jar.|Refrigerate at least 1 day for the best flavor. They keep for 3 weeks.","Mexican"],
[3495,"Frijoles de la Olla","sides","🫘",150,"Very easy",7.5,8,"Pot beans simmered slowly with onion and garlic until creamy, with a rich broth.","1 lb|pinto beans|dried, rinsed;1/2|onion|halved;3 clove|garlic|peeled;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 sprig|epazote|optional;1 tbsp|salt","Pick through the beans for stones and rinse well.|Combine the beans, onion, garlic, oil, and 8 cups water in a large pot and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat to a low simmer, partially cover, and cook for 1 1/2 to 2 hours, adding hot water if the beans become uncovered.|When the beans are almost tender, stir in the salt and epazote.|Simmer another 20 to 30 minutes until creamy and tender, then serve in bowls with the broth.","Mexican"],
[3496,"Sarza Criolla (Peruvian Onion Salad)","sides","🧅",30,"Very easy",7.5,6,"Thin red onion half moons marinated in lime, chili, and cilantro, the tangy topping for grilled meats and rice.","2|red onion|very thinly sliced;1/4 cup|lime juice;1|jalapeno|minced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|cumin|ground","Soak the sliced onions in cold salted water for 10 minutes to mellow their bite, then drain and pat dry.|Whisk the lime juice, olive oil, salt, and cumin.|Combine the onions, jalapeno, and cilantro in a bowl.|Pour the dressing over and toss.|Let marinate 10 minutes before serving at room temperature.","Peruvian"],
[3497,"Yuca con Mojo","sides","🧄",45,"Easy",7.5,6,"Tender boiled cassava drenched in warm garlic-citrus mojo sauce.","2 lb|yuca|peeled, fresh or frozen, cut in chunks;6 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 cup|olive oil;1/3 cup|orange juice;1/4 cup|lime juice;1 tsp|oregano;1 tsp|cumin|ground;1 tsp|salt","Place the yuca in a large pot with enough cold water to cover and 1 tablespoon salt.|Bring to a boil, then simmer for 25 to 30 minutes until fork-tender, and drain well.|Meanwhile, warm the olive oil in a small saucepan over medium-low heat and cook the garlic for 1 to 2 minutes until fragrant, without browning.|Remove from the heat and carefully stir in the orange juice, lime juice, oregano, cumin, and salt as it will sputter.|Pour the warm mojo over the hot yuca, toss, and serve.","Cuban"],
[3498,"Arroz Verde (Green Rice)","sides","🍚",40,"Easy",7.5,4,"Mexican rice toasted in oil and cooked in a blend of poblano, cilantro, and garlic.","1 cup|long-grain rice;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|poblano pepper|seeded and chopped;1 cup|cilantro|packed;1/4|onion|chopped;2 clove|garlic;2 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|salt;1|jalapeno|optional","Blend the poblano, cilantro, onion, garlic, jalapeno, and 1 cup of the chicken broth until smooth.|Heat the oil in a saucepan over medium heat and add the rice, stirring for 4 to 5 minutes until lightly golden.|Pour in the blended mixture, the remaining 1 cup broth, and the salt and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat to low, cover, and cook for 17 minutes without lifting the lid.|Rest covered for 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork.","Mexican"],
[3499,"Ensalada de Nopales","sides","🌵",35,"Easy",7.5,4,"Tender cactus paddles with tomato, onion, cilantro, and queso fresco in a bright lime dressing.","1 lb|nopales|cleaned and diced;1/4|onion|halved, for boiling;2|tomatoes|diced;1/4|white onion|finely diced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1|serrano|minced;2 tbsp|lime juice;1 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 cup|queso fresco|crumbled;1 tsp|oregano;|salt|to taste","Boil the nopales in a pot of salted water with the halved onion piece for 10 to 15 minutes until tender and olive green.|Drain, rinse well under cold water to remove the slime, and drain again.|Combine the nopales, tomatoes, diced onion, cilantro, and serrano in a bowl.|Whisk the lime juice, olive oil, oregano, and a pinch of salt.|Toss with the nopales and top with the queso fresco.","Mexican"],
[3500,"Fish and Chips","comfort","🐟",60,"Medium",9,4,"Crisp beer-battered cod with thick, fluffy chips, served with malt vinegar and tartar sauce.","2 lb|russet potatoes|cut into 1/2 inch thick chips;1 1/2 lb|cod|4 fillets, patted dry;1 cup|flour|plus 1/4 cup for dusting;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt|plus more for seasoning;3/4 cup|beer|very cold lager;6 cup|vegetable oil|for frying;1|lemon|cut into wedges;|malt vinegar|to serve;|tartar sauce|to serve","Soak the cut chips in cold water for 20 minutes, then drain and dry them very well on a clean towel.|Heat the oil in a deep heavy pot to 300°F and fry the chips in batches for 6 to 7 minutes until soft but not colored. Drain on a rack.|Whisk 1 cup flour, the baking powder and 1 teaspoon salt, then stir in the cold beer until just combined. Do not overmix.|Raise the oil to 375°F. Season the cod with salt, dust with the extra flour, dip in the batter and lower gently into the oil.|Fry the fish for 4 to 5 minutes, turning once, until deep golden and the fish flakes. Drain on a rack and keep warm in a 200°F oven.|Fry the chips again for 3 to 4 minutes until golden and crisp, then salt well. Serve with vinegar, tartar sauce and lemon.","British"],
[3501,"Bangers and Mash","comfort","🌭",40,"Easy",9,4,"Browned pork sausages on buttery mashed potatoes, smothered in sweet onion gravy.","8|pork sausage|good quality bangers;2 lb|russet potatoes|peeled and cut into chunks;4 tbsp|butter|divided;1/2 cup|milk|warm;2|onion|thinly sliced;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|flour;2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|worcestershire;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 cup|frozen peas|to serve;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cover the potatoes with cold salted water, bring to a boil and cook 15 to 18 minutes until very tender.|Meanwhile, brown the sausages in the oil in a large skillet over medium heat for 12 to 15 minutes, turning, until cooked through. Remove and keep warm.|In the same skillet, cook the onions in 2 tablespoons butter with the sugar for 12 minutes until deeply golden.|Stir in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the broth, worcestershire and mustard. Simmer 8 minutes until thick and glossy.|Drain the potatoes and mash with the remaining butter and warm milk. Season well with salt and pepper.|Cook the peas in a little boiling water for 2 minutes. Pile the mash on plates, top with sausages, peas and plenty of onion gravy.","British"],
[3502,"Steak and Ale Pie","comfort","🥧",200,"Medium",9,6,"Beef slow-braised in dark ale until tender, topped with a golden puff pastry lid.","2 lb|beef stew meat|cut into 1 inch cubes;2 tbsp|flour;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;2|onion|chopped;2|carrots|diced;8 oz|mushrooms|quartered;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 1/2 cup|beer|brown ale or stout;1 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|worcestershire;2 sprig|fresh thyme;2|bay leaves;14 oz|puff pastry|thawed;1|eggs|beaten, for brushing;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Toss the beef with the flour, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper. Brown in batches in the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat, about 8 minutes total, and set aside.|Cook the onions, carrots and mushrooms in the same pot for 8 minutes. Add the garlic and tomato paste and cook 1 minute.|Pour in the ale and scrape up the browned bits. Return the beef, add the broth, worcestershire, thyme and bay leaves.|Cover and cook in a 325°F oven for 2 hours until the beef is very tender and the gravy is thick. Remove the herbs and cool for 20 minutes.|Spoon the filling into a 2 quart baking dish. Roll the pastry slightly larger than the dish, lay it over the top and trim and crimp the edges.|Brush with the egg, cut a steam vent and bake at 400°F for 25 to 30 minutes until puffed and deep golden.","British"],
[3503,"Cornish Pasty","comfort","🥟",120,"Medium",9,4,"Hand-held pastry parcels filled with beef, potato, swede and onion, baked until golden.","3 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|salt;12 tbsp|butter|cold and cubed;1/2 cup|water|ice cold, about;12 oz|chuck roast|finely diced;8 oz|potatoes|peeled and cut into small dice;6 oz|rutabaga|peeled and cut into small dice;1|onion|finely chopped;2 tbsp|butter|for the filling;1|eggs|beaten, for glazing;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Rub the 12 tablespoons cold butter into the flour and salt until crumbly, then add the ice water a spoonful at a time until a dough forms. Wrap and chill 30 minutes.|Mix the beef, potatoes, rutabaga and onion with 1 teaspoon salt and plenty of black pepper.|Divide the dough into 4 pieces and roll each into a 8 inch circle.|Pile the filling on one half of each circle, dot with the 2 tablespoons butter, brush the edge with water, fold over and crimp firmly into a thick rope edge.|Place on a lined baking sheet, cut a small steam slit and brush with egg.|Bake at 400°F for 20 minutes, then lower to 350°F and bake 40 minutes until deep golden. Rest 10 minutes before eating.","British"],
[3504,"Cullen Skink","soup","🍲",45,"Easy",9.5,4,"A creamy Scottish soup of smoked haddock, potatoes and leeks, rich and gently smoky.","1 lb|smoked haddock|undyed if possible;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|finely chopped;1|leek|white part, sliced;1 lb|potatoes|peeled and diced;2 cup|milk;2 cup|chicken broth;1|bay leaves;1/2 cup|heavy cream;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;|black pepper|to taste","Place the haddock in a wide pan with the milk and bay leaf. Bring to a gentle simmer and poach 6 to 8 minutes until it flakes.|Lift out the fish and strain the milk into a bowl. Flake the fish, discarding the skin and bones.|Melt the butter in a large pot and cook the onion and leek 6 minutes until soft but not browned.|Add the potatoes, the chicken broth and the poaching milk. Simmer 15 minutes until the potatoes are very tender.|Mash about a third of the potatoes against the side of the pot to thicken the soup.|Stir in the flaked fish and cream and warm gently 3 minutes. Season with pepper and finish with chives.","British"],
[3505,"Dublin Coddle","comfort","🍲",75,"Easy",9,4,"Sausages, bacon, potatoes and onions simmered together in a savory broth, a Dublin classic.","1 lb|pork sausage|Irish style bangers;8 slice|bacon|cut into pieces;2 lb|potatoes|peeled and sliced 1/4 inch thick;2|onion|sliced;2|carrots|sliced;3 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|dried thyme;1|bay leaves;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the sausages lightly in a Dutch oven for 5 minutes and cut each into thirds. Remove and set aside.|Cook the bacon in the same pot for 5 minutes, leaving the fat.|Layer in the onions, carrots, potatoes, sausages and bacon, sprinkling with thyme and pepper between layers.|Pour in the broth and add the bay leaf.|Cover and simmer gently over low heat for 50 to 60 minutes until the potatoes are tender and the broth has thickened slightly.|Discard the bay leaf, sprinkle with parsley and serve in wide bowls with soda bread.","Irish"],
[3506,"Scotch Broth","soup","🥣",120,"Easy",9.5,6,"A hearty Scottish soup of lamb, barley, split peas and root vegetables.","1 1/2 lb|lamb shoulder|bone-in, cut into chunks;1/2 cup|pearl barley|rinsed;1/4 cup|split peas|rinsed;2|carrots|diced;1|turnip|peeled and diced;1|leek|sliced;1|onion|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;1 cup|cabbage|shredded;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Place the lamb in a large pot with 8 cups cold water and bring slowly to a boil, skimming off the foam.|Add the barley, split peas, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper. Simmer, partly covered, for 45 minutes.|Add the carrots, turnip, leek, onion and celery.|Simmer another 40 minutes until the lamb is tender and the vegetables are soft.|Remove the lamb, pull the meat off the bones and return it to the pot.|Stir in the cabbage and cook 5 minutes. Adjust the seasoning and finish with parsley.","British"],
[3507,"Welsh Cakes","baking","🍪",30,"Easy",8.5,8,"Little griddled currant cakes, buttery and lightly spiced, best eaten warm with a sprinkle of sugar.","2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|sugar|plus more for dusting;1 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 tsp|salt;8 tbsp|butter|cold and cubed;1/2 cup|currants;1|eggs;2 tbsp|milk","Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder, cinnamon and salt in a bowl.|Rub in the cold butter with your fingertips until the mix looks like fine crumbs. Stir in the currants.|Beat the egg with the milk and stir in to form a soft dough, adding a splash more milk if dry.|Roll out on a floured surface to 1/4 inch thick and cut into 2 1/2 inch rounds.|Cook on a lightly greased griddle or skillet over medium-low heat for 3 minutes per side until golden brown and cooked through.|Dust with sugar while still warm.","British"],
[3508,"Cranachan","treats","🥣",20,"Very easy",9,4,"A Scottish dessert of whipped cream, toasted oats, honey, whisky and fresh raspberries.","1/2 cup|oats|rolled;1 1/2 cup|heavy cream;3 tbsp|honey|divided;2 tbsp|whisky;2 cup|raspberries|fresh","Toast the oats in a dry skillet over medium heat for 4 to 5 minutes until golden and fragrant. Cool completely.|Crush half of the raspberries lightly with a fork and keep the rest whole.|Whip the cream to soft peaks, then fold in 2 tablespoons honey and the whisky.|Fold in most of the toasted oats, saving a spoonful for the top.|Layer the cream and raspberries in 4 glasses, finishing with whole berries.|Drizzle with the remaining honey, sprinkle with the reserved oats and serve right away.","British"],
[3509,"Quiche Lorraine","lunch","🥧",90,"Medium",8,8,"A buttery pastry shell filled with smoky bacon, Gruyere and a silky egg custard.","1 1/4 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|salt;8 tbsp|butter|cold and cubed;3 tbsp|water|ice cold;8 slice|bacon|chopped;4|eggs;1 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|milk;1 cup|gruyere|shredded;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;|black pepper|to taste","Pulse the flour, salt and butter until pea-sized crumbs form, then add the ice water and mix until the dough just holds together. Chill 30 minutes.|Roll out and fit into a 9 inch tart pan. Prick the base, line with parchment and weights and blind bake at 400°F for 15 minutes.|Remove the weights and bake 5 minutes more until pale golden. Lower the oven to 350°F.|Cook the bacon until crisp, about 8 minutes, and drain. Scatter it and the Gruyere over the crust.|Whisk the eggs, cream, milk, nutmeg, 1/2 teaspoon salt and pepper and pour over the filling.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until the center is just set. Rest 15 minutes before slicing.","French"],
[3510,"Croque Monsieur","lunch","🥪",25,"Easy",8,4,"A Parisian cafe sandwich of ham and Gruyere, topped with creamy bechamel and broiled until golden.","8 slice|bread|firm white sandwich bread;8 oz|ham|thinly sliced;2 tbsp|butter;2 tbsp|flour;1 1/4 cup|milk|warm;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 1/2 cup|gruyere|shredded, divided;2 tbsp|dijon mustard;2 tbsp|butter|softened, for the bread;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt 2 tablespoons butter in a saucepan, whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute. Gradually whisk in the milk and simmer 4 minutes until thick.|Stir in the nutmeg, 1/2 cup Gruyere, salt and pepper. Set the bechamel aside.|Heat the oven to 425°F. Spread the softened butter on one side of each slice of bread and the mustard on the other.|Build 4 sandwiches with mustard sides in, filling each with ham and 1/4 cup Gruyere. Place on a baking sheet.|Spread the bechamel over the tops and sprinkle with the remaining cheese.|Bake 10 minutes until bubbling, then broil 2 minutes until golden brown.","French"],
[3511,"French Crepes","breakfast","🥞",40,"Easy",8.5,4,"Thin, lacy, golden crepes that can be filled with sugar and lemon, jam or anything you like.","1 cup|flour;2|eggs;1 1/4 cup|milk;2 tbsp|butter|melted and cooled, plus more for the pan;1 tbsp|sugar;1/4 tsp|salt;1 tsp|vanilla;1|lemon|cut into wedges;|sugar|to serve","Blend or whisk the flour, eggs, milk, melted butter, sugar, salt and vanilla until completely smooth.|Rest the batter for 30 minutes at room temperature.|Heat an 8 inch nonstick skillet over medium heat and brush lightly with butter.|Pour in about 1/4 cup batter and swirl the pan to coat the bottom thinly.|Cook 1 minute until the edges lift and the underside is golden, flip and cook 30 seconds more.|Stack the crepes on a plate, then fill and fold with sugar and lemon juice or your favorite filling.","French"],
[3512,"French Onion Tart","lunch","🧅",100,"Medium",8,6,"Sweet caramelized onions, thyme and Gruyere baked in a flaky pastry shell with a light custard.","8 oz|puff pastry|1 sheet, thawed;3|onion|thinly sliced;3 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|sugar;1 tbsp|fresh thyme|leaves;1/4 cup|white wine;2|eggs;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/2 cup|gruyere|shredded;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter with the oil in a large skillet over medium-low heat. Add the onions, sugar and 1/2 teaspoon salt.|Cook, stirring often, for 35 to 40 minutes until deep golden brown and jammy. Add the thyme and wine and cook until evaporated.|Fit the pastry into a 9 inch tart pan and prick the base. Chill 15 minutes.|Bake at 400°F for 12 minutes until just set and pale.|Whisk the eggs, cream, nutmeg and pepper. Spread the onions in the shell, sprinkle with Gruyere and pour in the custard.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes until puffed and golden. Cool 10 minutes before slicing.","French"],
[3513,"Moules Marinieres","light","🦪",30,"Easy",7.5,2,"Fresh mussels steamed in white wine, shallots, garlic and parsley, served with crusty bread for the broth.","2 lb|mussels|scrubbed and debearded;2 tbsp|butter;2|shallot|finely chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|white wine|dry;1|bay leaves;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1|french bread|baguette, sliced and toasted;|black pepper|to taste","Discard any mussels that stay open when tapped. Rinse the rest under cold water.|Melt the butter in a large pot with a lid over medium heat and cook the shallots 3 minutes. Add the garlic for 30 seconds.|Pour in the wine, add the bay leaf and boil 2 minutes.|Add the mussels, cover and steam over high heat for 5 to 7 minutes, shaking the pot, until the shells open.|Discard any mussels that did not open. Stir in the cream and parsley and season with pepper.|Ladle into bowls with the broth and serve with toasted baguette.","French"],
[3514,"Blanquette de Veau","comfort","🍲",150,"Medium",9,6,"Tender veal poached with vegetables and finished with a lemony cream and egg yolk sauce.","2 lb|veal|shoulder, cut into 2 inch pieces;1|onion|halved and studded with 2 whole cloves;2|carrots|cut into chunks;1|leek|white part, halved;1|bay leaves;3 sprig|fresh thyme;4 cup|chicken broth;8 oz|mushrooms|quartered;8 oz|pearl onions|peeled;4 tbsp|butter|divided;1/4 cup|flour;2|eggs|yolks only;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 1/2 cup|rice|to serve;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Place the veal in a Dutch oven, cover with the broth and bring to a gentle simmer, skimming the foam for the first 10 minutes.|Add the studded onion, carrots, leek, bay leaf, thyme and 1 teaspoon salt. Simmer partly covered for 1 hour 15 minutes until the veal is tender.|Meanwhile, simmer the pearl onions in a little water for 8 minutes and saute the mushrooms in 1 tablespoon butter for 6 minutes.|Strain the veal and keep warm, reserving 3 cups of the broth. Discard the vegetables and herbs.|Melt 3 tablespoons butter, whisk in the flour for 2 minutes, then whisk in the reserved broth and simmer 10 minutes until thickened.|Whisk the yolks with the cream, temper with a ladle of hot sauce and stir back in off the heat with the lemon juice and nutmeg.|Return the veal, mushrooms and onions to the sauce and warm gently without boiling. Serve over rice.","French"],
[3515,"Chocolate Mousse","treats","🍫",210,"Medium",9,6,"A light, airy dark chocolate mousse made the classic French way with whipped egg whites.","6 oz|dark chocolate|chopped;3 tbsp|butter;3|eggs|separated;2 tbsp|sugar;3/4 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|vanilla;1 pinch|salt","Melt the chocolate and butter together in a heatproof bowl set over barely simmering water, stirring until smooth. Cool 5 minutes.|Stir the egg yolks into the chocolate one at a time and add the vanilla.|Whip the cream to soft peaks and set aside in the fridge.|Beat the egg whites with the salt until foamy, then add the sugar gradually and beat to stiff glossy peaks.|Fold a third of the whites into the chocolate to lighten it, then fold in the rest gently, followed by the whipped cream.|Spoon into 6 glasses and chill at least 3 hours until set.","French"],
[3516,"Cherry Clafoutis","treats","🍒",60,"Easy",9,6,"A rustic French baked custard studded with sweet cherries, puffed and golden.","1 lb|cherries|pitted;3|eggs;1/3 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|flour;1 1/4 cup|milk;1 tsp|vanilla;1 pinch|salt;1 tbsp|butter|for the dish;1 tbsp|powdered sugar|for dusting","Heat the oven to 375°F and butter a 9 inch baking dish or deep pie plate.|Spread the cherries in the dish.|Whisk the eggs and sugar until pale, then whisk in the flour and salt until smooth.|Whisk in the milk and vanilla to make a thin batter.|Pour the batter over the cherries.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until puffed, golden and just set. Cool 10 minutes, dust with powdered sugar and serve warm.","French"],
[3517,"Albondigas en Salsa","comfort","🧆",60,"Medium",9,4,"Tender Spanish meatballs simmered in a garlicky tomato and white wine sauce with peas.","1/2 lb|ground beef;1/2 lb|ground pork;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;1/4 cup|milk;1|eggs;2 clove|garlic|minced, for the meatballs;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|paprika;1/4 cup|flour|for dredging;3 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|finely chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced, for the sauce;1/2 cup|white wine;1 can|crushed tomatoes|14 oz;1 cup|chicken broth;1|bay leaves;1/2 cup|frozen peas;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes, then mix with the beef, pork, egg, 2 cloves garlic, parsley, paprika, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper.|Roll into 24 small meatballs and dredge lightly in the flour.|Brown the meatballs in the olive oil in a wide skillet over medium-high heat for 5 to 6 minutes, then remove.|In the same pan, cook the onion for 6 minutes, add the 3 cloves garlic for 1 minute, then pour in the wine and boil 2 minutes.|Add the tomatoes, broth and bay leaf. Return the meatballs and simmer covered for 20 minutes.|Add the peas for the last 5 minutes. Adjust seasoning and serve with crusty bread or rice.","Spanish"],
[3518,"Pollo al Ajillo","comfort","🍗",50,"Easy",9,4,"Spanish garlic chicken, pan-browned and simmered with white wine, thyme and lots of golden garlic.","2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skin-on;16 clove|garlic|peeled and lightly smashed;1/4 cup|olive oil;1/2 cup|white wine|dry white or dry sherry;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 sprig|fresh thyme;1|bay leaves;1 tsp|paprika;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Pat the chicken dry and season well with salt, pepper and the paprika.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and brown the chicken skin side down for 6 to 8 minutes, then flip and brown 3 minutes. Remove.|Lower the heat to medium and add the garlic to the pan. Cook 3 to 4 minutes until golden but not burnt.|Pour in the wine and let it bubble 2 minutes, scraping up the browned bits.|Return the chicken, add the broth, thyme and bay leaf. Cover and simmer over low heat for 25 minutes until cooked through.|Finish with the lemon juice and parsley and serve with the garlic and pan juices.","Spanish"],
[3519,"Bacalhau à Brás","comfort","🍳",45,"Medium",9,4,"Shredded salt cod scrambled with crispy matchstick potatoes, onions and eggs, a Lisbon favorite.","1 lb|salt cod|soaked in cold water 24 to 36 hours, changing the water often;1 lb|potatoes|cut into thin matchsticks;2 cup|vegetable oil|for frying the potatoes;1/4 cup|olive oil;1|onion|thinly sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;6|eggs|beaten;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;12|olives|black, to garnish;|black pepper|to taste","After soaking, simmer the cod in fresh water for 10 minutes. Drain, remove the skin and bones and shred into small flakes.|Dry the potato matchsticks well. Fry in the vegetable oil at 350°F in batches for 3 to 4 minutes until crisp and golden. Drain on paper towels.|Heat the olive oil in a large skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 8 minutes until soft. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the cod and cook 3 minutes, stirring.|Fold in most of the fried potatoes, pour in the beaten eggs and stir gently over low heat for 2 to 3 minutes until just creamy and barely set.|Season with pepper, scatter the parsley, olives and remaining potatoes on top and serve immediately.","Portuguese"],
[3520,"Caldo Verde","soup","🍲",50,"Easy",9.5,6,"Portugal's beloved green soup of silky potato, shredded kale and smoky chorizo.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 lb|potatoes|peeled and cubed;6 cup|chicken broth;8 oz|chorizo|sliced thin;1 bunch|kale|stems removed, very thinly sliced;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion 5 minutes. Add the garlic for 1 minute.|Add the potatoes and broth and bring to a boil. Simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes are very soft.|Meanwhile, brown the chorizo slices in a dry skillet for 4 minutes until crisp at the edges and drain on paper towels.|Mash or puree the soup with an immersion blender until smooth and creamy.|Stir in the kale and simmer 5 to 8 minutes until tender but still bright green.|Season with salt and pepper and serve topped with the chorizo and a drizzle of olive oil.","Portuguese"],
[3521,"Salmorejo","soup","🍅",150,"Easy",9.5,4,"A thick, chilled Cordoba tomato and bread soup, topped with hard-boiled egg and serrano ham.","2 lb|tomatoes|ripe, quartered;4 oz|french bread|day-old, crust removed, torn;1 clove|garlic;1/2 cup|olive oil;2 tbsp|sherry vinegar;1 tsp|salt;2|eggs|hard-boiled and chopped;2 oz|serrano ham|diced","Blend the tomatoes until very smooth and push through a sieve to remove the skins and seeds.|Return the tomato puree to the blender and add the bread. Let it soak for 10 minutes.|Add the garlic, vinegar and salt and blend until smooth.|With the blender running, slowly drizzle in the olive oil until the soup is thick and creamy.|Chill at least 2 hours until very cold.|Serve in small bowls topped with chopped egg, serrano ham and a drizzle of olive oil.","Spanish"],
[3522,"Fabada Asturiana","comfort","🫘",180,"Medium",9,6,"A rich Asturian stew of white beans slow-cooked with chorizo, morcilla and pork belly.","1 lb|dried white beans|soaked overnight and drained;8 oz|chorizo|Spanish cured, whole;8 oz|morcilla|Spanish blood sausage, optional;6 oz|bacon|slab or pancetta, in one piece;1|onion|halved;3 clove|garlic|peeled;1 tsp|paprika|smoked;1 pinch|saffron|threads;2|bay leaves;1 tbsp|olive oil;|salt|to taste","Place the soaked beans in a large heavy pot with the onion, garlic, bay leaves, bacon and olive oil. Cover with 2 inches of cold water.|Bring slowly to a boil, skim off the foam and reduce to a bare simmer. Add a splash of cold water twice during cooking to keep the beans tender.|After 1 hour, add the chorizo, morcilla, paprika and saffron.|Simmer gently for 1 more hour, shaking the pot occasionally instead of stirring so the beans stay whole.|Season with salt in the last 15 minutes. The stew should be thick and creamy.|Remove the meats, slice and return to the pot. Rest 10 minutes before serving.","Spanish"],
[3523,"Bacalhau com Natas","comfort","🐟",70,"Medium",9,6,"A creamy baked casserole of salt cod, potatoes and onions in a nutmeg-scented cream sauce.","1 1/2 lb|salt cod|soaked in cold water 24 to 36 hours, changing the water often;1 1/2 lb|potatoes|peeled and thinly sliced;2|onion|thinly sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|olive oil;3 tbsp|butter;1/4 cup|flour;2 cup|milk;1 cup|heavy cream;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|black pepper|to taste","After soaking, simmer the cod in fresh water for 10 minutes. Drain, remove the skin and bones and flake it.|Boil the potato slices in unsalted water for 8 minutes until just tender and drain.|Cook the onions in the olive oil over medium heat for 12 minutes until soft and golden, adding the garlic for the last minute.|Melt the butter in a saucepan, whisk in the flour for 1 minute, then add the milk and cream and simmer 6 minutes until thick. Add the nutmeg and pepper.|Layer half the potatoes, the cod, the onions and the remaining potatoes in a buttered 9 by 13 inch dish and pour the sauce over.|Top with the parmesan and bake at 400°F for 20 minutes until bubbling and golden. Sprinkle with parsley.","Portuguese"],
[3524,"Wiener Schnitzel","comfort","🍖",30,"Medium",9,4,"Thin breaded veal cutlets, fried until golden and served with lemon wedges.","1 1/2 lb|veal cutlets|4 cutlets, pounded 1/4 inch thin;1 cup|flour;3|eggs|beaten;1 1/2 cup|breadcrumbs|fine, plain;1 cup|vegetable oil|for shallow frying;4 tbsp|butter;1|lemon|cut into wedges;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Pound the cutlets between plastic wrap to an even 1/4 inch thickness and season both sides with salt and pepper.|Set up three shallow dishes with the flour, the beaten eggs and the breadcrumbs.|Dredge each cutlet in the flour and shake off the excess, dip in the egg, then press into the breadcrumbs. Do not press too hard.|Heat the oil and butter in a large skillet over medium-high heat to 350°F so the crumbs sizzle right away.|Fry the cutlets 2 to 3 minutes per side, swirling the pan so the coating puffs, until deep golden.|Drain on a rack, scatter with parsley and serve right away with lemon wedges. Pork cutlets work equally well.","German"],
[3525,"Bratwurst with Sauerkraut","comfort","🌭",40,"Easy",9,4,"Browned bratwurst simmered in beer with sauerkraut, apple and onion, served with boiled potatoes.","6|bratwurst;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|sliced;1|apple|peeled and sliced;1 lb|sauerkraut|drained;1/2 cup|beer|lager;1 tsp|caraway seeds;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 lb|baby potatoes|halved;2 tbsp|mustard|spicy brown, to serve","Brown the bratwurst in the oil in a large deep skillet over medium heat for 8 minutes, turning, then remove.|Add the onion to the pan and cook 5 minutes. Add the apple, sauerkraut, caraway, brown sugar and beer.|Return the sausages to the pan, cover and simmer over low heat for 20 minutes until cooked through to 160°F.|Meanwhile, boil the potatoes in salted water for 15 minutes until tender and drain.|Serve the sausages over a bed of sauerkraut with the potatoes and mustard.","German"],
[3526,"Swedish Meatballs","comfort","🧆",50,"Medium",9,6,"Small, tender spiced meatballs in a creamy gravy, served with mashed potatoes and lingonberry jam.","1 lb|ground beef;1/2 lb|ground pork;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|milk;1|onion|finely grated;1|eggs;1/2 tsp|allspice;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;1 tsp|salt;2 tbsp|butter|for frying;3 tbsp|butter|for the gravy;1/4 cup|flour;2 cup|beef broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tsp|soy sauce;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1/4 cup|lingonberry jam|to serve;|black pepper|to taste","Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes, then mix with the beef, pork, onion, egg, allspice, nutmeg, salt and pepper.|Chill 15 minutes, then roll into 1 inch meatballs.|Brown the meatballs in batches in 2 tablespoons butter over medium heat for 6 to 8 minutes, rolling to keep them round. Transfer to a plate.|In the same pan melt the 3 tablespoons butter, whisk in the flour and cook 1 minute.|Whisk in the broth, soy sauce and mustard and simmer 5 minutes until thickened. Stir in the cream.|Return the meatballs and simmer 10 minutes until cooked through. Serve with mashed potatoes and lingonberry jam.","Scandinavian"],
[3527,"Gravlax","light","🐟",2880,"Easy",7.5,8,"Salmon cured for two days in salt, sugar and dill, sliced thin and served with mustard-dill sauce.","1 1/2 lb|salmon|skin-on center-cut fillet, very fresh;1/4 cup|coarse salt;1/4 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|black pepper|coarsely crushed;1 bunch|dill|roughly chopped;2 tbsp|aquavit|or vodka, optional;3 tbsp|dijon mustard;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1/4 cup|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|dill|finely chopped, for the sauce","Run your fingers over the salmon and pull out any pin bones. Place skin side down on a large sheet of plastic wrap.|Mix the salt, sugar and pepper and rub it over the flesh. Sprinkle with the aquavit and cover with the dill.|Wrap tightly, set in a baking dish and put a small board and a can or two on top for light weight.|Refrigerate for 48 hours, flipping the package every 12 hours and spooning off the liquid that collects.|Unwrap, scrape off the dill and most of the cure, and pat dry.|For the sauce, whisk the mustard, honey, vinegar and 1/2 teaspoon salt, then slowly whisk in the oil and fold in the chopped dill.|Slice thinly on the diagonal away from the skin and serve with the sauce on dark bread or crispbread.","Scandinavian"],
[3528,"Rouladen","comfort","🥩",150,"Medium",9,4,"Thin beef slices rolled around bacon, pickle, onion and mustard, then braised in a rich gravy.","2 lb|top round|8 thin slices, pounded thin;8 slice|bacon;3 tbsp|mustard|German or dijon;1|onion|thinly sliced;4|pickles|dill, quartered lengthwise;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|carrots|diced;1 stalk|celery|diced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1/2 cup|red wine;2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|cornstarch;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Lay the beef slices flat, season with salt and pepper and spread each with mustard.|Top each with a slice of bacon, some onion and a pickle spear. Roll up tightly from the short end and tie with kitchen twine or secure with toothpicks.|Brown the rolls in the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat for 8 minutes, turning, then remove.|Cook the carrot, celery and any leftover onion in the pot for 5 minutes. Stir in the tomato paste, then add the wine and boil 2 minutes.|Add the broth and return the rolls. Cover and simmer over low heat for 1 hour 30 minutes until fork tender.|Remove the rolls. Stir the cornstarch with 2 tablespoons water, add to the sauce and simmer 3 minutes. Strain if desired and serve with potatoes or red cabbage.","German"],
[3529,"Käsespätzle","comfort","🧀",45,"Medium",9,4,"Tender egg noodle dumplings layered with melted Gruyere and topped with crispy fried onions.","2 cup|flour;4|eggs;1/2 cup|milk;1/2 tsp|salt|plus more for the water;1/4 tsp|nutmeg;2 cup|gruyere|shredded;3 tbsp|butter;2|onion|thinly sliced;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;|black pepper|to taste","Whisk the flour, eggs, milk, salt and nutmeg into a thick, smooth, stretchy batter and rest 10 minutes.|Cook the onions in 2 tablespoons butter over medium-low heat for 20 minutes until deeply golden and crisp at the edges. Set aside.|Bring a large pot of well-salted water to a boil. Press the batter through a spaetzle maker or a large-holed colander directly into the water in batches.|Cook each batch 2 to 3 minutes until the spaetzle float, then lift out with a slotted spoon.|Toss the hot spaetzle in the remaining butter and layer in an ovenproof dish with the Gruyere.|Bake at 400°F for 8 to 10 minutes until the cheese is melted and bubbling. Top with onions, chives and pepper.","German"],
[3530,"German Potato Salad","sides","🥔",45,"Easy",7.5,6,"Warm southern German potato salad in a tangy bacon, mustard and vinegar dressing.","2 lb|potatoes|waxy, such as Yukon Gold;6 slice|bacon|chopped;1|onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|beef broth|hot;1/4 cup|white wine vinegar;1 tbsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|sugar;2 tbsp|chives|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Boil the whole potatoes in salted water for 20 to 25 minutes until just tender. Drain and cool 10 minutes, then peel and slice 1/4 inch thick.|Cook the bacon in a large skillet over medium heat for 8 minutes until crisp. Remove, leaving 2 tablespoons fat in the pan.|Cook the onion in the bacon fat for 4 minutes until soft.|Whisk in the broth, vinegar, mustard and sugar and simmer 2 minutes.|Pour the warm dressing over the potatoes, add the bacon and fold gently so the slices stay intact.|Season with salt and pepper, sprinkle with chives and serve warm.","German"],
[3531,"Apple Strudel","baking","🍎",90,"Medium",8.5,8,"Flaky layers of pastry wrapped around cinnamon-spiced apples, raisins and toasted crumbs.","2 lb|apple|tart apples, peeled and thinly sliced;1/2 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|raisins;1/2 cup|walnuts|chopped;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;8 tbsp|butter|melted, divided;10 oz|phyllo dough|thawed;2 tbsp|powdered sugar|for dusting","Toast the breadcrumbs in 2 tablespoons butter in a skillet for 3 to 4 minutes until golden and set aside.|Toss the apples with the sugar, raisins, walnuts, cinnamon and lemon juice.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Lay a sheet of phyllo on a clean towel, brush with butter and repeat until you have 8 layers.|Sprinkle the toasted crumbs over the lower third of the phyllo, spoon the apple mixture on top and fold in the sides.|Roll up tightly using the towel to help, finishing seam side down on a lined baking sheet.|Brush with butter, cut a few steam slits and bake 35 to 40 minutes until deep golden. Cool 15 minutes and dust with powdered sugar.","German"],
[3532,"Chicken Tagine with Preserved Lemon and Olives","comfort","🍗",90,"Easy",9,4,"Chicken braised with ginger, turmeric and saffron, finished with briny olives and preserved lemon.","2 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in, skin-on;2 tbsp|olive oil;2|onion|thinly sliced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|ginger|ground;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1 pinch|saffron|crumbled;1 1/2 cup|chicken broth;1|preserved lemon|rind rinsed and sliced, or zest of 2 lemons;1/2 cup|olives|green, pitted;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the ginger, turmeric, cumin, paprika, cinnamon, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper and rub half into the chicken. Marinate 20 minutes.|Brown the chicken in the olive oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat for 4 minutes per side, then remove.|Cook the onions in the pot for 8 minutes, add the garlic and remaining spice mix and cook 1 minute.|Add the broth, saffron and half the herbs and return the chicken.|Cover and simmer over low heat for 40 minutes until tender, then uncover and add the olives and preserved lemon.|Simmer uncovered for 10 minutes until the sauce thickens. Sprinkle with the remaining herbs and serve with couscous or bread.","Moroccan"],
[3533,"Seven-Vegetable Couscous","comfort","🥘",90,"Medium",9,6,"A Moroccan Friday feast of fluffy couscous topped with a spiced vegetable and chickpea stew.","2 tbsp|olive oil;2|onion|cut into wedges;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|ginger|ground;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|black pepper;6 cup|vegetable broth;3|carrots|cut into chunks;2|turnip|peeled and quartered;1/2 head|cabbage|cut into wedges;2 cup|butternut squash|cubed;2|zucchini|cut into chunks;2|tomatoes|chopped;1 can|chickpeas|15 oz, drained;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;2 cup|couscous;2 tbsp|butter;1 tbsp|harissa|to serve;|salt|to taste","Cook the onions in the olive oil in a large pot for 6 minutes, then add the garlic, tomato paste and all the spices and stir 1 minute.|Add 5 cups of the broth, the carrots and turnips and simmer, covered, for 15 minutes.|Add the cabbage, squash and tomatoes and simmer 15 minutes more.|Add the zucchini and chickpeas and cook 10 minutes until all the vegetables are tender. Season with salt and stir in the cilantro.|Meanwhile, bring 2 cups water and the remaining cup of broth to a boil, pour over the couscous with 1 teaspoon salt and the butter, cover and rest 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork.|Mound the couscous on a large platter, top with the vegetables and ladle on the broth. Serve harissa on the side.","Moroccan"],
[3534,"Harira","soup","🥣",90,"Medium",9.5,6,"Moroccan tomato soup with lentils, chickpeas and spiced beef, traditionally eaten to break the Ramadan fast.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|finely chopped;2 stalk|celery|finely chopped;8 oz|beef stew meat|cut into small cubes;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|ginger|ground;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 pinch|saffron|crumbled;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;6 cup|beef broth;1/2 cup|lentils|brown or green;1 can|chickpeas|15 oz, drained;1/2 cup|vermicelli|broken;2 tbsp|flour;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1|lemon|juice only;|salt|to taste","Cook the onion, celery and beef in the olive oil in a large pot for 8 minutes until the beef loses its pink color.|Stir in the turmeric, ginger, cinnamon, pepper, saffron and tomato paste for 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes and broth, bring to a boil and simmer, covered, for 30 minutes.|Add the lentils and chickpeas and cook 20 minutes until the lentils and beef are tender.|Whisk the flour with 1/2 cup cold water until smooth and stir it in, along with the vermicelli. Simmer 8 minutes until thickened.|Stir in the herbs and lemon juice, season with salt and serve with dates and lemon wedges.","Moroccan"],
[3535,"Chicken B'stilla","comfort","🥧",150,"Medium",9,8,"A sweet and savory Moroccan pie of spiced shredded chicken, eggs and almonds in crisp phyllo, dusted with cinnamon.","1 1/2 lb|chicken thighs|bone-in;2|onion|finely chopped;1 tsp|ginger|ground;1 tsp|turmeric;1 tsp|cinnamon|plus more for dusting;1 pinch|saffron|crumbled;2 cup|chicken broth;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;3|eggs|beaten;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 cup|almonds|toasted and coarsely chopped;3 tbsp|powdered sugar|plus more for dusting;10 oz|phyllo dough|thawed;8 tbsp|butter|melted;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Combine the chicken, onions, ginger, turmeric, 1 teaspoon cinnamon, saffron, broth, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper in a pot. Cover and simmer 40 minutes until the chicken is very tender.|Remove the chicken, shred the meat and discard the bones. Boil the sauce uncovered for 15 minutes until reduced to about 1 cup.|Lower the heat and stir in the eggs, stirring constantly for 2 minutes until they form soft curds. Add the herbs and lemon juice, then mix in the shredded chicken and cool.|Mix the almonds with the 3 tablespoons powdered sugar and 1/2 teaspoon cinnamon.|Heat the oven to 375°F. Brush a 10 inch springform or cake pan with butter and layer 6 sheets of phyllo, brushing each and letting the edges overhang.|Spread half the almond mixture, then the chicken mixture, then the remaining almonds. Fold over the overhang and cover with 3 more buttered sheets, tucking in the edges.|Bake 30 to 35 minutes until deep golden. Invert onto a plate and dust with powdered sugar and a lattice of cinnamon.","Moroccan"],
[3536,"Zaalouk","sides","🍆",45,"Easy",7.5,6,"A warm Moroccan salad of roasted eggplant and tomato cooked down with garlic, cumin and paprika.","2 lb|eggplant|cut into 1 inch cubes;4|tomatoes|ripe, chopped;4 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|olive oil|divided;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste","Toss the eggplant with 2 tablespoons olive oil and 1 teaspoon salt and roast on a baking sheet at 425°F for 25 minutes until soft and golden.|Heat the remaining olive oil in a wide skillet over medium heat and cook the garlic for 30 seconds.|Add the tomatoes, cumin, paprika and cayenne and simmer for 12 minutes until jammy.|Add the roasted eggplant and mash roughly with a fork.|Cook 10 minutes, stirring often, until thick and spreadable.|Stir in the herbs and lemon juice, adjust the salt and serve warm or at room temperature with bread.","Moroccan"],
[3537,"Kefta Tagine with Eggs","comfort","🧆",50,"Easy",9,4,"Spiced beef meatballs simmered in a cumin-scented tomato sauce with eggs poached on top.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|grated, for the meatballs;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;2 tsp|cumin|divided;2 tsp|paprika|divided;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 tsp|cayenne;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|finely chopped, for the sauce;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 cup|chicken broth;4|eggs;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the beef, grated onion, parsley, cilantro, 1 teaspoon cumin, 1 teaspoon paprika, cinnamon, cayenne, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper. Roll into 20 small meatballs.|Heat the olive oil in a wide shallow pan over medium heat and cook the chopped onion 6 minutes. Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, broth, turmeric, and remaining cumin and paprika. Simmer 10 minutes.|Nestle the meatballs into the sauce, cover and simmer for 15 minutes until cooked through.|Make 4 wells in the sauce and crack an egg into each. Cover and cook 4 to 6 minutes until the whites are set.|Season with salt and pepper and serve straight from the pan with crusty bread.","Moroccan"],
[3538,"Moroccan Vegetable Tagine","comfort","🥘",60,"Easy",9,4,"Sweet potatoes, carrots and chickpeas simmered with dried apricots and warm spices.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|cinnamon;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|turmeric;1/2 tsp|ginger|ground;1|sweet potatoes|large, peeled and cubed;2|carrots|sliced;1|zucchini|cut into chunks;1 can|chickpeas|15 oz, drained;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;1/2 cup|dried apricots|halved;1 1/2 cup|vegetable broth;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/4 cup|almonds|toasted slivered;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cook the onion in the olive oil in a large Dutch oven over medium heat for 6 minutes. Add the garlic and all the spices and stir 1 minute.|Add the sweet potato and carrots, then the tomatoes, broth, apricots and 1 teaspoon salt.|Bring to a boil, reduce the heat, cover and simmer 20 minutes.|Add the zucchini and chickpeas and simmer uncovered 12 to 15 minutes until the vegetables are tender and the sauce is thick.|Season with salt and pepper, then stir in half the cilantro.|Serve over couscous topped with almonds and the remaining cilantro.","Moroccan"],
[3539,"Baked Fish with Chermoula","light","🐟",55,"Easy",7.5,4,"White fish baked on potatoes and tomatoes under a bright cilantro, garlic and cumin chermoula.","1 1/2 lb|cod|4 fillets;1/2 cup|cilantro|packed;1/2 cup|parsley|packed;4 clove|garlic;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/4 tsp|cayenne;1/3 cup|olive oil;2|lemon|juice of 1 and the other cut into wedges;1 lb|potatoes|thinly sliced;2|tomatoes|sliced;1|bell pepper|thinly sliced;|salt|to taste","Blend the cilantro, parsley, garlic, cumin, paprika, cayenne, olive oil, juice of 1 lemon and 3/4 teaspoon salt into a loose chermoula.|Toss the sliced potatoes with a third of the chermoula and 1/2 teaspoon salt and spread in a baking dish. Bake at 425°F for 15 minutes.|Layer on the bell pepper and tomatoes and bake 10 more minutes.|Season the fish with salt and coat in half of the remaining chermoula.|Nestle the fish over the vegetables and bake 12 to 15 minutes until the fish flakes easily.|Spoon the last of the chermoula over the top and serve with lemon wedges.","Moroccan"],
[3540,"Msemen","breakfast","🫓",90,"Medium",8.5,8,"Flaky, layered Moroccan flatbreads cooked on a griddle and served with honey and butter.","3 cup|flour;1/2 cup|semolina;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|sugar;1 tsp|yeast|instant;1 1/4 cup|warm water;1/2 cup|vegetable oil|for shaping;4 tbsp|butter|melted;|honey|to serve","Mix the flour, semolina, salt, sugar and yeast, add the warm water and knead 10 minutes into a soft, smooth dough.|Divide into 8 balls, coat with oil and rest covered for 20 minutes.|Oil your work surface and hands, then stretch one ball into a very thin large square as thin as you can without tearing.|Brush with melted butter and fold into thirds, brush again and fold into a square packet. Repeat with the rest and let them rest 10 minutes.|Flatten each square gently to about 5 inches. Heat a skillet or griddle over medium heat.|Cook 2 to 3 minutes per side until golden brown and flaky. Serve warm with honey and butter.","Moroccan"],
[3541,"Breakfast Sausage Casserole","breakfast","🍳",75,"Easy",8.5,8,"Cubed bread, browned sausage, cheddar and a savory egg custard baked into a make-ahead brunch crowd pleaser.","1 lb|breakfast sausage;6 slice|bread|cubed;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;6|eggs;2 cup|milk;1/2 tsp|dry mustard;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|butter|for the dish","Butter a 9x13 inch baking dish and heat the oven to 350°F when you are ready to bake.|Brown the sausage in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 8 to 10 minutes, breaking it up, then drain well.|Spread the bread cubes in the dish and scatter the sausage and 1 1/2 cups of the cheddar over the top.|Whisk the eggs, milk, dry mustard, salt and pepper until smooth and pour evenly over the bread.|Cover and refrigerate for at least 30 minutes or overnight so the bread soaks up the custard.|Sprinkle with the remaining cheddar and bake uncovered for 45 to 50 minutes until puffed, golden and set in the center.|Rest 10 minutes before cutting into squares.","American"],
[3542,"Baked French Toast Casserole","breakfast","🍞",80,"Easy",8.5,8,"Cinnamon custard-soaked bread under a buttery brown sugar streusel, assembled the night before.","12 oz|french bread|cubed;6|eggs;1 1/2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/3 cup|sugar;2 tsp|vanilla extract;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/4 tsp|salt;1/2 cup|brown sugar;1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|cinnamon|for the topping;1/2 cup|butter|cold, cubed;1/2 cup|pecans|chopped, optional;|maple syrup|for serving","Grease a 9x13 inch baking dish and spread the bread cubes in it.|Whisk the eggs, milk, cream, sugar, vanilla, 1 teaspoon cinnamon and the salt until the sugar dissolves, then pour over the bread.|Press the bread down so it soaks up the custard, cover and refrigerate at least 1 hour or overnight.|Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix the brown sugar, flour and 1 teaspoon cinnamon, then cut in the cold butter with your fingers until crumbly and stir in the pecans.|Scatter the streusel evenly over the bread and bake for 45 to 50 minutes until golden and the center is set.|Rest 10 minutes and serve warm with maple syrup.","American"],
[3543,"Eggs Benedict","breakfast","🍳",30,"Medium",8.5,2,"Poached eggs and Canadian bacon on toasted English muffins under silky homemade hollandaise.","2|english muffins|split;4 slice|canadian bacon;4|eggs;1 tbsp|white vinegar;3|eggs|yolks only, for the hollandaise;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1/2 cup|butter|melted and warm;1 pinch|cayenne;1/4 tsp|salt;1 tbsp|chives|chopped","Make the hollandaise first. Whisk the 3 yolks, lemon juice and 1 tablespoon water in a heatproof bowl set over a pan of barely simmering water for 3 to 4 minutes until thick and pale.|Remove from the heat and slowly drizzle in the warm melted butter while whisking constantly until the sauce is smooth, then season with salt and cayenne. Keep warm.|Bring a wide pan of water to a gentle simmer and add the vinegar.|Swirl the water, crack each egg into a cup and slide it in. Poach 3 to 4 minutes until the whites are set and the yolks are still runny, then lift out with a slotted spoon.|Toast the English muffins and warm the Canadian bacon in a skillet for 1 minute per side.|Stack bacon on each muffin half, top with a poached egg, spoon over the hollandaise and finish with chives.","American"],
[3544,"Avocado Toast with Poached Egg","breakfast","🥑",15,"Easy",8.5,2,"Crusty toast piled with lemony smashed avocado, a runny poached egg and chili flakes.","2 slice|sourdough bread|thick cut;1|avocado|ripe;1 tbsp|lemon juice;2|eggs;1 tsp|white vinegar;1 tbsp|olive oil;1/2 tsp|red pepper flakes;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring a small pan of water to a gentle simmer and stir in the vinegar.|Mash the avocado with the lemon juice, a pinch of salt and pepper, leaving it a little chunky.|Toast the bread until deeply golden and brush with the olive oil.|Crack each egg into a cup, stir the water into a gentle whirlpool and slide the eggs in. Poach 3 minutes for a runny yolk and lift out with a slotted spoon.|Spread the avocado on the toast, top with the eggs, and finish with red pepper flakes, salt and pepper.","American"],
[3545,"Homemade Granola","breakfast","🥣",45,"Very easy",8.5,10,"Big crunchy clusters of oats, nuts and maple, baked low and slow with dried cranberries stirred in.","3 cup|rolled oats;1 cup|pecans|chopped;1/3 cup|maple syrup;1/3 cup|coconut oil|melted;1/4 cup|brown sugar;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|vanilla extract;1/2 cup|dried cranberries","Heat the oven to 325°F and line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment.|Stir the oats, pecans, cinnamon and salt together in a large bowl.|Whisk the maple syrup, melted coconut oil, brown sugar and vanilla, pour over the oat mixture and toss until evenly coated.|Spread in an even layer and press down firmly so it clumps.|Bake 25 to 30 minutes, stirring once halfway, until golden brown.|Let it cool completely on the pan without stirring so it crisps into clusters, then break apart and mix in the cranberries.","American"],
[3546,"Buttermilk Waffles","breakfast","🧇",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crisp-edged, fluffy waffles from a simple buttermilk batter, ready for butter and syrup.","2 cup|flour;2 tbsp|sugar;2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|salt;2|eggs;1 3/4 cup|buttermilk;6 tbsp|butter|melted;1 tsp|vanilla extract;|maple syrup|for serving","Heat a waffle iron and the oven to 200°F to keep finished waffles warm.|Whisk the flour, sugar, baking powder, baking soda and salt in a large bowl.|In another bowl whisk the eggs, buttermilk, melted butter and vanilla.|Pour the wet ingredients into the dry and stir just until combined, leaving a few small lumps.|Let the batter rest 5 minutes, then grease the iron and pour in enough batter to fill it.|Cook 3 to 5 minutes until golden and steam slows, and keep the waffles on a rack in the oven while you finish the batter.","American"],
[3547,"Crispy Hash Browns","breakfast","🥔",35,"Easy",8.5,4,"Diner-style shredded potato patties, squeezed dry so they fry up shatteringly crisp outside and tender inside.","2 lb|potatoes|russet, peeled;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;2 tbsp|butter","Shred the potatoes on the large holes of a box grater and rinse them in a bowl of cold water, swishing to remove the starch.|Drain, then wring the potatoes out in a clean kitchen towel until very dry.|Toss with the salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Heat half the oil and half the butter in a large nonstick or cast-iron skillet over medium-high heat.|Press half the potatoes into the pan in a thin even layer and cook undisturbed 5 to 6 minutes until deep golden underneath.|Flip in sections and cook another 4 to 5 minutes, then drain on paper towels and repeat with the remaining oil, butter and potatoes.","American"],
[3548,"Sausage and Cheddar Frittata","breakfast","🍳",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"A skillet frittata with browned sausage, onion and sharp cheddar, finished in the oven.","8 oz|breakfast sausage;1/2|onion|diced;8|eggs;1/4 cup|milk;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;2|green onion|sliced;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Brown the sausage with the onion in a 10 inch oven-safe skillet over medium-high heat for 6 to 8 minutes, breaking up the meat.|Whisk the eggs, milk, salt and pepper until smooth and stir in 3/4 cup of the cheddar.|Pour the eggs over the sausage and cook on the stovetop without stirring for 2 to 3 minutes until the edges begin to set.|Sprinkle with the remaining cheese and transfer to the oven.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until puffed and set in the center, then scatter with green onion and rest 5 minutes before slicing.","American"],
[3549,"Berry Smoothie Bowl","breakfast","🍓",10,"Very easy",8.5,2,"A thick frozen berry and banana smoothie in a bowl, topped with granola, fresh fruit and chia seeds.","2 cup|frozen mixed berries;1|banana|frozen, sliced;1/2 cup|greek yogurt;1/4 cup|milk;1/4 cup|granola;1/2 cup|blueberries;1 tbsp|chia seeds;1 tbsp|honey","Add the frozen berries, frozen banana, yogurt and milk to a blender.|Blend on high, scraping down the sides and adding milk a tablespoon at a time only if needed, until thick and spoonable like soft serve.|Divide between two bowls and smooth the tops.|Top with the granola, fresh blueberries, chia seeds and a drizzle of honey and eat right away.","American"],
[3550,"Bacon, Egg and Cheese Bagel","breakfast","🥯",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Toasted bagels stacked with crisp oven bacon, a soft fried egg and melted cheddar.","4|bagels|split;8 slice|bacon;4|eggs;4 slice|cheddar;1 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 400°F and lay the bacon on a rack set over a lined baking sheet.|Bake 15 to 20 minutes until crisp and drain on paper towels.|Toast the bagels until golden and butter them lightly.|Melt the butter in a nonstick skillet over medium heat, crack in the eggs and cook 2 to 3 minutes, flipping once, until the whites are set and the yolks are just firm. Season with salt and pepper.|Lay a slice of cheddar over each hot egg for the last 30 seconds so it melts.|Build each sandwich with an egg, 2 slices of bacon and the bagel top and serve warm.","American"],
[3551,"Denver Omelet","breakfast","🍳",20,"Easy",8.5,2,"A diner favorite folded around diced ham, bell pepper, onion and melted cheddar.","6|eggs;2 tbsp|milk;4 oz|ham|diced;1/2|green bell pepper|diced;1/2|onion|diced;1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt 1 teaspoon of the butter in a nonstick skillet over medium heat and cook the pepper and onion 4 to 5 minutes until soft.|Add the ham and cook 1 minute more, then scoop the filling into a bowl.|Whisk the eggs with the milk, salt and pepper.|Melt half the remaining butter in the skillet, pour in half the eggs and let them set for 30 seconds, then pull the cooked edges toward the center, tilting the pan so runny egg fills the gaps.|When the top is nearly set, scatter half the filling and cheese over one side, fold the omelet over and slide onto a plate.|Repeat with the remaining butter, eggs and filling to make the second omelet.","American"],
[3552,"Dutch Baby Pancake","breakfast","🥞",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"A giant puffed oven pancake that balloons in a hot skillet, served with lemon and powdered sugar.","3|eggs;3/4 cup|milk;3/4 cup|flour;1 tbsp|sugar;1/4 tsp|salt;1 tsp|vanilla extract;3 tbsp|butter;1|lemon|cut in wedges;2 tbsp|powdered sugar;1 cup|strawberries|sliced, optional","Place a 10 to 12 inch cast-iron skillet in the oven and heat the oven to 425°F.|Blend the eggs, milk, flour, sugar, salt and vanilla in a blender for 30 seconds until completely smooth.|Carefully remove the hot skillet, add the butter and swirl until it melts and coats the pan.|Pour in the batter right away and return the skillet to the oven.|Bake 18 to 20 minutes without opening the door until the pancake is deeply golden and puffed high on the sides.|Serve immediately with lemon juice, powdered sugar and strawberries. It will deflate as it cools.","American"],
[3553,"Egg in a Hole","breakfast","🍳",10,"Very easy",8.5,2,"An egg fried right in the middle of a slice of buttery toast, with a crisp cut-out on the side.","2 slice|bread|thick cut;2|eggs;2 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Cut a 2 to 3 inch hole in the center of each slice of bread with a small glass or biscuit cutter and keep the rounds.|Melt 1 tablespoon of butter in a skillet over medium heat.|Place the bread slices in the pan, crack an egg into each hole and season with salt and pepper.|Cook 2 minutes until the egg white begins to set, and add the cut-out rounds to toast alongside.|Dot with the remaining butter, flip carefully with a wide spatula and cook another 1 to 2 minutes for a runny yolk or 3 minutes for firm.|Serve hot with the toasted rounds.","American"],
[3554,"Lemon Bars","treats","🍋",70,"Easy",9,16,"A buttery shortbread crust topped with a bright, tart lemon curd filling and dusted with powdered sugar.","1 cup|butter|softened;1/2 cup|powdered sugar;2 cup|flour;1/4 tsp|salt;4|eggs;1 1/2 cup|sugar;1/4 cup|flour|for the filling;4|lemon|zest 1 tbsp, then juice about 2/3 cup;2 tbsp|powdered sugar|for dusting","Heat the oven to 350°F and line a 9x13 inch pan with parchment, leaving an overhang.|Beat the butter, 1/2 cup powdered sugar, 2 cups flour and the salt until a soft dough forms and press it firmly into the pan.|Bake the crust 18 to 20 minutes until lightly golden at the edges.|Whisk the eggs, sugar, 1/4 cup flour, 1 tablespoon lemon zest and the lemon juice until smooth.|Pour the filling over the hot crust and bake 20 to 25 minutes until just set in the center.|Cool completely in the pan, chill for 1 hour, lift out and cut into squares, then dust with powdered sugar.","American"],
[3555,"Oatmeal Raisin Cookies","treats","🍪",35,"Easy",9,24,"Chewy, cinnamon-scented cookies loaded with oats and plump raisins.","1 cup|butter|softened;1 cup|brown sugar|packed;1/2 cup|sugar;2|eggs;2 tsp|vanilla extract;1 1/2 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking soda;1 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 tsp|salt;3 cup|rolled oats;1 cup|raisins","Heat the oven to 350°F and line two baking sheets with parchment.|Beat the butter, brown sugar and sugar for 2 to 3 minutes until fluffy, then beat in the eggs and vanilla.|Whisk the flour, baking soda, cinnamon and salt, then stir into the butter mixture until just combined.|Fold in the oats and raisins.|Scoop rounded tablespoons of dough 2 inches apart onto the sheets.|Bake 10 to 12 minutes until the edges are golden and the centers still look slightly soft.|Cool 5 minutes on the sheet before moving to a rack.","American"],
[3556,"Snickerdoodles","treats","🍪",40,"Easy",9,24,"Soft, tangy sugar cookies rolled in cinnamon sugar with crackly tops.","1 cup|butter|softened;1 1/2 cup|sugar;2|eggs;2 tsp|vanilla extract;2 3/4 cup|flour;2 tsp|cream of tartar;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 cup|sugar|for rolling;2 tsp|cinnamon|for rolling","Heat the oven to 375°F and line two baking sheets with parchment.|Cream the butter and 1 1/2 cups sugar until fluffy, then beat in the eggs and vanilla.|Whisk the flour, cream of tartar, baking soda and salt and mix into the butter mixture to form a soft dough. Chill 30 minutes if it feels sticky.|Stir the 1/4 cup sugar and cinnamon together in a small bowl.|Roll the dough into 1 1/2 inch balls and roll each in the cinnamon sugar.|Bake 8 to 10 minutes until the edges are set and the centers look slightly puffy.|Cool on the sheet for 5 minutes, then move to a rack.","American"],
[3557,"Red Velvet Cake","treats","🍰",100,"Medium",9,12,"A tender, cocoa-kissed crimson layer cake with tangy buttermilk crumb and cream cheese frosting.","2 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cocoa powder;1 tsp|baking soda;1 tsp|salt;1 1/2 cup|vegetable oil;1 cup|buttermilk;2|eggs;2 tbsp|red food coloring;1 tsp|vanilla extract;1 tsp|white vinegar;16 oz|cream cheese|softened;1/2 cup|butter|softened;4 cup|powdered sugar;2 tsp|vanilla extract|for the frosting","Heat the oven to 350°F. Grease and flour two 9 inch round cake pans and line the bottoms with parchment.|Whisk the flour, sugar, cocoa, baking soda and salt in a large bowl.|In another bowl whisk the oil, buttermilk, eggs, food coloring, 1 teaspoon vanilla and the vinegar, then mix into the dry ingredients until smooth.|Divide the batter between the pans and bake 28 to 32 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 10 minutes in the pans, turn out onto a rack and cool completely.|Beat the cream cheese and butter until smooth, then beat in the powdered sugar and 2 teaspoons vanilla until fluffy.|Spread frosting between the layers and over the top and sides, then chill 30 minutes before slicing.","Southern"],
[3558,"Chocolate Lava Cake","treats","🍫",30,"Medium",9,4,"Individual chocolate cakes baked until the edges set and the center flows out like warm fudge sauce.","6 oz|semisweet chocolate|chopped;1/2 cup|butter;1 cup|powdered sugar;2|eggs;2|eggs|yolks only;6 tbsp|flour;1 tsp|vanilla extract;1 pinch|salt;1 tbsp|cocoa powder|for the ramekins;1 tbsp|butter|for the ramekins","Heat the oven to 425°F. Butter four 6 ounce ramekins and dust them with cocoa powder, tapping out the excess.|Melt the chocolate and 1/2 cup butter together in the microwave in 30 second bursts, stirring until smooth.|Whisk in the powdered sugar, then the whole eggs, egg yolks, vanilla and salt.|Stir in the flour until just combined and divide the batter among the ramekins.|Set the ramekins on a baking sheet and bake 12 to 14 minutes until the edges are firm but the centers still jiggle.|Cool 1 minute, run a knife around the edges, invert onto plates and serve right away.","American"],
[3559,"Rice Krispies Treats","treats","🍫",20,"Very easy",9,16,"Gooey, buttery marshmallow bars with crisp rice cereal, ready in 20 minutes.","4 tbsp|butter;10 oz|marshmallows;1 tsp|vanilla extract;1/4 tsp|salt;6 cup|crispy rice cereal","Grease a 9x13 inch pan or line it with parchment.|Melt the butter in a large pot over low heat.|Add the marshmallows and stir for 3 to 4 minutes until completely melted and smooth.|Remove from the heat and stir in the vanilla and salt.|Fold in the cereal until evenly coated.|Press into the pan with a greased spatula, cool for 30 minutes and cut into squares.","American"],
[3560,"Blueberry Cobbler","treats","🫐",55,"Easy",9,6,"Juicy blueberries bubbling under tender sweet drop biscuits with crisp sugared tops.","5 cup|blueberries;1/2 cup|sugar;1 tbsp|cornstarch;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 cup|flour;1/4 cup|sugar|for the biscuit;1 1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/4 tsp|salt;4 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed;1/2 cup|milk;1 tbsp|sugar|for sprinkling","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Toss the blueberries with 1/2 cup sugar, the cornstarch and lemon juice and spread in a 2 quart baking dish.|Whisk the flour, 1/4 cup sugar, baking powder and salt, then cut in the cold butter until the mixture looks like coarse crumbs.|Stir in the milk until a soft, sticky dough forms.|Drop spoonfuls of dough over the berries, leaving gaps, and sprinkle with the remaining sugar.|Bake 35 to 40 minutes until the filling bubbles and the biscuits are golden.|Cool 15 minutes and serve warm, ideally with vanilla ice cream.","Southern"],
[3561,"Homemade Vanilla Ice Cream","treats","🍦",420,"Medium",9,8,"Rich custard-style vanilla ice cream churned in an ice cream maker, with a creamy scoopable texture.","2 cup|heavy cream;1 cup|milk;3/4 cup|sugar;4|eggs|yolks only;1 tbsp|vanilla extract;1/8 tsp|salt","Heat the cream, milk and half the sugar in a saucepan over medium heat until steaming, but not boiling.|Whisk the yolks with the remaining sugar until pale, then slowly whisk in about 1 cup of the hot cream to temper them.|Pour the yolk mixture back into the pan and cook over medium-low heat, stirring constantly, for 5 to 7 minutes until it coats the back of a spoon and reaches 175°F.|Strain into a bowl, stir in the vanilla and salt and chill for at least 4 hours or overnight.|Churn in an ice cream maker for 20 to 25 minutes until it looks like soft serve.|Transfer to a container and freeze at least 2 hours until firm.","American"],
[3562,"Peanut Butter Fudge","treats","🍫",120,"Easy",9,25,"Creamy, old-fashioned fudge made with peanut butter and marshmallow creme.","2 cup|sugar;1/2 cup|butter;1/2 cup|milk;1 cup|peanut butter|creamy;7 oz|marshmallow creme;1 tsp|vanilla extract","Line an 8 inch square pan with parchment, leaving an overhang.|Combine the sugar, butter and milk in a heavy saucepan over medium heat and stir until the butter melts.|Bring to a full rolling boil and boil for 5 minutes, stirring constantly.|Remove from the heat and quickly stir in the peanut butter, marshmallow creme and vanilla until smooth.|Pour into the pan and smooth the top.|Cool at room temperature, then chill for at least 1 hour until firm and cut into small squares.","American"],
[3563,"Lemon Meringue Pie","treats","🥧",210,"Medium",9,8,"A tart lemon custard in a flaky crust under a tall, toasted meringue.","1|pie crust|9 inch;1 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|cornstarch;1/4 tsp|salt;4|eggs|yolks only;2 tbsp|butter;3|lemon|zest 1 tbsp, then juice about 1/2 cup;4|eggs|whites only, for the meringue;1/4 tsp|cream of tartar;1/2 cup|sugar|for the meringue;1/2 tsp|vanilla extract","Heat the oven to 400°F, fit the crust into a 9 inch pie plate, prick it, line with parchment and weights and bake 12 minutes. Remove the weights and bake 6 minutes more until golden, then lower the oven to 350°F.|Whisk 1 cup sugar, cornstarch and salt in a saucepan, then whisk in 1 1/2 cups water and cook over medium heat, stirring, until thick and bubbling, about 6 minutes.|Whisk a little hot filling into the yolks, then pour the yolks back into the pan and cook 2 minutes more, stirring constantly.|Off the heat stir in the butter, lemon zest and lemon juice and pour into the hot crust.|Beat the whites with the cream of tartar to soft peaks, then add 1/2 cup sugar a spoonful at a time and the vanilla and beat to stiff glossy peaks.|Spread the meringue over the hot filling, sealing it to the crust edges and swirling the top.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden, cool 1 hour at room temperature, then chill at least 2 hours before slicing.","American"],
[3564,"Classic Pound Cake","treats","🍰",90,"Easy",9,12,"A buttery, fine-crumbed vanilla pound cake with a golden crust, perfect plain or with berries.","1 cup|butter|softened;2 cup|sugar;4|eggs;2 tsp|vanilla extract;2 1/2 cup|flour;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;3/4 cup|milk","Heat the oven to 325°F and grease and flour a 10 inch tube or bundt pan.|Beat the butter and sugar for 4 to 5 minutes until very light and fluffy.|Beat in the eggs one at a time, then the vanilla.|Whisk the flour, baking powder and salt and add to the batter in three parts, alternating with the milk, mixing just until combined.|Scrape into the pan and smooth the top.|Bake 60 to 70 minutes until a toothpick comes out clean.|Cool 15 minutes in the pan, then turn out onto a rack to cool completely.","American"],
[3565,"Cut-Out Sugar Cookies","treats","🍪",100,"Easy",9,30,"Soft, buttery cookies that hold their shape for cutters, with a simple vanilla icing.","1 cup|butter|softened;1 cup|sugar;1|eggs;2 tsp|vanilla extract;3 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;2 cup|powdered sugar|for the icing;2 tbsp|milk|for the icing;1/2 tsp|vanilla extract|for the icing","Beat the butter and sugar until light and fluffy, then beat in the egg and 2 teaspoons vanilla.|Whisk the flour, baking powder and salt and mix into the butter until a soft dough forms.|Divide into two discs, wrap and chill for 1 hour.|Heat the oven to 350°F. Roll each disc on a floured surface to 1/4 inch thick and cut out shapes.|Place on parchment-lined baking sheets and bake 8 to 10 minutes until the edges are barely golden.|Cool completely on a rack.|Stir the powdered sugar, milk and 1/2 teaspoon vanilla until smooth, adding milk by the teaspoon if too thick, and ice the cooled cookies.","American"],
[3566,"Strawberry Shortcake","treats","🍓",60,"Easy",9,6,"Flaky buttery biscuits split and filled with juicy macerated strawberries and softly whipped cream.","2 cup|flour;2 tbsp|sugar;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;6 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed;2/3 cup|milk;1|eggs;2 lb|strawberries|hulled and sliced;1/4 cup|sugar|for the berries;1 1/2 cup|heavy cream;2 tbsp|powdered sugar;1 tsp|vanilla extract","Toss the strawberries with 1/4 cup sugar and let them sit for 30 minutes until juicy.|Heat the oven to 425°F. Whisk the flour, 2 tablespoons sugar, baking powder and salt, then cut in the cold butter until it looks like coarse crumbs.|Whisk the milk and egg and stir into the flour mixture just until a shaggy dough forms.|Drop six large mounds onto a parchment-lined baking sheet and bake 15 to 18 minutes until golden.|Whip the cream with the powdered sugar and vanilla to soft peaks.|Split the warm biscuits, fill with berries and juices and cream, and replace the tops with another spoonful of each.","American"],
[3567,"Banana Cream Pie","treats","🍌",260,"Medium",9,8,"Sliced bananas and vanilla custard in a graham cracker crust, crowned with whipped cream.","1 1/2 cup|graham cracker crumbs;1/4 cup|sugar;6 tbsp|butter|melted;2 3/4 cup|milk;2/3 cup|sugar|for the custard;1/3 cup|cornstarch;1/4 tsp|salt;4|eggs|yolks only;3 tbsp|butter|for the custard;2 tsp|vanilla extract;3|bananas|sliced;1 cup|heavy cream;2 tbsp|powdered sugar","Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix the graham crumbs, 1/4 cup sugar and melted butter, press into a 9 inch pie plate and bake 10 minutes. Cool.|Whisk 2/3 cup sugar, the cornstarch and salt in a saucepan, then whisk in the milk and yolks.|Cook over medium heat, whisking constantly, for 6 to 8 minutes until thick and bubbling, then cook 1 minute more.|Off the heat whisk in the 3 tablespoons butter and the vanilla and press plastic wrap onto the surface. Cool 20 minutes.|Layer half the bananas in the crust, spread half the custard over, then add the remaining bananas and custard.|Chill at least 4 hours.|Whip the cream with the powdered sugar to stiff peaks and spread over the pie before serving.","American"],
[3568,"Whoopie Pies","treats","🍪",45,"Medium",9,12,"Soft, cakey chocolate rounds sandwiched around a fluffy marshmallow cream filling.","1/2 cup|butter|softened;1 cup|sugar;1|eggs;1 tsp|vanilla extract;2 cup|flour;1/2 cup|cocoa powder;1 tsp|baking soda;1/2 tsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1 cup|buttermilk;1/2 cup|butter|softened, for the filling;2 cup|powdered sugar;7 oz|marshmallow creme;1 tsp|vanilla extract|for the filling","Heat the oven to 350°F and line two baking sheets with parchment.|Beat 1/2 cup butter and the sugar until fluffy, then beat in the egg and 1 teaspoon vanilla.|Whisk the flour, cocoa, baking soda, baking powder and salt and add to the batter in thirds, alternating with the buttermilk.|Drop heaping tablespoons of batter 2 inches apart to make 24 rounds.|Bake 9 to 11 minutes until the tops spring back, then cool completely on a rack.|Beat the filling butter, powdered sugar, marshmallow creme and vanilla until fluffy.|Spread filling on the flat side of half the cakes and top with the remaining cakes.","American"],
[3569,"Homemade Chocolate Pudding","treats","🍫",150,"Easy",9,6,"Silky stovetop chocolate pudding made with cocoa and real chocolate, nothing like the box.","3 cup|milk;2/3 cup|sugar;1/3 cup|cocoa powder;1/4 cup|cornstarch;1/4 tsp|salt;3 oz|bittersweet chocolate|chopped;2 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 tsp|vanilla extract","Whisk the sugar, cocoa, cornstarch and salt in a saucepan, then whisk in about 1/2 cup of the milk to make a smooth paste.|Whisk in the remaining milk and cook over medium heat, whisking constantly, for 6 to 8 minutes until thick and bubbling.|Boil for 1 minute while whisking, then remove from the heat.|Stir in the chopped chocolate, butter and vanilla until melted and glossy.|Strain into a bowl or divide into cups and press plastic wrap onto the surface to prevent a skin.|Chill at least 2 hours and serve with whipped cream.","American"],
[3570,"Sheet-Pan Shrimp Fajitas","quick","🌮",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Shrimp, peppers and onions roasted together on one pan with fajita spices and warmed in tortillas.","1 1/2 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;3|bell pepper|sliced;1|red onion|sliced;3 tbsp|olive oil;2 tsp|chili powder;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|salt;2|lime|juiced;8|flour tortillas;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Heat the oven to 425°F and line a large rimmed baking sheet with parchment.|Mix the chili powder, cumin, paprika, garlic powder and salt.|Toss the peppers and onion with 2 tablespoons of the oil and half the spice mix, spread on the pan and roast 10 minutes.|Toss the shrimp with the remaining oil and spices and the juice of 1 lime.|Push the vegetables aside, add the shrimp in a single layer and roast 6 to 8 minutes until pink and opaque.|Squeeze the second lime over everything, scatter with cilantro and serve with warm tortillas.","Tex-Mex"],
[3571,"One-Pan Chicken and Rice","quick","🍗",30,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seasoned chicken pieces and fluffy rice cooked together in a single skillet with peas.","1 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch cubes;1 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 cup|white rice|long grain;2 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|dried thyme;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 cup|frozen peas","Toss the chicken with the paprika, thyme, salt and pepper.|Heat the oil in a large deep skillet over medium-high heat and brown the chicken 3 to 4 minutes, then remove it to a plate.|Cook the onion in the same pan for 3 minutes, add the garlic for 30 seconds, then stir in the rice and toast 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and scrape up the browned bits, then return the chicken.|Bring to a boil, cover, reduce the heat to low and cook 15 minutes without lifting the lid.|Scatter the peas on top, cover and let stand off the heat 5 minutes, then fluff with a fork.","American"],
[3572,"20-Minute Shrimp Stir Fry","quick","🍤",20,"Easy",8.5,4,"Juicy shrimp with broccoli, peppers and snap peas in a glossy garlic-ginger sauce.","1 lb|shrimp|peeled and deveined;2 cup|broccoli|florets;1|bell pepper|sliced;1 cup|snap peas;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|cornstarch;1/4 cup|chicken broth;1 tbsp|ginger|grated;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1 tsp|sesame oil;2|green onion|sliced;2 cup|rice|cooked, for serving","Whisk the soy sauce, honey, cornstarch, broth and sesame oil in a small bowl.|Heat 1 tablespoon of the vegetable oil in a large skillet or wok over high heat and sear the shrimp 1 to 2 minutes per side until pink, then remove to a plate.|Add the remaining oil and stir-fry the broccoli and pepper for 3 minutes, adding the snap peas for the last minute.|Add the ginger and garlic and stir 30 seconds until fragrant.|Stir the sauce, pour it in and cook 1 minute until glossy and thick, then return the shrimp and toss for 30 seconds.|Serve over rice, topped with the green onion.","Chinese"],
[3573,"Honey Garlic Salmon","quick","🐟",20,"Easy",8.5,4,"Seared salmon fillets glazed in a sticky honey, garlic and soy sauce.","1 1/2 lb|salmon|4 fillets;1 tbsp|olive oil;3 tbsp|honey;2 tbsp|soy sauce;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Pat the salmon dry and season with salt and pepper.|Stir the honey, soy sauce, garlic and lemon juice together.|Heat the oil in a large nonstick skillet over medium-high heat and cook the salmon skin side up for 4 minutes until golden.|Flip the fillets, reduce the heat to medium and cook 3 minutes more.|Add the butter and honey mixture, spooning it over the fish for 2 minutes until the glaze thickens and the salmon reaches 145°F.|Spoon the sauce over each fillet and serve.","American"],
[3574,"Cheeseburger Macaroni Skillet","quick","🍔",30,"Easy",8.5,6,"Ground beef, macaroni and melted cheddar in one skillet with a savory cheeseburger flavor.","1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 cup|beef broth;1 cup|milk;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;2 cup|elbow macaroni|dry;1 tbsp|yellow mustard;1 tbsp|ketchup;1 tsp|paprika;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Brown the beef with the onion in a large deep skillet over medium-high heat for 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up, and drain any excess fat.|Stir in the garlic for 30 seconds.|Add the broth, milk, tomato sauce, mustard, ketchup, paprika, salt and pepper and bring to a simmer.|Stir in the macaroni, cover and simmer 12 to 14 minutes, stirring occasionally, until the pasta is tender and the sauce is thick.|Remove from the heat and stir in 1 1/2 cups of the cheese until melted.|Top with the remaining cheese, cover for 2 minutes and serve.","American"],
[3575,"Sausage and Potato Skillet","quick","🥔",30,"Very easy",8.5,4,"Smoked sausage, crispy-edged baby potatoes and peppers in a single seasoned skillet.","1 lb|smoked sausage|sliced;1 1/2 lb|baby potatoes|cut in 1/2 inch cubes;1|bell pepper|diced;1/2|onion|diced;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|paprika;1/2 tsp|garlic powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped","Heat 1 tablespoon of the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and brown the sausage 4 to 5 minutes, then remove it to a plate.|Add the remaining oil and the potatoes with the paprika, garlic powder, salt and pepper.|Cook 5 minutes, stirring occasionally, then add 1/4 cup water, cover and steam 6 to 8 minutes until the potatoes are nearly tender.|Uncover, add the pepper and onion and cook 5 minutes until the potatoes are crisp and golden.|Return the sausage, toss for 1 to 2 minutes and finish with the parsley.","American"],
[3576,"Pork Tenderloin Medallions with Dijon Cream Sauce","quick","🥩",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Quick-seared pork medallions in a creamy mustard-thyme pan sauce.","1 1/4 lb|pork tenderloin|cut in 1 inch slices;1/4 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|butter;1|shallot|minced;1/2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tbsp|dijon mustard;1/2 tsp|dried thyme","Press each pork slice flat to about 1/2 inch with your palm and season with salt and pepper, then dredge lightly in the flour.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat and sear the pork 3 minutes per side until golden and 145°F inside. Move to a plate.|Melt the butter in the pan, add the shallot and cook 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and scrape up the browned bits, then simmer 2 minutes.|Whisk in the cream, mustard and thyme and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until slightly thickened.|Return the pork and juices to the pan for 1 minute to warm through and serve with the sauce.","American"],
[3577,"Blackened Tilapia with Avocado Salsa","quick","🐟",20,"Easy",8.5,4,"Spice-crusted tilapia seared in a hot skillet and served with a cool avocado tomato salsa.","1 1/2 lb|tilapia|4 fillets;2 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|onion powder;1 tsp|dried thyme;1/2 tsp|cayenne;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|avocado|diced;1|tomato|diced;1/4|red onion|minced;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;2|lime|juiced","Mix the paprika, garlic powder, onion powder, thyme, cayenne, salt and pepper.|Stir the avocado, tomato, red onion, cilantro and the juice of 1 lime together with a pinch of salt.|Pat the fish dry and press the spice mix onto both sides.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat until shimmering.|Cook the fillets 3 minutes per side until dark and crusted and the fish flakes easily.|Squeeze the remaining lime over the fish and serve topped with the salsa.","American"],
[3578,"Sloppy Joes","quick","🍔",30,"Easy",8.5,6,"Ground beef in a tangy-sweet tomato sauce piled onto soft toasted buns.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;1|green bell pepper|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;3/4 cup|ketchup;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|worcestershire sauce;1 tbsp|yellow mustard;1 tsp|chili powder;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste;6|hamburger buns|toasted","Brown the beef with the onion and pepper in a large skillet over medium-high heat for 8 minutes, breaking up the meat, then drain the fat.|Stir in the garlic for 30 seconds.|Add the ketchup, tomato sauce, brown sugar, Worcestershire, mustard, chili powder, salt and pepper.|Simmer on medium-low for 10 to 12 minutes, stirring now and then, until thick and glossy.|Taste and adjust the seasoning, then spoon onto the toasted buns.","American"],
[3579,"Salmon Patties","quick","🐟",25,"Easy",8.5,4,"Crisp pan-fried patties made from canned salmon, onion and seafood seasoning.","1 can|pink salmon|14.75 oz, drained;1/2 cup|panko;2|eggs;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1/4 cup|onion|finely diced;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|seafood seasoning;1/4 tsp|black pepper;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|lemon|cut in wedges","Flake the salmon into a bowl, removing any large bones or skin.|Add the panko, eggs, mayonnaise, onion, lemon juice, seafood seasoning and pepper and mix gently until it holds together.|Let the mixture rest 5 minutes, then form into 8 patties about 1/2 inch thick.|Heat the oil in a large skillet over medium heat.|Fry the patties 3 to 4 minutes per side until deeply golden and crisp.|Drain on paper towels and serve with lemon wedges.","Southern"],
[3580,"Beef Pot Pie","comfort","🥧",180,"Medium",9,6,"Tender braised beef and vegetables in rich gravy under a golden flaky crust.","1 1/2 lb|beef chuck|cut in 1 inch cubes;3 tbsp|flour;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;2|carrot|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|tomato paste;2 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|worcestershire sauce;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 cup|frozen peas;2|pie crust|9 inch;1|eggs|beaten, for the wash;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Season the beef with salt and pepper and toss with the flour.|Heat the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat and brown the beef in batches, 5 minutes per batch, then set aside.|Cook the onion, carrots and celery in the pot for 5 minutes, add the garlic and tomato paste and cook 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and Worcestershire, add the thyme and the beef, then cover and simmer on low for 1 hour 15 minutes until the beef is tender and the gravy is thick.|Stir in the peas and cool the filling for 20 minutes.|Heat the oven to 400°F. Line a 9 inch pie plate with one crust, add the filling, cover with the second crust, crimp the edges and cut vents.|Brush with the beaten egg and bake 30 to 35 minutes until deep golden, then rest 10 minutes.","American"],
[3581,"Beef and Rice Stuffed Peppers","comfort","🫑",70,"Easy",9,6,"Bell peppers filled with seasoned ground beef, rice and tomato, baked until tender under melted mozzarella.","6|bell pepper|tops removed and seeded;1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;2 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 cup|rice|cooked;1 can|tomato sauce|15 oz, divided;1 tsp|italian seasoning;1 tsp|worcestershire sauce;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1 cup|mozzarella|shredded","Heat the oven to 375°F.|Brown the beef with the onion in a skillet for 7 to 8 minutes, add the garlic for 30 seconds and drain the fat.|Stir in the rice, half of the tomato sauce, the Italian seasoning, Worcestershire, salt and pepper and cook 2 minutes.|Stand the peppers upright in a baking dish, trimming the bottoms slightly if needed, and fill them with the beef mixture.|Pour the remaining tomato sauce over and around the peppers and add a splash of water to the dish.|Cover with foil and bake 30 minutes, then uncover, top with the mozzarella and bake 15 minutes more until the peppers are tender and the cheese is bubbly.","American"],
[3582,"Tuna Noodle Casserole","comfort","🍲",60,"Easy",9,6,"Egg noodles, tuna and peas in a creamy mushroom sauce with a crunchy buttery topping.","8 oz|egg noodles;4 tbsp|butter;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1/2|onion|diced;1/4 cup|flour;2 cup|milk;1/2 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;2 can|tuna|5 oz each, drained;1 cup|frozen peas;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper;1 cup|panko;2 tbsp|butter|melted, for the topping","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the noodles 2 minutes short of the package time and drain.|Melt 4 tablespoons butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the mushrooms and onion for 6 to 8 minutes until golden.|Stir in the flour for 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the milk and broth and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until thick.|Stir in the cheddar until melted, then add the salt, pepper, tuna, peas and noodles.|Transfer to a 9x13 inch baking dish.|Toss the panko with the melted butter and sprinkle over the top.|Bake 20 to 25 minutes until bubbly and golden.","American"],
[3583,"Beef and Noodles","comfort","🍜",160,"Easy",9,6,"Fork-tender beef in a rich, savory broth gravy served over wide egg noodles.","2 lb|beef chuck|cut in 1 inch cubes;2 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;6 cup|beef broth;1 tbsp|worcestershire sauce;1 tsp|dried thyme;2|bay leaf;12 oz|egg noodles|wide;2 tbsp|cornstarch;2 tbsp|butter;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Season the beef with salt and pepper.|Heat the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat and brown the beef in batches, then set aside.|Cook the onion in the pot for 4 minutes, add the garlic for 30 seconds, then pour in the broth, Worcestershire, thyme and bay leaves and return the beef.|Cover and simmer on low for 1 hour 45 minutes until the beef is very tender.|Remove the bay leaves, raise the heat to a boil and stir in the noodles. Cook 8 to 10 minutes until tender.|Whisk the cornstarch with 3 tablespoons cold water, stir it in with the butter and simmer 2 minutes until thickened, then adjust the seasoning and serve.","American"],
[3584,"Chicken Divan","comfort","🥦",55,"Easy",9,6,"Chicken and broccoli in a creamy cheddar-curry sauce with a golden buttery crumb topping.","1 lb|broccoli|florets;3 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;3 tbsp|butter;3 tbsp|flour;1 1/2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tsp|lemon juice;1/2 tsp|curry powder;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1/2 cup|panko;1 tbsp|butter|melted, for the topping;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 350°F. Steam or blanch the broccoli 3 minutes until bright green and drain well.|Melt 3 tablespoons butter in a saucepan, stir in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the broth and cream.|Simmer 4 to 5 minutes until thickened, then whisk in the mayonnaise, lemon juice, curry powder, 3/4 cup of the cheddar, salt and pepper.|Arrange the broccoli in a 9x13 inch baking dish, top with the chicken and pour the sauce over.|Mix the panko with the melted butter, scatter it with the remaining cheese over the top.|Bake 25 minutes until bubbling and golden and serve over rice if you like.","American"],
[3585,"Chicken Tetrazzini","comfort","🍝",60,"Easy",9,6,"Spaghetti and chicken in a creamy mushroom sherry sauce, baked with a Parmesan crust.","8 oz|spaghetti|broken in half;4 tbsp|butter;8 oz|mushrooms|sliced;1/4 cup|flour;2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1/4 cup|dry white wine;3 cup|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;1/2 cup|frozen peas;1 cup|parmesan|grated;1/2 cup|panko;1/2 tsp|salt;1/4 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the spaghetti 2 minutes short of the package time and drain.|Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the mushrooms 6 to 8 minutes until browned.|Stir in the flour for 1 minute, then whisk in the broth, cream and wine and simmer 4 to 5 minutes until thick.|Stir in 1/2 cup of the Parmesan, the salt and pepper, then fold in the chicken, peas and spaghetti.|Transfer to a greased 9x13 inch baking dish and top with the panko mixed with the remaining Parmesan.|Bake 20 to 25 minutes until bubbling and golden on top.","American"],
[3586,"Chicken Broccoli Rice Casserole","comfort","🥦",80,"Easy",9,6,"Chicken, broccoli and rice baked in a creamy cheddar sauce, all in one dish.","2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;3 tbsp|flour;2 cup|chicken broth;1 cup|milk;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 cup|white rice|long grain, uncooked;1 1/2 lb|chicken breast|cut in 1 inch cubes;3 cup|broccoli|small florets;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;1/2 tsp|garlic powder","Heat the oven to 375°F and grease a 9x13 inch baking dish.|Melt the butter in a saucepan and cook the onion 4 minutes, then stir in the flour for 1 minute.|Whisk in the broth and milk and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until thickened, then stir in 1 cup of the cheddar, the salt, pepper and garlic powder.|Spread the rice, chicken and broccoli in the dish and pour the hot sauce over, stirring gently so the rice is submerged.|Cover tightly with foil and bake 50 minutes until the rice is tender and the chicken reaches 165°F.|Uncover, top with the remaining cheese and bake 8 to 10 minutes more until melted, then rest 5 minutes.","American"],
[3587,"Baked Ziti","comfort","🍝",70,"Easy",9,8,"Ziti tossed in meaty tomato sauce with creamy ricotta, baked under a blanket of mozzarella.","1 lb|ziti;1 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|tomato sauce|8 oz;1 tbsp|italian seasoning;1 tsp|sugar;15 oz|ricotta;1|eggs;3 cup|mozzarella|shredded;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;2 tbsp|basil|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F. Boil the ziti 3 minutes short of the package time and drain.|Brown the beef with the onion in a large pot for 8 minutes, add the garlic for 30 seconds and drain the fat.|Add the crushed tomatoes, tomato sauce, Italian seasoning, sugar, salt and pepper and simmer 15 minutes.|Stir the ricotta, egg, half the Parmesan and a pinch of salt together.|Toss the ziti with the sauce, then spread half in a 9x13 inch dish, dot with the ricotta mixture and 1 cup mozzarella, and top with the remaining ziti.|Cover with the remaining mozzarella and Parmesan, bake covered 25 minutes, then uncovered 10 minutes until browned, and finish with basil.","Italian"],
[3588,"Smothered Pork Chops","comfort","🍖",50,"Easy",9,4,"Seared bone-in pork chops simmered in onion gravy until fork tender.","4|pork chops|bone-in, 3/4 inch thick;1/4 cup|flour|for dredging;3 tbsp|flour|for the gravy;1 tsp|paprika;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;3 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|sliced;2 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 tbsp|worcestershire sauce","Mix the 1/4 cup flour with the paprika, garlic powder, salt and pepper and dredge the pork chops, shaking off the excess.|Heat the oil in a large deep skillet over medium-high heat and sear the chops 3 to 4 minutes per side until golden. Remove to a plate.|Cook the sliced onion in the drippings for 5 minutes until soft.|Sprinkle the 3 tablespoons flour over the onion and stir for 1 minute, then slowly whisk in the broth, thyme and Worcestershire.|Bring to a simmer, scraping up the browned bits, and nestle the chops back into the gravy.|Cover and cook on low for 20 to 25 minutes until the pork is tender and 145°F, then spoon the gravy over and serve with rice or mashed potatoes.","Southern"],
[3589,"French Lentil Soup","soup","🥣",50,"Easy",9.5,6,"A humble pot of green lentils, carrots and thyme, brightened with a splash of vinegar at the end.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 cup|green lentils|French green, rinsed;6 cup|chicken broth;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;2|bay leaves;1 tsp|dried thyme;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the olive oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion, carrots and celery for 8 minutes until softened.|Stir in the garlic and thyme and cook for 1 minute.|Add the lentils, broth, tomatoes and bay leaves and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a simmer, partly cover and cook 30 to 35 minutes until the lentils are tender.|Remove the bay leaves and stir in the vinegar. Season with salt and pepper.|For a thicker soup, blend about a third of it with an immersion blender and stir it back in.","French"],
[3590,"Pumpkin Soup","soup","🎃",50,"Easy",9.5,6,"Silky roasted-sweet pumpkin soup with onion, a hint of nutmeg and a swirl of cream.","3 lb|pumpkin|peeled and cubed;2 tbsp|butter;1|onion|chopped;2 clove|garlic|minced;4 cup|chicken broth;1/2 tsp|nutmeg;1/2 tsp|cinnamon;1/2 cup|heavy cream;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion for 5 minutes until soft.|Add the garlic and cook 30 seconds.|Add the pumpkin, broth, nutmeg and cinnamon and bring to a boil.|Simmer 20 to 25 minutes until the pumpkin is very tender.|Blend the soup until completely smooth with an immersion blender.|Stir in the cream, warm gently for 2 minutes and season with salt and pepper.","American"],
[3591,"Chicken and Rice Soup","soup","🍲",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Cozy chicken soup with tender rice, carrots and celery, ready in under an hour.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|sliced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;8 cup|chicken broth;1 lb|chicken breast;2 sprig|thyme;2|bay leaves;3/4 cup|white rice|long grain;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1 tbsp|lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion, carrots and celery for 6 minutes.|Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute.|Pour in the broth and add the chicken, thyme and bay leaves. Bring to a boil, then simmer 15 minutes until the chicken reaches 165°F.|Remove the chicken and shred it with two forks.|Stir the rice into the soup and simmer 15 minutes until tender.|Return the chicken to the pot, discard the bay leaves and thyme stems, and stir in the parsley and lemon juice. Season to taste.","American"],
[3592,"Ham and Bean Soup","soup","🫘",150,"Easy",9.5,8,"Smoky ham hock simmered with navy beans, carrots and celery into a thick, hearty soup.","1 lb|dried navy beans|soaked overnight and drained;1|ham hock|about 1 1/2 lb;1 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;2|carrots|diced;2 stalk|celery|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;8 cup|chicken broth;2|bay leaves;1 tsp|dried thyme;|black pepper|to taste;|salt|to taste","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion, carrots and celery for 6 minutes.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the drained beans, ham hock, broth, bay leaves and thyme and bring to a boil.|Reduce to a low simmer, partly cover and cook 1 1/2 to 2 hours until the beans are very tender.|Remove the ham hock, shred the meat and discard the bone and skin.|Mash some beans against the pot to thicken, stir the meat back in and season with pepper and salt only as needed since ham is salty.","American"],
[3593,"Cream of Mushroom Soup","soup","🍄",40,"Easy",9.5,5,"Velvety soup of browned mushrooms, onion and thyme finished with cream.","1 1/2 lb|mushrooms|cremini, sliced;3 tbsp|butter;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|flour;4 cup|chicken broth;1 tsp|dried thyme;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tbsp|sherry vinegar|or lemon juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt 2 tablespoons butter in a large pot over medium-high heat and cook the mushrooms in two batches for 8 minutes each until deeply browned. Set a few aside for topping.|Add the remaining butter and the onion and cook 5 minutes.|Stir in the garlic, thyme and flour and cook 1 minute.|Slowly whisk in the broth, scraping up browned bits, and simmer 15 minutes.|Blend until smooth with an immersion blender.|Stir in the cream and vinegar, warm through and season. Top with the reserved mushrooms.","French"],
[3594,"Vegetable Beef Soup","soup","🥣",90,"Easy",9.5,8,"Chunks of beef and garden vegetables simmered in a rich tomato broth.","1 1/2 lb|beef chuck|cut in 3/4 inch cubes;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;3|carrots|sliced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|tomato paste;6 cup|beef broth;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;2|potatoes|diced;1 cup|green beans|cut in pieces;1 cup|frozen corn;1 tsp|dried thyme;2|bay leaves;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Season the beef with salt and pepper and brown it in the oil in a large pot over medium-high heat in two batches. Set aside.|Cook the onion, carrots and celery in the same pot for 5 minutes. Add garlic and tomato paste and cook 1 minute.|Return the beef to the pot with the broth, tomatoes, thyme and bay leaves. Bring to a boil.|Cover and simmer on low for 1 hour until the beef is nearly tender.|Add the potatoes and green beans and simmer 20 minutes more.|Stir in the corn, cook 5 minutes, discard bay leaves and adjust the seasoning.","American"],
[3595,"Chile Verde","soup","🌶️",150,"Easy",9.5,6,"Tender pork shoulder simmered in a tangy roasted tomatillo and green chile sauce.","3 lb|pork shoulder|cut in 1 1/2 inch cubes;1 tbsp|vegetable oil;1|onion|diced;4 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 lb|tomatillos|husked and halved;2|poblano peppers|seeded;2|jalapeno peppers|seeded;1 tsp|cumin;1 tsp|dried oregano;2 cup|chicken broth;1/2 cup|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the broiler. Broil the tomatillos, poblanos and jalapenos on a sheet pan for 8 to 10 minutes until charred in spots.|Blend the charred vegetables with the garlic, cilantro and 1 cup broth until chunky-smooth.|Season the pork with salt and pepper and brown it in the oil in a Dutch oven over medium-high heat in batches. Add the onion and cook 4 minutes.|Add the sauce, remaining broth, cumin and oregano and bring to a simmer.|Cover and simmer on low 1 1/2 to 2 hours until the pork is fork-tender.|Skim excess fat, adjust the seasoning and serve with warm tortillas and rice.","Mexican"],
[3596,"Tomato Bisque","soup","🍅",40,"Easy",9.5,6,"Smooth, rich tomato soup with a touch of cream and a little sweetness from onion and carrot.","3 tbsp|butter;1|onion|chopped;1|carrot|chopped;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|flour;2 can|whole tomatoes|28 oz each;2 cup|chicken broth;1 tbsp|tomato paste;1 tsp|sugar;1/2 cup|heavy cream;2 tbsp|basil|torn;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion and carrot for 8 minutes until soft.|Stir in the garlic, tomato paste and flour and cook for 2 minutes.|Add the tomatoes with their juice, broth and sugar. Bring to a boil and simmer 20 minutes.|Blend with an immersion blender until completely smooth.|Stir in the cream and basil and warm through without boiling.|Season with salt and pepper and serve with grilled cheese or crusty bread.","American"],
[3597,"Potato Leek Soup","soup","🥣",45,"Easy",9.5,6,"Classic French soup of leeks and potatoes, simple, creamy and deeply comforting.","3 tbsp|butter;3|leeks|white and light green parts, sliced and rinsed;3 clove|garlic|minced;1 1/2 lb|potatoes|peeled and cubed;5 cup|chicken broth;1 sprig|thyme;1/2 cup|heavy cream;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a large pot over medium-low heat and cook the leeks for 10 minutes without browning.|Add the garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the potatoes, broth and thyme. Bring to a boil and simmer 20 minutes until the potatoes are soft.|Remove the thyme sprig and blend the soup until smooth.|Stir in the cream and warm through.|Season with salt and pepper and top with chives.","French"],
[3598,"Albondigas Soup","soup","🍲",60,"Medium",9.5,6,"Mexican meatball soup with rice-and-mint meatballs in a light tomato vegetable broth.","1 lb|ground beef;1/4 cup|white rice|uncooked;1|egg;2 tbsp|mint|chopped;1 tsp|cumin;2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2|carrots|sliced;2|zucchini|diced;1 can|diced tomatoes|14 oz;6 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|dried oregano;2 tbsp|cilantro|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Mix the beef, rice, egg, mint, cumin, 1 teaspoon salt and pepper. Roll into 1 inch meatballs.|Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion and carrots 5 minutes. Add the garlic.|Add the tomatoes, broth and oregano and bring to a gentle simmer.|Drop in the meatballs one at a time. Cover and simmer 25 minutes.|Add the zucchini and cook 10 minutes more until the rice in the meatballs is tender and the meat is cooked through.|Stir in the cilantro and serve with lime and tortillas.","Mexican"],
[3599,"Carrot Ginger Soup","soup","🥕",40,"Easy",9.5,6,"Bright, velvety carrot soup warmed with fresh ginger and finished with a little lime.","2 tbsp|olive oil;1|onion|chopped;2 tbsp|fresh ginger|grated;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 lb|carrots|sliced;4 cup|vegetable broth;1/2 cup|coconut milk;1 tbsp|lime juice;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Heat the oil in a large pot over medium heat and cook the onion for 5 minutes.|Add the ginger and garlic and cook 1 minute.|Add the carrots and broth and bring to a boil.|Simmer 20 to 25 minutes until the carrots are very soft.|Blend until smooth, then stir in the coconut milk and lime juice.|Season with salt and pepper and warm gently before serving.","American"],
[3600,"Poke Bowl","light","🍣",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Cubed raw ahi tuna tossed in soy-sesame dressing over rice with avocado, cucumber and edamame.","1 lb|sushi-grade tuna|cut in 3/4 inch cubes;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|rice vinegar;1 tsp|honey;2|green onion|sliced;2 cup|sushi rice|cooked;1|avocado|sliced;1|cucumber|sliced;1 cup|edamame|shelled, cooked;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;1 tsp|sriracha","Whisk the soy sauce, sesame oil, vinegar, honey and sriracha in a bowl.|Gently toss the tuna and half the green onions with the dressing and chill 10 to 15 minutes. Do not marinate longer or the fish will turn firm.|Divide the warm or room-temperature rice among 4 bowls.|Arrange the tuna, avocado, cucumber and edamame on top.|Sprinkle with sesame seeds and remaining green onions and serve right away.","Hawaiian"],
[3601,"Chicken Salad","light","🥗",25,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Creamy chicken salad with celery, grapes and a little Dijon, great on greens or in a sandwich.","3 cup|cooked chicken|shredded or diced;1/2 cup|mayonnaise;2 tbsp|greek yogurt;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tbsp|lemon juice;2 stalk|celery|diced;1/2 cup|red grapes|halved;2 tbsp|green onion|sliced;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Stir the mayonnaise, yogurt, mustard and lemon juice together in a large bowl.|Add the chicken, celery, grapes, green onion and parsley.|Fold gently until evenly coated.|Season with salt and pepper.|Chill at least 30 minutes so the flavors blend, then serve over lettuce or in sandwiches.","American"],
[3602,"Caesar Salad","light","🥗",25,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crisp romaine with a garlicky anchovy-lemon dressing, parmesan and crunchy croutons.","2 head|romaine lettuce|chopped;3 slice|bread|cut in cubes;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 clove|garlic|minced;2|anchovy fillets|mashed;1|egg yolk;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|worcestershire sauce;1/3 cup|olive oil|for the dressing;1/2 cup|parmesan|grated;|black pepper|to taste;|salt|to taste","Heat the oven to 375°F. Toss the bread cubes with 2 tablespoons olive oil and a pinch of salt and bake 10 to 12 minutes until golden.|In a bowl whisk the garlic, anchovies, egg yolk, lemon juice, mustard and Worcestershire.|Slowly whisk in 1/3 cup olive oil in a thin stream until creamy. Stir in half the parmesan.|Toss the romaine with enough dressing to coat.|Top with croutons, remaining parmesan and plenty of black pepper.","Italian"],
[3603,"Tuna Salad","light","🐟",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Classic tuna salad with celery, pickles and a squeeze of lemon, perfect for lunch.","2 can|tuna|5 oz each, drained;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|dijon mustard;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;2 tbsp|red onion|finely diced;2 tbsp|dill pickle|chopped;1 tbsp|parsley|chopped;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Flake the tuna into a bowl with a fork.|Add the mayonnaise, mustard and lemon juice and stir.|Mix in the celery, onion, pickle and parsley.|Season with salt and pepper.|Serve right away or chill for 30 minutes on bread, crackers or lettuce.","American"],
[3604,"Mediterranean Quinoa Salad","light","🥗",35,"Easy",7.5,6,"Fluffy quinoa with cucumber, tomatoes, olives, chickpeas and feta in a lemon-oregano dressing.","1 cup|quinoa|rinsed;1 can|chickpeas|15 oz, drained;1|cucumber|diced;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1/2 cup|kalamata olives|sliced;1/2|red onion|finely diced;1/2 cup|feta|crumbled;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1/4 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|dried oregano;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Bring the quinoa and 2 cups water to a boil in a saucepan, then cover and simmer on low 15 minutes.|Fluff with a fork and spread on a plate to cool for 10 minutes.|Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, oregano, salt and pepper.|Combine the quinoa, chickpeas, cucumber, tomatoes, olives, onion and parsley in a large bowl.|Toss with the dressing and fold in the feta.|Serve at room temperature or chilled.","Greek"],
[3605,"Kale Salad","light","🥬",20,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Massaged kale with lemon vinaigrette, parmesan, toasted almonds and dried cranberries.","1 bunch|kale|stems removed, thinly sliced;1/4 cup|olive oil;3 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|dijon mustard;1 tsp|honey;1/3 cup|parmesan|shaved;1/3 cup|almonds|sliced, toasted;1/3 cup|dried cranberries;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Whisk the olive oil, lemon juice, mustard, honey, salt and pepper.|Place the kale in a large bowl and pour on half the dressing.|Massage the kale with your hands for 2 minutes until darker and softened.|Add the parmesan, almonds and cranberries.|Toss with more dressing to taste and let sit 10 minutes before serving.","American"],
[3606,"Taco Salad","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Seasoned ground beef over crisp romaine with beans, cheddar, tomatoes and a creamy salsa dressing.","1 lb|ground beef;1 packet|taco seasoning|1 oz;6 cup|romaine lettuce|chopped;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|cherry tomatoes|halved;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1|avocado|diced;1 cup|tortilla chips|crushed;1/2 cup|salsa;1/2 cup|sour cream;1 tbsp|lime juice","Brown the ground beef in a skillet over medium-high heat for 6 to 8 minutes, breaking it up. Drain excess fat.|Stir in the taco seasoning and 1/3 cup water and simmer 3 to 4 minutes until thickened.|Whisk the salsa, sour cream and lime juice for the dressing.|Arrange the lettuce in bowls and top with the warm beef, beans, tomatoes, cheddar and avocado.|Add the crushed chips, drizzle with the dressing and serve.","Tex-Mex"],
[3607,"Waldorf Salad","light","🍎",15,"Very easy",7.5,4,"Crisp apples, celery, grapes and walnuts in a light creamy dressing, a New York classic.","3|apples|diced;2 stalk|celery|sliced;1 cup|red grapes|halved;1/2 cup|walnuts|chopped, toasted;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1/3 cup|greek yogurt;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 tsp|honey;|salt|to taste;1 head|butter lettuce|leaves separated","Whisk the mayonnaise, yogurt, lemon juice, honey and a pinch of salt.|Dice the apples and toss with the lemon dressing right away so they do not brown.|Add the celery, grapes and walnuts and fold gently.|Chill 20 minutes.|Spoon into lettuce leaves or a bowl to serve.","American"],
[3608,"Chinese Chicken Salad","light","🥗",30,"Easy",7.5,4,"Crunchy cabbage, carrots and chicken with a sesame-ginger dressing and crispy noodles.","2|chicken breast|cooked and shredded;4 cup|napa cabbage|shredded;2 cup|red cabbage|shredded;2|carrots|shredded;3|green onion|sliced;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped;1/2 cup|crispy chow mein noodles;2 tbsp|sesame seeds;3 tbsp|rice vinegar;2 tbsp|soy sauce;2 tbsp|sesame oil;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|fresh ginger|grated;2 tbsp|vegetable oil","Whisk the vinegar, soy sauce, sesame oil, honey, ginger and vegetable oil for the dressing.|Combine the cabbages, carrots, green onions, cilantro and chicken in a large bowl.|Toast the sesame seeds in a dry skillet for 2 minutes.|Toss the salad with the dressing.|Top with the crispy noodles and sesame seeds just before serving.","Chinese"],
[3609,"Italian Sub","lunch","🥖",15,"Very easy",8,4,"Layers of salami, ham and provolone with crisp lettuce and a tangy oil-and-vinegar dressing on a crusty roll.","4|sub rolls|split;1/4 lb|salami|sliced;1/4 lb|ham|sliced;1/4 lb|capicola|sliced;8 slice|provolone;1 cup|iceberg lettuce|shredded;1|tomato|sliced;1/2|red onion|thinly sliced;1/4 cup|pepperoncini|sliced;3 tbsp|olive oil;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|dried oregano;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Whisk the olive oil, vinegar, oregano, salt and pepper.|Open the rolls and brush the cut sides with a little of the dressing.|Layer the provolone, salami, ham and capicola on the bottom halves.|Top with tomato, onion, lettuce and pepperoncini and drizzle with remaining dressing.|Close, press gently and slice in half. For the best flavor, wrap and rest 10 minutes before serving.","Italian"],
[3610,"Muffuletta","lunch","🥪",30,"Easy",8,6,"New Orleans sandwich of cured meats and cheeses on round bread with a briny olive salad.","1|round loaf|10 inch, split;1 cup|green olives|chopped;1/2 cup|giardiniera|chopped;2 tbsp|capers;2 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|olive oil;1 tbsp|red wine vinegar;1 tsp|dried oregano;1/4 lb|ham|sliced;1/4 lb|salami|sliced;1/4 lb|mortadella|sliced;6 slice|provolone;6 slice|mozzarella","Stir the olives, giardiniera, capers, garlic, olive oil, vinegar and oregano together. Let sit at least 20 minutes, or overnight.|Hollow out a little of the bread from the top and bottom halves.|Spread half the olive salad on the bottom half and layer the ham, salami, mortadella and cheeses.|Top with the remaining olive salad and the top half of the loaf.|Wrap tightly in plastic and press under a heavy pan for 30 minutes.|Cut into wedges and serve at room temperature.","American"],
[3611,"Lobster Roll","lunch","🦞",25,"Easy",8,4,"Chunks of sweet lobster in a light mayo dressing piled into a buttery toasted split-top bun.","1 1/2 lb|cooked lobster meat|chopped in chunks;1/4 cup|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|lemon juice;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;4|hot dog buns|split-top;3 tbsp|butter|melted;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Gently stir the mayonnaise, lemon juice, celery, chives, salt and pepper together.|Fold in the lobster meat and chill while you toast the buns.|Brush the outsides of the buns with melted butter.|Toast in a skillet over medium heat 1 to 2 minutes per side until golden.|Fill with the lobster salad and serve right away.","American"],
[3612,"French Dip Sandwich","lunch","🥪",25,"Easy",8,4,"Thin-sliced roast beef and melted provolone on a toasted roll with warm beef au jus for dipping.","1 lb|roast beef|thinly sliced;4|sub rolls|split;8 slice|provolone;1 tbsp|butter;1 1/2 cup|beef broth;1 tsp|worcestershire sauce;1 clove|garlic|minced;1/2 tsp|dried thyme;1|onion|thinly sliced;|black pepper|to taste","Melt the butter in a skillet over medium heat and cook the onion 8 to 10 minutes until golden.|Add the broth, Worcestershire, garlic, thyme and pepper and simmer 5 minutes to make the jus.|Add the roast beef to the jus and warm 2 minutes.|Heat the broiler. Toast the rolls cut side up for 1 to 2 minutes.|Pile the beef and onions on the rolls, top with provolone and broil 1 to 2 minutes until melted.|Serve with small cups of the jus.","American"],
[3613,"Patty Melt","lunch","🍔",25,"Easy",8,4,"A burger patty with Swiss and caramelized onions griddled between buttered rye bread.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;2|onion|sliced;4 tbsp|butter;8 slice|rye bread;8 slice|swiss cheese;2 tbsp|mayonnaise;1 tsp|worcestershire sauce;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Melt 1 tablespoon butter in a skillet over medium heat and cook the onions 12 to 15 minutes until deep golden. Set aside.|Mix the beef with Worcestershire, salt and pepper and form 4 oval patties the size of the bread.|Cook the patties in the skillet over medium-high heat 3 to 4 minutes per side until cooked through to 160°F.|Spread mayonnaise on one side of each bread slice. Butter the other sides.|Layer cheese, a patty, onions and more cheese between two slices of bread, buttered sides out.|Griddle 3 minutes per side over medium heat until golden and the cheese melts.","American"],
[3614,"Egg Salad Sandwich","lunch","🥪",25,"Very easy",8,4,"Creamy egg salad with a touch of mustard and chives piled on soft bread with lettuce.","8|eggs;1/3 cup|mayonnaise;1 tbsp|dijon mustard;1 stalk|celery|finely diced;1 tbsp|chives|chopped;1 tsp|lemon juice;8 slice|bread;4|lettuce leaves;|salt|to taste;|black pepper|to taste","Place the eggs in a saucepan, cover with cold water and bring to a boil. Cover, remove from heat and let stand 11 minutes.|Cool the eggs in ice water for 5 minutes, then peel and chop.|Mix the mayonnaise, mustard, lemon juice, celery and chives.|Fold in the chopped eggs and season with salt and pepper.|Spread on 4 slices of bread, top with lettuce and the remaining bread.","American"],
[3615,"Meatball Sub","lunch","🥖",45,"Easy",8,4,"Tender meatballs in marinara tucked into a toasted roll with melted mozzarella.","1 lb|ground beef;1/2 cup|breadcrumbs;1/4 cup|parmesan|grated;1|egg;2 clove|garlic|minced;2 tbsp|parsley|chopped;1/2 tsp|salt;2 cup|marinara sauce;4|sub rolls|split;8 slice|mozzarella;1 tbsp|olive oil","Heat the oven to 400°F. Mix the beef, breadcrumbs, parmesan, egg, garlic, parsley and salt and roll into 12 meatballs.|Bake on a lined sheet pan 15 to 18 minutes until cooked through to 160°F.|Simmer the meatballs in the marinara for 10 minutes.|Brush the rolls with olive oil and toast cut side up under the broiler 2 minutes.|Fill with meatballs and sauce, top with mozzarella and broil 2 minutes until melted and bubbly.","Italian"],
[3616,"Slow Cooker Pulled Chicken","prep","🍗",250,"Very easy",9,8,"Fall-apart shredded chicken in a smoky-sweet sauce, easy to portion for sandwiches, bowls and tacos all week.","3 lb|chicken breast;1 cup|barbecue sauce;1/2 cup|chicken broth;2 tbsp|brown sugar;1 tbsp|apple cider vinegar;1 tbsp|chili powder;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|smoked paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Whisk the barbecue sauce, broth, brown sugar, vinegar and spices in the slow cooker.|Add the chicken and turn to coat.|Cover and cook on low 4 to 5 hours or on high 2 1/2 to 3 hours until the chicken reaches 165°F and shreds easily.|Shred the chicken with two forks right in the pot and stir to soak up the juices.|Cool and portion into containers. Refrigerate up to 4 days or freeze up to 3 months.","American"],
[3617,"Freezer Chicken Enchiladas","prep","🌯",60,"Medium",9,8,"Two trays of chicken and cheese enchiladas assembled ahead and frozen, ready to bake on a busy night.","3 cup|cooked chicken|shredded;2 cup|monterey jack|shredded;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1/2 cup|green onion|sliced;1 tsp|cumin;12|flour tortillas|8 inch;3 cup|enchilada sauce;1 cup|cheddar|shredded;1 tbsp|olive oil;1/4 cup|cilantro|chopped","Mix the chicken, 1 cup monterey jack, beans, green onion, cumin and 1/2 cup of the enchilada sauce.|Spread 1/2 cup enchilada sauce in each of two foil pans.|Fill each tortilla with about 1/3 cup filling, roll and place seam down in the pans.|Pour remaining sauce over the top and sprinkle with the remaining jack and the cheddar.|Cover tightly with foil and freeze up to 3 months.|To bake, thaw overnight in the fridge. Bake covered at 375°F for 25 minutes, then uncovered 10 minutes until bubbling. From frozen, bake covered at 375°F for 60 minutes, then uncovered 10 minutes.","Mexican"],
[3618,"Freezer Meatballs","prep","🍝",50,"Easy",9,10,"Juicy beef and pork meatballs baked on sheet pans and frozen for quick pasta, subs and soups.","1 lb|ground beef;1 lb|ground pork;1 cup|breadcrumbs;1/2 cup|milk;2|eggs;3/4 cup|parmesan|grated;4 clove|garlic|minced;1/4 cup|parsley|chopped;1 tsp|dried oregano;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper","Heat the oven to 400°F and line two sheet pans with parchment.|Soak the breadcrumbs in the milk for 5 minutes.|Mix in the eggs, parmesan, garlic, parsley, oregano, salt and pepper, then add the meat and mix gently until just combined.|Roll into about 40 meatballs, 1 1/2 inches each, and place on the pans.|Bake 18 to 20 minutes until cooked through to 160°F.|Cool completely, freeze on the pans for 1 hour, then transfer to freezer bags. Keep up to 3 months and reheat in sauce for 15 to 20 minutes.","Italian"],
[3619,"Big Batch Chili","prep","🍲",120,"Easy",9,12,"A large pot of beef and bean chili that freezes beautifully in single-serve containers.","2 lb|ground beef;2 tbsp|olive oil;2|onion|diced;2|bell peppers|diced;6 clove|garlic|minced;3 tbsp|chili powder;1 tbsp|cumin;1 tbsp|smoked paprika;2 tsp|dried oregano;2 can|crushed tomatoes|28 oz each;3 tbsp|tomato paste;2 can|kidney beans|15 oz each, drained;2 can|black beans|15 oz each, drained;2 cup|beef broth;2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|black pepper","Brown the beef in a large pot with the oil over medium-high heat for 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the onions and peppers and cook 6 minutes.|Stir in the garlic, spices and tomato paste and cook 2 minutes.|Add the tomatoes, beans, broth, salt and pepper and bring to a boil.|Reduce the heat and simmer partly covered for 1 hour, stirring now and then.|Cool completely and portion into containers. Refrigerate up to 4 days or freeze up to 4 months.","American"],
[3620,"Chia Pudding Jars","prep","🫙",15,"Very easy",9,4,"Make-ahead jars of creamy vanilla chia pudding topped with berries, ready for the week's breakfasts.","1/2 cup|chia seeds;2 cup|milk;2 tbsp|maple syrup;1 tsp|vanilla extract;1 pinch|salt;1 cup|blueberries;1 cup|strawberries|sliced;1/4 cup|granola","Whisk the chia seeds, milk, maple syrup, vanilla and salt in a large bowl.|Let it sit 5 minutes, then whisk again to break up any clumps.|Divide among 4 jars, cover and refrigerate at least 4 hours or overnight until thick.|Stir each jar before serving and top with berries and granola.|Keeps in the fridge up to 5 days. Add the granola just before eating.","American"],
[3621,"Freezer Bean and Beef Burritos","prep","🌯",50,"Easy",9,12,"Hearty burritos with seasoned beef, beans, rice and cheese, wrapped individually and frozen for grab-and-go lunches.","1 lb|ground beef;1 packet|taco seasoning|1 oz;1 can|refried beans|16 oz;2 cup|cooked rice;1 cup|salsa;2 cup|cheddar|shredded;12|flour tortillas|10 inch","Brown the beef in a skillet 6 to 8 minutes and drain. Stir in the taco seasoning and 1/3 cup water and simmer 3 minutes.|Mix the beef with the refried beans, rice and salsa.|Warm the tortillas for 10 seconds each in the microwave so they fold without cracking.|Spoon about 1/2 cup filling and sprinkle of cheese into each tortilla, fold in the sides and roll tightly.|Cool completely, wrap each in foil or parchment and freeze in a bag up to 3 months.|To reheat, microwave unwrapped from frozen in a damp paper towel for 2 to 3 minutes, flipping halfway, until hot in the center.","Mexican"],
[3622,"Freezer Taco Soup","prep","🍲",45,"Very easy",9,8,"A cozy taco-flavored soup with beef, beans and corn that portions and freezes well.","1 1/2 lb|ground beef;1|onion|diced;3 clove|garlic|minced;2 packet|taco seasoning|1 oz each;1 can|diced tomatoes|28 oz;1 can|black beans|15 oz, drained;1 can|kidney beans|15 oz, drained;1 cup|frozen corn;4 cup|beef broth;1 can|green chiles|4 oz","Brown the beef with the onion in a large pot for 8 minutes. Drain excess fat.|Add the garlic and taco seasoning and cook 1 minute.|Add the tomatoes, beans, corn, broth and green chiles.|Bring to a boil, then simmer 20 minutes.|Cool completely and ladle into freezer bags or containers, leaving room to expand. Freeze up to 3 months.|Thaw overnight in the fridge and reheat, then serve with sour cream, cheddar and tortilla chips.","Tex-Mex"],
[3623,"Chicken and Rice Meal Prep Bowls","prep","🍱",50,"Easy",9,5,"Seasoned chicken, rice and roasted broccoli packed into five containers for easy weekday lunches.","2 lb|chicken breast;2 tbsp|olive oil;1 tsp|garlic powder;1 tsp|smoked paprika;1 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|black pepper;2 cup|white rice;2 head|broccoli|cut in florets;3 tbsp|soy sauce;1 tbsp|honey;1 tbsp|rice vinegar","Heat the oven to 425°F. Toss the chicken with 1 tablespoon oil and the garlic powder, paprika, salt and pepper.|Toss the broccoli with the remaining oil and a pinch of salt.|Roast the chicken and broccoli on separate sheet pans, 20 to 25 minutes for the chicken to reach 165°F and 18 to 20 minutes for the broccoli.|Cook the rice according to the package.|Whisk the soy sauce, honey and vinegar for the sauce.|Slice the chicken and divide with the rice and broccoli into 5 containers. Drizzle with sauce. Refrigerate up to 4 days.","American"],
[3624,"Cheese Scones","baking","🧀",35,"Easy",8.5,8,"Tall, tender savory scones packed with sharp cheddar and a pinch of mustard powder.","2 cup|flour;1 tbsp|baking powder;1/2 tsp|salt;1/2 tsp|mustard powder;1/4 tsp|cayenne pepper;4 tbsp|butter|cold, cubed;1 1/2 cup|cheddar|shredded, sharp;2/3 cup|milk;1|egg|beaten, for brushing","Heat the oven to 425°F and line a baking sheet with parchment.|Whisk the flour, baking powder, salt, mustard powder and cayenne.|Rub in the cold butter with your fingertips until the mixture looks like coarse crumbs.|Stir in 1 cup of the cheddar, then add the milk and mix just until a soft dough forms.|Pat out on a floured surface to 1 inch thick and cut into 8 rounds with a 2 1/2 inch cutter.|Place on the sheet, brush with egg, top with remaining cheese and bake 12 to 15 minutes until risen and golden.","British"],
[3625,"Homemade Crackers","baking","🍘",40,"Easy",8.5,8,"Thin, crisp crackers with olive oil and flaky salt, made from just a few pantry ingredients.","2 cup|flour;1 tsp|salt;1 tsp|baking powder;1/4 cup|olive oil;2/3 cup|milk;1 tbsp|sesame seeds;1 tsp|flaky sea salt","Heat the oven to 400°F.|Whisk the flour, salt and baking powder, then stir in the oil and milk to make a firm dough. Knead briefly until smooth.|Divide in half and roll each piece out as thinly as possible, about 1/16 inch, on parchment paper.|Prick all over with a fork, brush lightly with water and sprinkle with sesame seeds and flaky salt.|Cut into squares with a pizza cutter and slide the parchment onto a baking sheet.|Bake 12 to 15 minutes until golden, watching closely, then cool on a rack to crisp.","American"],
[3626,"Flour Tortillas","baking","🫓",45,"Easy",8.5,8,"Soft, pliable flour tortillas cooked in a hot skillet, far better than store-bought.","3 cup|flour;1 tsp|baking powder;1 tsp|salt;1/3 cup|lard|or vegetable shortening","Whisk the flour, baking powder and salt in a large bowl.|Rub in the lard until the mixture looks like sand.|Add 1 cup warm water and stir to form a dough, then knead 2 minutes until smooth.|Divide into 8 balls, cover and rest 20 minutes.|Roll each ball into a thin 8 inch circle.|Cook in a dry skillet over medium-high heat 30 to 45 seconds per side until puffed with light brown spots. Keep wrapped in a towel to stay soft.","Mexican"],
[3627,"Pretzel Rolls","baking","🥨",120,"Medium",8.5,8,"Chewy, mahogany-crusted rolls with the classic pretzel flavor from a quick baking soda bath.","2 1/4 tsp|active dry yeast;1 tbsp|brown sugar;3 1/2 cup|flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;3 tbsp|butter|melted;1/2 cup|baking soda;1|egg|beaten;1 tbsp|coarse salt","Stir 1 1/4 cups warm water, yeast and brown sugar and let sit 5 minutes until foamy.|Mix in the flour, salt and butter and knead 8 minutes until smooth. Let rise covered 1 hour until doubled.|Divide into 8 pieces and shape into smooth rolls. Rest 10 minutes. Heat the oven to 425°F.|Bring 10 cups water and the baking soda to a boil in a wide pot. Boil each roll 30 seconds per side.|Place on a parchment-lined sheet, brush with egg, slash the tops and sprinkle with coarse salt.|Bake 15 to 18 minutes until deep brown.","American"],
[3628,"Croissants","baking","🥐",720,"Medium",8.5,12,"Flaky, buttery croissants made with a simple folded dough, worth the weekend project.","4 cup|flour;1/4 cup|sugar;2 tsp|salt;2 1/4 tsp|instant yeast;1 1/4 cup|milk|cold;3 tbsp|butter|softened;1 1/4 cup|butter|cold, in one block, 10 oz;1|egg|beaten with 1 tbsp milk","Mix the flour, sugar, salt, yeast, milk and softened butter into a dough, knead 5 minutes, wrap and chill 1 hour.|Pound the cold butter block between parchment into a 6 inch square.|Roll the dough into a 12 inch square, place the butter diagonally in the center, fold the corners over and seal.|Roll into a 20 inch long rectangle and fold in thirds like a letter. Chill 30 minutes. Repeat the roll and fold twice more, chilling 30 minutes between each.|Chill 4 hours or overnight, then roll into a 8 by 24 inch rectangle and cut into 12 long triangles. Roll each from the wide end into a crescent.|Proof on parchment 1 1/2 to 2 hours until puffy. Brush with egg wash and bake at 400°F for 18 to 20 minutes until deep golden.","French"],
[3629,"Baguette","baking","🥖",240,"Medium",8.5,3,"Crisp-crusted French baguettes with an open crumb, made at home with just flour, water, yeast and salt.","4 cup|flour|bread flour;1 1/2 tsp|salt;1 tsp|instant yeast","Mix the flour, salt, yeast and 1 1/2 cups warm water into a shaggy dough, cover and rest 30 minutes.|Knead 8 minutes until smooth and elastic, then let rise covered 1 1/2 hours until doubled.|Divide into 3 pieces and pre-shape into rectangles. Rest 15 minutes.|Roll each into a 14 inch log, place on a floured towel or parchment and proof 45 minutes. Heat the oven to 475°F with a pan on the bottom rack.|Slash each loaf 3 to 4 times diagonally and slide onto a baking sheet or stone.|Pour 1 cup hot water in the pan to steam, bake 20 to 25 minutes until deep golden and cool on a rack.","French"],
[3630,"Ciabatta","baking","🍞",300,"Medium",8.5,2,"Rustic Italian loaves with a crackly crust and big holes, from a very wet dough.","3 1/2 cup|flour|bread flour;1 3/4 tsp|salt;1 tsp|instant yeast;2 tbsp|olive oil","Mix the flour, salt, yeast, 1 3/4 cups room-temperature water and olive oil into a very wet, sticky dough with a spoon. Cover.|Let rise 1 hour, then fold the dough over itself four times in the bowl. Repeat the rest and fold twice more over 2 hours total.|Heat the oven to 450°F with a baking sheet inside.|Turn the dough onto a generously floured surface, divide in two and gently stretch each into a 10 inch slipper shape. Do not knead or degas.|Rest on parchment 30 minutes.|Slide onto the hot sheet and bake 22 to 25 minutes until deep golden and hollow-sounding. Cool 30 minutes before slicing.","Italian"]];
